      "questionTextEng": "Karen considers teaching drawing in a gallery or taking a fine art programme in a university in France. Which of\n     the following would increase Karen’s cost of taking a fine art programme in France?\n\n           A.    The gallery closes down.\n           B.    The gallery raises the salaries of all teachers.\n           C.    The teaching quality of the fine art programme is not as good as Karen expected.\n           D.    The climate in France is pleasant and Karen enjoys living in France.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n     Karen’s cost of taking a fine art programme in France is the value of teaching drawing in a gallery.\n     Option B: The gallery raising the salaries of all teachers would increase the value of teaching drawing in\n     a gallery, thus increasing the cost of taking a fine art programme in France.\n     Option A: The option of teaching drawing in a gallery no longer exists. As there is no choice, there is no\n     cost.\n     Options C and D: These would only affect the value of taking a fine art programme in France without\n     affecting the value of teaching drawing in a gallery. Karen’s cost of taking a fine art programme in\n     France will not be affected.",
