      "questionTextEng": "There are metered parking spaces in many places in Hong Kong. Drivers can park their cars in the metered\n      parking spaces after paying fees. Which of the following statements about these parking spaces is CORRECT?\n\n            A.    These parking spaces are allocated on a first-come-first-served basis, so they are public goods.\n            B.    These parking spaces are rival in consumption, so they are private goods.\n            C.    Anyone can pay to use these parking spaces, so they are consumer goods.\n            D.    People need to pay to use these parking spaces, so they are economic goods.",
