      "questionTextEng": "Mr. Wong is the owner of a renovation company. The company employs many workers for different stages of a\n      renovation project, including painters, plumbers and water and electrical technicians. Mr. Wong is responsible for\n      contacting customers. Which of the following statements are CORRECT?\n\n            (1)   Mr. Wong is an entrepreneurship and his workers are labour.\n            (2)   Mr. Wong’s company adopts complex division of labour.\n            (3)   The workers do not need to learn every task involved in a project, thus training time can be reduced.\n\n            A.    (1) and (2) only\n            B.    (1) and (3) only\n            C.    (2) and (3) only\n            D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n     (1): Since Mr. Wong is the owner of the company, he is the human effort that makes decisions and bears\n     business risks, so he is an entrepreneurship. His workers are the human effort used in production, so\n     they are labour.\n     (2): Different workers specialise in different stages of a renovation project, so the company adopts a\n     complex division of labour.\n     (3): Since each worker specialises in a particular stage of a renovation project, they do not have to learn\n     every skill. Training time can thus be reduced.",
