      "questionTextEng": "The table below shows the cost-output relationship of a firm.\n\n                                          Output (units)         Average cost ($)\n                                               1                       15\n                                                 2                      16\n                                                 3                      17\n                                                 4                      18\n                                                 5                      19\n\n      Based on the above table, we can conclude that when the market price decreases from $21 to $19,\n\n            (1)   the firm will enjoy economies of scale.\n            (2)   the profit of the firm will decrease by $6.\n            (3)   the total cost of the firm will decrease from $72 to $51.\n\n            A.    (1) and (2) only\n            B.    (1) and (3) only\n            C.    (2) and (3) only\n            D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n                    Output (units)      Average cost ($)          Total cost ($)      Marginal cost ($)\n                          1                    15                      15                     -\n                          2                    16                      32                     17\n                          3                    17                      51                     19\n                          4                    18                      72                     21\n                          5                    19                      95                     23\n\n    When the market price decreases from $21 to $19, the firm’s total cost decreases from $72 to $51.\n    When the market price is $21, the output is 4 units and the total revenue is $84. Profit is $12 (= $84 −\n    $72). When the market price is $19, the output is 3 units and the total revenue is $57. Profit is $6\n    (= $57 − $51). Therefore, the profit of the firm will decrease by $6.",
