      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/27/a-p1-15.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following is INCONSISTENT with the law of demand?\n\n            A.    When the fine for littering increases, fewer people litter.\n            B.    When people visiting Hong Kong need to quarantine, their average number of stay days after\n                  quarantine increases.\n            C.    When the government increases the per-unit tax on tobacco products, the quantity of high-quality\n                  tobacco products sold decreases.\n            D.    When the cost of transporting fruits from South Korea to Hong Kong increases, the average quality of\n                  fruits imported from South Korea decreases.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    The law of demand states that an increase in the price of a good will result in a decrease in its quantity\n    demanded, ceteris paribus.\n    Option D: When the cost of transporting fruits from South Korea to Hong Kong increases, the relative\n    price of high-quality South Korean fruits decreases. According to the law of demand, Hong Kong will\n    import more high-quality South Korean fruits relative to low-quality South Korean fruits. The\n    proportion of high-quality fruits imported from South Korea increases, so the average quality of fruits\n    imported from South Korea will increase.\n    Option B: When both long trips and short trips involve the same costs of quarantine, the price of long\n    trips relative to short trips decreases. The proportion of tourists taking long trips after quarantine\n    increases, thus increasing their average number of stay days after quarantine.\n    Option C: When the government increases the per-unit tax on tobacco products, the price of tobacco\n    products increases, the quantity of tobacco products (including high-quality tobacco products) sold\n    decreases.",
