      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    Before the imposition of the tax, the price is $16 and the quantity transacted is 11 units.\n    After the imposition of the tax, the price is $18 and the quantity transacted is 10 units.\n    Option A: Consumers’ tax burden = ($18 – $16) × 10 units = $20\n    Producers’ tax burden = [$16 – ($18 – $4)] × 10 units = $20\n    Consumers bear the same tax burden as producers.\n    Option B: Change in total expenditure = $18 × 10 units − $16 × 11 units = $4. Total expenditure will\n    increase by $4.\n    Option C: Change in total revenue net of tax = ($18 − $4) × 10 units − $16 × 11 units = −$36.\n    Option D: Total government tax revenue = $4 × 10 units = $40.",
