      "questionTextEng": "Country A has imposed an effective quota on paper. Suppose electronic leaflets and bills are now more commonly\n      used to reduce the use of paper. Which of the following statements about the paper market are CORRECT?\n\n            (1)   The quota may become ineffective.\n            (2)   The producer surplus will decrease.\n            (3)   The deadweight loss will decrease.\n\n            A.    (1) and (2) only\n            B.    (1) and (3) only\n            C.    (2) and (3) only\n            D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    (1): As the demand for paper decreases, the quantity transacted will decrease. If the quantity transacted\n    falls below the quota limit, the quota will become ineffective.\n    (2): The demand for paper decreases. If the quota is still effective, the price will decrease and the\n    quantity transacted will remain unchanged. If the quota becomes ineffective, the price and the quantity\n    transacted will decrease. Producer surplus will decrease in both cases.\n    (3): A decrease in demand reduces the gap between marginal benefit and marginal cost. The deadweight\n    loss will decrease.",
