      "questionTextEng": "Mr. Cheung’s son often plays ball at home. Miss Li, who lives in the apartment below Mr. Cheung’s, often\n      complains to him that the noise of his son playing ball is very annoying. Which of the following statements is\n      CORRECT?\n\n            A.     If Mr. Cheung needs to compensate Miss Li for the noise, there will be no divergence between private\n                   and social costs.\n            B.     If Mr. Cheung needs to compensate Miss Li for the noise, the noise generated from Mr. Cheung’s\n                   home will be reduced.\n            C.     If Miss Li receives compensation from Mr. Cheung, she will not complain about the noise any more.\n            D.     Economic efficiency can be achieved only when the government intervenes and asks Mr. Cheung to\n                   compensate Miss Li.",
