      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/27/a-p2-09.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Income inequality is an issue of great public concern in Hong Kong.\n\n                                                          Source A: Gini coefficient of Hong Kong in 2011 and 2016\n                                                                                                                          2011        2016\n                                                           Gini coefficient based on original monthly household\n                                                                                                                          0.537      0.539\n                                                           income\n                                                           Gini coefficient based on post-tax post-social transfer\n                                                                                                                          0.475      0.473\n                                                           monthly household income\n                                                          (Source: Census and Statistics Department, HKSAR Government)\n\n                                                          Source B: Median monthly wage of employees by age group in Hong Kong, May – June 2020\n                                                                      By age group                   Median monthly wage (HKD)\n                                                                          15-24                                  13,600\n                                                                          25-34                                  19,500\n                                                                          35-44                                  21,400\n                                                                          45-54                                  18,900\n                                                                           ≥ 55                                  15,400\n                                                          (Source: Census and Statistics Department, HKSAR Government)\n\n                                                          Source C: News excerpt about the government lowering the eligible age of the Government Public Transport\n                                                          Fare Concession Scheme for the Elderly and Eligible Persons with Disabilities\n                                                           Starting from 27 February, 2022, the eligible age of the Government Public Transport Fare Concession\n                                                           Scheme for the Elderly and Eligible Persons with Disabilities ($2 Scheme) will be lowered from 65 to 60.\n                                                           Eligible persons can travel on designated public transport modes and services at a concessionary fare of\n                                                           $2 per trip, including MTR, franchised buses, ferries, minibuses, trams and kaitos. Residents’ services (居\n                                                           民巴士) are not included.\n\n                                                           The government reimburses the Public Transport Operators the actual applicable fares charged by them\n                                                           minus the $2 per trip paid by an eligible beneficiary on an accountable basis.\n                                                          (Source: various newspapers)\n\n                                                        Source D: Views of different stakeholders on the $2 Scheme\n\n                                                                                      Many people aged over 60 are still employed. The $2 Scheme can encourage\n                                                                                      employment.\n\n                                                            A government official\n                                                                                      The $2 Scheme can help elderly people reduce their home-to-work transport\n                                                                                      costs.\n\n                                                               A social worker\n                                                                                      I go out more after I became eligible for the $2 Scheme.\n\n                                                             A low-income elder\n\n                                                        (a) Refer to Source A. Describe the income distribution trend between 2011 and 2016 as reflected by the Gini\n                                                            coefficients based on original monthly household income. Explain whether the government’s taxes and\n                                                            social transfers are effective in reducing income inequality.                                 (2 marks)\n\n                                                        (b) Suggest ONE possible reason to explain the difference in the median monthly wage between employees\n                                                            aged 55 or over and those aged 25-54 as shown in Source B.                               (2 marks)\n\n                                                        (c) Refer to Sources C and D. Explain the behaviour of the low-income elder in Source D.               (2 marks)\n\n                                                        (d) Refer to Source C. With the aid of a demand-supply diagram, explain how the lowering of the eligible age\n                                                            of the $2 Scheme will affect the number of passengers of residents’ services.                (5 marks)\n\n                                                        For part (e), candidates are required to present their answer in essay form. Criteria for marking will include the\n                                                        use of sources and economic theories, relevant content, logical presentation and clarity of expression.\n\n                                                        (e) With reference to the above sources and your own knowledge in Economics, discuss the effects of lowering\n                                                            the eligible age of the $2 Scheme on Hong Kong, including:\n                                                           - efficiency,\n                                                           - Gini coefficient based on post-tax post-social transfer monthly household income, and\n                                                           - other economic variable(s).\n                                                                                                                                                          (11 marks)",
