      "questionTextEng": "Ricky is the only owner of an audiovisual production company. He does not have to bear legal responsibility for\n     the company. Which of the following statements MUST be true?\n\n           A.    The company needs to disclose its accounting information to the public.\n           B.    The company can raise capital by issuing shares or bonds to the public.\n           C.    Ricky’s loss is confined to the amount of his investment.\n           D.    The company will no longer exist if Ricky dies.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n     Since Ricky does not have to bear legal responsibility for the company, the form of business ownership\n     of the company is a limited company.\n     Option C: Owners of a limited company enjoy limited liability.\n     Option A: If the company is a private limited company, it is not required to disclose its accounting\n     information to the public.\n     Option B: If the company is a private limited company, it cannot issue shares and bonds to the public.\n     Option D: Since a limited company is a legal entity, it can still exist after the death of the owner.",
