      "section": "-",
      "questionNumber": "7",
      "questionTextChi": "甲廠商\t乙廠商\n工人數目\t15\t10\n每工人每日的工作時數\t8\t8\n每日的總產量 (單位)\t100\t100\n產出質素不合格率\t10%\t5%\n根據上表，以下哪項是甲廠商和乙廠商在勞工生產力上有差異的一個可能原因？\nA.\t乙廠商向工人提供較多訓練。\nB.\t甲廠商是以件計薪而乙廠商是以時計薪。\nC.\t乙廠商使用的機器較落後。\nD.\t甲廠商較乙廠商進行較高度的分工。",
      "plainText": "甲廠商\t乙廠商\n工人數目\t15\t10\n每工人每日的工作時數\t8\t8\n每日的總產量 (單位)\t100\t100\n產出質素不合格率\t10%\t5%\n根據上表，以下哪項是甲廠商和乙廠商在勞工生產力上有差異的一個可能原因？\nA.\t乙廠商向工人提供較多訓練。\nB.\t甲廠商是以件計薪而乙廠商是以時計薪。\nC.\t乙廠商使用的機器較落後。\nD.\t甲廠商較乙廠商進行較高度的分工。",
      "topic": "生產要素",
      "question": "MT28-P1-07",
      "answerMC": "A",
      "answerChi": "答案：A\n甲廠商的平均勞工生產力 = 100單位產出 / (15 × 8)工時 = 0.83單位產出/工時\n乙廠商的平均勞工生產力 = 100單位產出 / (10 × 8)工時 = 1.25單位產出/工時\n由於乙廠商的工人的生產力較高，可以推斷乙廠商很可能向工人提供較多訓練。\n選項B：甲廠商的勞工生產力較乙廠商低，意味甲廠商的員工很可能不用急於增加產量以賺取更多收入，因此甲廠商可能是以時計薪。\n選項C：若乙廠商使用的機器較落後，其勞工生產力很可能較低，與以上的計算不相符。\n選項D：若甲廠商進行較高度的分工，其勞工生產力很可能較高，與以上的計算不相符。",
      "curriculumClassification": [
        "B 廠商與生產"
      ],
      "AristochapterClassification": [
        "Ch05"
      ],
      "concepts": [
        "勞工生產力"
      ],
      "patterns": [
        "表格判讀",
        "選擇最佳答案"
      ],
      "graphType": "-",
      "tableType": "投入產出表",
      "multipleSelectionType": "-",
      "calculationType": "-",
      "source": "模擬試卷二十八 卷一",
      "reviewedByAI": "Y",
      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/28/q-p1-07.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/28/a-p1-07.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Firm A           Firm B\n                  Number of workers                                           15               10\n                  Number of working hours per worker per day                   8                8\n                  Total output per day (units)                               100              100\n                  Percentage of output with quality below standard           10%               5%\n\n     Based on the above table, which of the following is a possible reason for the difference between the labour\n     productivity of firm A and firm B?\n\n           A.    Firm B provides more training for its workers.\n           B.    Firm A adopts piece rate while firm B adopts time rate.\n           C.    Firm B uses less advanced machinery.\n           D.    Firm A practises a higher degree of division of labour than firm B.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n     Average labour productivity of firm A = 100 units of output / (15 × 8) man-hours = 0.83 units of output\n     per man-hour\n     Average labour productivity of firm B = 100 units of output / (10 × 8) man-hours = 1.25 units of output\n     per man-hour\n     As firm B’s workers are more productive than that of firm A, we can infer that firm B probably provides\n     more training for its workers.\n\n     Option B: Firm A’s labour productivity is lower than that of firm B, showing that firm A’s workers may\n     not need to rush for more output to earn more income, so firm A may have adopted time rate.\n     Option C: If firm B uses less advanced machinery, its labour productivity will probably be lower, which\n     is not consistent with the above calculation.\n     Option D: If firm A practises a higher degree of division of labour than firm B, its labour productivity\n     will probably be higher, which is not consistent with the above calculation.",
