      "questionTextEng": "The following table shows the production plan of a firm. The firm employs two inputs only, namely capital and\n      labour.\n\n                        Capital (units)              Labour (units)              Total product (units)\n                              5                           1                               10\n                              5                           2                               21\n                              5                           3                               33\n                              5                           4                               Q1\n                              5                           5                               Q2\n\n      Suppose the above data illustrates the law of diminishing marginal returns. Which of the following figures is/are\n      INCONSISTENT with the law?\n\n      (1)    Q1 = 48; Q2 = 60\n      (2)    Q1 = 49; Q2 = 69\n      (3)    Q1 = 40; Q2 = 38\n\n             A.    (1) only\n             B.    (2) only\n             C.    (1) and (2) only\n             D.    (1) and (3) only",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n          Capital (units)        Labour (units)     Total product (units)     Marginal product (units)\n                5                      1                      10                         10\n                5                      2                      21                         11\n                5                      3                      33                         12\n                5                      4                      Q1                         X\n                5                      5                      Q2                         Y\n     (2): When Q1 = 49 and Q2 = 69, X = 16 and Y = 20. As marginal product keeps increasing, the above\n     data does not illustrate the law of diminishing marginal returns.\n     (1): When Q1 = 48 and Q2 = 60, X = 15 and Y = 12. When labour increases from 4 units to 5 units,\n     marginal product decreases from 15 units to 12 units. The above data illustrates the law of diminishing\n     marginal returns.\n     (3): When Q1 = 40 and Q2 = 38, X = 7 and Y = –2. When labour increases from 3 units to 4 units,\n     marginal product decreases from 12 units to 7 units. The above data illustrates the law of diminishing\n     marginal returns.",
