      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/28/q-p1-13.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/28/a-p1-13.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The following table shows the cost-output relationship of a price-taking firm.\n\n                                        Output (units)         Average cost ($)\n                                             1                       20\n                                             2                       21\n                                             3                       22\n                                             4                       23\n                                             5                       24\n\n      Suppose the market price is $26. If the fixed cost increases from $5 to $10 and the average cost decreases by $2\n      for every unit of output, the profit-maximising output will __________, and the profit will __________.\n\n            A.    increase … increase\n            B.    increase … decrease\n            C.    decrease … increase\n            D.    decrease … decrease",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n      Output      Original         Original        Original         New              New            New\n      (units)   average cost      total cost       marginal      average cost      total cost      marginal\n                      ($)             ($)           cost ($)          ($)             ($)           cost ($)\n         1            20              20              15              18               18               8\n         2            21              42              22              19               38              20\n         3            22              66              24              20               60              22\n         4            23              92              26              21               84              24\n         5            24             120              28              22              110              26\n      Before the changes in the costs, when the market price is $26, the profit-maximising output is 4 units.\n      Profit = $26 × 4 − $92 = $12.\n      After the changes in the costs, when the market price is $26, the profit-maximising output is 5 units.\n      Profit = $26 × 5 − $110 = $20. Both the profit-maximising output and the profit will increase.",
