      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/28/a-p1-14.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The government of a country provides a per-unit subsidy on electric cars. Which of the following statements are\n      CORRECT?\n\n       (1) If the demand for electric cars is elastic, total sales revenue will increase.\n       (2) People will buy fewer high-quality electric cars.\n       (3) The ratio of high-quality electric cars sold to total electric cars sold will decrease.\n\n            A.    (1) and (2) only\n            B.    (1) and (3) only\n            C.    (2) and (3) only\n            D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    (1): When the government provides a per-unit subsidy on electric cars, the price of electric cars will\n     decrease, and the quantity demanded will increase. If the demand for electric cars is elastic, the\n     percentage decrease in price will be smaller than the percentage increase in quantity demanded. Total\n     sales revenue will increase.\n     (3): When the government provides a per-unit subsidy on electric cars, the price of high-quality electric\n    cars relative to low-quality electric cars will increase. A lower proportion of buyers will buy high-\n    quality electric cars, so the ratio of high-quality electric cars sold to total electric cars sold will decrease.\n    (2): When the government provides a per-unit subsidy on electric cars, the price of electric cars will\n    decrease. People will buy more electric cars, including high-quality electric cars.",
