      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/28/a-p1-16.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The diagram below shows the demand-supply diagram for local workers in Country A. E0 is the initial\n      equilibrium point.\n\n                              Wage rate\n\n                                                         S2\n                                                    E1        S0\n                                                                   S1\n                                                   E0\n                                          E4                  E2\n\n                                                    E3\n                                                                        D1\n                                                                   D0\n                                                              D2\n                                 0                                       Quantity\n\n      Suppose more local workers decide to retire. At the same time, the government increases the quota for importing\n      foreign workers. The new equilibrium point will be ____________.\n\n           A.    E1\n           B.    E2\n           C.    E3\n           D.    E4",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    More local workers retiring will cause the supply of local workers to decrease, shifting the supply curve\n    to the left. The government increasing the quota for importing foreign workers will cause the wage rate\n    of foreign workers to decrease. As local workers and foreign workers are substitutes, demand for local\n    workers will decrease, shifting the demand curve to the left.",
