      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/28/a-p1-17.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Read the following news excerpt.\n\n                 On 19 December 2021, some public transport operators, including those of buses,\n                 MTR and trams, offered free rides. A minibus operator revealed that, because\n                 minibuses did not offer free rides, their total revenue on that day decreased by 80%.\n\n      Which of the following statements are CORRECT?\n\n       (1) There was an excess supply of minibus service.\n       (2) The demand for the public transport services that offered free rides remained unchanged.\n       (3) There was an excess demand for services provided by the public transport operators that offered free rides.\n\n           A.    (1) and (2) only\n           B.    (1) and (3) only\n           C.    (2) and (3) only\n           D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n     (1): Minibus service and other public transport services are substitutes. When the fee of other public\n     transport services decreased, demand for minibus service decreased. There was an excess supply of\n     minibus service.\n     (2): The quantity demanded of public transport services that offered free rides increased while the\n     demand for them remained unchanged.\n     (3): The other public transport services are economic goods. When the price was zero, the quantity\n     demanded would be larger than the quantity supplied, and there would be an excess demand.",
