      "questionTextEng": "Suppose a per-unit tax is levied on good X. If the demand for good X is ___________, and the supply of good X\n      is ___________, the consumers’ tax burden will be smaller than the producers’ tax burden.\n\n           A.    perfectly inelastic … elastic\n           B.    unitarily elastic … perfectly elastic\n           C.    inelastic … elastic\n           D.    elastic … unitarily elastic",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    How the tax burden is shared between consumers and producers depends on the relative magnitude of\n    price elasticities of demand and supply. The more elastic party will have a smaller share of the tax\n    burden.\n    Options A, B, C: Since the price elasticity of supply is higher than the price elasticity of demand,\n    producers’ tax burden will be smaller.",
