      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/28/a-p1-19.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Refer to the following demand and supply schedules for good X.\n\n                   Unit price ($)                     10        12       14        16        18\n                   Quantity supplied (units)          10        15       20        25        30\n                   Quantity demanded (units)          30        25       20        15        10\n\n      Suppose the government lowers the price ceiling from $16 to $12. According to the above table, which of the\n      following statements is CORRECT?\n\n           A.    The market price will drop to $14.\n           B.    The quantity transacted will remain unchanged.\n           C.    Consumers’ expenditure will decrease by $100.\n           D.    The surplus of good X will disappear.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    When the price ceiling is $16, the price ceiling is ineffective. The price is $14 and the quantity\n    transacted is 20 units. Consumers’ expenditure is $14 × 20 = $280.\n    When the price ceiling is $12, the price ceiling is effective. The quantity transacted will be equal to the\n    quantity supplied, i.e. 15 units. Consumers’ expenditure will be $12 × 15 = $180.\n    Consumers’ expenditure will decrease by $100.",
