      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/28/a-p1-27.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The diagram below shows the aggregate demand curve, the short run aggregate supply curve and the long run\n      aggregate supply curve of an economy. The economy is initially at E0.\n\n                     Price level\n                                     LRAS\n                                                       SRAS0\n                                                                SRAS1\n\n                                            E0\n\n                                                               AD1\n                                                       AD0\n                         0                                           Output level\n\n      Which of the following can best explain the changes shown in the above diagram?\n\n           A.    an increase in government transfer payments and an increase in government expenditure on education\n           B.    an increase in the number of tourists and an occurrence of a large-scale strike in the economy\n           C.    a decrease in asset demand for money and a decrease in the profits tax rate\n           D.    a decrease in the price of raw materials and a decrease in the salaries tax rate",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    A decrease in the price of raw materials will cause the short run aggregate supply to increase. A decrease\n    in the salaries tax rate will cause private consumption expenditure to increase. Aggregate demand will\n    increase.\n    Option A: The government increasing transfer payments will increase private consumption expenditure.\n    Aggregate demand will increase. Increasing expenditure on education will increase government\n    expenditure, and aggregate demand will increase. The economy’s productive capacity will also increase.\n    Both the short run aggregate supply and the long run aggregate supply will increase.\n    Option B: An increase in the number of tourists will cause net exports to increase. Aggregate demand\n    will increase. An occurrence of a large-scale strike in the economy will cause the short run aggregate\n    supply to decrease.\n    Option C: A decrease in asset demand for money will cause the interest rate to decrease. Investment and\n    consumption will increase. Aggregate demand will increase. A decrease in the profits tax rate will cause\n    investment expenditure to increase. Aggregate demand will increase.",
