      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following will cause an economy’s price level and aggregate output to increase in the short run?\n\n           A.    People’s desire to save increases.\n           B.    Consumers expect the future price level to increase.\n           C.    The money supply decreases.\n           D.    The economy’s major trading partner experiences a recession.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    Consumers expecting the future price level to increase will raise current consumption. Private\n    consumption expenditure will increase. Aggregate demand will increase. The price level and aggregate\n    output will increase in the short run.\n    Option A: An increase in people’s desire to save will lead to a decrease in private consumption\n    expenditure. Aggregate demand will decrease. The price level and aggregate output will decrease in the\n    short run.\n    Option C: When the money supply decreases, the interest rate will increase. Consumption and\n    investment will decrease. Aggregate demand will decrease. The price level and aggregate output will\n    decrease in the short run.\n    Option D: When the economy’s major trading partner experiences a recession, net exports will decrease.\n    Aggregate demand will decrease. The price level and aggregate output will decrease in the short run.",
