      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/28/q-p1-31.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/28/a-p1-31.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Mr. Tai withdraws HK$100,000 cash from a deposit-taking company. He keeps half of the amount as cash at\n      home and remits the remainder overseas.\n\n      What will be the immediate effect of the above actions on the money supply of Hong Kong?\n\n           A.    M1 will remain unchanged.\n           B.    Both M1 and M2 will increase by HK$50,000.\n           C.    M3 will decrease by HK$100,000.\n           D.    M1, M2 and M3 will decrease by HK$50,000.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    Withdrawing HK$100,000 cash from a deposit-taking company will increase M1 and M2 by\n    HK$100,000, while M3 will remain unchanged.\n    Keeping half of the amount ($50,000) as cash at home will not affect M1, M2 and M3.\n    Remitting the remainder ($50,000) overseas will result in a decrease in M1, M2 and M3 by HK$50,000,\n    as this amount is no longer included in Hong Kong’s money supply.\n    The overall effect of the above actions on M1, M2 and M3:\n    M1 will increase by HK$50,000.\n    M2 will increase by HK$50,000.\n    M3 will decrease by HK$50,000.",
