      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/28/a-p1-32.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Study the following information. Suppose the banks do not hold excess reserves.\n\n                                                                          $ million\n                         Currency in public circulation                      20\n                         Monetary base                                      100\n                         Money supply                                       420\n\n      If the public withdraw $10 million from the banking system and hold it in cash,\n\n           A.    the maximum amount of deposits will be $350 million.\n           B.    the money supply will remain unchanged.\n           C.    the monetary base will increase by $10 million.\n           D.    the maximum amount of loans will decrease by $280 million.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    Original reserves = Monetary base − Currency in public circulation = $(100 − 20) million = $80 million\n    Original deposits = Money supply − Currency in public circulation = $(420 − 20) million = $400 million\n    Original loans = $(400 – 80) million = $320 million\n    Required reserve ratio = ($80 million/$400 million) × 100% = 20%\n    After the public withdraw $10 million from the banking system and hold it in cash:\n    New currency in public circulation = $(20 + 10) million = $30 million\n    New reserves = $(80 – 10) million = $70 million\n    Maximum amount of deposits = $70 million × (1/20%) = $350 million\n    Option B: New money supply = $(350 + 30) million = $380 million. The money supply will decrease.\n    Option C: New monetary base = $(30 + 70) million = $100 million. The monetary base will remain\n    unchanged.\n    Option D: Maximum amount of loans = $(350 – 70) million = $280 million. The maximum amount of\n    loans will decrease by $40 million.",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/28/ae-p1-32.jpg",
      "originalQuestionImageEng": "originals/28/qe-p1-32.jpg",
      "stemPatterns": [
        "(某人)作出一系統提款存款活動，問M1, M2, M3的影響"
      ]
