      "multipleSelectionType": "三項陳述組合",
      "calculationType": "-",
      "source": "模擬試卷二十八 卷一",
      "reviewedByAI": "Y",
      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/28/q-p1-35.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/28/a-p1-35.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Suppose the growth rate of the price level is increasing. If the growth rate of the money supply is increasing and is\n      higher than the growth rate of the price level, according to the quantity theory of money,\n\n       (1) nominal output is increasing.\n       (2) real output is increasing.\n       (3) the velocity of circulation of money is decreasing.\n\n            A.    (1) and (2) only\n            B.    (1) and (3) only\n            C.    (2) and (3) only\n            D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    Quantity theory of money: MV = PY, where M = money supply, V = velocity of circulation of money, P\n    = price level and Y = real output, assuming V is constant.\n    % change in M ≈ % change in P + % change in Y ≈ % change in nominal output\n    (1): As the growth rate of M is increasing, the growth rate of nominal output is also increasing, showing\n    that nominal output is increasing.\n    (2): When the growth rate of M is increasing and higher than that of P, the growth rate of Y will be\n    positive, showing that the real output is increasing.",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/28/ae-p1-35.jpg",
