      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/28/a-p1-36.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following will most likely cause the unemployment rate of an economy to decrease?\n\n            A.    The government relaxes the policy on importing foreign workers.\n            B.    The government raises the unemployment benefits.\n            C.    There is a decrease in the number of places in post-secondary education.\n            D.    More firms expand their businesses.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    More firms expanding their businesses implies that the number of job positions will increase. The\n    unemployed population will decrease. The unemployment rate will decrease.\n    Option A: If the government relaxes the policy on importing foreign workers, the labour force will\n    increase. As the imported foreign workers may replace local workers, the unemployed population may\n    increase. The unemployment rate may increase.\n    Option B: The increase in unemployment benefits will reduce people’s incentive to work. The\n    unemployed population will increase and the unemployment rate will increase.\n    Option C: The reduction in the number of places in post-secondary education will cause more young\n    people to enter the labour market as they cannot continue their studies. The labour force will increase.\n    However, some of them may not be able to find a job, so the change in the unemployment rate is\n    uncertain",
