      "questionTextEng": "Country A is facing fiscal deficit and trade deficit. Which of the following may improve the fiscal deficit and\n      trade deficit at the same time?\n\n       (1) an increase in money supply\n       (2) a decrease in the basic allowance of the salaries tax\n       (3) an appreciation of Country A’s currency\n\n            A.    (1) only\n            B.    (2) only\n            C.    (1) and (3) only\n            D.    (2) and (3) only",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    (2): A decrease in the basic allowance of the salaries tax may increase government revenue, improving\n    the fiscal deficit. It will reduce people’s disposable income, causing imports to decrease, improving\n    trade deficit.\n    (1): An increase in the money supply will cause the interest rate to decrease. Consumption and\n    investment will increase. Aggregate demand will increase. An increase in national income will cause\n    government tax revenue to increase, improving the fiscal deficit. However, an increase in national\n    income will lead to an increase in imports, worsening the trade deficit.\n    (3): An appreciation of Country A’s currency will cause its export price (in terms of foreign currency) to\n    increase, the volume of exports will decrease. The export value (in terms of Country A’s currency) will\n    decrease. At the same time, the import price (in terms of Country A’s currency) will decrease and the\n    volume of imports will increase. The change in the import value (in terms of Country A’s currency) will\n    be uncertain, depending on the price elasticity of demand. The effect on trade deficit will thus be\n    uncertain. The decrease in export value will negatively affect the business of export-related industries,\n    decreasing government profits tax revenue and worsening the fiscal deficit.",
