      "questionTextEng": "The diagram below shows the market situation of good X in a small open economy.\n\n                          Unit price\n                                                                    S\n\n                            P1\n\n                            P0\n                                                                         D\n\n                             0             Q1              Q2                Quantity\n\n      P0 is the world price of the good and the import quota imposed by the government is (Q2 − Q1) units. If the world\n      price of the good increases to P1,\n\n             A.   the domestic price of the good will remain unchanged.\n             B.   the quantity of imports will increase.\n             C.   the domestic production of the good will increase.\n             D.   the shortage of the good will be eliminated.",
