      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/28/a-p1-44.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Refer to the following information about the balance of payments of an economy in a certain year.\n\n                                                    Item                       $ million\n                                 Exports of goods                                 50\n                                 Imports of goods                                 10\n                                 Exports of services                              15\n                                 Imports of services                              25\n                                 Income receivable from abroad                    40\n                                 Income payable abroad                            20\n                                 Current transfer received from abroad            10\n                                 Current transfer to abroad                       25\n                                 Decrease in reserve assets                       20\n\n      According to the above information, which of the following statements are CORRECT?\n\n       (1)   The economy’s gross national income is smaller than its gross domestic product.\n       (2)   The invisible trade deficit is $10 million.\n       (3)   The current account surplus is $35 million.\n       (4)   The balance of payments deficit is $20 million.\n\n             A.   (1) and (3) only\n             B.   (2) and (4) only\n             C.   (1), (2) and (3) only\n             D.   (2), (3) and (4) only",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    (2): Invisible trade balance = $(15 – 25) million = −$10 million\n    (3): Current account balance = Visible trade balance + Invisible trade balance + Net factor income from\n    abroad + Net current transfers\n     = $[(50 −10) + (−10) + (40 – 20) + (10 – 25)] million\n     = $35 million\n    (4): As there is a decrease in reserve assets of $20 million, the balance of payments deficit is $20\n    million.\n    (1): As the income receivable from abroad is larger than the income payable abroad, the net factor\n    income from abroad is positive. The economy’s gross national income is larger than its gross domestic\n    product.",
