      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/28/q-p1-45.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/28/a-p1-45.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Under the linked exchange rate system of Hong Kong, which of the following statements are CORRECT?\n\n      (1) The monetary base of Hong Kong is fully backed by the US dollars.\n      (2) The market exchange rate of the US dollar against the Hong Kong dollar is fixed at US$1 = HK$7.8.\n      (3) If the US dollar depreciates against other currencies, the average price of Hong Kong imports will tend to\n          decrease.\n      (4) If the US dollar depreciates against other currencies, the total value of Hong Kong exports (in terms of the\n          Hong Kong dollar) will increase.\n\n           A.   (1) and (2) only\n           B.   (1) and (4) only\n           C.   (2) and (3) only\n           D.   (3) and (4) only\n\n                                                EN D O F PAP E R",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    (1): To issue Hong Kong dollar banknotes, the note-issuing banks have to submit an equivalent amount\n    of US dollars in exchange for the Certificate of Indebtedness issued by the Exchange Fund at the linked\n    rate. Therefore, Hong Kong’s monetary base (i.e. cash in public circulation + bank reserves) is fully\n    backed by US dollars.\n    (4): Under the linked exchange rate system, when the US dollar depreciates against other currencies, the\n    Hong Kong dollar will depreciate against other currencies accordingly. The price of Hong Kong exports\n    (in terms of other currencies) will decrease, the volume of exports will increase. The total value of Hong\n    Kong exports (in terms of Hong Kong dollars) will increase.\n    (2): Only the official exchange rate between the Hong Kong Monetary Authority and the note-issuing\n    banks is fixed at HK$1 to HK$7.8.\n\n    (3): Under the linked exchange rate system, when the US dollar depreciates against other currencies, the\n    Hong Kong dollar will depreciate against other currencies accordingly. The price of Hong Kong imports\n    (in terms of Hong Kong dollars) will increase. The average price of Hong Kong imports will tend to\n    increase.",
