      "questionTextEng": "The table below shows the balance sheet of a banking system. Suppose the banks hold $1,000 excess\n                                                           reserves and the public do not hold cash.\n\n                                                                                         Assets ($)                        Liabilities ($)\n                                                                             Reserves                   3,000   Deposits                     8,000\n                                                                             Loans                      5,000\n\n                                                          (a)   Calculate the required reserve ratio.                                                           (1 mark)\n\n                                                          (b) Suppose someone withdraws $1,500 from the banking system and holds it in cash.\n\n                                                                 (i)   Explain whether the monetary base changes.                                              (2 marks)\n\n                                                                 (ii) Calculate the maximum possible amount of money supply. Show your working.                (3 marks)",
