      "questionTextEng": "Country A and Country B each possess 90 units of resources. The following table shows the number of\n                                                           resources required by the two countries for the production of juice and bread.\n\n                                                                                                   1 unit of juice            1 unit of bread\n                                                                               Country A               27 units                   9 units\n                                                                               Country B               15 units                   6 units\n\n                                                          (a)   Which country has a comparative advantage in producing juice? Explain.                           (3 marks)\n\n                                                          (b) Find the total output of juice and bread of the two countries after they completely specialise their\n                                                              production.                                                                              (2 marks)\n\n                                                          (c)   The juice-exporting country exports 5 units of juice in exchange for 14 units of bread. Calculate the total\n\n                                                                gain from trade for the juice-exporting country.                                                (3 marks)",
