      "questionTextEng": "Since 2020, many mask factories have been set up in Hong Kong to produce masks.\n\n                                                          (a)   Suggest ONE possible reason to explain why the market structure of mask factories in Hong Kong is\n                                                                NOT perfectly competitive.                                                              (2 marks)\n\n                                                          (b) Suppose the price of raw materials for masks has decreased. With the aid of a diagram, explain under\n                                                              what condition the total revenue of the mask factories would decrease.                     (7 marks)\n\n                                                          (c)   Give ONE reason to explain why the contribution of these mask factories to Hong Kong’s gross domestic\n                                                                product might be less than their sales revenue of the current year.                         (2 marks)\n\n                                                          (d) Wearing a mask can effectively prevent an individual from contracting viruses and from spreading viruses\n                                                              to others. Explain how the behaviour of wearing a mask may involve externality.\n                                                                                                                                                            (3 marks)",
