      "inlineDiagrams": "diagrams/MT28-P2-09.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Figure 1 shows the AS-AD diagram of economy A. Point E is the original short run equilibrium of the\n                                                           economy.\n                                                                                                  Figure 1\n\n                                                                                  Price level\n                                                                                                LRAS0\n                                                                                                                   SRAS0\n\n                                                                                                        E\n\n                                                                                                                     AD0\n                                                                                      0                                     Aggregate output\n\n                                                          (a)   Explain if there is an inflationary (output) gap or a deflationary (output) gap.                (2 marks)\n\n                                                          Suppose the government wants to restore the economy to its long run equilibrium by raising the salaries tax\n                                                          rate or imposing a contractionary monetary policy.\n\n                                                          (b) With the aid of the above diagram, explain how a contractionary monetary policy can help restore\n                                                              economy A to its long run equilibrium.                                                (7 marks)\n\n                                                          (c)   Briefly discuss ONE advantage and ONE disadvantage of raising the salaries tax rate for economy A as\n                                                                compared to imposing a contractionary monetary policy.                                      (4 marks)\n\n                                                          (d) Other than the above policies, suggest ONE policy that affects the short run aggregate supply that can\n                                                              help restore economy A to its long run equilibrium. Briefly explain your answer.            (2 marks)",
