      "questionTextEng": "Lok’s Amusement Park is the only indoor amusement park in Country A. It adopts uniform pricing. Figure 2\n                                                                 shows its demand curve and marginal cost curve.\n                                                                                                         Figure 2\n                                                                                      Unit price\n\n                                                                                                                                      MC0\n\n                                                                                                                         D\n                                                                                         0                                               Quantity\n\n                                                           (a)     Indicate the marginal revenue curve (MR), the profit-maximising output level (QM) and the price (PM) of\n                                                                   Lok’s Amusement Park in Figure 2.                                                            (3 marks)\n\n                                                           (b) With the aid of Figure 2, explain why Lok’s Amusement Park adopting uniform pricing will lead to a\n                                                               deadweight loss.                                                                        (2 marks)\n\n                                                           (c)     Suppose the marginal cost of Lok’s Amusement Park increases and the park does not change its output and\n                                                                   price. With the aid of Figure 2, explain whether economic efficiency will be affected.       (3 marks)\n\n                                                           (d) The following is the pricing arrangement of Lok’s Amusement Park:\n\n                                                                                      Weekdays                                      Weekends\n\n                                                                       Adult: $80 per hour                          Adult: $150 per hour\n                                                                       Child aged 1-12: $130 per hour               Child aged 1-12: $200 per hour\n\n                                                                   Explain if the difference in prices between weekdays and weekends constitutes price discrimination.\n                                                                                                                                                                  (3 marks)\n\n                                                           (e)     It is reported that Lok’s Amusement Park makes an agreement with its potential competitor that if Lok’s\n                                                                   Amusement Park does not expand its business to Country B, its potential competitor will not expand its\n                                                                   business to Country A. Which anti-competitive behaviour does Lok’s Amusement Park engage in? List\n                                                                   TWO possible motives for it.                                                                (3 marks)\n\n                                                           (f)     Some citizens criticise that there is only one indoor amusement park in Country A and that Lok’s\n                                                                   Amusement Park may be involved in anti-competitive behaviour. Give ONE reason to explain why the fact\n                                                                   that Country A has only one indoor amusement park is not necessarily anti-competitive.    (2 marks)",
