      "questionTextEng": "Refer to Figure 3. PPFA is the production possibility frontier of Country A. P A is the production point of\n                                                             Country A under autarky. The slope of the dotted line AB is the world price of good X.\n\n                                                                                                       Figure 3\n                                                                             Good Y\n\n                                                                                  A\n\n                                                                                                     PA\n\n                                                                                                          B              PPFA\n                                                                              0                                                             Good X\n                                                                                                                                 100\n\n                                                           (a)   Explain why the production possibility frontier of Country A is concave to the origin.            (2 marks)\n\n                                                           (b) Indicate, in Figure 3, the opportunity cost of producing good X. Explain whether Country A has a\n                                                               comparative advantage in producing good X.\n                                                               (Hint: you may add a straight line at PA.)                                             (4 marks)\n\n                                                           (c)   Suppose Country A engages in trade. In Figure 3,\n\n                                                                 (i)   indicate the production point (PT) and consumption possibility frontier (CPFA) of Country A after\n                                                                       trade.                                                                                 (3 marks)\n\n                                                                 (ii) indicate the consumption point (CT) of Country A after trade. Explain why Country A will gain after\n                                                                      trade.                                                                                  (2 marks)\n\n                                                                 (iii) indicate the export volume of Country A.                                                     (1 mark)\n\n                                                           (d) The following table shows some data of Country A before and after opening up to trade.\n\n                                                                                                                  Before trade           After trade\n                                                                       Human Development Index (HDI)                 0.62                   0.75\n                                                                          Life expectancy at birth                    74                     74\n\n                                                                 (i)   Give ONE possible reason to explain the change in HDI after trade.                          (2 marks)\n\n                                                                 (ii) Despite an increase in HDI, residents of Country A think that their living standard has decreased. Give\n                                                                      TWO possible reasons to explain their view.                                                  (2 marks)",
