      "questionTextEng": "Mr. Wong is considering the following two investments:\n\n     (1)   setting up a photography company in the form of a sole proprietorship\n     (2)   joining a friend’s photography company as a partner\n\n     Which of the following is a possible reason for Mr. Wong deciding to set up a photography company in the form\n     of a sole proprietorship?\n\n           A.    He can enjoy a higher degree of autonomy.\n           B.    He is subject to a lower profits tax rate.\n           C.    He does not need to use his personal assets to settle the debts of the business.\n           D.    He wants the business to have better continuity.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n     Since there is only one owner in a sole proprietorship, the owner does not need to get approval before\n     making decisions. Thus, the owner enjoys a higher degree of flexibility and autonomy.\n     Option B is incorrect. A sole proprietorship and a partnership are subject to the same profits tax rate.\n     Option C is incorrect. Neither a sole proprietorship nor a partnership is a legal entity, so the owner(s)\n     bear(s) unlimited liability.\n     Option D is incorrect. Neither a sole proprietorship nor a partnership is a legal entity, so the continuity\n     of the business depends on the lifespan of the owner(s).",
