      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n     Under the previous wage payment scheme, the workers were inefficient and had poor service attitudes,\n     reflecting that their wages may not have directly depended on output and service quality. Thus, it may\n     have been a time rate scheme.\n     Under the new wage payment scheme, the number of customers served each day increased and fewer\n     complaints were received from customers, reflecting that the wages of the workers may depend on\n     output and service quality. Thus, it may be a basic salary plus commission scheme.",
