      "questionTextEng": "Firm A and firm B produce the same good. The labour supply of both firms is the same while firm A’s output is\n     twice firm B’s. Which of the following is a possible reason for the difference in labour productivity between firm\n     A and firm B?\n\n     (1)   Firm A uses time rate while firm B uses piece rate to pay their workers.\n     (2)   More capital goods are used in firm A.\n     (3)   Firm A practises a higher degree of division of labour.\n\n           A.    (1) and (2) only\n           B.    (1) and (3) only\n           C.    (2) and (3) only\n           D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
