      "questionTextEng": "Anson runs an indoor photography studio. In which of the following situations will Anson increase his production\n      to maximise his profit?\n\n            A.     The hourly wage of photographers falls.\n            B.     The monthly rental payment for the studio decreases.\n            C.     The electricity fee increases.\n            D.     The business registration fee increases.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    The hourly wage of photographers is a variable cost. The decrease in the hourly wage of photographers\n     will lead to a decrease in marginal cost. When the marginal cost of each unit of output decreases, the\n     level of output that the firm is willing and able to supply at every given price will increase. The\n     profit-maximising output level will thus increase.\n     Options B and D are incorrect. They involve changes in fixed costs, which will not affect the\n     determination of the profit-maximising output level.\n     Option C is incorrect. This will result in an increase in marginal cost. The profit-maximising output\n     level will decrease.",
