      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/29/q-p1-12.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/29/a-p1-12.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "People of Country A love to eat oysters. Suppose the government of Country A imposes a per-unit tax on each\n      kilogram of oysters. Which of the following statements is CORRECT?\n\n            A.     The proportion of high-quality oysters sold in Country A will increase.\n            B.     The total weight of oysters consumed by the people of Country A will increase.\n            C.     The total expenditure of the people of Country A on oysters will decrease.\n            D.     The average quality of oysters sold in Country A will decrease.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    The money price of high-quality oysters is generally higher than that of low-quality oysters. When the\n    per-unit tax is added, the relative price of high-quality oysters (in terms of low-quality oysters) will\n    decrease. According to the law of demand, people will buy more high-quality oysters relative to\n    low-quality oysters, so the proportion of high-quality oysters sold in Country A will increase.\n    Option B is incorrect. When the per-unit tax is added, the price of oysters will increase and the quantity\n    demanded will decrease. The total weight of oysters consumed by the people of Country A will\n    decrease.\n    Option C is incorrect. When the per-unit tax is added, the price of oysters will increase and the quantity\n    demanded will decrease. The change in total expenditure is uncertain, depending on the price elasticity\n    of demand.\n    Option D is incorrect. As the proportion of high-quality oysters sold in Country A will increase, the\n    average quality of oysters sold in Country A will increase.",
