      "questionTextEng": "If the price of ___________ decreases, the demand for __________ will increase.\n\n       (1) air travel … airports\n       (2) construction materials … houses\n       (3) film cameras … film\n\n            A.     (1) only\n            B.     (3) only\n            C.     (1) and (2) only\n            D.     (1) and (3) only",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    (1) is correct. The demand for air travel will lead to a derived demand for airports. When the price of air\n    travel decreases, its quantity demanded will increase and the demand for airports will increase.\n    (3) is correct. Film cameras and film are in joint demand. When the price of film cameras decreases,\n    their quantity demanded will increase. The demand for film will also increase.\n    (2) is incorrect. Construction materials are factors of production for houses. Changes in the price of\n    construction materials would affect the supply of houses, but not the demand.",
