      "questionTextEng": "When the supply of good X decreases, its price and quantity transacted change by 10% and 5% respectively.\n      Which of the following best explains the extent of the changes in the price and quantity transacted of good X?\n\n           A.    There are many close substitutes for good X.\n           B.    The expenditure on good X accounts for a small proportion of people’s income.\n           C.    The factors of production for good X are easily available.\n           D.    A low level of technology is required to produce good X.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    The supply of good X decreases. As the percentage change in price is greater than the percentage change\n    in quantity demanded, demand for good X is inelastic.\n    Option B is correct. When the expenditure on good X accounts for a small proportion of people’s\n    income, demand for good X tends to be less elastic. This is because a change in its price has little effect\n    on the total expenditure.\n    Option A is incorrect. If there are many close substitutes for good X, demand for good X will tend to be\n    more elastic. Consumers are more likely to switch to the substitutes when the price of good X increases.\n    Options C and D are incorrect. They are factors affecting price elasticity of supply.",
