      "questionTextEng": "The following table shows the marginal cost schedule of a coffee producer.\n\n                                     Quantity (units)           Marginal cost ($)\n                                            1                         10\n                                            2                         11\n                                            3                         12\n                                            4                         13\n                                            5                         14\n                                            6                         15\n\n      If the price of coffee increases from $12 to $13, the producer surplus will __________.\n\n           A.    increase by $1\n           B.    increase by $3\n           C.    decrease by $1\n           D.    decrease by $3",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    When the price is $12, the quantity supplied is 3 units. Producer surplus = ($12 − $10) + ($12 − $11) +\n    ($12 − $12) = $3.\n    When the price is $13, the quantity supplied is 4 units. Producer surplus = ($13 − $10) + ($13 − $11) +\n    ($13 – $12) + ($13 − $13) = $6.\n    Therefore, if the price of coffee increases from $12 to $13, the producer surplus will increase by $3.",
