      "questionTextEng": "Refer to the following demand and supply schedules for good X.\n\n                     Unit price ($)      Quantity demanded (units)           Quantity supplied (units)\n                            5                       35                                  20\n                           10                       30                                  20\n                           15                       25                                  20\n                           20                       20                                  20\n                           25                       15                                  20\n                           30                       10                                  20\n\n      If the government sets a price floor of $25 on good X,\n\n             A.    the producers can receive a higher total sales revenue.\n             B.    the sales volume will remain unchanged.\n             C.    the demand for good X’s substitutes will increase.\n             D.    the consumer surplus will increase.",
