      "questionTextEng": "After the government provides a per-unit subsidy of $3 for producers of milk, the market price of milk decreases\n      by $2. Which of the following statements is CORRECT?\n\n             A.    The producer surplus decreases.\n             B.    Within the range of the original and new market prices, the elasticity of demand for milk is smaller\n                   than its elasticity of supply.\n             C.    The ratio of producers’ share of the subsidy to consumers’ share of the subsidy is 3:2.\n             D.    The change in the total revenue including the subsidy is uncertain.",
