      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/29/q-p1-23.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/29/a-p1-23.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following may lead to an increase in aggregate output and a narrower income gap in Hong Kong at\n      the same time?\n\n       (1) launching the Working Family Allowance Scheme for eligible low-income families\n       (2) building more public housing\n       (3) decreasing the progressivity of the salaries tax\n\n           A.    (1) and (2) only\n           B.    (1) and (3) only\n           C.    (2) and (3) only\n           D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    (1) is correct. Launching the Working Family Allowance Scheme for eligible low-income families will\n    increase the disposable income of low-income households. Private consumption expenditure will\n    increase. Aggregate demand will increase. Aggregate output will increase. At the same time, the scheme\n    will increase the income of low-income households while the income of high-income households\n    remains unchanged. The income gap between the high-income households and the low-income\n    households will be narrowed.\n    (2) is correct. Building more public housing will increase government expenditure. Aggregate demand\n    will increase. Aggregate output will increase. At the same time, public housing as a transfer in kind can\n    raise the real income of low-income households. The income gap between the high-income households\n    and the low-income households will be narrowed.\n\n    (3) is incorrect. Decreasing the progressivity of the salaries tax will increase people’s disposable income.\n    Private consumption expenditure will increase. Aggregate demand will increase. Aggregate output will\n    increase. However, as decreasing the progressivity of the salaries tax will lower the tax rates imposed on\n    higher-income households, the income gap between the high-income households and the low-income\n    households will be widened.",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/29/ae-p1-23.jpg",
