      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/29/q-p1-25.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/29/a-p1-25.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The following table shows gross domestic product (GDP) data of an economy in a certain year.\n\n                           Change in price level                             2%\n                           Change in population size                         2.5%\n                           Change in nominal GDP                             1.2%\n\n      Based on the information above, we can conclude that in that year,\n\n             A.    both the real GDP and the per capita nominal GDP increased.\n             B.    both the real GDP and the per capita nominal GDP decreased.\n             C.    the real GDP increased and the per capita nominal GDP decreased.\n             D.    the real GDP decreased and the per capita nominal GDP increased.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    Since the price level decreased (with a negative percentage change) and the nominal GDP increased\n    (with a positive percentage change), the real GDP increased.\n    1 + Growth rate of per capita nominal GDP = (1 + Growth rate of nominal GDP) / (1 + Growth rate of\n    population size)\n    Growth rate of per capita nominal GDP = (1 + 1.2%) / (1 + 2.5%)  1 = 1.3%\n    The growth rate of per capita nominal GDP is negative, meaning that the per capita nominal GDP\n    decreased.",
