      "questionTextEng": "Price level\n\n                                                                  AD0\n                                                           AD1\n                                                                        Aggregate output\n                                    0\n\n      Which of the following are possible reasons for the above movement of the aggregate demand curve?\n\n       (1)   A major trading partner suffers an economic recession.\n       (2)   The government raises the salaries tax rate.\n       (3)   Firms expect the general price level to increase.\n       (4)   The government increases tax incentives for firms.\n\n             A.    (1) and (2) only\n             B.    (3) and (4) only\n             C.    (1), (2) and (3) only\n             D.    (2), (3) and (4) only",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    (1) is correct. When a major trading partner suffers an economic recession, the demand for domestic\n    exports will decrease, and net exports will thus decrease. Aggregate demand will decrease and the\n    aggregate demand curve will shift to the left.\n    (2) is correct. The government raising the salaries tax rate will reduce people’s disposable income and\n    private consumption expenditure will decrease. Aggregate demand will decrease and the aggregate\n    demand curve will shift to the left.\n    (3) is incorrect. When firms expect the general price level to increase, they will reduce their present\n    supply. Short run aggregate supply will decrease while aggregate demand will not change.\n    (4) is incorrect. When the government increases tax incentives for firms, investment expenditure will\n    increase. Aggregate demand will increase and the aggregate demand curve will shift to the right.",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/29/ae-p1-27.jpg",
