      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following will cause the unemployment rate in Hong Kong to increase?\n\n           A.    The government reduces the assistance to the unemployed.\n           B.    Some new graduates who studied abroad are recruited by Hong Kong companies and return to Hong\n                 Kong to work, and do not replace any domestic workers.\n           C.    Multinational enterprises invest in Hong Kong.\n           D.    The government raises the statutory minimum wage.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    The increase in the statutory minimum wage will lead to an increase in labour costs, so some employers\n     may lay off their employees, leading to an increase in the unemployed population. The unemployment\n     rate will increase.\n     Option A is incorrect. When the government reduces the assistance to the unemployed, more people\n     may look for jobs more actively for financial reasons. The unemployed population will decrease, and\n     the unemployment rate will thus decrease.\n     Option B is incorrect. The new graduates returning to Hong Kong to work will increase the labour force\n     while the unemployed population remains unchanged, so the unemployment rate will decrease.\n     Option C is incorrect. The investments of multinational enterprises in Hong Kong can create\n     employment opportunities, and the unemployed population will decrease. The unemployment rate will\n     thus decrease.",
