      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following would offset the effect of lowering the required reserve ratio on aggregate output?\n\n            A.    a reduction in government transfer payments\n            B.    an open market purchase of government bonds\n            C.    a decrease in the asset demand for money\n            D.    an increase in production subsidies",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    When the required reserve ratio is lowered, the money supply will increase and the interest rate will\n    decrease. Consumption and investment will increase. Aggregate demand will increase. Aggregate output\n    will increase.\n    Option A is correct. The reduction in government transfer payments will reduce private consumption\n    expenditure. Aggregate demand will decrease, which can offset the effect of lowering the required\n    reserve ratio on aggregate output.\n    Option B is incorrect. An open market purchase of government bonds will lead to an increase in the\n    money supply and a decrease in the interest rate. Consumption and investment will increase. Aggregate\n    demand will increase. Aggregate output will increase.\n    Option C is incorrect. A decrease in the asset demand for money will lead to a decrease in the interest\n    rate. Consumption and investment will increase. Aggregate demand will increase. Aggregate output will\n    increase.\n    Option D is incorrect. An increase in production subsidies will lead to an increase in short run aggregate\n    supply. Aggregate output will increase.",
