      "questionTextEng": "The diagram below shows the imposition of a quota on an imported good in a small open economy.\n\n                           Price ($)\n\n                                                                S0\n\n                                                                     Sq\n\n                           30\n                           20                                         World price\n\n                                                                          D\n                                                                              Quantity (units)\n                           0           30    45          75   90\n\n      If the world price of the good increases to $30,\n\n       (1) the domestic consumption of the good will decrease by 15 units.\n       (2) the revenue of domestic producers of the good will increase by $750.\n       (3) the total import value of the good will be $900.\n\n            A.    (3) only\n            B.    (1) and (2) only\n            C.    (2) and (3) only\n            D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    After the world price increases, total import value = (75 units – 45 units) × $30 = $900.\n    (1) is incorrect. The domestic consumption of the good will remain unchanged at 75 units.\n    (2) is incorrect. The domestic price of the good will remain unchanged at $30 while the domestic\n    production of the good will remain unchanged at 45 units. The revenue of domestic producers of the\n    good will thus remain unchanged.",
