      "questionTextEng": "In order to improve its huge fiscal deficit, a country decides to impose a per-unit tax on all packages of rice\n                                                           (regardless of the package size). Suppose people’s demand for packaged rice is inelastic.\n\n                                                          (a)    (i)   Explain whether the above tax is a direct tax or an indirect tax.                          (2 marks)\n\n                                                                 (ii) Explain whether the imposition of the above tax follows the tax principle of ‘equity’ put forward\n                                                                      by Adam Smith.                                                                           (2 marks)\n\n                                                          (b) With the aid of a diagram, explain how the above tax would affect people’s total expenditure on\n                                                              packaged rice.                                                                        (6 marks)\n\n                                                          (c)   Using the law of demand, explain why the average weight of packages of rice purchased by people\n                                                                would increase after the imposition of the per-unit tax.                               (5 marks)",
