      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/29/a-p2-09.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The government announced that the Normal Old Age Living Allowance (Normal OALA) and Higher Old\n                                                           Age Living Allowance (Higher OALA) will be merged in September 2022. The merged OALA will adopt\n                                                           the more relaxed asset limits of the Normal OALA and the payment rate of the Higher OALA. Elderly\n                                                           persons who are currently receiving Normal OALA will switch to Higher OALA and will receive an\n                                                           additional amount of about $1,000 per month.\n\n                                                          (a)   Explain whether the amount of the Old Age Living Allowance paid by the government will be included\n                                                                in the calculation of Hong Kong’s gross domestic product (GDP).                          (2 marks)\n\n                                                          (b) Discuss the effect of the above measure on Hong Kong’s income inequality.                       (2 marks)\n\n                                                          (c)   Suppose there is a deflationary (output) gap in Hong Kong’s economy. With the aid of an AD-AS\n                                                                diagram, explain how the above measure will affect the deflationary (output) gap in the short run.\n                                                                                                                                                               (7 marks)",
