      "inlineDiagrams": "diagrams/MT29-P2-12.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Refer to Figure 2. PPFA and PPFB are the production possibility frontiers of Country A and Country B\n                                                             respectively. Both countries have the same amount of resources. P B is the production point of Country B\n                                                             before trade. The slope of the dotted line is the world price of clothing.\n\n                                                                                                             Figure 2\n\n                                                                                       Food\n\n                                                                                                       PB\n\n                                                                                                        PPFA            PPFB\n\n                                                                                        0                                               Clothing\n\n                                                           (a)   Which country has an absolute advantage in producing clothing? Explain.                         (2 marks)\n\n                                                           (b) Explain which country has a comparative advantage in producing clothing.                          (2 marks)\n\n                                                           (c)   Suppose both countries engage in complete specialisation according to their comparative advantages and\n                                                                 trade. In Figure 2,\n\n                                                                 (i)   indicate the production points of Country A and Country B after trade as PTA and PTB respectively.\n                                                                                                                                                                 (2 marks)\n\n                                                                 (ii) indicate the consumption possibility frontier (CPFB) of Country B after trade.             (2 marks)\n\n                                                           (d) Suppose Country B consumes the same amount of food before and after trade. In Figure 2, indicate the\n                                                               consumption point (CTB), export volume and import volume of Country B after trade.        (3 marks)\n\n                                                           (e)   The following table shows some data of Country A and Country B.\n\n                                                                                                                          Country A            Country B\n                                                                       Per capita GDP                                     $50 billion          $60 billion\n                                                                       Life expectancy at birth                            75 years             80 years\n                                                                       Number of schools per 1,000,000 population            150                  100\n\n                                                                 (i)   Based on the above information, which country do you think will have a higher Human\n                                                                       Development Index (HDI)? Explain.                                           (2 marks)\n\n                                                                 (ii) Give ONE possible reason to explain why HDI will increase after a country opens up to trade.\n                                                                                                                                                               (1 mark)\n\n                                                                 (iii) Most citizens of Country B think that their living standard is lower than that of Country A. Give\n                                                                       ONE possible reason to explain their view.                                              (2 marks)",
