      "questionTextEng": "Miss Tang spent $8,000 on buying a computer two years ago. Suppose she can resell it for $2,000. Alternatively,\n     she needs to spend $3,000 on upgrading the computer hardware before she can continue to use it. What is her cost\n     of continuing to use the computer?\n\n           A.    $2,000\n           B.    $3,000\n           C.    $5,000\n           D.    $10,000",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n     The opportunity cost of continuing to use the computer is the value of the highest-valued option forgone,\n     i.e. the value of reselling the computer ($2,000). The repairing cost of $3,000 is the monetary cost of\n     continuing to use the computer. The cost of continuing to use the computer = $2,000 + $3,000 = $5,000.",
