      "questionTextEng": "Karson is a secondary school student. He is considering which extracurricular activity to join. He has several\n     options and his order of preference is as follows.\n\n      First option: Joining the choir\n      Second option: Joining the astronomical society\n      Third option: Joining the soccer team\n\n     Which of the following factors would be LEAST likely to affect the cost-benefit analysis for Karson’s choice?\n\n           A.    The choir changes their practice venue to somewhere farther away from Karson’s home.\n           B.    The astronomical society purchases a more advanced telescope for stargazing.\n           C.    The soccer team invites a famous football player for demonstrations and coaching.\n           D.    Karson’s best friend quits the soccer team.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n     Karson would choose the first option as the benefit of choosing the first option (the value of the first\n     option) is higher than the cost (the value of the second option).\n     Option D is correct. This would reduce the value of the third option. This would not affect Karson’s cost\n     or benefit of choosing the first option.\n     Option A is incorrect. This would reduce the value of the first option, thus reducing Karson’s benefit of\n     choosing the first option.\n     Option B is incorrect. This would raise the value of the second option, thus raising Karson’s cost of\n     choosing the first option.\n     Option C is incorrect. This may increase the value of the third option to a level higher than that of the\n     second option, so the cost of choosing the first option may change from the value of the second option\n     to that of the third option.",
