      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/30/a-p1-03.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "An electrical appliance retail chain provides free delivery service for any purchase of or above a specified amount.\n     The delivery service is __________________ because ___________________.\n\n           A.    an economic good ... the marginal cost of providing the delivery service is positive\n           B.    an economic good ... the delivery service can satisfy customers’ wants\n           C.    a free good ... the delivery service is free of charge\n           D.    a free good ... more is not preferred",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n     Provision of the delivery service involves the use of scarce resources, such as drivers, trucks and\n     gasoline, which have alternative uses. The marginal cost of providing the delivery service is positive.\n     The delivery service is thus an economic good.\n     Option B is incorrect. Both free goods and economic goods can satisfy human wants.\n     Option C is incorrect. Goods that are free of charge are not necessarily free goods. Economic goods can\n     be provided to consumers free of charge.\n     Option D is incorrect. More of the free delivery service is preferred.",
