      "questionTextEng": "Cyrus plans to set up a retail firm selling sports equipment in Hong Kong. He is considering setting up a sole\n          proprietorship or a private limited company. Which of the following is a possible reason for him to choose to set\n          up a sole proprietorship?\n\n                A.    A sole proprietorship has wider sources of capital compared to a private limited company.\n                B.    A sole proprietorship is subject to a lower profits tax rate compared to a private limited company.\n                C.    A sole proprietorship does not need to disclose its accounting information to the public while a private\n                      limited company needs to do so.\n                D.    A sole proprietorship is not a legal entity while a private limited company is a legal entity.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n     Option A is incorrect. A private limited company can issue shares and bonds to raise capital while a sole\n     proprietorship cannot, so a sole proprietorship does not have a wider source of capital than a private\n     limited company.\n     Option C is incorrect. A private limited company is not required to disclose its accounting information\n     to the public either.\n     Option D is incorrect. A sole proprietorship is not a legal entity, implying that Cyrus bears unlimited\n     liability and he may have to use personal property to settle the firm’s outstanding debts. This would not\n     be a reason for Cyrus’s setting up a sole proprietorship.",
