      "questionTextEng": "Study the following information about firm A and firm B.\n\n                                                          Firm A                          Firm B\n                      Number of owners                      20                              100\n                      Continuity                If an owner goes bankrupt,     If an owner goes bankrupt,\n                                               the firm has to be dissolved.      the firm can still exist.\n\n           Based on the above table, which of the following descriptions of firm A and firm B is CORRECT?\n\n                A.    Firm B cannot keep its accounting information confidential while firm A can.\n                B.    Owners of both firm A and firm B enjoy limited liability.\n                C.    Firm A has a higher risk of being taken over by others than firm B.\n                D.    Firm B earns a higher profit than firm A.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n     As the number of owners of firm A is more than one and it lacks lasting continuity, firm A is a\n     partnership. As firm B has more than 50 owners and there is lasting continuity, firm B is a public limited\n     company.\n     Option A is correct. Firm B (a public limited company) must disclose its accounting information to the\n     public regularly while firm A (a partnership) need not do so.\n     Option B is incorrect. Firm A (a partnership) is not a legal entity and its owners bear unlimited liability.\n     Firm B (a public limited company) is a legal entity and its owners enjoy limited liability.\n     Option C is incorrect. The shares of firm B (a public limited company) can be transferred without the\n     consent of other shareholders while the ownership of firm A (a partnership) can only be transferred with\n     the consent of all partners, so firm B has a higher risk of being taken over.\n     Option D is incorrect. Public limited companies are not necessarily more profitable than partnerships.",
