      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/30/q-p1-10.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/30/a-p1-10.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Refer to the following news article.\n\n        In order to attract more overseas talent to work in Hong Kong, the government launches the Top\n        Talent Pass Scheme (高端人才通行證計劃). Eligible people such as those with annual income\n        reaching HK$2.5 million or above in the year immediately preceding the date of application, or\n        graduates of designated universities, are allowed to stay in Hong Kong for 24 months.\n\n      Which of the following would likely occur after the implementation of the above scheme?\n\n            (1)   Hong Kong’s labour productivity will increase.\n            (2)   The geographical mobility of graduates from designated universities will increase.\n            (3)   The occupational mobility of Hong Kong workers will increase.\n\n            A.    (1) and (2) only\n            B.    (1) and (3) only\n            C.    (2) and (3) only\n            D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    (1) is correct. Talents are well-educated and experienced. Attracting more talents to work in Hong Kong\n    will increase the average labour productivity of Hong Kong.\n    (2) is correct. The scheme raises the ability of graduates from designated universities to move to work in\n    Hong Kong from other places, their geographical mobility will increase.\n    (3) is incorrect. The scheme does not affect the ability or willingness of Hong Kong workers to change\n    from one occupation to another.",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/30/ae-p1-10.jpg",
      "originalQuestionImageEng": "originals/30/qe-p1-10.jpg",
