      "questionTextEng": "The table below shows the cost-output relationship of a price-taking firm.\n\n                    Output (units)                       2             3           4              5\n                    Average variable cost ($)            3             4           5              6\n\n      Suppose the profit-maximising output level is 4 units and the average fixed cost at 4 units is $2. The profit and the\n      producer surplus of the firm are ______ and ______ respectively.\n\n            A.    $2 … $10\n            B.    $2 … $12\n            C.    $4 … $10\n            D.    $4 … $12",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n     Output (units)                      2              3              4              5\n     Average variable cost ($)           3              4              5              6\n     Total variable cost ($)             6             12              20             30\n     Marginal cost ($)                   -              6              8              10\n     Total fixed cost ($)                8              8              8              8\n     Total cost ($)                      14            20              28             38\n    At the profit-maximising output level (4 units), the marginal revenue equals the marginal cost (= $8).\n    Profit = Total revenue – Total cost = ($8 × 4) – $28 = $4\n    Producer surplus = Total revenue – Total variable cost = ($8 × 4) – $20 = $12",
