      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/30/a-p1-14.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Mr. Cheung runs a leather product store selling homemade leather products. Which of the following will reduce\n      its profit-maximising output?\n\n            A.    The cost of importing leather increases.\n            B.    The rental of the store increases.\n            C.    Leather products become more popular.\n            D.    The wage rate of part-time workers decreases.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    When the cost of importing leather increases, the marginal cost of producing leather products will\n    increase and the profit-maximising output will decrease.\n    Option B is incorrect. When the rental of the store increases, the fixed cost of producing leather\n    products will increase and the profit-maximising output will not be affected.\n    Option C is incorrect. When leather products become more popular, demand for leather products and the\n    market price will increase. The profit-maximising output will increase.\n    Option D is incorrect. When the wage rate of part-time workers decreases, the marginal cost of\n    producing leather products will decrease, and the profit-maximising output will increase.",
