      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    (1) is correct. As the price of white-plate sushi increases, its quantity demanded will decrease.\n    (2) is correct. After the price of all dishes is increased by $2, the relative price of white-plate sushi (in\n    terms of black-plate sushi) will increase. According to the law of demand, people will consume less\n    white-plate sushi relative to black-plate sushi. The ratio of white-plate sushi sold to black-plate sushi\n    sold will thus decrease.\n    (3) is incorrect. The change in total revenue of the restaurant will be uncertain, depending on the price\n    elasticity of demand for sushi.",
