      "questionTextEng": "Refer to the following news article.\n\n                  During the peak season of influenza, the average waiting time for the services of\n                  accident and emergency departments increases. The government urges citizens with\n                  mild illnesses to seek medical treatment at private hospitals or clinics.\n\n      As a result, the price of private medical services has changed by 5% and the quantity transacted has changed by\n      10%. Which of the following statements is CORRECT?\n\n            A.    The demand for private medical services is elastic.\n            B.    The demand for private medical services is inelastic.\n            C.    The supply of private medical services is elastic.\n            D.    The supply of private medical services is inelastic.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    Demand for private medical services increases. Given an upward-sloping supply curve, both the\n    equilibrium price and quantity will increase. The supply is elastic because the percentage change in\n    quantity supplied (10%) is greater than the percentage change in price (5%).",
