      "calculationType": "-",
      "source": "模擬試卷三十 卷一",
      "reviewedByAI": "Y",
      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/30/q-p1-22.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/30/a-p1-22.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Refer to the following supply and demand schedules for good X.\n\n                   Unit price ($)                   6          8          10        12       14\n                   Quantity demanded (units)        28         24         20        16       12\n                   Quantity supplied (units)        20         20         20        20       20\n\n      If the government imposes a price ceiling on good X at $6,\n\n           A.    the quantity transacted will increase by 8 units.\n           B.    consumers’ total expenditure will decrease by $80.\n           C.    there will be a surplus of 8 units of good X in the market.\n           D.    the demand for good X’s complements will decrease.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    Before the imposition of the price ceiling, the price of good X is $10 and the quantity transacted is 20\n    units.\n    After the imposition of the price ceiling, the price of good X is $6 and the quantity transacted is 20\n    units.\n    Option B is correct. The original total expenditure is $200 = (20 units × $10) and the new total\n    expenditure is $120 (= 20 units × $6), so the total expenditure decreases by $80.\n    Option A is incorrect. The quantity transacted will remain at 20 units.\n    Option C is incorrect. When the price is $6, the quantity demanded (28 units) will be greater than the\n    quantity supplied (20 units). There will be a shortage of good X.\n\n    Option D is incorrect. When the price of good X decreases, the demand for its complements will\n    increase.",
