      "questionTextEng": "The following diagram shows the demand and supply curves of good X.\n\n                                       Price\n                                                                   S1\n\n                                                                        S0\n\n                                             V\n                                              W      X\n                                             Y\n                                               Z\n\n                                                                        D\n                                       0                                                 Quantity\n\n      The production cost of good X increases and the supply curve of good X shifts from S0 to S1. The change in\n      consumer surplus equals ___________ and the change in total social surplus equals ___________.\n\n           A.    area (W + X) … area (X + Z)\n           B.    area (W + X) … area (V + W + Y)\n           C.    area (V + W + X) … area (X + Z)\n           D.    area (V + W + X) … area (V + W + Y)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    The original consumer surplus is equal to area (V + W + X) and the new consumer surplus is equal to\n    area V. The consumer surplus is reduced by area (W + X).\n    The original total social surplus is equal to area (V + W + X + Y + Z) and the new total social surplus is\n    equal to area (V + W + Y). The total social surplus is reduced by area (X + Z).",
