      "questionTextEng": "A country imposes a per-unit tax on good X. When the demand for good X increases, which of the following\n      statements are CORRECT?\n\n           (1)   The producer surplus will increase.\n           (2)   Total tax revenue will increase.\n           (3)   The gap between marginal benefit and marginal cost will be widened.\n\n           A.    (1) and (2) only\n           B.    (1) and (3) only\n           C.    (2) and (3) only\n           D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    (1) is correct. After the increase in demand, the price and quantity transacted of good X will increase\n    while the marginal cost of good X will remain unchanged, so the producer surplus will increase.\n    (2) is correct. After the increase in demand, the quantity transacted of good X will increase, while the\n    per-unit tax will remain unchanged, so the total tax revenue will increase.\n\n    (3) is incorrect. When the government imposes a per-unit tax on good X, the difference between\n    marginal benefit and marginal cost is equal to the amount of the per-unit tax. After the increase in\n    demand, the per-unit tax remains unchanged, so the gap between marginal benefit and marginal cost will\n    also remain unchanged.\n\n                      Unit price\n                                                  S1 = S0 + t\n                                                      S0\n                     MB2\n\n                     MB1\n                     MC2\n\n                     MC1\n\n                                                     D0         D1\n                                                                         Quantity\n                        0          Q1 Q0 Q2",
