      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/30/a-p1-28.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The government issues a penalty ticket to a restaurant for poor sanitation, which\n                   has caused a rodent infestation (鼠患) that seriously affects residents living\n                   nearby. If the poor sanitary conditions continue, the restaurant will face a higher\n                   penalty.\n\n      With reference to the above information, which of the following statements is CORRECT?\n\n           A.    The restaurant should give compensation to residents living nearby.\n           B.    After the restaurant is fined, efficiency will be restored.\n           C.    Fining the restaurant is the only way to improve efficiency.\n           D.    Fining the restaurant increases the marginal private cost of the restaurant and improves efficiency.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    Fining the restaurant will increase the restaurant’s marginal private cost so that the external cost can be\n    internalised. The gap between marginal social cost and marginal social benefit will be narrowed and\n    efficiency will improve.\n    Option A is incorrect. Which solution should be adopted depends on many factors, such as the cost of\n    the solution. There is not enough information to determine which solution should be adopted.\n    Option B is incorrect. Fining the restaurant may improve efficiency, but efficiency may not be restored.\n    If the fine cannot accurately reflect the external cost, social optimality will not be reached.\n    Option C is incorrect. Other than fining the restaurant, there are other market solutions. For example, the\n    residents living nearby can pay the restaurant to improve its sanitation.",
