      "questionTextEng": "The following diagram shows the Gini coefficient of Country A.\n\n                   0.5\n                   0.4\n                   0.3\n                   0.2\n                   0.1\n                     0\n                      1981     1986    1991    1996     2001      2006   2011    2016    2021\n\n                              Gini coefficient based on original monthly household income\n                              Gini coefficient based on post-tax monthly household income\n\n      From the diagram above, we can conclude that\n\n           A.    income for high-income households increased while income for low-income households decreased\n                 between 1981 and 2006.\n           B.    the government cut the amount of transfer payments to the poor between 2016 and 2021.\n           C.    Country A’s tax system was likely to be progressive between 1981 and 2021.\n           D.    High-income households paid the least amount of tax.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    Country A’s Gini coefficient based on original monthly household income has always been higher than\n    the Gini coefficient based on post-tax monthly household income, reflecting that its tax system can help\n    improve income inequality. A progressive tax system can help improve income inequality.\n    Option A is incorrect. The diagram does not reflect the income of households.\n    Option B is incorrect. The Gini coefficient based on post-tax monthly household income does not reflect\n    the effect of transfer payments on income distribution.\n    Option D is incorrect. The difference between the Gini coefficient based on original monthly household\n    income and the Gini coefficient based on post-tax monthly household income does not reflect the\n    amount of tax payment.",
