      "inlineDiagrams": "diagrams/MT30-P2-09-1.jpg,diagrams/MT30-P2-09-2.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The price of Australian natural gas has soared since 2021.\n\n                                                           Source A: Main uses of natural gas produced in Australia\n\n                                                                                                          Electricity\n                                                                                                          generation\n\n                                                                                      Used by\n\n                                                                                    homes and                                  Exported to\n                                                                                                            Natural\n                                                                                     businesses                                   other\n                                                                                    for cooking              gas                countries\n                                                                                    and heating\n\n                                                                                                          Used in the\n                                                                                                          production\n                                                                                                          of industrial\n                                                                                                           products\n\n                                                           Source B: Wholesale prices for natural gas in two different parts of Australia\n\n                                                                               30\n                                                                               25\n                                                             $ per gigajoule\n\n                                                                               20\n                                                                               15\n                                                                               10                                                                        Victoria\n                                                                                5                                                                        Brisbane\n                                                                                0\n\n                                                                                                         Year\n\n                                                           2022/23 data is current as of January 2023.\n                                                           (Source: Australian Energy Regulator)\n\n                                                           Source C: A news excerpt about methods of electricity generation in Australia\n                                                            Australia generates electricity from both non-renewable energy sources (e.g. fossil fuels such\n                                                            as natural gas, petroleum and coal) and renewable energy sources (e.g. hydroelectricity, wind\n                                                            power and solar energy). To produce an equal amount of energy, burning natural gas for energy\n                                                            results in lower carbon emissions than burning petroleum and coal.\n                                                           (Source: various newspapers)\n\n                                                           Source D: Some views on the Australian natural gas market\n                                                                                             I am in favor of the government capping the domestic\n                                                                                             wholesale price of natural gas at $12 per gigajoule, as this can\n                                                                                             ensure Australians can get natural gas at a reasonable price.\n\n                                                                   An Australian\n                                                                 government official\n                                                                                             To ensure domestic buyers have enough natural gas, the\n                                                                                             Australian government should limit the amount of natural gas\n\n                                                                                             exported.\n\n                                                                A news commentator\n                                                                                             If the export of natural gas is restricted, I will sell natural gas\n                                                                                             to various domestic buyers.\n\n                                                             The owner of an Australian\n                                                              natural gas manufacturer\n\n                                                        (a) Refer to Source A. Illustrate, with ONE example, under what condition natural gas produced in Australia\n                                                            would be considered a producer good.                                                          (1 mark)\n\n                                                        (b) Refer to Source B. Suggest TWO possible reasons to explain why there is a difference in the wholesale\n                                                            price of natural gas in different parts of Australia.                                       (4 marks)\n\n                                                        (c) Refer to Sources A and B. With the aid of a diagram, explain how the change in the price of natural gas in\n                                                            2021/22 would affect the producer surplus of industrial product manufacturers.                   (5 marks)\n                                                            (For simplicity, assume the supply and demand curves of natural gas shift in a parallel manner.)\n\n                                                        For part (d), candidates are required to present their answer in essay form. Criteria for marking will include the\n                                                        use of sources and economic theories, relevant content, logical presentation and clarity of expression.\n\n                                                        (d) With reference to the above sources and your own knowledge in Economics, compare the effects of\n                                                            imposing a price ceiling on Australian natural gas and imposing quantity restrictions on Australian natural\n                                                            gas exported on the following:\n                                                           - exporters of Australian natural gas\n                                                           - domestic buyers of Australian natural gas\n                                                           - carbon emissions in Australia\n                                                                                                                                                            (12 marks)",
