      "questionTextEng": "Mr. Cheung is considering renting out his residential unit in a private housing estate. Which of the following\n          would increase the cost of renting out the unit?\n\n                A.    The management fee borne by Mr. Cheung increases.\n                B.    The average rent of residential units in the same housing estate increases.\n                C.    The government raises the property tax rate.\n                D.    The market price of residential units decreases.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n     When the government raises the property tax rate, Mr. Cheung needs to pay more tax for renting out his\n     property in Hong Kong and the money cost of renting out the unit increases.\n     Option A is incorrect. Mr. Cheung has to pay the management fee whether he rents out the unit or not.\n     An increase in the management fee would not affect the cost of renting out the unit.\n     Option B is incorrect. An increase in the average rent of residential units in the same housing estate\n     increases the value of renting out the unit but has no effect on the cost of renting out the unit.\n     Option D is incorrect. If Mr. Cheung does not rent out the residential unit, he may be able to sell it. The\n     cost of renting out the unit is the market price of selling the unit. A decrease in the market price of\n     residential units will lower the cost of renting out the unit.",
