      "questionTextEng": "Suppose Kevin lent a new smartphone to his brother. His brother promised to return the smartphone along with a\n          smartphone case to Kevin one month later. The smartphone case can be regarded as\n\n                (1)   a free good to Kevin.\n                (2)   the cost of using the smartphone to Kevin’s brother.\n                (3)   interest to Kevin.\n                (4)   interest to Kevin’s brother.\n\n                A.    (1) and (2) only\n                B.    (3) and (4) only\n                C.    (1), (2) and (3) only\n                D.    (2), (3) and (4) only",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n     To Kevin’s brother, the smartphone case is the cost of earlier availability of the smartphone. To Kevin,\n     the smartphone case is his compensation for deferring current consumption. The smartphone case is\n     interest to both of them.\n     (1) is incorrect. The smartphone case is an economic good because its provision involves the use of\n     scarce resources which have alternative uses.",
