      "questionTextEng": "Miss Lee runs a self-service bakery store. Customers can make cakes in the store and can use the ingredients and\n           baking equipment provided by the store.\n\n           Miss Lee has the right to ____________ while customers of the store have the right to ___________.\n\n                A.    sell the ingredients for income ... take away the ingredients to make cakes at home later\n                B.    use the baking equipment to make cakes of different flavours ... sell the ingredients for income\n                C.    transfer the store for income ... lease the baking equipment to others for income\n                D.    hold a baking class in the store for income ... use the baking equipment in the store to make cakes for\n                      their friends",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n     Miss Lee has the exclusive right to use, the exclusive right to receive income from, and the right to\n     transfer the ingredients and the baking equipment in the store. She has the right to hold a baking class in\n     the store for income.\n     Options A, B and C are incorrect. Customers of the self-service bakery store do not have the exclusive\n     right to receive income from and the right to transfer the ingredients and the baking equipment in the\n     store. They cannot take away, sell or lease out the ingredients and the baking equipment in the store for\n     income.",
