      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/31/q-p1-04.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/31/a-p1-04.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The following table shows information about two firms in Hong Kong.\n\n                                                     Firm A                       Firm B\n                          Number of\n                                                       30                           30\n                           owners\n                                             If one of the owners       If one of the owners goes\n                          Continuity        goes bankrupt, the firm     bankrupt, the firm has to\n                                               continues to exist              be dissolved\n                        Disclosure of\n                                             Required to disclose to     Not required to disclose\n                         accounting\n                                                   the public                 to the public\n                        information\n\n     Based on the above information, which of the following statements about the above firms is CORRECT?\n\n           A.    Neither firm can issue shares or bonds to the public.\n           B.    Both firms pay the same profits tax rate.\n           C.    Firm A requires the consent of other shareholders to transfer ownership, while firm B does not.\n           D.    Firm A has an independent legal status while firm B does not.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n     Firm A is a public limited company as it is required to disclose its accounting information to the public.\n     Firm B is a partnership as there is more than one owner and there is a lack of continuity. Firm A is a\n     legal entity and has independent legal status, while firm B is not a legal entity and has no independent\n     legal status.\n     Option A is incorrect. Firm A (public limited company) can issue shares and bonds to the public.\n     Option B is incorrect. Firm A (public limited company) pays a higher profits tax rate than firm B\n     (partnership).\n     Option C is incorrect. The ownership of firm A (public limited company) can be freely transferred\n     without the consent of other shareholders, while a transfer of ownership of firm B (partnership) requires\n     the consent of other shareholders.",
