      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/31/q-p1-05.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/31/a-p1-05.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The fan club of a popular singer launched a free ice cream giveaway. Ice cream trucks displaying the portrait of\n     the idol will distribute free ice cream to people at designated time slots and locations. The ice cream will be\n     distributed on a first-come-first-served basis, while stocks last.\n\n     This free ice cream is __________ because ___________.\n\n           A.    a free good … the public do not need to pay for it\n           B.    an economic good … it can be used to produce other goods and services\n           C.    a private good … it is rival in consumption\n           D.    a public good … it is non-excludable in consumption",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n     The consumption of ice cream reduces the amount available to others. The ice cream is rival in\n     consumption and therefore is a private good instead of a public good.\n     Option A is incorrect. Since the quantity available is not sufficient to satisfy all human wants and people\n     prefer more of the ice cream, it is an economic good instead of a free good.\n     Option B is incorrect. The fact that ice cream can be used to produce other goods and services does not\n     explain why it is an economic good.",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/31/ae-p1-05.jpg",
