      "questionTextEng": "The table below shows the input-output relationship of a firm.\n\n           Machinery (units)               5           5                5             5             5\n           Labour (units)                  1           2                3             4             5\n           Total product (units)           20          60              114           156            X\n\n     Diminishing marginal returns sets in when the 4th unit of labour is employed. The average product of 5 units of\n     labour may be ________ units.\n\n           A.    39\n           B.    40\n           C.    41\n           D.    42",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n         Machinery (units)                  5             5          5              5            5\n         Labour (units)                     1             2          3              4            5\n         Total product (units)            20             60         114           156        X < 198\n         Marginal product (units)         20             40         54             42          < 42\n     As diminishing marginal returns sets in when the 4th unit of labour is employed, the marginal product of\n     the 5th unit of labour would be smaller than 42, and the value of X would be smaller than 198. The\n    average product of 5 units of labour would be smaller than 39.6 (= 198 / 5).",
