      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/31/q-p1-13.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/31/a-p1-13.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following would most likely lead to a reduction in the supply of hotel services in Hong Kong?\n\n              A.       The Hong Kong government distributes free air tickets for flights to Hong Kong to foreign tourists.\n              B.       More applications for converting hotels into residential premises are approved.\n              C.       The government provides more subsidies for training programmes in the hotel industry.\n              D.       The average price of hotel services decreases.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    More applications for converting hotels into residential premises being approved will reduce the\n    quantity supplied of hotel services at every given price. The supply of hotel services will decrease.\n    Option A is incorrect. Distributing free air tickets for flights to Hong Kong to foreign tourists will\n    increase the demand for Hong Kong’s hotel services.\n    Option C is incorrect. Providing more subsidies for training programmes in the hotel industry may cause\n    more people to join the hotel industry, so the supply of labour in the hotel industry may increase. The\n    cost of production may decrease and the supply may increase.\n    Option D is incorrect. A decrease in the average price of hotel services will lead to a decrease in the\n    quantity supplied of hotel services rather than a decrease in supply.",
