      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/31/a-p1-14.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "A country imports red wine, which includes high-quality red wine and low-quality red wine. Which of the\n      following will cause consumers’ expenditure on imported low-quality red wine to decrease?\n\n              A.       The transportation cost that consumers pay for each bottle of wine imported decreases.\n              B.       A ship carrying a large quantity of high-quality red wine sinks.\n              C.       A ship carrying a large quantity of low-quality red wine sinks.\n              D.       Low-quality red wine is an inferior good and people’s income generally increases.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    When people’s income generally increases and low-quality red wine is an inferior good, people’s\n    demand for imported low-quality red wine will decrease. Consumers’ expenditure on imported\n    low-quality red wine will decrease.\n    Option A is incorrect. When the transportation cost for each bottle of wine imported decreases, the price\n    of imported low-quality red wine will decrease and the quantity demanded will increase. The change in\n    consumers’ expenditure on imported low-quality red wine will be uncertain, depending on the price\n    elasticity of demand for imported low-quality red wine.\n    Option B is incorrect. When a ship carrying a large quantity of high-quality red wine sinks, the supply\n    of imported high-quality red wine will decrease and the price will increase. As imported high-quality red\n    wine and imported low-quality red wine are substitutes, demand for imported low-quality red wine will\n    increase. Consumers’ expenditure on imported low-quality red wine will increase.\n    Option C is incorrect. When a ship carrying a large quantity of low-quality red wine sinks, the supply of\n    imported low-quality red wine will decrease. The price will increase and the quantity transacted will\n    decrease. The change in consumers’ expenditure on imported low-quality red wine will be uncertain,\n    depending on the price elasticity of demand for imported low-quality red wine.",
