      "inlineDiagrams": "diagrams/MT31-P1-17.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Refer to the following demand-supply diagram for good X.\n\n                           Unit price\n                                          S1           S2\n\n                              P3\n\n                              P2\n\n                              P1\n\n                                                              D\n\n                               0                                         Quantity\n                                          Q1    Q2     Q3\n\n      If the government increases the quota limit from Q1 to Q3,\n\n           (1)   the market price of good X will increase to P 3.\n           (2)   consumers’ total expenditure on good X will be (P 2 × Q2).\n           (3)   there will be an excess supply of good X.\n\n           A.    (1) only\n           B.    (2) only\n           C.    (1) and (3) only\n           D.    (2) and (3) only",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    The quota changes from effective to ineffective.\n    When the quota is Q1, the quantity transacted is Q1 and the market price is P3.\n    When the quota is Q3, the quantity transacted is Q2 and the market price is P2. Consumers’ total\n    expenditure on good X will be (P2 × Q2).\n    (3) is incorrect. When the quota is Q3, the quantity transacted is Q2 and the market price is P2. There is\n    no excess supply of good X as the quantity demanded is equal to the quantity supplied.",
