      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/31/a-p1-20.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The following table shows the marginal benefit schedule of a coffee consumer.\n\n                                      Quantity (units)       Marginal benefit ($)\n                                             1                       20\n                                             2                       19\n                                             3                       18\n                                             4                       17\n                                             5                       16\n                                             6                       15\n\n      If the price of coffee increases from $17 to $18, the consumer surplus will __________.\n\n           A.    increase by $1\n           B.    increase by $3\n           C.    decrease by $1\n           D.    decrease by $3",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    When the price is $17, the quantity demanded is 4 units. Consumer surplus\n    = ($20 − $17) + ($19 − $17) + ($18 − $17) + ($17 − $17) = $6.\n    When the price is $18, the quantity demanded is 3 units. Consumer surplus\n    = ($20 − $18) + ($19 − $18) + ($18 – $18) = $3.\n    Therefore, if the price of coffee increases from $17 to $18, the consumer surplus will decrease by $3.",
