      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/31/q-p1-22.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/31/a-p1-22.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following is NOT an example of the divergence between private and social costs?\n\n           A.    The police block several traffic lanes because of a traffic accident caused by a drunk driver.\n           B.    The fruits and vegetables grown by a house owner attract birds, whose excrement dirties the\n                 neighbour’s garden.\n           C.    An audience member makes loud noises while watching a movie in a cinema.\n           D.    A construction company pays a farmland owner for permission to dump construction waste on the\n                 farmland.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    When the farmland owner reaches an agreement with the construction company, the external cost of\n    dumping construction waste is internalised and the divergence between private and social costs is\n    eliminated.\n    Option A is incorrect. As the drunk driver has a negative impact on other road users (imposes an\n    external cost), but other road users do not receive any compensation, there is a divergence between\n    private and social costs.\n    Option B is incorrect. As the birds have a negative impact on the nearby residents (impose an external\n    cost), but the nearby residents do not receive any compensation, there is a divergence between private\n    and social costs.\n    Option C is incorrect. As the noises made have a negative impact on other audience members (impose\n    an external cost), but other audience members do not receive any compensation, there is a divergence\n    between private and social costs.",
