      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/31/a-p1-24.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The following diagram shows a production chain of farm products in Country A.\n\n           Imported raw                                               Local       $7,000      Overseas\n                                                       $4,000\n             materials        $50       Local farm                  exporters                consumers\n                                         product\n            Local raw                  manufacturers\n                               $200                                               $5,000       Local\n            materials                                  $2,000        Local\n                                                                                             consumers\n                                                                    retailers\n\n      Suppose the above production chain has included a subsidy of $800 that is given to local farm product\n      manufacturers. The contribution of local farm product manufacturers to Country A’s GDP at factor cost is\n      __________.\n\n           A.    $4,950\n           B.    $6,550\n           C.    $12,750\n           D.    $13,550",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    The contribution of local farm product manufacturers to Country A’s GDP at factor cost\n    = $4,000 + $2,000 ‒ $50 ‒ $200 + $800 = $6,550",
