      "questionTextEng": "Billy is a professor from South Korea. He was invited to teach a six-month course at a university in Hong Kong\n      and received a salary of $100,000. He then returned to South Korea. The income from the course was $80,000.\n      Organising the above course would lead to ___________ in Hong Kong’s GDP and ___________ in Hong Kong’s\n      GNI.\n\n            A.     an increase … an increase\n            B.     an increase … a decrease\n            C.     a decrease … an increase\n            D.     a decrease … a decrease",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    The GDP would increase (by $80,000), because the course is the production of a resident producing unit\n    (the university) in the current year and the value of the course would be included in the GDP.\n    The GNI would decrease (by $20,000). Billy worked as a professor in Hong Kong for less than a year\n    and he is not a Hong Kong resident. Therefore, the $100,000 he received would be counted as factor\n    income earned by a non-resident within the economic territory and would be deducted from GDP when\n    calculating GNI. Thus, the change in GNI = change in GDP (+$80,000) + change in net factor income\n    from abroad (‒$100,000).",
