      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/31/a-p1-27.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following measures may lead to an increase in Hong Kong’s aggregate output but at the same time\n      worsen income inequality?\n\n            A.     reducing the standard rate of the salaries tax\n            B.     tightening the eligibility for the Comprehensive Social Security Assistance Scheme\n            C.     increasing the amount of health care vouchers distributed to eligible elderly persons\n            D.     distributing consumption vouchers to all residents",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    Reducing the standard rate of the salaries tax would increase the disposable income of high-income\n    people. Private consumption expenditure would increase. Aggregate demand would increase and\n    aggregate output would increase. On the other hand, as the income of high-income people increases\n    while that of low-income people remains unchanged, the income gap would be widened.\n    Option B is incorrect. Tightening the eligibility for the Comprehensive Social Security Assistance\n    Scheme would decrease the disposable income of low-income people. Private consumption expenditure\n    would decrease. Aggregate demand would decrease and aggregate output would decrease.\n    Option C is incorrect. Increasing the amount of health care vouchers distributed to eligible elderly\n    persons would increase government expenditure. Aggregate demand would increase and aggregate\n    output would increase. However, since most of the eligible elderly are low-income people, increasing\n    the amount of health care vouchers would increase their income and the income gap would be narrowed.\n    Option D is incorrect. Since the same consumption voucher brings a greater increase in the income of\n    low-income people than that of high-income people, the income gap would be narrowed.",
