      "questionTextEng": "Free Lunch at Schools is a regular government assistance programme that provides free lunch at schools for\n      primary students from low-income families. Participating schools are provided with funding for lunches for their\n      eligible students by the Education Bureau. Which of the following statements about the programme is/are\n      CORRECT?\n\n            (1)    The programme will help improve equity.\n            (2)    The programme will lead to an increase in aggregate demand in Hong Kong.\n            (3)    The government spending on the programme will not be included in the calculation of Hong Kong’s\n                   GDP.\n            (4)    The programme will lead to a fiscal deficit.\n\n            A.     (1) only\n            B.     (1) and (2) only\n            C.     (2) and (3) only\n            D.     (2), (3) and (4) only",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    (1) is correct. Since eligible primary students are from low-income families, the programme can\n    increase their income while high-income families are not eligible for the assistance. The income gap\n    between the rich and the poor will be narrowed and equity will be improved.\n    (2) is correct. The programme will cause government expenditure to increase. Aggregate demand will\n    increase.\n    (3) is incorrect. Since the spending of the programme will be used by schools to pay for students’\n    lunches, it reflects the value of these lunches in the current period and should be included in the\n    calculation of Hong Kong’s GDP.\n    (4) is incorrect. Although the programme will increase government expenditure, it will not necessarily\n    lead to a fiscal deficit. Whether there is a fiscal deficit depends on the government’s fiscal balance.",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/31/ae-p1-28.jpg",
      "originalQuestionImageEng": "originals/31/qe-p1-28.jpg",
      "stemPatterns": [
        "(政府計劃) 以下哪(幾)項有關此計劃的陳述是正確的？"
      ]
