      "questionTextEng": "A few universities plan to build additional teaching and research facilities. For example, the Faculty of Medicine\n      of the University of Hong Kong plans to build a new teaching building in Pok Fu Lam. The estimated cost of the\n      project is more than $1 billion and it is expected to be completed in 2028. Which of the following statements\n      about the construction of the new teaching and research facilities are CORRECT?\n\n            (1)   During the construction period, the unemployed population will decrease.\n            (2)   In the short run, aggregate output will increase.\n            (3)   In the long run, the price level will increase.\n\n            A.    (1) and (2) only\n            B.    (1) and (3) only\n            C.    (2) and (3) only\n            D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    (1) is correct. The demand for construction workers can be regarded as a derived demand for the\n    construction projects. Therefore, the construction of the new teaching and research facilities implies that\n    more construction workers will be employed and the unemployed population will decrease.\n    (2) is correct. Investment expenditure will increase and aggregate demand will increase. In the short run,\n    aggregate output will increase.\n    (3) is incorrect. Hong Kong’s productive capacity will increase and the long run aggregate supply will\n    increase. In the long run, the price level will decrease.",
