      "questionTextEng": "Initially an economy operates at the long run equilibrium. Which of the following will result in an inflationary\n      (output) gap?\n\n            A.    The domestic currency depreciates.\n            B.    The government tightens the regulations on disposal of construction waste.\n            C.    The government increases the profits tax rate.\n            D.    The government increases the quota for importing overseas labour.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    When the domestic currency depreciates, the relative prices of exports will decrease and the relative\n    prices of imports will increase, resulting in an increase in exports and a decrease in imports. Net exports\n    will increase and aggregate demand will increase. The output level in the short run will increase to a\n    level higher than the full-employment output level, resulting in an inflationary (output) gap.\n    Option B is incorrect. The government’s tightening of regulations on disposal of construction waste will\n    increase the cost of production, resulting in a decrease in the short run aggregate supply. The output\n    level in the short run will decrease to a level lower than the full-employment output level, resulting in a\n    deflationary (output) gap.\n    Option C is incorrect. The increase in the profits tax rate will lead to a decrease in investment\n    expenditure, and aggregate demand will decrease. The output level in the short run will decrease to a\n    level lower than the full-employment output level, resulting in a deflationary (output) gap.\n    Option D is incorrect. Increasing the quota for importing overseas labour will increase the productive\n    capacity of the economy. Both short run and long run aggregate supply will increase. The output level in\n    the short run will be equal to the full-employment output level.",
