      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following transactions would decrease the money supply M1 of Hong Kong?\n\n           A.    Mr. Cheng withdraws $5,000 from his current account with a licensed bank and holds the amount as\n                 cash.\n           B.    Ms. Chan deposits $5,000 cash into her savings account with a licensed bank.\n           C.    Mr. Chau transfers $5,000 from his time deposit account with a licensed bank to his current account\n                 with the same bank.\n           D.    Ms. Wong withdraws $5,000 from her time deposit account with a deposit-taking company and remits\n                 it overseas.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    M1 = Legal tender notes and coins held by the public + Customers’ demand deposits with licensed\n    banks\n    Option B is correct. The legal tender held by the public will decrease and the money supply M1 will\n    decrease.\n    Option A is incorrect. The reduction in demand deposits with licensed banks is offset by the increase in\n    legal tender held by the public, so the money supply M1 will remain unchanged.\n    Option C is incorrect. Demand deposits with licensed banks will increase and the money supply M1 will\n    increase.\n    Option D is incorrect. The money supply M3 will decrease and the money supply M1 will not be\n    affected.",
