      "graphType": "-",
      "tableType": "-",
      "multipleSelectionType": "-",
      "calculationType": "-",
      "source": "模擬試卷三十一 卷一",
      "reviewedByAI": "Y",
      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/31/q-p1-41.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/31/a-p1-41.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Firms in an economy generally were pessimistic about their business prospects and decreased investment. At the\n      same time, the central bank of the economy sold government bonds in the open market, which affected the\n      economy’s output level and interest rate.\n\n      Which of the following policies can stabilise the economy’s output level and interest rate at the same time in the\n      short run?\n\n            A.    The government raises the discount rate.\n            B.    The government raises the profits tax rate.\n            C.    The government issues more licenses for electronic payment tools.\n            D.    The government lowers the income tax rate.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    Investment expenditure decreased and aggregate demand decreased. The output level decreased. The\n    sale of government bonds in the open market reduced the money supply and the interest rate increased.\n    Consumption and investment decreased. The output level decreased. Policy that would result in an\n    increase in the output level and a decrease in the interest rate would help stabilise the output level and\n    interest rate.\n    Option C is correct. Issuing more licenses for electronic payment tools will reduce the transaction\n    demand for money, causing the interest rate to decrease. Consumption and investment will increase.\n    Aggregate demand will increase and the output level will increase.\n    Option A is incorrect. Raising the discount rate will reduce the money supply and the interest rate will\n    increase. Consumption and investment will decrease. Aggregate demand will decrease and the output\n    level will further decrease.\n    Option B is incorrect. Raising the profits tax rate will suppress investment, leading to a decrease in\n    investment expenditure. Aggregate demand will decrease and the output level will further decrease.\n    Option D is incorrect. Lowering the income tax rate will raise people’s disposable income, private\n    consumption expenditure will increase and aggregate demand will increase. The output level will\n    increase. However, when people’s disposable income increases, the transaction demand for money will\n    increase and the interest rate will further increase.",
