      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/31/q-p1-43.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/31/a-p1-43.jpg",
      "inlineDiagrams": "diagrams/MT31-P1-43.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The following diagram shows the imposition of a tariff on good X in a small open economy.\n\n                               Unit price\n\n                                                                    S\n\n                                P1\n                                                                            Tariff (t)\n                                P0\n\n                                                                        D\n\n                                  0                                             Quantity\n                                             Q1 Q2      Q3 Q4\n\n      P0 is the world price of good X. Which of the following statements about good X is CORRECT?\n\n            A.    The import volume after the tariff is (Q4 – Q1).\n            B.    If the tariff is reduced, domestic production of good X will be higher than Q 2.\n            C.    If the world price of good X decreases, the government’s tariff revenue will be higher than\n                  (Q3 – Q2) × t.\n            D.    If the tariff is raised, the excess demand for good X will be less than (Q3 – Q2).",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    If the world price of good X decreases, domestic production will decrease and domestic consumption\n    will increase. The volume of imports will increase. With the per-unit tariff unchanged, the government’s\n    tariff revenue will increase, i.e. will be higher than (Q3 – Q2) × t.\n    Option A is incorrect. The import volume after the tariff is (Q3 – Q2).\n    Option B is incorrect. If the tariff is reduced, domestic production of good X will decrease to a level\n    below Q2.\n    Option D is incorrect. For a small open economy, exporting countries can supply as much as it demands\n    at the world price. As a result, there will be no excess demand for good X in the market whether the\n    tariff changes or not.",
