      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/31/a-p2-08.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The following table shows the number of man-hours required by Country A and Country B for producing\n                                                          1 unit of computers and 1 unit of wheat.\n\n                                                                                                Computers                              Wheat\n                                                                     Country A                 2 man-hours                          6 man-hours\n                                                                     Country B                 3 man-hours                          3 man-hours\n\n                                                          (a)   Explain whether Country A has an absolute advantage in producing computers.                     (2 marks)\n\n                                                          (b) Which good will Country A export according to its comparative advantage? Explain.                 (3 marks)\n\n                                                          (c)   Suppose 2 units of computers can be exchanged for 3 units of wheat when trade opens up between the\n                                                                two countries. A transportation cost of 0.5 units of wheat is required to exchange for 1 unit of computers\n                                                                for both countries. Calculate the gain per unit of export of Country A. Show your workings. (3 marks)\n\n                                                                                                   END OF SECTION A\n\n                                                     Section B (60 marks)",
