      "questionTextEng": "In early 2023, Hong Kong Disneyland announced plans to recruit 600 full-time and part-time frontline\n                                                           staff, including positions in hotels and park operations, catering, security and more, to fill the needs in\n                                                           park operations with anticipated tourist visits growth. The park stated that it will launch new attractions\n                                                           and performances in the future, including a new themed area based on the movie Frozen.\n\n                                                          (a)   Explain which factor of production the staff of Hong Kong Disneyland belongs to.                  (2 marks)\n\n                                                          (b) Hong Kong Disneyland provides different types of attractions for visitors. Explain whether these\n                                                              attractions are consumer goods or capital goods.                                       (2 marks)\n\n                                                          (c)    (i)   What type of expansion does Hong Kong Disneyland’s launch of a new themed area belong to?\n                                                                                                                                                          (1 mark)\n\n                                                                 (ii) List TWO possible motives for this type of expansion.                                       (2 marks)\n\n                                                          (d) Suppose, after opening the new themed area, the average cost of production of Hong Kong Disneyland\n                                                              increases. Explain with TWO reasons why this happens.                                    (4 marks)",
