      "questionTextEng": "Singapore raised its goods and sales tax (GST) from 1 January, 2023, from 7% to 8%. All goods are subject\n                                                           to GST, including imported goods.\n\n                                                           (a)   Explain whether the above GST\n\n                                                                  (i)   is a direct tax or an indirect tax.                                                   (2 marks)\n\n                                                                  (ii) is a progressive tax, proportional tax or regressive tax.                              (2 marks)\n\n                                                           (b) Evaluate the above change of the tax system in terms of equality.                              (2 marks)\n\n                                                           (c)   A news commentator said, ‘The increase in the GST will reduce the government’s tax revenue.’\n\n                                                                  (i)   Explain whether this is a positive statement or a normative statement.                (2 marks)\n\n                                                                  (ii) Explain under what condition an increase in the GST will reduce the government’s tax revenue\n                                                                       from GST.                                                                             (3 marks)",
