      "questionTextEng": "Refer to Figure 2. PPFA is the production possibility frontier of Country A. Point P is the production point of\n                                                                 Country A without trade. The slope of the production possibility frontier at point P is 1. The slope of the\n                                                                 dotted line is the world price of good X.\n\n                                                                                                           Figure 2\n                                                                                     Good Y\n\n                                                                                                              P\n\n                                                                                      5\n\n                                                                                                                          PPFA\n                                                                                       0                                              Good X\n                                                                                                                         10\n\n                                                           (a)     Explain why the production possibility frontier of Country A is concave to the origin.              (1 mark)\n\n                                                           (b) Explain whether Country A has a comparative advantage in producing good X.                             (3 marks)\n\n                                                           (c)     Suppose Country A engages in trade. In Figure 2,\n\n                                                                   (i)   indicate the consumption possibility frontier of Country A after trade as CPFT.               (1 mark)\n\n                                                                   (ii) indicate the production point of Country A after trade as P T.                                 (1 mark)\n\n                                                           (d) Suppose after Country A engages in trade, the quantity of both good X and good Y consumed increases.\n                                                               In Figure 2, indicate the consumption point (CT), export volume and import volume of Country A after\n                                                               trade.                                                                                    (3 marks)\n\n                                                           (e)     Suppose the world price of good X continues to increase. Explain under what condition this would affect\n                                                                   your answer in (b).                                                                          (2 marks)\n\n                                                           (f)     The per capita real GDP of Country A increases after opening up to trade, but its HDI remains\n                                                                   unchanged.\n\n                                                                   (i)   Give ONE possible reason to explain the above phenomenon.                                     (1 mark)\n\n                                                                   (ii) Although the HDI of Country A remains unchanged, the residents of Country A generally agree that\n                                                                        their standard of living has deteriorated. State TWO reasons to explain their point of view. (4 marks)",
