      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n     (1) is correct. The university in Hong Kong giving Charlotte an admission scholarship will increase the\n     value of the highest-valued option forgone.\n     (2) is correct. When the Hong Kong dollar depreciates against the British pound, each unit of the Hong\n     Kong dollar can be exchanged for fewer British pounds. Her monetary cost (in terms of the Hong Kong\n     dollar) of studying a bachelor’s degree programme in the UK will increase.\n     (3) is incorrect. The fact that university life in the UK is more boring than she expected will reduce the\n     value of the chosen option, without affecting her highest-valued option forgone.",
