      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/32/a-p1-03.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Under the Government Public Transport Fare Concession Scheme for the Elderly and Eligible Persons with\n     Disabilities (the $2 Scheme), Hong Kong residents aged 60 or above can travel on designated public transport\n     modes and services at a concessionary fare of $2 per trip. Some politicians suggested the government increase the\n     fare from $2 to $3 per trip.\n\n     Which of the following statements about the above suggestion is/are CORRECT?\n\n           (1)   The above suggestion will not affect the opportunity cost for Hong Kong residents aged 60 or above\n                 taking public transport modes.\n           (2)   The above suggestion is related to the ‘for whom to produce’ question in economics.\n           (3)   The above suggestion is an example of using government command to solve the basic economic\n                 problem.\n\n           A.    (2) only\n           B.    (3) only\n           C.    (2) and (3) only\n           D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n     (2) is correct. The suggestion is about who gets access to public transport services, and this is related to\n     the ‘for whom to produce’ problem.\n     (3) is correct. The adjustment of the concessionary fare of the ‘the $2 Scheme’ is determined by\n     government decision.\n     (1) is incorrect. The increase of the fare from $2 to $3 per trip will increase the monetary cost of\n     travelling on public transport modes for people aged 60 and above.",
