      "questionTextEng": "The following table shows the information about firm A and firm B.\n\n                                                      Firm A                      Firm B\n                    Number of owners                     30                         50\n                    Liability                        unlimited                    limited\n\n     Based on the above information, which of the following statements about the above firms is CORRECT?\n\n          A.    Firm A does not need to disclose its financial information to the public while Firm B does.\n          B.    If one of the owners goes bankrupt, firm A has to be dissolved while firm B will continue to exist.\n          C.    Firm B has a higher risk of being taken over than firm A.\n          D.    Neither firm A nor firm B can issue shares to the public.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n     Firm A is a partnership while firm B may be a private limited company or a public limited company.\n     Option B is correct. A partnership lacks lasting continuity. If one of the partners goes bankrupt, the\n     partnership will be dissolved. As a limited company is a legal entity, when one of the owners goes\n     bankrupt, firm B will continue to exist.\n     Option A is incorrect. If firm B is a private limited company, it does not need to disclose its financial\n     information to the public.\n     Option C is incorrect. If firm B is a private limited company, shareholders must obtain the consent of\n     other shareholders to transfer their shares. Thus, the risk of being taken over will not be higher than that\n     of firm A.\n     Option D is incorrect. If firm B is a public limited company, it can issue shares to the public.",
