      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following statements about public goods is CORRECT?\n\n          A.    Books in public libraries are an example of public goods.\n          B.    Public goods are goods provided by the government.\n          C.    The cost of producing an additional unit of a public good is zero.\n          D.    The additional cost of serving an extra consumer to use a public good is zero.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n     Public goods are non-rival in consumption. Once a public good is produced, the additional cost of\n     serving it to an extra consumer is zero. For example, the cost of serving an extra ship to use the guiding\n     service of a lighthouse is zero.\n     Option A is incorrect. When a book is borrowed by a reader, it cannot be borrowed by another reader. A\n     book is rival in consumption.\n     Option B is incorrect. Public goods are not necessarily provided by the government. Private enterprises\n     can also provide public goods.\n     Option C is incorrect. The cost of producing an additional unit of a public good can be greater than zero.",
