      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/32/a-p1-07.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Both the labour supply and average labour productivity of an economy decreased. Which of the following can\n     best explain the above change?\n\n          A.    More experienced workers retired.\n          B.    More enterprises adopted artificial intelligence to replace workers.\n          C.    More residents moved to work in neighbouring areas.\n          D.    The degree of division of labour decreased.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n     Experienced workers are generally more productive. The fact that more experienced workers have\n     retired will reduce the labour supply and average labour productivity.\n     Option B is incorrect. Labour productivity will increase when more enterprises adopted artificial\n     intelligence to replace workers.\n     Option C is incorrect. More residents moving to work in neighbouring areas will lead to a decrease in\n     the labour supply, but the change in average labour productivity is uncertain.\n     Option D is incorrect. A decrease in the degree of division of labour will reduce the average labour\n     productivity, but it will not affect the labour supply.",
