      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/32/q-p1-10.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/32/a-p1-10.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The table below shows the cost-output relationship of a price-taking firm.\n\n                            Output (units)                Average cost ($)\n                                 5                              10\n                                 6                              10\n                                 7                              11\n                                 8                              12\n                                 9                              13\n\n      Suppose the average cost for each unit of output increases by $2 and the market price decreases from $21 to $19.\n      The profit-maximising output of the firm will ________ while the profit will __________.\n\n            A.    decrease by 1 unit … decrease to $42\n            B.    decrease by 1 unit … decrease to $56\n            C.    decrease by 2 units … decrease to $42\n            D.    decrease by 2 units … decrease to $56",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n       Output        Original           Original     Original       New              New            New\n       (units)       average           total cost    marginal      average         total cost      marginal\n                     cost ($)             ($)        cost ($)      cost ($)           ($)          cost ($)\n          5             10                50               -          12               60                 -\n          6             10                60            10            12               72              12\n          7              11               77            17            13               91              19\n          8             12                96            19            14              112              21\n          9             13                117           21            15              135              23\n     The original market price is $21 and the profit-maximising output is 9 units, as marginal revenue equals\n    marginal cost at this output level.\n    The new market price is $19, and the profit-maximising output is 7 units.\n    New profit = ($19 × 7) – $91 = $42",
