      "questionTextEng": "In April 2023, Sega Sammy Holdings, a game developer, proposed to acquire Rovio Entertainment, the developer\n      of the famous mobile game ‘Angry Birds’. Which of the following are likely the motives for the acquisition?\n\n            (1)   to enjoy economies of scale\n            (2)   to reduce competition\n            (3)   to ensure a higher profit for the company\n            (4)   to increase market share\n\n            A.    (1) and (2) only\n            B.    (3) and (4) only\n            C.    (1), (2) and (4) only\n            D.    (2), (3) and (4) only",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n     (1) is correct. The company may enjoy economies of scale after the expansion of the production scale.\n\n    (2) is correct. Both Sega Sammy Holdings and Rovio Entertainment are engaged in the game\n    development business. The acquisition could reduce the number of competitors and thus reduce\n    competition.\n    (4) is correct. Both Sega Sammy Holdings and Rovio Entertainment are engaged in the game\n    development business. The acquisition could increase Sega Sammy Holdings’s market share.\n    (3) is incorrect. Acquiring another game developer does not guarantee a higher profit.",
