      "inlineDiagrams": "diagrams/MT32-P1-12.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Refer to the following figure.\n\n                                       Country A       120 km\n\n                                                                        Country C\n                                          30 km\n                                                   Country B\n\n      Suppose Country A exports apples to Country B and Country C. The cost of transporting 1 unit of apples per\n      kilometre is fixed. Which of the following is INCONSISTENT with the law of demand?\n\n            A.    Compared with Country B, Country C imports a greater proportion of high-quality apples from\n                  Country A.\n            B.    The average quality of apples sold in Country C is lower than that of apples sold in Country B.\n            C.    When the cost of transporting 1 unit of apples decreases, the total expenditure of consumers in\n                  Country B and Country C on apples imported from Country A will decrease.\n            D.    When the cost of transporting 1 unit of apples increases, both Country B and Country C will import\n                  fewer apples.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    According to the figure, compared with Country B, Country C is farther away from Country A. The\n    transport cost of exporting 1 unit of apples from Country A to Country C is higher than that to Country\n    B.\n    With the per-unit transport cost, the relative price of high-quality apples in Country C is lower than that\n    in Country B, so the proportion of high-quality apples imported by Country C will be higher. The\n    average quality of apples sold in Country C will be higher.\n    Option A is incorrect. With the per-unit transport cost, the relative price of high-quality apples in\n    Country C is lower than that in Country B, so the proportion of high-quality apples imported by Country\n    C will be higher.\n    Option C is incorrect. When the cost of transporting 1 unit of apples decreases, the price of apples\n    imported from Country A will fall in Country B and Country C and the quantity demanded will increase.\n    If the demand for apples is inelastic, total expenditure will decrease.\n    Option D is incorrect. When the cost of transporting 1 unit of apples increases, the monetary cost of\n    importing apples to both countries will increase and the quantity of imported apples will decrease.",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/32/ae-p1-12.jpg",
