      "questionTextEng": "The following diagram shows the supply curve (S) of electric vehicles.\n                          Unit price\n\n                                                         S\n\n                                                   A\n\n                                            B\n\n                             0                                         Quantity\n\n      Which of the following reasons best explains the change in equilibrium position from A to B?\n\n            A.    The production cost for electric vehicle batteries increases.\n            B.    More traditional automakers enter the electric vehicle market.\n            C.    Some studies suggest that electric vehicles perform poorly in cold environments.\n            D.    The government offers tax exemptions to buyers of electric vehicles.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    The release of studies that suggest that electric vehicles perform poorly in cold environments will\n    reduce the demand for electric vehicles, causing the equilibrium position to shift from A to B.\n    Option A is incorrect. Electric vehicle batteries are a factor of production of electric vehicles. An\n    increase in the production cost for electric vehicle batteries will reduce the supply of electric vehicles.\n    Option B is incorrect. More traditional automakers entering the electric vehicle market will increase the\n    supply of electric vehicles.\n    Option D is incorrect. The government offering tax exemptions to buyers of electric vehicles will\n    increase the demand for electric vehicles.",
