      "inlineDiagrams": "diagrams/MT32-P1-17.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The following diagram shows the supply and demand curves of good X. The government imposes a price ceiling\n      on good X at PC.\n\n                        Unit price\n\n                                          S\n\n                           Pc\n\n                                                   D1    D0\n                           0                                     Quantity\n                                          Q0\n\n      Suppose the demand for good X decreases from D0 to D1. Which of the following statements about the market for\n      good X is CORRECT?\n\n            A.    Consumers’ total spending on good X will increase.\n            B.    The excess demand for good X will disappear.\n            C.    The quantity transacted of good X will decrease.\n            D.    The price of good X will remain unchanged.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n\n                              Unit price\n\n                                               S\n\n                                Pc\n                                P1\n\n                                                       D1     D0\n                                 0             Q0                    Quantity\n\n    Before the decrease in demand, the price ceiling at PC is effective and the quantity transacted is Q0.\n    When the demand decreases from D0 to D1, the price ceiling at PC becomes ineffective. The new price is\n    P1 and the quantity transacted is Q0.\n    The price of good X will decrease and the quantity transacted will remain unchanged and total spending\n    will decrease. The market of good X will be at the equilibrium after the price ceiling becomes\n    ineffective. Excess demand for good X will disappear.",
