      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/32/q-p1-18.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/32/a-p1-18.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Refer to the following demand-supply schedule of good X.\n\n      Unit price ($)                         9        10            11         12              13      14          15\n      Quantity demanded (units)              50       45            40         35              30      25          20\n      Quantity supplied (units)              20       25            30         35              40      45          50\n\n      Which of the following statements about the market of good X is CORRECT?\n\n            A.    If a price floor is set at $10, the quantity transacted of good X will decrease by 10 units.\n            B.    If a production quota is set at 25 units, consumers’ total expenditure on good X will increase by\n                  $70.\n            C.    If a per-unit tax of $2 is imposed, the market price of good X will increase by $2.\n            D.    If a per-unit subsidy of $2 is provided, the total revenue including subsidy will increase to $520.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n      Unit price ($)             9           10           11          12           13           14              15\n      Quantity demanded\n                                50           45           40          35           30           25              20\n      (units)\n      Quantity supplied\n                                20           25           30          35           40           45              50\n      (units)\n      Quantity supplied\n                                 -            -           20          25           30           35              40\n      after tax (units)\n      Quantity supplied\n                                30           35           40          45           50            -              -\n      after subsidy (units)\n    Before the market intervention, the equilibrium price of good X is $12 and the equilibrium quantity is\n    35 units. Consumers’ total expenditure on good X is $420.\n    Option D is correct. After a per-unit subsidy of $2 is provided, the new market price is $11 and the\n    quantity transacted is 40 units. The total revenue including subsidy is $520 [= ($11 + $2) × 40].\n    Option A is incorrect. As the price floor of $10 is below the equilibrium price, the price floor is\n    ineffective and the quantity transacted will remain unchanged at 35 units.\n    Option B is incorrect. If a production quota is set at 25 units, the market price will be $14. Consumers’\n    total expenditure on good X will be $350, which is a decrease of $70 compared to the amount before the\n    quota.\n    Option C is incorrect. If a per-unit tax of $2 is imposed, the new market price will be $13, which is an\n    increase of $1.",
