      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/32/q-p1-22.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/32/a-p1-22.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Jason often plays the piano at home. His neighbour, Kelly, appreciates his performance very much and wants to\n      enjoy more piano performances. Which of the following statements is CORRECT?\n\n           A.    If Kelly pays Jason to play the piano for longer periods, economic efficiency can be improved.\n           B.    Jason has to pay compensation to Kelly in order to reduce the divergence between private and social\n                 costs.\n           C.    If Kelly pays Jason, there will be no divergence between private and social benefits.\n           D.    The government should intervene and ask Kelly to compensate Jason to achieve efficiency.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    Kelly benefits from Jason’s performance without paying any compensation to Jason. External benefit\n    exists and there is a divergence between private and social benefits.\n    Option A is correct. The marginal private cost for Jason of playing the piano will decrease. Jason will\n    play more and Kelly can enjoy more. The divergence between private and social benefits will decrease\n    and economic efficiency will improve.\n    Option B is incorrect. There is no divergence between private and social costs in this case.\n    Option C is incorrect. Kelly’s payment to Jason will narrow the divergence between private and social\n    benefits, but it does not mean that the divergence will necessarily be eliminated.\n    Option D is incorrect. There is not enough information to determine whether government intervention is\n    needed to achieve efficiency.",
