      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/32/a-p1-24.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The government of an economy launched a Consumption Voucher Scheme, distributing consumption vouchers of\n      the same value to all residents aged 18 or above. The vouchers can be used to purchase goods and services within\n      a specified period of time. Which of the following statements about the scheme are CORRECT?\n\n           (1)   This reduces income inequality, as the value of consumption vouchers results in a higher percentage\n                 increase in the income of lower-income groups.\n           (2)   This helps equalise opportunity, as all residents aged 18 or above have an equal opportunity to receive\n                 the consumption vouchers.\n           (3)   Aggregate output will increase in the short run.\n\n           A.    (1) and (2) only\n           B.    (1) and (3) only\n           C.    (2) and (3) only\n           D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    (1) is correct. The value of consumption vouchers accounts for a higher percentage of the income of\n    low-income groups, which can reduce income inequality.\n    (3) is correct. Distributing consumption vouchers will increase private consumption expenditure.\n    Aggregate demand will increase. In the short run, aggregate output will increase.\n    (2) is incorrect. It does not help equalise opportunities. The poor do not get more resources to improve\n    their productivity or increase future income relative to the rich.",
