      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/32/q-p1-25.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/32/a-p1-25.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The following diagram shows a production chain of automobiles in Country A.\n\n        Raw materials        $X                                               $520\n                                                                                                            Overseas\n        imported from\n                                                                                                           consumers\n          Country B                                                                        $140\n                                             Local\n                                          manufacturers\n          Local raw                                                                                          Local\n                                                                         Local retailers\n      material producers    $100                             $230                                 $260     consumers\n\n      Suppose the above production chain has included a subsidy of $50 that is given to the local manufacturers. If the\n      contribution of the above production chain to Country A’s GDP at factor cost is $800, the value of X is ________.\n\n           A.    $70\n           B.    $170\n           C.    $370\n           D.    $420",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    Value added of local raw material producers = $100\n    Value added of local manufacturers = ($520 + $230) – (X + $100) = $650 – X\n    Value added of local retailers = ($140 + $260) – $230 = $170\n    The contribution of the above production chain to Country A’s GDP at market prices = $100 + $650 – X\n    + $170 = $920 – X\n    The contribution of the above production chain to Country A’s GDP at factor cost = $920 – X + $50\n    $920 – X + $50 = $800\n    X = $170",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/32/ae-p1-25.jpg",
