      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/32/q-p1-26.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/32/a-p1-26.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Suppose a closed economy produces good X and good Y only. The output of 2021 and 2022 are as follows:\n\n                     Price of good X      Output of good X      Price of good Y      Output of good Y\n          Year\n                            ($)               (units)                  ($)               (units)\n         2021               15                   50                    30                   40\n         2022               18                   48                    28                   42\n\n      Which of the following statements about the economy are CORRECT?\n\n           (1)   Nominal GDP in 2022 is higher than that in 2021.\n           (2)   Real GDP in 2022 is higher than that in 2021.\n           (3)   The GDP deflator in 2022 is higher than that in 2021.\n\n           A.    (1) and (2) only\n           B.    (1) and (3) only\n           C.    (2) and (3) only\n           D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    Suppose 2021 is the base year.\n    Nominal GDP in 2021 = $15 × 50 + $30 × 40 = $1,950\n    Nominal GDP in 2022 = $18 × 48 + $28 × 42 = $2,040\n    Real GDP in 2021 = $15 × 50 + $30 × 40 = $1,950\n    Real GDP in 2022 = $15 × 48 + $30 × 42 = $1,980\n    GDP deflator in 2021 = 100\n    GDP deflator in 2022 = ($2,040 / $1,980) × 100 = 103.03",
