      "questionTextEng": "Refer to the data for an economy.\n\n                    Gross national income (GNI) at market prices            $475 million\n                    GDP at factor cost                                      $515 million\n                    GDP at market prices                                    $500 million\n                    GDP deflator                                                95\n\n      Which of the following statements about the economy are CORRECT?\n\n           (1)   Net factor income from abroad is greater than zero.\n           (2)   The amount of subsidies is greater than that of indirect taxes.\n           (3)   Real GDP is greater than nominal GDP.\n\n           A.    (1) and (2) only\n           B.    (1) and (3) only\n           C.    (2) and (3) only\n           D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    (2) is correct. GDP at market prices + Subsidies – Indirect taxes = GDP at factor cost\n    The GDP at market prices ($500 million) is smaller than the GDP at factor cost ($515 million), which\n    means that the amount of subsidies minus indirect taxes is greater than zero, i.e. the amount of subsidies\n    is greater than the indirect taxes.\n    (3) is correct. The GDP deflator is smaller than 100, which means that the real GDP is greater than the\n    nominal GDP.\n    (1) is incorrect. GDP at market prices + Net factor income from abroad = GNI at market prices\n    The GDP at market prices ($500 million) is greater than the GNI at market prices ($475 million), which\n    means that the net factor income from abroad is less than zero.",
