      "questionTextEng": "Suppose many factories in an economy are closed due to a mass labour strike. Which of the following will offset\n      its effect on the economy’s price level in the short run?\n\n           A.    The income of the economy’s trading partners increases.\n           B.    People’s desire to save increases.\n           C.    The government raises the minimum wage rate.\n           D.    Producers expect the price level to increase.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    When many factories are closed due to a mass labour strike, the short run aggregate supply will decrease,\n    and the price level will increase in the short run.\n    Option B is correct. When people’s desire to save increases, private consumption expenditure will\n    decrease. Aggregate demand will decrease and the price level will decrease, which will offset the effect\n    of a decrease in the short run aggregate supply on the price level in the short run.\n    Option A is incorrect. When the income of the economy’s trading partners increases, the economy’s net\n    exports will increase. Aggregate demand will increase and the price level will increase further.\n    Option C is incorrect. When the government raises the minimum wage rate, production cost will\n    increase. Short run aggregate supply will decrease and the price level will increase further.\n\n    Option D is incorrect. When producers expect the price level to increase, the short run aggregate supply\n    will decrease and the price level will increase further.",
