      "questionTextEng": "Suppose hyperinflation occurs in Country A. People are generally unwilling to use the currency of Country A and\n      they use the currency of Country B which has a relatively stable value for transactions. Which of the following\n      statements are CORRECT?\n\n           (1)   The function of Country A’s currency of being a store of value weakens.\n           (2)   Country B’s currency is regarded as money in Country A.\n           (3)   Country B’s currency serves the function of money as a medium of exchange.\n\n           A.    (1) and (2) only\n           B.    (1) and (3) only\n           C.    (2) and (3) only\n           D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    (1) is correct. When hyperinflation occurs in Country A, the purchasing power of its currency will\n    decrease.\n    (2) is correct. Money is anything that is generally acceptable as a medium of exchange. When people\n    generally use the currency of Country B as a medium of exchange, the currency of Country B can be\n    regarded as money.\n    (3) is correct. Country B’s currency serves as a medium to facilitate people’s buying and selling of\n    goods and services.",
