      "questionTextEng": "Titus withdraws HK$800,000 from his time deposits account with a deposit-taking company in Hong Kong. He\n      puts one-fourth of the amount into his safe deposit box in a licensed bank and deposits $500,000 into his account\n      with a restricted licence bank. He remits the remaining amount overseas.\n\n      What will be the immediate effects of the above actions on the Hong Kong dollar money supply?\n\n            (1)   M1 will increase by HK$200,000.\n            (2)   M2 will decrease by HK$600,000.\n            (3)   M3 will decrease by HK$100,000.\n\n            A.    (1) and (2) only\n            B.    (1) and (3) only\n            C.    (2) and (3) only\n            D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    A withdrawal of HK$800,000 from a time deposit account with a deposit-taking company will increase\n    M1 and M2 by HK$800,000, while M3 will remain unchanged.\n    Putting HK$200,000 into his safe deposit box in a licensed bank will not affect M1, M2 and M3.\n    Putting HK$500,000 into his account with a restricted licence bank will cause M1 and M2 to decrease\n    by HK$500,000, while M3 will remain unchanged.\n    Remitting the remaining HK$100,000 overseas will cause M1, M2 and M3 to decrease by HK$100,000.\n    In summary, M1 and M2 will increase by HK$200,000, and M3 will decrease by HK$100,000.",
