      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/32/a-p1-32.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The following table shows the balance sheet of the banking system of a country. All banks do not hold excess\n      reserves and the public hold $200 million cash.\n\n                               Assets ($ million)                  Liabilities ($ million)\n                       Reserves                        450   Deposits                      1,800\n                       Loans                         1,350\n\n      Which of the following statements about the above banking system is CORRECT?\n\n            A.    The money supply is $1,800 million.\n            B.    If the public withdraw $100 million from the bank and hold it in cash, the maximum possible decrease\n                  in loans will be $400 million.\n            C.    If the required reserve ratio is increased to 30%, the maximum amount of deposits will be $1,500\n                  million.\n            D.    If the required reserve ratio is increased to 30%, the reserves will be $540 million.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    If the required reserve ratio is increased to 30%, the maximum amount of deposits will be $1,500\n    million [= $450 million × (1/30%)].\n    Option A is incorrect. Money supply = $1,800 million + $200 million = $2,000 million\n    Option B is incorrect. Required reserve ratio = ($450 million / $1,800 million) × 100% = 25%\n    After the public withdraw $100 million from the bank,\n    Maximum amount of deposits = ($450 million – $100 million) × (1/25%) = $1,400 million\n    Maximum amount of loans = $1,400 million – $350 million = $1,050 million\n    Maximum possible decrease in loans = $300 million\n\n    Option D is incorrect. The increase in the required reserve ratio will not affect the amount of the\n    reserves.",
