      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following statements about the classical quantity theory of money is CORRECT?\n\n               A.     An increase in the price level will cause money supply to increase by the same percentage.\n               B.     If the growth rate of money supply is constant, the inflation rate will equal 0%.\n               C.     When money supply grows by a constant percentage each year, real output will also grow by the same\n                      percentage each year.\n               D.     When money supply grows by a constant percentage each year, nominal output will also grow by the\n                      same percentage each year.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    According to the classical quantity theory of money, a change in the money supply causes a proportional\n    change in nominal GDP.\n    Option A is incorrect. According to the classical quantity theory of money, a change in the price level\n    does not lead to a change in the money supply.\n    Option B is incorrect. According to the classical quantity theory of money, when the money supply\n    changes by a fixed percentage, the price level will also change by a fixed percentage, i.e. the inflation\n    rate will be greater than zero.\n    Option C is incorrect. According to the classical quantity theory of money, real output is assumed to be\n    constant and does not change with the money supply.",
