      "source": "模擬試卷三十二 卷一",
      "reviewedByAI": "Y",
      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/32/q-p1-36.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/32/a-p1-36.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Refer to the following unemployment data of Country A.\n\n                                        800,000                                                       3.5%\n                                        700,000                                                       3.0%\n                  (Number of persons)   600,000\n                                                                                                      2.5%\n                                        500,000\n                                                                                                      2.0%\n                                        400,000\n                                                                                                      1.5%\n                                        300,000\n                                                                                                      1.0%\n                                        200,000\n                                        100,000                                                       0.5%\n\n                                             0                                                        0.0%\n                                                         2020                    2022\n\n                                                  Unemployed population   Unemployment rate\n\n      Which of the following best explains the change in the unemployment data of Country A from 2020 to 2022?\n\n           A.    More manufacturers closed their businesses in Country A.\n           B.    More employed people went overseas to work under the Working Holiday Scheme.\n           C.    Some unemployed workers gave up seeking jobs.\n           D.    The government provided a transport subsidy to the employed.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    From 2020 to 2022, the unemployed population in Country A increased while the unemployment rate\n    decreased.\n    Unemployment rate = (Unemployed population / Labour force) × 100%\n    The above phenomenon can be explained by the percentage increase in labour force which is greater\n    than the percentage increase in the unemployed population.\n    Option D is correct. When the government provides a transport subsidy to the employed, people’s\n    incentive to seek jobs will increase and the labour force will increase. As some of them may not be able\n    to find a job, the unemployed population may increase. If the percentage increase in the labour force is\n    greater than the percentage increase in the unemployed population, the unemployment rate will\n    decrease.\n    Option A is incorrect. The unemployed population would have increased if more manufacturers had\n    closed their businesses. Assume that the labour force had remained unchanged, the unemployment rate\n    would have increased, which does not match the data.\n    Option B is incorrect. When employed people go overseas to work through the Working Holiday\n    Scheme, the labour force will decrease.\n    Option C is incorrect. When some unemployed workers give up seeking jobs, the unemployed\n    population will decrease, which does not match the data.",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/32/ae-p1-36.jpg",
      "originalQuestionImageEng": "originals/32/qe-p1-36.jpg",
      "stemPatterns": [
        "(失業率數據) 下列哪項最能解釋 (某國) 失業數據的改變？"
      ]
