      "questionTextEng": "Anson lives and works in Hong Kong. He has the following incomes in 2022:\n\n           (1)   commission earned as a salesperson\n           (2)   rental income received from renting out a car park space\n           (3)   interest earned from time deposits with licensed banks\n           (4)   dividend received from a listed company in Hong Kong\n\n      According to the tax system of Hong Kong, which of the above incomes are subject to taxation?\n\n           A.    (1) only\n           B.    (1) and (2) only\n           C.    (2) and (3) only\n           D.    (1), (2) and (4) only",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    (1) is correct. Income from employment is subjected to salaries tax.\n    (2) is correct. Rental income derived from letting out properties is subjected to property tax.\n\n    (3) is incorrect. There is no interest tax in Hong Kong, so interest income is not subject to taxation.\n    (4) is incorrect. There is no dividend tax in Hong Kong, so dividend income is not subject to taxation.",
