      "inlineDiagrams": "diagrams/MT32-P1-43.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The following diagram shows the market of good X in a small open economy. The economy imposes an import\n      quota on good X.\n\n                                                                                   PW = World price\n                       Unit price\n                                                            S0\n                                                                 S1\n\n                        PW\n                                     Import\n                                      quota\n                                                            D\n                         0                                              Quantity\n\n      If the demand for good X increases, which of the following are CORRECT?\n\n            (1)   The world price of good X will increase.\n            (2)   The domestic production of good X will increase.\n            (3)   The import volume of good X will remain unchanged.\n            (4)   There will be an excess demand for good X.\n\n            A.    (1) and (2) only\n            B.    (1) and (3) only\n            C.    (2) and (3) only\n            D.    (2) and (4) only",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n         Unit price                                                         PW = world price\n                                                                            P1 = domestic price before the\n                                                          S0\n                                                                            increase in demand\n                                                               S1           P2 = domestic price after the\n                                                                            increase in demand\n                                                                            Q1 = domestic production before\n            P2                                                              the increase in demand\n                                      Import quota                          Q2 = domestic production after\n            P1                                                              the increase in demand\n           PW\n                       Import quota\n\n                                                     D0             D1\n            0         Q1       Q2                                        Quantity\n\n    (2) is correct. The domestic production of good X will increase from Q1 to Q2.\n    (3) is correct. The import volume of good X will be equal to the quantity of quota.\n    (1) is incorrect. The world price of good X will remain unchanged.\n    (4) is incorrect. The quantity demanded of good X is equal to the quantity supplied. The market for\n    good X is in equilibrium.",
