      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/32/q-p1-45.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/32/a-p1-45.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Study the following information about Country A.\n\n                                  600\n                                  500\n                                  400\n                                  300\n                                                                                     Value of total exports of\n                    ($ million)\n\n                                  200                                                goods\n                                  100                                                Balance of visible trade\n                                    0\n                                                           2021         2022\n                                  -100\n                                  -200\n                                  -300\n\n      Which of the following best explains the above changes in the economy from 2021 to 2022?\n\n           A.    Country A’s value of garments imported from other countries increased.\n           B.    Manufacturers in Country A replaced foreign imported raw materials with local raw materials.\n           C.    More residents from other countries purchased life insurance from insurance companies in Country A.\n           D.    Expenditure of residents of Country A during their visits to other countries increased.\n\n                                                                  EN D O F PAP E R",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    Balance of visible trade = Value of total exports of goods − Value of imports of goods\n    From 2021 to 2022, the value of exports of goods increased while the deficit of visible trade increased,\n    implying that the value of imports of goods increased during the period.\n    Option A is correct. When Country A’s value of goods imported from other countries increased, the\n    value of imports of goods would increase.\n\n    Option B is incorrect. If manufacturers in Country A had replaced foreign imported raw materials with\n    local raw materials, the value of imports of goods would have decreased, which does not match the data.\n    Option C is incorrect. When more residents from other countries purchased life insurance from\n    insurance companies in Country A, the value of exports of services would increase, which is not shown\n    in the data.\n    Option D is incorrect. When expenditure of residents of Country A during their visits to other countries\n    increased, the value of imports of services would increase, which is not shown in the data.",
