      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/32/a-p2-10.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "In June 2023, the South Korean government distributed a set of coupons for local accommodation and tour\n                                                           packages to boost domestic consumption.\n\n                                                           (a)   When people purchased accommodation for a price exceeding 50,000 Korean won in any region in\n                                                                 South Korea, a coupon of 30,000 Korean won would be given.\n\n                                                                 Compared with directly distributing 30,000 Korean won to residents in cash, explain an advantage of\n                                                                 the above arrangement for the economy of South Korea.                                     (3 marks)\n\n                                                           Suppose South Korea initially has a deflationary (output) gap.\n\n                                                           (b) With the aid of a diagram, explain how the above action can help South Korea restore its aggregate\n                                                               output to the full-employment output level in the long run.                              (6 marks)\n\n                                                           (c)   WITHOUT using a diagram, explain why even without the help of the government, market forces can\n\n                                                                 restore South Korea’s aggregate output to its full-employment output level in the long run. (4 marks)",
