      "questionTextEng": "Figure 3 shows the production possibility frontier of Country A (PPFA) and the production possibility\n                                                                 frontier of Country B (PPFB).\n\n                                                                                                               Figure 3\n                                                                                Good Y (units)\n                                                                                    100\n\n                                                                                     64\n                                                                                                                  N\n\n                                                                                                  PPFA             PPFB\n                                                                                      0                                             Good X (units)\n                                                                                                         50        80\n\n                                                           (a)     Explain why the production possibility frontiers of both countries are straight lines but not concave to the\n                                                                   origin.                                                                                            (1 mark)\n\n                                                           (b) Explain which country has a comparative advantage in producing good X.                                (3 marks)\n\n                                                           (c)     Explain whether Country A can produce at point N.                                                 (2 marks)\n\n                                                           (d) Suppose the terms of trade is 1X = 1Y. After Country A engages in trade, the quantity of good Y\n                                                               consumed is 50 units. In Figure 3, indicate the consumption possibility frontier (CPFA), the consumption\n                                                               point (CT), export volume and import volume of Country A after trade.                          (4 marks)\n\n                                                           (e)     Explain whether Country A can gain from trade.                                                    (2 marks)\n\n                                                           (f)     Explain TWO costs of economic growth that may result from opening up to trade.                    (4 marks)",
