      "questionTextEng": "Carmen is a nursing graduate. After working as a full-time nurse in a public hospital for a year, she decides to quit\n     her job and switch to teaching piano full-time.\n\n     Which of the following would be the LEAST important factor for Carmen in deciding to change her occupation?\n\n           A.    Carmen spent a lot of time and money studying nursing.\n           B.    The working hours for teaching piano full-time are shorter.\n           C.    Working as a nurse in a public hospital has more opportunities for promotion.\n           D.    Carmen earns a lot more income from teaching piano.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n     The time and money spent by Carmen on studying nursing is a cost that has been paid in the past and\n     cannot be recovered, so it is not the opportunity cost of the choice and it does not affect current\n     decision-making.\n     Option B is incorrect. Shorter working hours for teaching piano full-time is related to the benefits of\n     changing her occupation.\n     Option C is incorrect. Opportunity for promotion in a public hospital is related to the cost of changing\n     her occupation.\n     Option D is incorrect. The income from teaching piano is related to the benefits of changing her\n     occupation.",
