      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/33/a-p1-11.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The following table shows the production plan of a firm. The firm employs two inputs only, namely machinery\n      and labour.\n\n                     Machinery (units)               Labour (units)             Total product (units)\n                            1                             10                             5\n                            2                             10                             15\n                            3                             10                             28\n                            4                             10                             Q1\n                            5                             10                             Q2\n\n      Suppose the above data illustrates the law of diminishing marginal returns. Which of the following figures is\n      NOT consistent with the law?\n\n            A.    Q1 = 40; Q2 = 50\n            B.    Q1 = 43; Q2 = 60\n            C.    Q1 = 45; Q2 = 42\n            D.    Q1 = 45; Q2 = 60",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n         Machinery (units)            Labour (units)          Total product (units)    Marginal product (units)\n                   1                        10                          5                          5\n                   2                        10                         15                         10\n                   3                        10                         28                         13\n                   4                        10                         Q1                          X\n                   5                        10                         Q2                          Y\n\n     Option B is correct. When Q1 = 43 and Q2 = 60, X = 15 and Y = 17. The data cannot illustrate the law of\n     diminishing marginal returns because the marginal product continues to increase.\n     Option A is incorrect. When Q1 = 40 and Q2 = 50, X = 12 and Y = 10. Since the marginal product first\n     increases and then decreases, the data illustrates the law of diminishing marginal returns.\n\n    Option C is incorrect. When Q1 = 45 and Q2 = 42, X = 17 and Y = –3. Since the marginal product first\n    increases and then decreases, the data illustrates the law of diminishing marginal returns.\n    Option D is incorrect. When Q1 = 45 and Q2 = 60, X = 17 and Y = 15. Since the marginal product first\n    increases and then decreases, the data illustrates the law of diminishing marginal returns.",
