      "questionTextEng": "A fitness center group has opened several new branches. The group invested a lot of money to promote the new\n      branches, but not many new members have been attracted.\n\n      Based on the above information, the fitness center group may __________.\n\n            A.    enjoy internal economies of scale\n            B.    enjoy external economies of scale\n            C.    suffer internal diseconomies of scale\n            D.    suffer external diseconomies of scale",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    The fitness center group may suffer internal diseconomies of scale because expanding its production\n    scale may increase its average cost. As consumers did not respond satisfactorily to the firm’s additional\n    promotion, the increase in the number of customers may not be able to cover the increase in marketing\n    expenses, resulting in an increase in average cost.",
