      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/33/a-p1-13.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Mr. Cheung runs a second-hand handbag shop and sells second-hand designer handbags. Which of the following\n      would increase its profit-maximising output?\n\n            A.    The monthly rental payment of the store decreases.\n            B.    The demand for second-hand designer handbags increases.\n            C.    The wage rate of workers who repair designer handbags increases.\n            D.    Acquiring second-hand designer handbags becomes more difficult.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    When the demand for second-hand designer handbags increases, the market price will increase. The\n    marginal revenue will increase and the profit-maximising output will increase.\n    Option A is incorrect. When the monthly rental payment of the store decreases, the fixed cost of selling\n    second-hand designer handbags will decrease and the profit-maximising output will not be affected.\n    Option C is incorrect. When the wage rate of workers who repair designer handbags increases, the\n    marginal cost of selling second-hand designer handbags will increase and the profit-maximising output\n    will decrease.\n    Option D is incorrect. When acquiring second-hand designer handbags becomes more difficult, the\n    marginal cost of selling second-hand designer handbags will increase and the profit-maximising output\n    will decrease.",
