      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    (2) is correct. After the increase in price, the quantity transacted will decrease and consumer surplus will\n    decrease.\n\n    (3) is correct. After adding $1 to the prices of all products, the relative price of higher-priced meals (in\n    terms of lower-priced meals) will fall. According to the law of demand, people will buy more\n    higher-priced meals relative to lower-priced meals. The proportion of higher-priced meals sold to\n    lower-priced meals sold will increase.\n    (1) is incorrect. The quantity transacted will decrease after the increase in price. The change in total\n    revenue is uncertain, depending on the price elasticity of demand for restaurant services.",
