      "questionTextEng": "When good X and good Y are in ______________, an increase in the price of good X will lead to a decrease in\n      the ________________.\n\n            A.    joint supply … quantity transacted of good Y\n            B.    competitive supply … total revenue from the sale of good Y\n            C.    joint demand … producer surplus in the market of good Y\n            D.    competitive demand … producer surplus in the market of good Y",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    If good X and good Y are in joint demand, when the price of good X increases, the demand for good Y\n    will decrease. Both the price and quantity transacted will decrease. The producer surplus in the market\n    of good Y will decrease.\n    Option A is incorrect. If good X and good Y are in joint supply, when the price of good X increases, the\n    supply of good Y will increase. Its price will decrease and the quantity transacted will increase.\n    Option B is incorrect. If good X and good Y are in competitive supply, when the price of good X\n    increases, the supply of good Y will decrease. Its price will increase and the quantity transacted will\n    decrease. Total revenue from the sale of good Y may increase, decrease or remain unchanged, depending\n    on the price elasticity of demand for good Y.\n    Option D is incorrect. If good X and good Y are in competitive demand, when the price of good X\n    increases, the demand for good Y will increase. Both its price and quantity transacted will increase. The\n    producer surplus in the market of good Y will increase.",
