      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/33/a-p1-18.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following situations is most likely to increase the supply of construction workers?\n\n            A.    There are more job opportunities in other industries.\n            B.    The average wage rate for construction workers increases.\n            C.    The government announces the construction of more public housing.\n            D.    The government abolishes restrictions on importing foreign workers.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    When the government abolishes restrictions on importing foreign workers, more foreign workers can\n    come to work, and the supply of construction workers will increase.\n    Option A is incorrect. When there are more jobs opportunities in other industries, more construction\n    workers may seek employment in other industries, and the supply of construction workers may\n    decrease.\n    Option B is incorrect. An increase in the average wage rate for construction workers will lead to an\n    increase in the quantity supplied of construction workers. The supply of construction workers will not\n    be affected.\n    Option C is incorrect. When the government announces the construction of more public housing, the\n    demand for construction workers will increase.",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/33/ae-p1-18.jpg",
      "originalQuestionImageEng": "originals/33/qe-p1-18.jpg",
      "stemPatterns": [
        "下列哪種情況最有可能令 (某勞工/物品) 的供應上升？"
      ]
