      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    Given that cruise services are normal goods, when people’s income increases, the demand for cruise\n    services will increase. The demand curve will shift to the right from D0 to D1.\n    When the maintenance cost of cruise ships increases sharply, the cost of providing cruise services will\n    increase. The supply of cruise services will decrease and the supply curve will shift to the left from S0 to\n    S2.",
