      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/33/q-p1-21.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/33/a-p1-21.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Suppose the demand for good X is a derived demand for good Y. When the demand for good Y decreases, the\n      equilibrium price of good X falls from $10 to $8 and the quantity transacted changes by 30%. Which of the\n      following statements is CORRECT?\n\n            A.    The supply of good X is elastic.\n            B.    The supply of good X is inelastic.\n            C.    The demand for good X is elastic.\n            D.    The demand for good X is inelastic.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    Given that the demand for good X is a derived demand for good Y, when the demand for good Y\n    decreases, the demand for good X will also decrease. The price and quantity transacted of good X will\n    decrease.\n    Percentage decrease in price = ($8 ‒ $10) / [($10 + $8) / 2] × 100% = 22.22%\n    Since the percentage change in quantity supplied (30%) is higher than the percentage change in price\n    (22.22%), the supply of good X is elastic.",
