      "questionTextEng": "The following shows the demand-supply diagram for good X.\n\n                          Unit price\n                                        S1           S2\n\n                            P2\n\n                            P1\n\n                                                           D\n                                                                     Quantity\n                              0         Q1          Q2\n\n      If the government increases the quota limit from Q1 to Q2, which of the following statements are CORRECT?\n\n            (1)   The consumers’ total expenditure on good X will change from (P1 × Q1) to (P2 × Q2).\n            (2)   The market of good X will be in equilibrium.\n            (3)   The marginal benefit of the last unit of good X will decrease.\n\n           A.     (1) and (2) only\n           B.     (1) and (3) only\n           C.     (2) and (3) only\n           D.     (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n                         Unit price\n                                     S1              S2\n\n                            P2\n\n                            P3\n\n                            P1\n\n                                                           D\n                                                                     Quantity\n                              0         Q1     Q3    Q2\n\n    (2) is correct. When the quota limit is Q2, the quota is ineffective. The quantity demanded and quantity\n    supplied will both be Q3 and the market of good X will be in equilibrium.\n    (3) is correct. When the quota limit increases from Q1 to Q2, the quota will become ineffective. The\n    quantity transacted will increase from Q1 to Q3 and the marginal benefit of the last unit of good X will\n    decrease from P2 to P3.\n    (1) is incorrect. When the quota limit is Q1, the price is P2 and the total expenditure is (P2 × Q1). When\n    the quota limit is Q2, the quota is ineffective. The price is P3 and the total expenditure is (P3 × Q3).",
