      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    Original price = $10\n    Original quantity transacted = 25 units\n     Unit price Quantity demanded             Quantity supplied       Quantity supplied\n        ($)             (units)                   (units)              after tax (units)\n         6                35                         15                        -\n         8                30                         20                        -\n        10                25                         25                       15\n        12                20                         30                       20\n        14                15                         35                       25\n        16                10                         40                       30\n    New quantity transacted = 20 units\n    Total tax revenue = $4 × 20 units = $80\n    The new price is $12. Since consumers’ tax burden ($2 per unit) equals producers’ tax burden ($2 per\n    unit), the price elasticity of demand is equal to the price elasticity of supply.",
