      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/33/a-p1-27.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "An environmental organisation proposed that the government impose a tax on plastic tableware. Which of the\n      following statements are CORRECT regarding the tax imposed on plastic tableware?\n\n            (1)   Consumer surplus in the market of plastic tableware will decrease.\n            (2)   If consumers’ demand for plastic tableware is inelastic, their total expenditure on plastic tableware\n                  will increase.\n            (3)   Total social surplus in the market of wooden tableware will decrease.\n\n            A.    (1) and (2) only\n            B.    (1) and (3) only\n            C.    (2) and (3) only\n            D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    (1) is correct. Imposing the tax will lead to a decrease in the supply of plastic tableware. The\n    equilibrium price will increase and the quantity transacted will decrease. Consumer surplus will\n    decrease.\n    (2) is correct. Imposing the tax will cause the equilibrium price of plastic tableware to increase and the\n    quantity transacted to decrease. If consumers’ demand for plastic tableware is inelastic, the percentage\n    increase in price will be greater than the percentage decrease in quantity demanded, and consumers’\n    total expenditure will increase.\n    (3) is incorrect. After imposing the tax, the equilibrium price of plastic tableware will increase. Wooden\n    tableware and plastic tableware are substitutes. When the price of plastic tableware increases, the\n    demand for wooden tableware will increase and the total social surplus will increase.",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/33/ae-p1-27.jpg",
