      "questionTextEng": "In Country A, the air pollution problem is serious. The government is considering how to improve the air\n                                                           quality.\n\n                                                          Source A: Major sources of air pollution in Country A\n\n                                                           Exhaust gas from diesel vehicles      Emissions from power plants         Pollutants emitted by factories\n\n                                                          Source B: News report on Country A’s government imposing an additional sewage charge on industrial firms\n                                                           To encourage enterprises to proactively improve their production systems to reduce the emission of\n                                                           pollutants, the government announced that, effective immediately, an additional sewage charge will\n                                                           be levied on industrial firms. The additional sewage charge is calculated based on their output. All\n                                                           firms that emit pollutants during the production process have to pay this additional sewage charge\n                                                           based on their output.\n\n                                                           The public generally welcome the measure and believe that pollutants emitted by industrial firms\n                                                           can be reduced and the air quality can be improved. However, many industrial firms said that the\n                                                           measure will make their business more difficult.\n\n                                                          Source C: Some views on air pollution\n                                                                                                   The air pollution in the area where I live is very serious. I need to use\n                                                                                                   an air purifier at home all the time.\n\n                                                                   An elderly woman\n                                                                                                   Air pollution affects health, causing issues such as nose and throat\n                                                                                                   irritation, coughing, and may aggravate symptoms for people with\n                                                                                                   chronic respiratory diseases.\n\n                                                                        A doctor\n                                                                                                   I am used to driving a car. If the government does not provide\n\n                                                                                                   incentives, I think I will not consider changing my travel mode. On\n                                                                                                   the other hand, the government can consider providing incentives to\n                                                                                                   encourage drivers to switch to electric cars that cause less air\n                                                                                                   pollution.\n                                                               A diesel private car driver\n\n                                                        (a) Refer to the above sources. Explain, in terms of externalities, how pollutants emitted by factories may\n                                                            result in inefficiency.                                                                       (3 marks)\n\n                                                        (b) With the aid of a diagram, justify the view of the industrial firms in Source B on the imposition of the\n                                                            additional sewage charge in terms of producer surplus.                                        (5 marks)\n\n                                                        (c) Refer to the view of the elderly person in Source C. Explain why ‘fresh air’ is an economic good in this\n                                                            case.                                                                                         (2 marks)\n\n                                                        For part (d), candidates are required to present their answer in essay form. Criteria for marking will include use\n                                                        of sources and economic theories, relevant content, logical presentation and clarity of expression.\n\n                                                        (d) Suppose there are two proposals to reduce the level of air pollution.\n\n                                                               Proposal I          Providing a tax concession for first-time buyers of electric cars\n                                                               Proposal II         Lowering public transport fares\n\n                                                             With reference to the above sources and your own knowledge in Economics, discuss which proposal,\n                                                             proposal I or II, each of the following groups of stakeholders would prefer:\n\n                                                             - private car drivers\n                                                             - low-income earners\n                                                             - environmentalists who are concerned about air pollution\n\n                                                            (Hint: You may discuss the reasons why one group of stakeholders would prefer a certain proposal OR\n                                                            why that group would not prefer the other proposal.)\n                                                                                                                                                                 (11 marks)",
