      "questionTextEng": "Tracy is a university graduate who is looking for a job. She has several options and her order of preference is\n     shown below:\n\n     First option: to work as an e-sports athlete in a company\n     Second option: to work as an administrative officer in the government\n     Third option: to continue studying for a master’s programme at university\n\n     Which of the following factors would LEAST likely affect Tracy’s cost-benefit analysis for her choice?\n\n           A.    The government lowers the starting salary of administrative officers.\n           B.    The government waives tuition fees for master’s programmes.\n           C.    The government actively promotes the development of the local e-sports industry.\n           D.    The employment prospects for graduates of the master’s programme are not as good as before.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n     Tracy would choose the first option as the benefit of choosing the first option (the value of the first\n     option) is higher than the cost (the value of the second option).\n     Option D is correct. This would reduce the value of the third option, without affecting Tracy’s cost or\n     benefit of choosing the first option.\n     Option A is incorrect. This would reduce the value of the second option, thus reducing Tracy’s cost of\n     choosing the first option.\n     Option B is incorrect. This may increase the value of the third option to a level higher than that of the\n     second option, so the cost of choosing the first option may change from the value of the second option\n     to that of the third option.\n     Option C is incorrect. This would increase the value of the first option, thus increasing Tracy’s benefit\n     of choosing the first option.",
