      "questionTextEng": "The table below shows the cost-output relationship of a price-taking firm. The fixed cost of the firm is $1.\n\n                            Output (units)                   Total cost ($)\n                                 1                                  5\n                                 2                                 11\n                                 3                                19\n                                 4                                29\n                                 5                                41\n\n     Suppose the market price decreases from $12 to $8 and the fixed cost of the firm increases by $2. As a result, the\n     profit-maximising output of the firm will ________ while the producer surplus will __________.\n\n           A.    decrease by 1 unit … decrease by $6\n           B.    decrease by 1 unit … decrease by $16\n           C.    decrease by 2 units … decrease by $6\n           D.    decrease by 2 units … decrease by $14",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n                                                                      Total cost after an      Marginal cost\n                                                     Marginal cost\n        Output (units)          Total cost ($)                         increase in fixed      after an increase\n                                                         ($)\n                                                                            cost ($)          in fixed cost ($)\n               1                        5                   4                    7                     4\n               2                        11                  6                 13                       6\n               3                     19                     8                 21                       8\n               4                     29                     10                31                       10\n               5                     41                     12                43                       12\n     The original market price is $12 and the profit-maximising output is 5 units.\n    Producer surplus = ($12 × 5) – ($4 + $6 + $8 + $10 + $12) = $20\n    The new market price is $8 and the profit-maximising output is 3 units.\n    Producer surplus = ($8 × 3) – ($4 + $6 + $8) = $6\n    The profit-maximising output decreases by 2 units and the producer surplus decreases by $14.",
