      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/34/a-p1-10.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following is INCONSISTENT with the law of demand?\n\n            (1)   When the government reduces unemployment benefits, the number of unemployed people will\n                  increase.\n            (2)   During cold spells, both the quantity transacted and the price of heaters will increase.\n            (3)   When the government raises the admission fee for public swimming pools, the average time of people\n                  staying in the swimming pools will decrease.\n\n            A.    (1) and (2) only\n            B.    (1) and (3) only\n            C.    (2) and (3) only\n            D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n     (1) is inconsistent. Reducing the unemployment benefits will increase the opportunity cost of people\n     being unemployed, the number of unemployed people will decrease.\n     (3) is inconsistent. The relative price of a long stay (in terms of a short stay) will decrease. According to\n     the law of demand, a higher proportion of visitors will choose to stay longer. The average time of people\n     staying in the swimming pools will increase.\n     (2) is consistent. The law of demand states that an increase in the price of a good will result in a\n     decrease in its quantity demanded, ceteris paribus. Cold spells are one of the factors other than the price\n     that affects the demand for heaters. As the demand for heaters increases, both their quantity transacted\n     and price will increase.",
