      "questionTextEng": "When the price of __________ decreases, the supply of __________ will decrease.\n\n            A.    flour … bread\n            B.    wooden furniture … wood chips\n            C.    tutorial services … tutors\n            D.    cross-harbour bus service … cross-harbour rail service",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    Wooden furniture and wood chips are in joint supply. When the price of wooden furniture decreases, its\n    quantity supplied will decrease, and the supply of wood chips will also decrease.\n    Option A is incorrect. Flour is the factor of production of bread. When the price of flour decreases, the\n     production cost of bread will decrease, and the supply of bread will increase.\n\n    Option C is incorrect. Tutors are the factors of production needed to provide tutoring services. The\n    change in the price of tutorial services will not affect the supply of tutors.\n    Option D is incorrect. Cross-harbour bus service and cross-harbour rail service are in competitive\n    demand. When the price of cross-harbour bus service decreases, the demand for cross-harbour rail\n    service will decrease, but its supply will not be affected.",
