      "inlineDiagrams": "diagrams/MT34-P1-12.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The following is the demand-supply diagram of the private courier service market. E 0 is the original equilibrium\n      point.\n                            Unit price\n\n                                                               S0\n                                                                     S1\n                                                 E0       E1\n\n                                                                          D1\n                                                                    D0\n\n                              0                                                Quantity\n      Which of the following events occurring simultaneously may explain the change in the equilibrium point from E0\n      to E1?\n\n            (1)   The government postal institution lowers its courier service charges.\n            (2)   Many couriers switch to other industries due to an increase in average wage in other industries.\n            (3)   People use online shopping services more often.\n            (4)   Courier companies introduce artificial intelligence (AI) to assist in the distribution of mail.\n\n            A.    (1) and (2) only\n            B.    (1) and (4) only\n            C.    (2) and (3) only\n            D.    (3) and (4) only",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    The diagram shows that both the demand for and supply of private courier services increase.\n    The increase in the use of online shopping services will increase people’s demand for courier services,\n    and the introduction of artificial intelligence to assist in the distribution of mail will increase the supply\n    of courier services, causing the equilibrium point to move from E0 to E1.\n    (1) is incorrect. Courier services provided by the government postal institution and courier services\n    provided by private courier companies are substitutes. When the government postal institution lowers\n    the courier service charges, the demand for private courier services will decrease.\n    (2) is incorrect. Many couriers switching to other industries will lead to a decrease in the supply of\n    courier services.",
