      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/34/a-p1-15.jpg",
      "inlineDiagrams": "diagrams/MT34-P1-15.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The following shows the supply and demand curves for good X. The government imposes a price floor on good X\n      at PA.\n\n                              Unit price\n\n                                                           S\n\n                                PA\n\n                                                          D0     D1\n                                 0                                       Quantity\n\n      Suppose the demand for good X increases from D0 to D1. Which of the following statements about the market for\n      good X are CORRECT?\n\n            (1)   Consumers’ total expenditure will increase.\n            (2)   The market of good X will change from having a surplus to a shortage.\n            (3)   Consumer surplus will increase.\n\n            A.    (1) and (2) only\n            B.    (1) and (3) only\n            C.    (2) and (3) only\n            D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n                              Unit price\n\n                                                            S\n\n                                         C\n                                  P1   A\n                                        B\n                                  PA\n\n                                                            D0   D1\n                                   0           QA Q1                  Quantity\n\n    Before the increase in demand, the price floor PA is effective, the quantity transacted is QA. There is a\n    surplus in the market of good X.\n    After the demand increases from D0 to D1, the price floor PA becomes ineffective. The new price is P1\n    and the quantity transacted is Q1.\n    (1) is correct. The total expenditure increases from (PA × QA) to (P1 × Q1).\n    (3) is correct. The consumer surplus will increase from area (A + B) to area (A + C).\n    (2) is incorrect. After the price floor becomes ineffective, the market of good X is in equilibrium.",
