      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following can explain why the market structure of cha chaan tengs (茶餐廳) in Hong Kong is NOT\n      perfectly competitive?\n\n           A.    Cha chaan tengs engage in non-price competition.\n           B.    Many customers visit cha chaan tengs every day.\n           C.    Cha chaan tengs are free to leave the market.\n           D.    There are many cha chaan tengs in the market.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    Option B is incorrect. There may be many buyers in both perfectly competitive market and imperfectly\n    competitive market, so this cannot be used to explain why the market structure of cha chaan tengs in\n    Hong Kong is not perfectly competitive.\n    Options C and D are incorrect. They are also features of a perfectly competitive market.",
