      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/34/q-p1-18.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/34/a-p1-18.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Suppose the marginal benefit per unit of rice decreases. Which of the following statements are CORRECT?\n\n           (1)   Economic efficiency will be worsened.\n           (2)   Producer surplus will decrease.\n           (3)   The marginal cost of the last unit of rice will decrease.\n\n           A.    (1) and (2) only\n           B.    (1) and (3) only\n           C.    (2) and (3) only\n           D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    (2) is correct. A decrease in the marginal benefit per unit of rice means that there is a decrease in\n     demand for rice. The price and quantity transacted will decrease, and producer surplus will decrease.\n     (3) is correct. Producers will supply rice until the price equals marginal cost. When the demand for rice\n     decreases, its price will decrease and the marginal cost of the last unit of rice will decrease.\n     (1) is incorrect. When demand decreases, total social surplus will decrease, but this does not mean that\n     economic efficiency will be worsened. Before and after the demand changes, at the equilibrium quantity,\n     the marginal benefit is equal to the marginal cost, and the total social surplus reaches the maximum, i.e.\n    economic efficiency is achieved.",
