      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/34/q-p1-19.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/34/a-p1-19.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The following diagram shows the supply and demand curves for good X.\n\n                                Unit price\n\n                                                                  S1\n\n                                                                   S0\n                                                g        c\n                                            b        f\n                                    PA\n\n                                        a\n\n                                                                       D\n\n                                    0                                       Quantity\n\n      Suppose the supply of good X changes from S0 to S1 and the government sets a price ceiling at PA. Which of the\n      following statements are CORRECT?\n\n           (1)   The marginal benefit will be greater than the marginal cost.\n           (2)   There is over-production for good X.\n           (3)   The new producer surplus will be area PAba.\n           (4)   The deadweight loss will be area cfg.\n\n           A.    (1) and (3) only\n           B.    (1) and (4) only\n           C.    (2) and (3) only\n           D.    (2) and (4) only",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n     When the supply of good X decreases from S0 to S1 and the government sets a price ceiling at PA, the\n     price ceiling will be lower than the new equilibrium price and the price ceiling is effective. The output\n     will equal to Q1 and producer surplus is PAba.\n     At Q1, output is lower than the efficient output level (Q0), i.e. there is under-production. Marginal\n     benefit is greater than marginal cost, there is a deadweight loss, which is the shaded part in the diagram\n     below.\n                            Unit price\n                                                             S1\n\n                                                             S0\n                                           g        c\n                                       b        f\n                              PA\n\n                               a\n                                                              D\n                                                                       Quantity\n                               0       Q1 Q0",
