      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    When calculating Hong Kong’s GDP, those living in owner-occupied units are assumed to provide\n    rental services to themselves, so estimated rental value of an owner-occupied unit would be included in\n    the calculation of Hong Kong’s GDP.\n    Options A and C are incorrect. Neither the funds raised from flag selling nor capital gains are generated\n    from production and therefore would not be included in the calculation of GDP.\n    Option D is incorrect. The residential unit was not produced in the current year and its value was\n    included in the calculation of GDP of the year when it was produced.",
