      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/34/q-p1-25.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/34/a-p1-25.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Refer to the following data for an economy.\n\n                                                             Growth rate (relative to\n                                                               the previous year)\n                           Per capita nominal GDP                     0%\n                           Real GDP                                   1%\n                           Population                                 –3%\n\n      Compared to the previous year, the general price level has ___________ and the per capita real GDP has\n      ___________ in the economy in the current year.\n\n            A.    increased … increased\n            B.    increased … decreased\n            C.    decreased … increased\n            D.    decreased … decreased",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    Growth rate of real GDP is 1%, reflecting an increase in real GDP.\n    Growth rate of population is negative, reflecting a decrease in population.\n    Per capita nominal GDP is 0% (i.e. no change), meaning that nominal GDP and population has changed\n    at the same percentage (‒3%). Nominal GDP has decreased while real GDP has increased (1%),\n    implying a decrease in the general price level.\n    As the population has decreased and the real GDP has increased, per capita real GDP has increased.",
