      "questionTextEng": "The diagram below shows the money demand and money supply curves of an economy. The initial equilibrium\n      point is at E.\n                      Nominal\n                    interest rate\n                                             MS\n\n                                               E\n\n                                                           Md\n                                                                     Quantity of money\n                          0\n\n      If people are more used to make payments for daily expenses by e-wallets and at the same time the central bank\n      sells government bonds to the public, the quantity of money __________ and the nominal interest rate\n      __________.\n\n           A.    will increase …will decrease\n           B.    will increase … may increase or decrease\n           C.    will decrease … will increase\n           D.    will decrease … may increase or decrease",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    When people are more used to making payments for daily expenses by e-wallets, they will hold less\n    money for transactions. Transaction demand for money will decrease.\n    When the central bank sells government bonds to the public, the money supply will decrease.\n    When the money demand and the money supply decrease at the same time, the quantity of money will\n    decrease and the nominal interest rate may increase or decrease, depending on the relative effects of the\n    decrease in money demand and the decrease in money supply on the nominal interest rate.",
