      "questionTextEng": "In Country A, many civil servants have retired in recent years. To reduce government expenditure, the\n      government has decided to fill only part of the job vacancies generated by the retirement wave. As a result, the\n      unemployment rate of Country A __________.\n\n            A.    would decrease\n            B.    would increase\n            C.    would remain unchanged\n            D.    cannot be determined",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    When many civil servants retired, the labour force would decrease. If the government has decided to fill\n    only part of the job vacancies generated by the retirement wave, the number of unemployed population\n    would fall, but the decrease would be smaller than the decrease in the labour force. The change in the\n    unemployment rate would be uncertain, depending on the percentage decrease in the unemployed\n    population and the percentage decrease in the labour force. If the percentage decrease in the\n    unemployed population is greater than the percentage decrease in the labour force, the unemployment\n    rate would decrease. If the percentage decrease in the unemployed population is lower than the\n    percentage decrease in the labour force, the unemployment rate would increase. If the percentage\n    decrease in the unemployed population is equal to the percentage decrease in the labour force, the\n    unemployment rate would remain unchanged.",
