      "questionTextEng": "The diagram below shows the change in the income tax system in economy A.\n\n                      Tax payment\n                                                           Old tax system\n\n                                                           New tax system\n\n                                                                            Income\n                          0\n\n      Under the new tax system,\n\n           A.    the income distribution will become more uneven.\n           B.    fewer people will fall into the tax net.\n           C.    the working incentive of all workers will be lower compared to the old tax system.\n           D.    the economy will result in a fiscal surplus.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    The old tax system was a proportional tax. The new tax system is a regressive tax and the tax allowance\n    is cancelled.\n    Under the new tax system, as there is no tax allowance, more low-income people will fall into the tax\n    net, while high-income group will pay a lower tax payment, income distribution will become more\n    uneven.\n    Option B is incorrect. Since there is no tax allowance under the new tax system, more people will fall\n    into the tax net.\n    Option C is incorrect. For high-income people, as the tax payment decreases for the same income, their\n    working incentive may increase.\n    Option D is incorrect. There is insufficient information to determine whether a fiscal surplus will be\n    resulted.",
