      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/34/a-p1-40.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following may lead to a rise in aggregate output and a deterioration in equity in Hong Kong at the\n      same time?\n\n           A.    a cash allowance of HK$20,000 to parents for each newborn baby\n           B.    a reduction in the profits tax rate\n           C.    a construction of a new railway spur line\n           D.    a provision of electronic learning devices to students from low-income families",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    Reducing the profits tax rate will increase investment expenditure. Aggregate demand will increase and\n    aggregate output will increase. Since most people who pay profits tax are high-income people, reducing\n    the profits tax rate will widen the income gap and result in a deterioration in equity.\n    Option A is incorrect. Distributing HK$20,000 to parents for each newborn baby will increase people’s\n    disposable income. Private consumption expenditure will increase and aggregate demand will increase.\n    Aggregate output will increase. Besides, since everyone can benefit regardless of their income, the\n    HK$20,000 accounts for a higher percentage of income of the low-income group. Income distribution\n    will become more even and result in an improvement in equity.\n    Option C is incorrect. The construction of a new railway spur line will increase government expenditure\n    and aggregate demand will increase. At the same time, the construction of a new railway spur line will\n    also increase the long run aggregate supply and aggregate output will increase. On the other hand, a\n    better transportation network may reduce the cost for low-income people to work farther away from\n    their residential areas, increasing their chances of finding jobs with higher income. An improvement in\n    equity will be resulted.\n    Option D is incorrect. A provision of electronic learning devices implies an increase in government\n    expenditure. Aggregate demand will increase. If students have more learning devices, productivity will\n    increase in the long term. The long run aggregate supply and aggregate output will increase. Besides,\n    providing electronic learning devices to students from low-income families allows them to receive more\n    education, thereby improving their future productivity and income-earning ability, preventing them from\n    being deprived of education because of their backgrounds, resulting in an improvement in equity.",
