      "questionTextEng": "Before trade, the output of Country A and Country B with all their resources evenly allocated between the\n      production of computers and bread is shown below:\n\n                                      Computers (units)                             Bread (units)\n                       Country A             20                  AND                      60\n                       Country B             40                  AND                      55\n\n      If Country A and Country B completely specialise their production and trade with each other, the total output of\n      computers will increase by ____________ units and the total output of bread will increase by ____________\n      units.\n\n            A.     5…5\n            B.     5 … 20\n            C.     20 … 5\n            D.     20 … 20",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    Country A can use all its resources to produce 40 units of computers or 120 units of bread while\n    Country B can use all its resources to produce 80 units of computers or 110 units of bread.\n    Country A’s opportunity cost of producing 1 unit of computers = 3 (= 120/40) units of bread\n    Country B’s opportunity cost of producing 1 unit of computers = 1.375 (= 110/80) units of bread\n    Since Country B has a lower opportunity cost in producing computers, Country B will specialise in\n    producing computers, while Country A will specialise in producing bread.\n    Before specialisation, the total output of computers is 60 units and the total output of bread is 115 units.\n    After specialisation, the total output of computers is 80 units and the total output of bread is 120 units.\n    The total output of computers will increase by 20 units, while the total output of bread will increase by\n    5 units.",
