      "inlineDiagrams": "diagrams/MT34-P1-43.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The following diagram shows the market of good X in a small open economy. The government imposes an import\n      tariff on good X.\n\n                   Unit price\n                                                                        PW = world price\n                                                                        t = per-unit tariff\n                                                   S\n\n                  Pw + t\n                     PW\n\n                                                          D\n\n                      0                                             Quantity\n\n      Suppose the world price of good X increases and the demand for good X increases at the same time. Which of the\n      following are CORRECT?\n\n            (1)    The total expenditure of local consumers on good X will increase.\n            (2)    The government’s tariff revenue from good X may increase, decrease or remain unchanged.\n            (3)    The domestic production of good X will increase.\n\n            A.     (1) and (2) only\n            B.     (1) and (3) only\n            C.     (2) and (3) only\n            D.     (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    (1) is correct. Both the domestic price and consumption of good X will increase, so the total expenditure\n    of local consumers on good X will increase.\n    (2) is correct. The change in import volume depends on the relative extent of the increase in the world\n    price and the increase in demand. As the change in import volume is uncertain, so the change in tariff\n    revenue is uncertain.\n    (3) is correct. As the domestic price increases, the domestic production of good X will increase.",
