      "source": "模擬試卷三十四 卷一",
      "reviewedByAI": "Y",
      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/34/q-p1-45.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/34/a-p1-45.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The table below shows the change in the exchange rate between the US dollar (USD) and the Japanese yen (JPY).\n\n                                                                     Exchange rate\n                                       1 June 2023                1 USD = 139.1 JPY\n                                    1 December 2023               1 USD = 148.0 JPY\n\n      During the period from 1 June to 1 December 2023, the change in the exchange rate between USD and JPY will\n      lead to _____________.\n\n           A.    a decrease in the total value of goods imported from Japan to the United States (in terms of the US\n                 dollar)\n           B.    an increase in the total value of goods exported from Hong Kong to Japan (in terms of the Hong Kong\n                 dollar)\n           C.    a decrease in the number of Japanese tourists visiting Hong Kong\n           D.    an appreciation of the Japanese yen against the Hong Kong dollar\n\n                                                 EN D O F PAP E R",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    More Japanese yen can be exchanged for each unit of the US dollar, the US dollar appreciates against\n    the Japanese yen. Under the linked exchange rate system, the Hong Kong dollar also appreciates against\n    the Japanese yen.\n    Option C is correct. The depreciation of the Japanese yen against the Hong Kong dollar makes the\n    goods and services in Hong Kong more expensive (in terms of Japanese yen) for Japanese tourists,\n    resulting in a decrease in the number of Japanese tourists visiting Hong Kong.\n    Option A is incorrect. The Japanese yen depreciates against the US dollar. Suppose the price of imports\n    from Japan to the United States (in terms of Japanese yen) remains unchanged. The price of imports in\n    terms of the US dollar will decrease. Import volume will increase and the change in total import value\n    (in terms of the US dollar) will be uncertain, depending on United States’s price elasticity of demand for\n    Japanese goods.\n    Option B is incorrect. When the Japanese yen depreciates against the Hong Kong dollar, assuming that\n    the price of goods exported from Hong Kong to Japan (in terms of the Hong Kong dollar) remains\n    unchanged, the price of exports in terms of Japanese yen will increase. Japan’s demand for Hong Kong’s\n    goods will decrease and Hong Kong’s exports of goods to Japan will decrease. The total value of goods\n    exported from Hong Kong to Japan (in terms of the Hong Kong dollar) will decrease.",
