      "questionTextEng": "To reduce air pollution caused by diesel private cars, the government of a country encourages people to\n                                                          commute by bicycles instead of diesel private cars. Some government officials have made the following two\n                                                          suggestions:\n\n                                                                Suggestion 1: to provide a subsidy to rental bicycle operators, with a fixed subsidy per rented\n                                                                               bicycle\n                                                                Suggestion 2: to provide a subsidy to bicycle users, offering a fixed subsidy for each bicycle rental\n\n                                                          (a)     Explain, in terms of externalities, how the use of diesel private cars may lead to inefficiency. (3 marks)\n\n                                                          (b) With the aid of a diagram, explain how suggestion 1 will affect consumer surplus in the rental bicycle\n                                                              market.                                                                                     (7 marks)\n\n                                                          (c)     Discuss how suggestion 2 will affect the average rental time for people using bicycles.          (4 marks)",
