      "questionTextEng": "The table below shows the balance sheet of the banking system of Country A.\n\n                                                                                   Assets ($ million)                 Liabilities ($ million)\n                                                                           Reserves                     3,000   Deposits                        8,000\n                                                                           Loans                        5,000\n\n                                                          Initially the banks hold $1,000 million excess reserves and the public always hold $500 million cash.\n                                                          Suppose the central bank purchases $20 million worth of government bonds from the public.\n\n                                                          (a)   Give ONE possible reason for the banks to hold excess reserves.                                 (1 mark)\n\n                                                          (b) Calculate the maximum possible change in money supply. Show your workings.                       (4 marks)\n\n                                                          (c)   Suppose there exists an inflationary (output) gap in Country A.\n\n                                                                (i)   Define inflationary (output) gap.                                                         (1 mark)\n\n                                                                (ii) With the aid of an AS-AD diagram, explain how the above monetary policy would affect the\n                                                                     inflationary (output) gap.                                                           (7 marks)",
