      "questionTextEng": "DingDingExpress is the only tram service provider in Country A. Figure 2 shows its demand curve and\n                                                             marginal cost curve. DingDingExpress adopts simple monopoly pricing.\n\n                                                                                                           Figure 2\n                                                                                  Unit price\n\n                                                                                                                         MC\n\n                                                                                                                         D = MB\n                                                                                     0                                        Quantity\n\n                                                           (a)   Indicate the profit-maximising output (QM) and price (PM) in Figure 2. Explain whether DingDingExpress\n                                                                 adopting simple monopoly pricing is efficient.                                               (5 marks)\n\n                                                           (b) Suppose the government provides a subsidy to DingDingExpress, which is a fixed amount regardless of\n                                                               the quantity produced.\n\n                                                                 (i)   Indicate the profit-maximising output (QS) and price (PS) after the provision of the subsidy in\n                                                                       Figure 2.                                                                                   (2 marks)\n\n                                                                 (ii) Explain whether economic efficiency would be affected as a result of the subsidy.           (2 marks)\n\n                                                           (c)   DingDingExpress offers an ‘early bird discount’. Passengers who take the tram before 8 a.m. can enjoy a\n                                                                 30% discount on the fare. Explain whether this arrangement constitutes price discrimination. (3 marks)\n\n                                                           (d) Suppose the government grants a few licenses for other tram service providers. However,\n                                                               DingDingExpress refuses to supply its railway facilities to them, and those facilities are essential for\n                                                               providing tram services.\n\n                                                                 (i)   Name the anti-competitive behaviour that DingDingExpress may constitute. List ONE possible\n                                                                       motive for DingDingExpress.                                                     (2 marks)\n\n                                                                 (ii) State TWO ways the above behaviour may harm consumers.                                      (2 marks)",
