      "questionTextEng": "Figure 3 shows the production possibility frontier AA’ of Country A. P A is the production point when there\n                                                                 is no trade.\n\n                                                                                                           Figure 3\n\n                                                                                 Good Y (units)\n\n                                                                                      T\n\n                                                                                      A           PA\n\n                                                                                                                                  Good X (units)\n                                                                                       0                        A’       T’\n\n                                                           (a)     Explain why the production possibility frontier of Country A is concave to the origin.           (1 mark)\n\n                                                           (b) Initially Country A did not engage in international trade. Indicate the consumption point of Country A as\n                                                               CA in Figure 3. Explain your answer.                                                            (2 marks)\n\n                                                           (c)     TT’ is the international price line of good X. Explain whether Country A would have a comparative\n                                                                   advantage in producing good X.                                                          (3 marks)\n\n                                                           (d) Country A decides to open up to international trade.\n\n                                                                   (i)   Country A consumes fewer good X and more good Y after trade. In Figure 3, indicate the\n                                                                         production point of Country A after trade as P T and its consumption point as CT. Explain\n                                                                         why Country A is better off after trade.                                              (3 marks)\n\n                                                                   (ii) Indicate the volume of exports in Figure 3.                                                 (1 mark)\n\n                                                           (e)     Suppose there is a technological enhancement in Country A which doubles its productivity on good X\n                                                                   and good Y. Explain whether your answer in (c) will change.                               (2 marks)\n\n                                                           (f)     Country A has achieved a higher Human Development Index after opening up to trade. Give TWO\n                                                                   possible reasons to explain this phenomenon.                                         (4 marks)",
