      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/35/a-p1-01.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Anson is a candidate for the Hong Kong Diploma of Secondary Education Examination (HKDSE) this year. He is\n     considering whether to become a firefighter or to study economics abroad.\n\n     Which of the following would be the LEAST important factor for Anson in choosing between becoming a\n     firefighter and studying abroad?\n\n           A.    The expense of studying abroad is higher than expected.\n           B.    The government raises the starting salary for new firefighters.\n           C.    Anson has already spent three years studying economics.\n           D.    More employers prefer to hire people who have studied abroad.",
