      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/35/a-p1-14.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Firm A and firm B produce the same mobile phone accessories. Both firms employ the same number of workers,\n    but the working hours for each worker at firm A are longer. It is found that the output of firm A is the same as that\n    of firm B. Which of the following may be the reason for the difference in labour productivity between firm A and\n    firm B?\n\n            A.    Firm A implements a higher degree of division of labour.\n            B.    Firm A adopts piece rate while firm B adopts time rate to pay their workers.\n            C.    The skill level of the workers at firm B is lower.\n            D.    More producer goods are used in firm B.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    As firm A produces the same amount of output as firm B with more man-hours, firm A has a lower\n    labour productivity than firm B (firm B has a higher labour productivity than firm A).\n    Option B is incorrect. If firm A adopts piece rate while firm B adopts time rate to pay their workers, as\n    the incomes of firm A’s workers directly depend on output, the labour productivity of firm A will likely\n    be higher than that of firm B, which is inconsistent with the information given in the question.",
