      "questionTextEng": "The occupational mobility of labour of Hong Kong will increase if\n\n            A.    more industries implement a licensing system.\n            B.    firms adopt a higher degree of division of labour.\n            C.    the monthly subsidy under the Public Transport Fare Subsidy Scheme is raised.\n            D.    the subsidy ceiling of the Continuing Education Fund is raised.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    Increasing the subsidy ceiling of the Continuing Education Fund can help workers acquire more skills\n    needed for certain jobs, increasing their ability to change from one occupation to another. The\n    occupational mobility of labour will thus increase.\n     Option A is incorrect. When more industries implement a licensing system, it will become more difficult\n     for people to enter those industries, thus reducing the occupational mobility of labour.\n     Option B is incorrect. Adopting a higher degree of division of labour will lower the occupational\n     mobility of labour as workers will lack skills required by other jobs.\n     Option C is incorrect. Increasing the monthly subsidy under the Public Transport Fare Subsidy Scheme\n     will reduce transportation costs for workers. The geographical mobility of labour will thus increase.",
