      "questionTextEng": "The following table shows the input-output relationship of a firm.\n\n                       Machinery (units)        Labour (units)       Total product of labour (units)\n                             10                      1                              5\n                             10                      2                             12\n                             10                      3                             24\n                             10                      4                             32\n                             10                      5                             35\n\n     Which of the following statements about the above firm are CORRECT?\n\n            (1)   The marginal product of labour will start to dimmish when the fourth unit of labour is put to work.\n            (2)   The above information shows a short run situation.\n            (3)   The average product of labour keeps increasing.\n\n            A.    (1) and (2) only\n            B.    (1) and (3) only\n            C.    (2) and (3) only\n            D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n           Machinery               Labour             Total product of   Average product of Marginal product\n            (units)                (units)             labour (units)      labour (units)   of labour (units)\n               10                     1                       5                  5                    5\n               10                     2                       12                 6                    7\n               10                     3                       24                 8                   12\n               10                     4                       32                 8                    8\n               10                     5                       35                 7                    3\n    (1) is correct. When the quantity of labour increases from 3 units to 4 units, the marginal product of\n    labour decreases from 12 units to 8 units.\n    (2) is correct. As there is a fixed factor (machinery), the information shows a short run situation.",
