      "questionTextEng": "After a firm doubles the quantity of all inputs, its total output and total cost change as follows.\n\n                                 Total output (units)                     Total cost ($)\n                                        1,000                                5,000\n                                        2,000                                8,000\n\n     Which of the following statements are CORRECT?\n\n            (1)   The firm enjoys internal economies of scale.\n            (2)   The above data illustrate the law of diminishing marginal returns.\n            (3)   It may be a result of lower buying costs.\n            (4)   The firm has a higher profit.\n\n            A.    (1) and (3) only\n            B.    (2) and (4) only\n            C.    (1), (3) and (4) only\n            D.    (2), (3) and (4) only",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n         Total output (units)                Total cost ($)              Average cost ($)\n                1,000                            5,000                          5\n                2,000                            8,000                          4\n    (1) is correct. Average cost decreases when the production scale increases, thus the firm enjoys internal\n    economies of scale.\n    (2) is incorrect. The law of diminishing marginal returns only applies in the short run.\n    (4) is incorrect. The effect of increasing output on the firm’s profit is uncertain. We do not know\n    whether the firm will be able to sell all the additional output. Also, we do not know what the selling\n    price will be when the firm expands its output.",
