      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    When there are more taekwondo schools in the market, the market supply of taekwondo courses will\n    increase and the market price will decrease. Marginal revenue will decrease and the profit-maximising\n    output will decrease.\n    Option A is incorrect. When the monthly salary of taekwondo instructors decreases, the marginal cost of\n    production will decrease. The profit-maximising output will increase.\n    Option B is incorrect. When an increasing number of primary schools place more importance on\n    students’ extracurricular performance in sports in admission decisions, demand for taekwondo courses\n    will increase and the market price will increase. Marginal revenue will increase and the\n    profit-maximising output will increase.\n    Option D is incorrect. When the rent for the premises of Mr. Wong’s taekwondo school decreases, the\n    fixed cost of production will decrease. The profit-maximising output will not be affected.",
