      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/35/a-p1-23.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following is CONSISTENT with the law of demand?\n\n            A.    When a hotel charges a 10% service fee, more people prefer deluxe rooms with better views to\n                  standard rooms.\n            B.    After the government increases the fixed penalty for littering, the number of people littering increases.\n            C.    A larger quantity of low-quality fruits is sold in a market near the farm than in a faraway market.\n            D.    When a per-unit import tariff is imposed on red wine, the average quality of imported red wine\n                  worsens.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    Since a fixed transportation cost is incurred in transporting fruits to a faraway market, the relative price\n     of low-quality fruits will increase. According to the law of demand, people shopping in a faraway\n     market will buy relatively fewer low-quality fruits than people shopping in a market near the farm.\n     Option A is incorrect. Charging a 10% service fee will not affect the relative prices of deluxe rooms and\n     standard rooms. Therefore, the ratio of people choosing deluxe rooms to standard rooms will not\n     change.\n     Option B is incorrect. When the fixed penalty for littering increases, the cost of littering will increase.\n     According to the law of demand, the number of people littering will decrease.\n     Option D is incorrect. When a per-unit import tariff is imposed on red wine, the relative price of\n     high-quality red wine will decrease. According to the law of demand, relatively more high-quality red\n     wine will be imported. The average quality of imported red wine will improve.",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/35/ae-p1-23.jpg",
