      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/35/a-p1-29.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Suppose the reproductive rate of cows in Country A increases significantly. This results in a 40% change in the\n      price of local beef and a 55% change in its quantity transacted. Which of the following statements are\n      CORRECT?\n\n            (1)   The demand for local beef increases.\n            (2)   The total expenditure on local beef increases.\n            (3)   The quantity transacted of imported beef decreases.\n            (4)   The total expenditure on imported beef may increase or decrease, depending on the price elasticity of\n                  demand.\n\n            A.    (1) and (3) only\n            B.    (1) and (4) only\n            C.    (2) and (3) only\n            D.    (2) and (4) only",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    An increase in the reproductive rate of cows will lead to an increase in the supply of local beef, causing\n    the price to decrease and the quantity transacted to increase.\n    (2) is correct. Since the percentage decrease in the price of local beef (40%) is smaller than the\n    percentage increase in the quantity transacted (55%), the total expenditure on local beef will increase.\n    (3) is correct. Local beef and imported beef are substitutes. A drop in the price of local beef will reduce\n    the demand for imported beef. The quantity transacted of imported beef will decrease.\n    (1) is incorrect. An increase in the supply of local beef will cause the quantity demanded of local beef to\n    increase, not the demand.\n\n    (4) is incorrect. A decrease in the demand for imported beef will cause the price and quantity transacted\n    to decrease. The total expenditure on imported beef will decrease.",
