      "questionTextEng": "Suppose nutritional supplements are normal goods. As people’s income in general has increased, there has been a\n      15% and 20% change in the price and quantity transacted of nutritional supplements respectively. Which of the\n      following best explains the above changes in the price and quantity transacted of nutritional supplements?\n\n            A.    The nutritional supplement manufacturers have spare production capacity.\n            B.    There are no close substitutes for nutritional supplements.\n            C.    There are strict licensing requirements for nutritional supplement manufacturers.\n            D.    Expenditure on nutritional supplements constitutes a small proportion of people’s income.\n\n                                                 EN D O F PAP E R",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    When people’s income in general increases, demand for nutritional supplements will increase. The price\n    and quantity transacted will increase. As the percentage change in price (15%) is smaller than the\n    percentage change in quantity transacted (20%), the supply of nutritional supplements is elastic.\n    Option A is correct. If the nutritional supplement manufacturers have spare production capacity, the\n    supply of nutritional supplements tends to be more elastic. When the price increases, they can increase\n    output flexibly by making use of their spare production capacity.\n    Option C is incorrect. If there are strict licensing requirements for nutritional supplement manufacturers,\n    new manufacturers cannot enter the industry easily. The supply tends to be less elastic.\n    Options B and D are incorrect. They are factors affecting price elasticity of demand.",
