      "questionTextEng": "SWIM Well is a profit-maximising swimming equipment manufacturer. The following table shows the\n                                                           average cost schedule of SWIM Well.\n\n                                                                   Output (units)         1               2            3              4             5\n                                                                  Average cost ($)        10              12           14             16           18\n\n                                                          (a)   Suppose the market price of the swimming equipment is $18. Find the profit-maximising output level\n                                                                and the corresponding profit of SWIM Well.                                              (2 marks)\n\n                                                          (b) Suppose the government decides to subsidise the production of sports goods, resulting in a $4 decrease\n                                                              in production cost per unit of output for SWIM Well. Explain whether the profit-maximising output\n                                                              level and profit of SWIM Well will change.                                                   (3 marks)\n\n                                                          (c)   Recently, SWIM Well has acquired a swimming school.\n\n                                                                 (i)   Explain which type of integration the above acquisition was.                          (2 marks)\n\n                                                                 (ii) List TWO possible advantages of this acquisition.                                      (2 marks)",
