      "questionTextEng": "A singer is going to hold a concert in Macau. Mr. Cheung spent $500 on a concert ticket a few months ago.\n     Suppose he can resell the ticket to a friend for $400. Alternatively, he can spend $180 on taking a bus to Macau to\n     watch the concert.\n\n     What is Mr. Cheung’s opportunity cost of going to Macau to watch the concert?\n\n           A.    $400\n           B.    $500\n           C.    $580\n           D.    $1,080",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n     The $500 Mr. Cheung spent on the concert ticket is a past expenditure that cannot be recovered, which\n     is not the opportunity cost of going to watch the concert.\n     The bus fare of $180 is the monetary cost of going to Macau to watch the concert.\n     If Mr. Cheung goes to watch the concert, he needs to give up the $400 in income that he could have\n     received from reselling the ticket to his friend. The $400 is the non-monetary cost of going to watch the\n     concert.\n     Mr. Cheung’s opportunity cost of going to Macau to watch the concert = $180 + $400 = $580",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/36/ae-p1-01.jpg",
      "originalQuestionImageEng": "originals/36/qe-p1-01.jpg",
