      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following cases are related to the problem of ‘what to produce’?\n\n           (1)   A smartphone manufacturer decides to develop a new foldable phone.\n           (2)   A smartphone manufacturer plans to provide more colour options for existing phone models.\n           (3)   A smartphone manufacturer considers moving its domestic production line overseas.\n           (4)   A smartphone manufacturer plans to increase the selling price of its smartphones.\n\n           A.    (1) and (2) only\n           B.    (1) and (4) only\n           C.    (2) and (3) only\n           D.    (3) and (4) only",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n     (1) and (2) are correct. The decisions to develop a new foldable phone and provide more colour options\n     for existing phone models are related to the kinds of goods to produce.\n     (3) is incorrect. Moving the domestic production line overseas involves a change in production method\n     and is related to the ‘how to produce’ problem.\n     (4) is incorrect. Increasing the selling price of smartphones is about who can get the smartphones and is\n     related to the ‘for whom to produce’ problem.",
