      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/36/a-p1-07.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Miss Chan runs a garment factory. If the rent of the factory and the price of fabrics increase at the same time, the\n     profit-maximising output of the factory will _____________ and the profit _____________.\n\n            A.    increase … may increase or decrease\n            B.    decrease … may increase or decrease\n            C.    increase … will increase\n            D.    decrease … will decrease",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n     The rent of the factory does not change with output and is a fixed cost. Fabrics are a variable factor in\n     the production of garments. An increase in the price of fabrics will increase the marginal cost per unit of\n     garments.\n     As the marginal cost per unit of garments increases, the profit-maximising output and the profit will\n     decrease. An increase in the fixed cost will not affect the profit-maximising output, but will reduce the\n     profit.\n     Thus, the profit-maximising output and the profit of the factory will both decrease.",
