      "questionTextEng": "If the price of _____________ decreases, the equilibrium quantity of _____________ will decrease.\n\n            (1)   butter ... margarine\n            (2)   smartphones ... smartphone cases\n            (3)   apple juice ... apple pies\n            (4)   lamb ... wool\n\n            A.    (1) and (2) only\n            B.    (1) and (4) only\n            C.    (2) and (3) only\n            D.    (3) and (4) only",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n     (1) is correct. Butter and margarine are substitutes. When the price of butter decreases, the demand for\n     margarine will decrease and the equilibrium quantity will decrease.\n     (4) is correct. Lamb and wool are in joint supply. When the price of lamb decreases, the supply of wool\n     will decrease and the equilibrium quantity will decrease.\n     (2) is incorrect. Smartphones and smartphone cases are complements. When the price of smartphones\n     decreases, the demand for smartphone cases will increase and the equilibrium quantity will increase.\n     (3) is incorrect. Apple juice and apple pies use the same inputs and are in competitive supply. When the\n     price of apple juice decreases, the supply of apple pies will increase and the equilibrium quantity will\n    increase.",
