      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/36/q-p1-11.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/36/a-p1-11.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Refer to the following supply and demand schedules for good X. Suppose the government has imposed a quota on\n    good X, and the market price is $8.\n\n         Unit price ($)                         4           6              8             10            12\n         Quantity demanded (units)              7           6              5              4             3\n         Quantity supplied (units)              5           6              7              8             9\n\n     After the government increases the quota on good X, the market price changes by $2. Which of the following\n     statements about the situation after the increase in the quota is CORRECT?\n\n           A.    There will be a shortage in the market for good X.\n           B.    The quantity transacted of good X will decrease by 1 unit.\n           C.    Producers’ total revenue will decrease.\n           D.    The equilibrium price of the complements of good X will decrease.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    Given that the original market price is $8, the original quantity transacted is 5 units (i.e. the original\n    quota on good X is 5 units).\n     When the government increases the quota, the market price will decrease. If the market price drops by\n     $2 from $8 to $6 (the equilibrium price), this implies that the new quota is ineffective.\n     Option C is correct. Total revenue drops from $40 (= $8 × 5) to $36 (= $6 × 6).\n     Option A is incorrect. The market for good X is at equilibrium and there will be no shortage.\n     Option B is incorrect. The quantity transacted will increase from 5 units to 6 units.\n     Option D is incorrect. When the market price of good X decreases, the demand for its complements will\n     increase and the equilibrium price will increase.",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/36/ae-p1-11.jpg",
      "originalQuestionImageEng": "originals/36/qe-p1-11.jpg",
