      "questionTextChi": "參閱以下物品X的供需表。\n單位價格 ($)\n9\n10\n11\n12\n13\n14\n需求量（單位）\n9\n8\n7\n6\n5\n4\n供應量（單位）\n6\n8\n10\n12\n14\n16\n假設政府向物品X徵收$3的從量銷售稅，下列哪項陳述是正確的？\nA.\t政府的總稅收會是$24。\nB.\t生產者的稅後總收入會是$72。\nC.\t消費者稅項負擔與生產者稅項負擔的比率是2:1。\nD.\t在原初和新的均衡價格範圍內，物品X的需求彈性小於一。",
      "plainText": "參閱以下物品X的供需表。\n單位價格 ($)\n9\n10\n11\n12\n13\n14\n需求量（單位）\n9\n8\n7\n6\n5\n4\n供應量（單位）\n6\n8\n10\n12\n14\n16\n假設政府向物品X徵收$3的從量銷售稅，下列哪項陳述是正確的？\nA.\t政府的總稅收會是$24。\nB.\t生產者的稅後總收入會是$72。\nC.\t消費者稅項負擔與生產者稅項負擔的比率是2:1。\nD.\t在原初和新的均衡價格範圍內，物品X的需求彈性小於一。",
      "topic": "市場干預",
      "question": "MT36-P1-12",
      "answerMC": "C",
      "answerChi": "答案︰C\n原來的均衡價格是$10，均衡數量是8單位。徵收從量銷售稅後，新的均衡價格是$12，新的均衡數量是6單位。\n單位價格 ($)\n9\n10\n11\n12\n13\n14\n需求量（單位）\n9\n8\n7\n6\n5\n4\n原來的供應量（單位）\n6\n8\n10\n12\n14\n16\n新的供應量（單位）\n-\n6\n8\n10\n選項C是正確的。\n消費者的稅項負擔 = $12 [= ($12 – $10) × 6]\n生產者的稅項負擔 = $6 [= [$10 – ($12 – $3)] × 6]\n消費者稅項負擔與生產者稅項負擔的比率會是2:1。\n選項A是不正確的。政府的總稅收會是$18 (= $3 × 6)。\n選項B是不正確的。生產者的稅後總收入會是$54 (=$12 × 6 – $3 × 6)。\n選項D是不正確的。當價格由$10上升至$12，總支出由$80 (= $10 × 8) 下降至$72 (= $12 × 6)。因此，在這價格範圍內，需求屬有彈性。\n或\n在原初和新的均衡價格範圍內，物品X的需求彈性大於一。",
      "curriculumClassification": [
        "C 市場與價格"
      ],
      "AristochapterClassification": [
        "Ch11"
      ],
      "concepts": [
        "均衡",
        "供需",
        "彈性",
        "稅項與津貼"
      ],
      "patterns": [
        "正誤判斷"
      ],
      "graphType": "-",
      "tableType": "-",
      "multipleSelectionType": "-",
      "calculationType": "-",
      "source": "模擬試卷三十六 卷一",
      "reviewedByAI": "Y",
      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/36/q-p1-12.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/36/a-p1-12.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Refer to the following supply and demand schedules for good X.\n\n        Unit price ($)                     9           10            11         12            13        14\n        Quantity demanded (units)          9            8             7          6             5         4\n        Quantity supplied (units)          6            8            10         12            14        16\n\n    Suppose the government imposes a per-unit sales tax of $3 on good X. Which of the following statements is\n    CORRECT?\n\n           A.    The total tax revenue of the government will be $24.\n           B.    The total revenue net of tax will be $72.\n           C.    The ratio of consumers’ tax burden to producers’ tax burden will be 2:1.\n           D.    Within the range of the original and the new equilibrium prices, the elasticity of demand of good X is\n                 smaller than one.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    The original equilibrium price is $10 and the equilibrium quantity is 8 units. After the imposition of the\n    per-unit sales tax, the new equilibrium price is $12 and the new equilibrium quantity is 6 units.\n      Unit price ($)                             9          10          11          12          13          14\n      Quantity demanded (units)                  9           8           7           6          5           4\n      Original quantity supplied (units)         6           8          10          12          14          16\n      New quantity supplied (units)              -           -           -           6          8           10\n     Option C is correct.\n     Consumers’ tax burden = $12 [= ($12 – $10) × 6]\n     Producers’ tax burden = $6 [= [$10 – ($12 – $3)] × 6]\n     The ratio of consumers’ tax burden to producers’ tax burden will be 2:1.\n     Option A is incorrect. The total tax revenue of the government will be $18 (= $3 × 6).\n     Option B is incorrect. The producers’ total revenue net of tax will be $54 (= $12 × 6 – $3 × 6).\n\n    Option D is incorrect. Total expenditure decreases from $80 (= $10 × 8) to $72 (= $12 × 6) as the price\n    increases from $10 to $12. Therefore, the demand is elastic within this price range.\n    OR\n    Within the range of the original and the new equilibrium prices, the elasticity of demand of good X is\n    larger than one.\n                                   (6 − 8)\n                                            × 100%\n                                  (8 + 6)/2\n    Arc elasticity of demand = |                    | = 1.57\n                                  (12 − 10)\n                                             × 100%\n                                 (10 + 12)/2",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/36/ae-p1-12.jpg",
      "originalQuestionImageEng": "originals/36/qe-p1-12.jpg",
      "stemPatterns": [
        "(供需表) 徵收從量稅，下列哪項陳述是正確的？"
      ]
