      "questionTextEng": "The diagram below shows the market share of different banks in the mortgage loan market in Country A in recent\n    years.\n\n                 35%\n\n                 30%\n\n                 25%\n\n                 20%\n\n                 15%\n\n                 10%\n\n                  5%\n\n                  0%\n                            2020             2021          2022            2023           2024\n\n                            Bank A           Bank B       Bank C        Bank D         Other banks\n\n     Based on the above information, we can conclude that the mortgage loan market in Country A can be regarded as\n     ______________ because ______________.\n\n           A.    monopolistic competition ... there are many banks in the market and each has a small market share\n           B.    monopolistic competition ... there are many mortgage loan applicants in the market\n           C.    oligopoly ... the banks are interdependent in their pricing strategies\n           D.    oligopoly ... a few major banks dominant the mortgage loan market\n\n1 5 . Refer to the following supply-demand diagram for good X.\n\n                                 Price\n                                              S0         S1\n\n                                          a\n                                 P0\n\n                                          b        c\n                                 P1\n\n                                          d        e          f\n                                                                   D\n                                  0                                              Quantity\n                                              Q0         Q1\n\n     Suppose the supply of good X changes from S0 to S1. As a result, consumer surplus will increase by _________\n     and total social surplus will increase by _________.\n\n           A.    area (a + b + c) ... area (c + e)\n           B.    area (a + b + c) ... area (c + e + f)\n           C.    area (b + c) ... area (c + e)\n           D.    area (b + c) ... area (c + e + f)\n\n1 6 . Refer to the following supply-demand diagram for good X.\n\n                                    Price                              S0\n\n                                                                            S1\n\n                                                         E0\n                                    P0\n\n                                                                            D\n                                      0                                           Quantity\n                                                         Q0\n\n     Suppose the government sets a price floor at P0. When the supply curve shifts from S0 to S1, which of the\n     following statements are CORRECT?\n\n           (1)   There will be an excess supply in the market of good X.\n           (2)   There will be a deadweight loss in the market of good X.\n           (3)   The marginal benefit of the last unit of good X will decrease.\n\n           A.    (1) and (2) only\n           B.    (1) and (3) only\n           C.    (2) and (3) only\n           D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
