      "inlineDiagrams": "diagrams/MT36-P1-16.jpg",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    (1) is correct. When the supply curve shifts from S0 to S1, the price floor P0 will be higher than the new\n    equilibrium price, and there will be an excess supply in the market of good X.\n    (2) is correct. At the quantity transacted Q0, the marginal benefit (MB1) is higher than the marginal cost\n    (MC1), so the output is lower than the efficient output level (Q1), and there will be a deadweight loss.\n\n    (3) is incorrect. The marginal benefit of the last unit of good X will remain unchanged (MB1).\n\n                     Price                             S0\n                                                                              Deadweight loss\n                                                              S1\n\n                                        E0    Excess supply\n            P0 = MB1\n\n                   MC1\n\n                                                              D\n                      0                                            Quantity\n                                         Q0 Q1",
