      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/36/a-p1-18.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "During the 2024 Summer Olympics, many shopping malls in Hong Kong provided live broadcasts, attracting\n      many people to watch the events and bringing customers to stores near the shopping malls. Which of the\n      following statements is CORRECT?\n\n            A.    The government needs to subsidise these shopping malls to improve efficiency.\n            B.    If the stores do not give any compensation to the shopping malls, the number of broadcasts of\n                  Olympic events will be lower than the efficient level.\n            C.    There is a divergence between private and social costs.\n            D.    If the stores give compensation to the shopping malls, the marginal social benefit will equal the\n                  marginal social cost.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    If the stores do not give any compensation to the shopping malls, there will be an external benefit. The\n    marginal social benefit of broadcasting Olympic events will be higher than the marginal social cost, and\n    the number of broadcasts of Olympic events will be lower than the efficient level.\n    Option A is incorrect. There is not enough information to determine whether government intervention is\n    needed to achieve efficiency.\n    Option C is incorrect. This case shows a divergence between private and social benefits, not a\n    divergence between private and social costs.\n    Option D is incorrect. Compensation provided by the stores to the shopping malls may narrow the gap\n    between marginal social benefit and marginal social cost, but they may not necessarily become equal.",
