      "questionTextEng": "The table below shows Singapore’s Gini coefficient from 2021 to 2023.\n\n                                                             2021              2022               2023\n            Gini coefficient based on pre-tax pre-           0.444             0.437              0.433\n            social transfer household income\n            Gini coefficient based on post-tax post-         0.385             0.378              0.371\n            social transfer household income\n\n      Based on the above information, we can conclude that, during this period,\n\n            (1)   the income distribution in Singapore became more even.\n            (2)   government tax revenue decreased while social transfers increased.\n            (3)   taxation and social transfers reduced income inequality in Singapore.\n\n            A.    (1) and (2) only\n            B.    (1) and (3) only\n            C.    (2) and (3) only\n            D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
