      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following would be included in the calculation of Hong Kong’s gross domestic product (GDP) in the\n      current year?\n\n           (1)   wages paid by the Social Welfare Department to its staff\n           (2)   rental income received by a private property owner from leasing office space to the Social Welfare\n                 Department\n           (3)   the disability allowance provided by the Social Welfare Department\n\n           A.    (1) only\n           B.    (2) only\n           C.    (3) only\n           D.    (1) and (2) only",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    (1) is correct. The Social Welfare Department is a government department. The payments made to\n    government employees would be included in government consumption expenditure.\n    (2) is correct. The rental payment reflects the income received by the owner of a factor of production\n    (the private property owner) for providing a factor service (the property).\n\n    (3) is incorrect. Disability allowance is a transfer payment and does not involve any production.",
