      "questionTextEng": "The following diagram shows a production chain of electric cars in Country A.\n\n        Imported raw\n                         $500                              $800\n          materials                  Domestic electric               Domestic electric      $400          Foreign\n                                     car manufacturers                 car retailers                     consumers\n       Domestic raw      $400\n        materials\n                                                                            $1,000\n\n                                   Increase in inventory                 Domestic\n                                           $300                         consumers\n\n      Suppose the government provides a subsidy of $200 to the domestic electric car manufacturers. The contributions\n      of the domestic electric car manufacturers and the above production chain to Country A’s GDP at factor cost are\n      ___________ and ____________ respectively.\n\n           A.    $200 ... $1,200\n           B.    $200 ... $1,400\n           C.    $400 ... $1,200\n           D.    $400 ... $1,400",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    Contribution of the domestic electric car manufacturers to Country A’s GDP at factor cost\n    = $800 + $300 – $500 – $400 + $200 = $400\n    Contribution of the above production chain to Country A’s GDP at factor cost\n    = $400 + ($800 + $300 – $500 – $400 + $200) + ($1,000 + $400 – $800) = $1,400",
