      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/36/a-p1-23.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Consider the following gross domestic product (GDP) data about Country A in a certain year.\n\n                                                         GDP components                            $ million\n                                    GDP at factor cost                                               750\n                                    Private consumption expenditure                                  250\n                                    Government consumption expenditure                               150\n                                    Gross domestic fixed capital formation                           200\n                                    Change in inventories                                             X\n                                    Depreciation                                                      10\n                                    Net exports                                                      180\n                                    Total imports                                                     40\n                                    Subsidies                                                         12\n                                    Indirect taxes                                                    27\n                                    Direct taxes                                                      20\n\n     The value of X is $ _____________ million.\n\n           A.                 –25\n           B.                 –15\n           C.                 5\n           D.                 25\n\n2 4 . The diagram below shows the GDP of Country A from 2000 to 2020.\n\n                              60\n\n                              50\n\n                              40\n                ($ billion)\n\n                              30\n\n                              20\n\n                              10\n\n                              0\n                               2000                  2005                 2010              2015               2020\n\n                                                             Nominal GDP         Real GDP\n\n    Based on the above diagram, which of the following is CORRECT?\n\n           A.                 The general price level in Country A decreased continuously every year between 2000 and 2010.\n           B.                 The general price level in 2015 was lower than that in 2005.\n           C.                 Country A’s nominal GDP and real GDP increased continuously every year between 2000 and 2020.\n           D.                 The GDP deflator in 2010 was the same as that in 2020.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    GDP at factor cost = GDP at market prices – Indirect taxes + Subsidies\n    GDP at factor cost = Private consumption expenditure + Gross investment + Government consumption\n    expenditure + Net exports – Indirect taxes + Subsidies\n    750 = 250 + (200 + X) + 150 + 180 – 27 + 12\n    X = –15",
