      "questionTextEng": "Hong Kong’s implicit price deflator of GDP increased by 2.8% in 2023, while its nominal GDP and population\n    increased by 6.1% and 0.7% respectively.\n\n    Based on the information above, we can conclude that Hong Kong’s per capita nominal GDP _____________ and\n    its per capita real GDP _____________ in 2023.\n\n           A.    increased ... increased\n           B.    increased ... decreased\n           C.    decreased ... increased\n           D.    decreased ... decreased",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    The growth rate of nominal GDP (6.1%) was higher than the growth rate of the population (0.7%),\n    reflecting an increase in per capita nominal GDP.\n    Real GDP = (Nominal GDP / Implicit price deflator of GDP) × 100\n    In 2023, the growth rate of nominal GDP (6.1%) was higher than the growth rate of the implicit price\n    deflator of GDP (2.8%), meaning that real GDP increased by about 3.2% [= (1 + 6.1%) / (1 + 2.8%) –1].\n    Since the growth rate of real GDP (3.2%) was higher than the growth rate of the population (0.7%), per\n    capita real GDP increased.",
