      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following will result in a rightward shift of the aggregate demand curve of an economy?\n\n           (1)   People increase their savings due to the desire for a better retired life.\n           (2)   The economy relaxes visa requirements for foreign travellers.\n           (3)   Electronic payments become more common.\n\n           A.    (1) and (2) only\n           B.    (1) and (3) only\n           C.    (2) and (3) only\n           D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    A rightward shift of the AD curve reflects an increase in aggregate demand.\n    (2) is correct. When the economy relaxes visa requirements for foreign travellers, the number of\n    travellers to the economy will increase. Net exports will increase, and aggregate demand will increase.\n    (3) is correct. When electronic payments become more common, the transaction demand for money will\n    decrease and the money demand will decrease. The equilibrium interest rate will decrease. Private\n    consumption expenditure/Investment expenditure will increase. Aggregate demand will increase.\n    (1) is incorrect. When people increase their savings, private consumption expenditure will decrease.\n    Aggregate demand will decrease.",
