      "questionTextEng": "Country A’s inflationary (output) gap is narrowed while the general price level increases. Which of the following\n    best explains the above changes?\n\n           A.    The transportation cost of raw materials increases.\n           B.    Country A’s production technology improves.\n           C.    The government provides subsidies to companies that invest in building factories.\n           D.    The government reduces the living allowance for the elderly.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    When the transportation cost of raw materials increases, the production cost of firms will increase and\n    short run aggregate supply will decrease. The aggregate output will decrease, narrowing the inflationary\n    (output) gap, while the general price level will increase.\n    Option B is incorrect. Improvement in production technology will increase short run aggregate supply\n    and long run aggregate supply. The general price level will decrease.\n    Option C is incorrect. When the government provides subsidies to companies that invest in building\n    factories, companies will increase their investment expenditure and aggregate demand will increase. The\n    inflationary (output) gap will be widened and the general price level will increase.\n\n    Option D is incorrect. The government reducing the living allowance for the elderly will reduce their\n    disposable income, and private consumption expenditure will decrease. Aggregate demand will decrease,\n    narrowing the inflationary (output) gap. However, the general price level will decrease.",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/36/ae-p1-31.jpg",
      "originalQuestionImageEng": "originals/36/qe-p1-31.jpg",
