      "questionTextEng": "The stock market in Country A has been booming recently, and therefore people are buying more locally produced\n    goods. Which of the following would offset the effect of the above event on aggregate output in the short run?\n\n           A.    Many manufacturers suspend production due to severe flooding.\n           B.    A billionaire funds the construction of a new university.\n           C.    A large-scale strike in Country A comes to an end.\n           D.    The government lowers the general sales tax rate.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    When people buy more locally produced goods, private consumption expenditure will increase and\n    aggregate demand will increase. In the short run, aggregate output will increase.\n    Option A is correct. When production is suspended, short run aggregate supply will decrease and\n    aggregate output will decrease, thereby offsetting the effect of the booming stock market on aggregate\n    output in the short run.\n    Option B is incorrect. When a billionaire funds the construction of a new university, investment\n    expenditure will increase. Aggregate demand will increase and aggregate output will increase further.\n    Option C is incorrect. When a large-scale strike in Country A comes to an end, short run aggregate\n    supply will increase, and aggregate output will increase further in the short run.\n    Option D is incorrect. When the government lowers the general sales tax rate, short run aggregate\n    supply will increase, and aggregate output will increase further in the short run.",
