      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/36/q-p1-38.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/36/a-p1-38.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Study the following information about the banking system of a country. The public always hold $100 million in\n    cash.\n\n                    Monetary base                             $600 million\n                    Money supply                             $1,100 million\n                    Excess reserves                           $100 million\n\n    Based on the above information, which of the following statements is CORRECT?\n\n           A.    The required reserves are $500 million.\n           B.    The actual banking multiplier is 2.\n           C.    If the public withdraw $50 million from the banking system, the excess reserves will immediately\n                 drop by $50 million.\n           D.    If the banks lend out all their excess reserves, the money supply will increase by $200 million.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    Monetary base = Cash in public circulation + Bank reserves\n    Bank reserves = $(600 – 100) million = $500 million\n    Money supply = Cash in public circulation + Bank deposits\n    Bank deposits = $(1,100 – 100) million = $1,000 million\n    Required reserve ratio = [(Actual reserves – Excess reserves) / Bank deposits] × 100%\n    = $[(500 – 100) million / $1,000 million] × 100% = 40%\n    Option B is correct.\n    Actual reserve ratio = (Actual reserves / Total deposits) × 100%\n    Actual reserve ratio = ($500 million / $1,000 million) × 100% = 50%\n    Actual banking multiplier = 1 / Actual reserve ratio = 1 / 50% = 2\n    Option A is incorrect. Required reserves = $1,000 million × 40% = $400 million\n    Option C is incorrect. If the public withdraw $50 million from the banking system, bank reserves will\n    become $450 million and bank deposits will become $950 million immediately. Required reserves will\n    be $380 million (= $950 million × 40%) and excess reserves will be $70 million (= $450 million – $380\n    million). The excess reserves will immediately drop by $30 million.\n    Option D is incorrect. If the banks lend out all their excess reserves, bank deposits will be $1,250\n    million [= $500 million × (1 / 40%)]. The new money supply will increase by $250 million to $1,350\n    million.",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/36/ae-p1-38.jpg",
      "originalQuestionImageEng": "originals/36/qe-p1-38.jpg",
