      "questionTextEng": "Climate change has led to huge disasters that hit people all over the world. To encourage the development of\n                                                          renewable energy, some environmental groups suggest converting agricultural land into solar farms. The\n                                                          following are some views on the proposal:\n\n                                                           The representative of an    Converting agricultural land into solar farms can help reduce reliance on fossil\n                                                           environmental group:        fuels, thereby reducing carbon emissions and helping alleviate climate change\n                                                                                       problems.\n                                                           A government official:      If more agricultural land is converted into solar farms, the consumer surplus in\n                                                                                       the market of crops will be affected.\n\n                                                          (a)   Explain whether the statement of the representative of an environmental group is a positive statement\n                                                                or a normative statement.                                                                   (2 marks)\n\n                                                          (b) Refer to the view of the government official. With the aid of a supply-demand diagram, explain the\n                                                              change in the consumer surplus in the market of crops.                                  (5 marks)\n\n                                                          Suppose the government provides a per-unit subsidy to agricultural landowners who convert agricultural\n                                                          land into solar farms. The amount of subsidy is calculated based on the number of solar power panels put\n                                                          into operation.\n\n                                                          (c)   Refer to the view of the representative of an environmental group. In terms of externality, explain how\n                                                                the subsidy could improve economic efficiency.                                                (4 marks)",
