      "questionTextEng": "To boost the birth rate, the South Korean government increased the amount of cash subsidies provided to\n                                                           families with babies aged under two years old in 2024.\n\n                                                          (a)   Explain whether the cash subsidies are included in the calculation of South Korea’s government\n                                                                consumption expenditure in 2024.                                                      (2 marks)\n\n                                                          (b) An economics student stated, ‘The provision of these cash subsidies may lower the general price level\n                                                              in South Korea after 20 years.’ With the aid of an AS-AD diagram, explain under what condition the\n                                                              student’s statement would be correct.                                                      (7 marks)\n\n                                                          (c)   To encourage childbirth, the South Korean government also announced a new scheme that allows\n                                                                Filipino domestic workers to work in South Korea. Explain how this scheme will affect the price\n                                                                elasticity of demand for local domestic workers in South Korea.                      (3 marks)",
