      "questionTextEng": "In 2024, many businesses said that Hong Kong’s retail market was weak, which raised public concerns.\n\n                                                          Source A: Data on Hong Kong’s gross domestic product (GDP) and total retail sales in the first and second\n                                                          quarters of 2024\n\n                                                                                900,000\n                                                                                800,000                 767,455                                  757,273\n\n                                                                                700,000\n                                                                （HK$ million）\n\n                                                                                600,000\n                                                                                500,000\n                                                                                400,000\n                                                                                300,000\n                                                                                200,000\n                                                                                                        101,444                                   90,022\n                                                                                100,000\n                                                                                     0\n                                                                                                           Q1                                       Q2\n\n                                                                                                                                2024\n\n                                                                                                 GDP at current market prices           Total retail sales\n\n                                                          (Source: Census and Statistics Department, HKSAR Government)\n\n                                                          Source B: News extract about Hong Kong’s retail industry\n                                                             The weak retail market has led to a decrease in both the rent and prices of some shop premises in\n                                                             Hong Kong’s commercial districts. An owner said that the value of his premises has significantly\n                                                             declined compared to last year.\n\n                                                          Source C: Some views on Hong Kong’s retail industry\n                                                                                                          The downturn in Hong Kong’s retail market is due to prices of\n                                                                                                          the same products being higher in Hong Kong than in nearby\n                                                                                                          regions, causing people to travel to those regions for shopping.\n                                                                                 A commentator\n                                                                                                          Many store owners have signed rental contracts. As the cost of\n                                                                                                          breaking these contracts is high, store owners may choose to\n                                                                                                          continue operating to minimise losses even in a weak retail\n                                                                  A local retail store owner              market.\n                                                                                                          Some shop premises remain vacant in the market at the current\n                                                                                                          level of rent. I would only consider opening a store if the rent of\n                                                                                                          the shop premises were lowered.\n                                                                A person who would like to\n                                                                       open a store\n\n                                                           (a)   Refer to Source A. Describe and explain whether the importance of Hong Kong’s retail industry\n                                                                 relative to the GDP of Hong Kong increased or decreased in the first half of 2024.        (2 marks)\n\n                                                           (b)   State ONE reason to explain why the contribution of Hong Kong’s retail industry to Hong Kong’s\n                                                                 GDP at current market prices in the second quarter of 2024 may be less than HK$90,022 million.\n                                                                                                                                                           (2 marks)\n\n                                                           (c)   Refer to Source B. Explain how the change in the value of the premises will affect Hong Kong’s\n                                                                 aggregate demand.                                                                          (2 marks)\n\n                                                           (d)   With reference to the view of the commentator in Source C, explain why the opportunity cost for\n                                                                 Hong Kong residents of buying goods in nearby regions may not be lower than that of buying the\n                                                                 same goods in Hong Kong.                                                                   (3 marks)\n\n                                                           For part (e), candidates are required to present their answer in essay form. Criteria for marking will include\n                                                           use of sources and economic theories, relevant content, logical presentation and clarity of expression.\n\n                                                           (e)   Suppose there are two proposals to boost Hong Kong’s retail market.\n                                                                  Proposal I    to distribute to all residents consumption vouchers which can only be used in retail\n                                                                                stores in Hong Kong\n                                                                  Proposal II to provide a rent subsidy to retail stores in Hong Kong\n\n                                                                 With reference to the above sources and your own knowledge in Economics, discuss the effects of the\n                                                                 above two proposals on Hong Kong, including:\n\n                                                                 - profit-maximising output of local retail stores\n                                                                 - income distribution\n                                                                 - general price level\n                                                                 (For simplicity, assume the retail sales market in Hong Kong is perfectly competitive.)\n                                                                                                                                                              (14 marks)",
