      "questionTextEng": "Josie is considering renting an industrial building unit to set up a studio for producing short films for her personal\n     social media channel. Otherwise, she will make short films at home. Which of the following will lower Josie’s\n     cost of renting an industrial building unit to make short films?\n\n           (1)   The landlord lowers the rent of the unit.\n           (2)   The tenant next to the unit often makes noise, which affects the quality of Josie’s short films.\n           (3)   Due to a lack of soundproofing equipment, Josie is often disturbed by noise when making short films\n                 at home.\n\n           A.    (1) and (2) only\n           B.    (1) and (3) only\n           C.    (2) and (3) only\n           D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n     (1) is correct. The monetary cost of renting an industrial building unit to make short films will decrease.\n     (3) is correct. This will reduce the value of the highest-valued option forgone (i.e. making short films at\n     home) and the cost of renting an industrial building unit to make short films will decrease.\n     (2) is incorrect. This will reduce the value of the chosen option, without affecting the highest-valued\n     option forgone.",
