      "questionTextEng": "On 4 August 2024, the Leisure and Cultural Services Department (LCSD) held ‘Sport For All Day 2024’, on\n     which most leisure facilities under LCSD, including public swimming pools, badminton courts and basketball\n     courts were opened for free use. The sessions for free use of facilities were allocated by drawing lots. The above\n     case is related to the __________ question(s) in economics.\n\n           A.    ‘what to produce’\n           B.    ‘for whom to produce’\n           C.    ‘how to produce’ and ‘for whom to produce’\n           D.    ‘what to produce’ and ‘for whom to produce’",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n     Opening most leisure facilities under the LCSD for free use on ‘Sport For All Day 2024’ is about who\n     can use the facilities while allocating the sessions for free use of facilities by drawing lots is about how\n     to distribute the facilities to people in society. Therefore, the case is related to the ‘for whom to produce’\n     problem.\n     Option D is incorrect. The types and quantities of facilities provided by the LCSD on the ‘Sport For All\n     Day 2024’ did not change, so it is not related to the ‘what to produce’ question.",
