      "questionTextEng": "The table below shows the production plan of a firm. The only two inputs required for production are labour and\n     machines.\n\n                  Labour (units)                     Machines (units)                  Average product (units)\n                       5                                   3                                     2\n                       5                                   4                                     4\n                       5                                   5                                     7\n                       5                                   6                                     X\n\n      If the above data illustrates the law of diminishing marginal returns, the value of X ____________.\n\n            A.    must be smaller than 9\n            B.    must be larger than 9\n            C.    can be 9\n            D.    can be 19",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n        Labour         Machines        Average product           Total product            Marginal product\n         (units)        (units)            (units)                  (units)                   (units)\n           5                 3                2                          6                         -\n           5                 4                4                          16                       10\n           5                 5                7                          35                       19\n           5                 6        X must be smaller       must be smaller than      must be smaller than\n                                       than 9 (= 54 / 6)        54 (= 35 + 19)                   19\n     Given the data illustrate the law of diminishing marginal returns, the marginal product of machines\n     begins to diminish when the 6th unit of machines is employed. The marginal product of the 6th unit of\n     machines must be smaller than 19 units. The total product must be smaller than 54 units and the average\n     product (X) must be smaller than 9 units.",
