      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/37/q-p1-10.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/37/a-p1-10.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The table below shows the cost-output relationship of a competitive firm.\n\n                   Output (units)                     1             2              3              4\n                   Average variable cost ($)          3             4              5              6\n\n     Suppose the profit-maximising output level is 3 units and the fixed cost at 3 units is $3. The producer surplus of\n     the firm is __________ while the profit is __________.\n\n            A.    $3 ... $3\n            B.    $3 ... $6\n            C.    $6 ... $3\n            D.    $6 ... $6",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n      Output (units)                    1             2             3              4\n      Average variable cost ($)         3             4             5              6\n      Total variable cost ($)           3             8             15             24\n      Total fixed cost ($)              3             3             3              3\n      Total cost ($)                    6             11            18             27\n      Marginal cost ($)                 3             5             7              9\n    Producer surplus = Total revenue – Total variable cost = ($7 × 3) – $15 = $6\n    At the profit-maximising output level (3 units), marginal revenue equals marginal cost ($7).\n    Profit = Total revenue – Total cost = ($7 × 3) – $18 = $3",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/37/ae-p1-10.jpg",
