      "questionTextEng": "The Hong Kong Housing Authority sells newly constructed flats under the Home Ownership Scheme (HOS).\n    Although some citizens meet the eligibility criteria and are willing to pay the selling price, they are unable to\n    purchase a flat due to being unsuccessful in the lottery.\n\n     From the information above, we can infer that the quantity supplied of the newly constructed HOS flats is\n     ____________, while their selling price is ____________.\n\n            A.    smaller than the quantity demanded ... lower than the equilibrium price\n            B.    smaller than the quantity demanded ... higher than the equilibrium price\n            C.    larger than the quantity demanded ... lower than the equilibrium price\n            D.    larger than the quantity demanded ... higher than the equilibrium price",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n     There is an excess demand for newly constructed HOS flats, so the quantity supplied is smaller than the\n    quantity demanded and the selling price is lower than the equilibrium price.",
