      "inlineDiagrams": "diagrams/MT37-P1-12.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The following is the demand-supply diagram of Country A’s catering service market. E is the original equilibrium\n    point.\n\n                            Unit price\n                                                             S1\n                                                                     S0\n                                                    E3\n                                                                          S2\n\n                                         E2         E           E4\n\n                                                   E1\n                                                                               D2\n                                                                     D0\n                                                           D1\n                                                                             Quantity\n                                0\n\n      Suppose the government of Country A increases the quota for imported foreign workers in the catering industry.\n      At the same time, a newly completed theme park in Country A attracts many tourists to visit Country A. The new\n      equilibrium point will be at ________.\n\n            A.    E1\n            B.    E2\n            C.    E3\n            D.    E4",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    When the government of Country A increases the quota for imported foreign workers in the catering\n    industry, the equilibrium wage rate for workers in the catering industry will decrease. The production\n    cost of the catering industry will decrease and supply will increase. The supply curve will shift to the\n    right from S0 to S2.\n    More tourists visiting Country A will lead to an increase in demand for catering services. The demand\n    curve will shift to the right from D0 to D2.\n    Therefore, the new equilibrium point will be at E4.",
