      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    Total subsidy = Per-unit subsidy × Quantity transacted after the subsidy\n    When the per-unit subsidy on good X is halved and the total subsidy granted by the government is also\n    halved, this implies that the quantity transacted remains unchanged.\n    Option A is correct. If the elasticity of demand for good X is equal to 0 (i.e. demand for good X is\n    perfectly inelastic), the quantity transacted will remain unchanged when the per-unit subsidy is reduced.\n    Options B, C and D are incorrect. The quantity transacted will decrease when the per-unit subsidy is\n    halved in all three situations.",
