      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    Q3 is an ineffective quota, while Q1 is an effective quota.\n    When the quota is lowered, the quantity transacted will decrease from Q2 to Q1 and the market price will\n    increase from P2 to P3. The new consumers’ total expenditure is (P3 × Q1) while the original consumers’\n    total expenditure is (P2 × Q2). Consumers’ total expenditure will decrease by (P2 × Q2) − (P3 × Q1).\n    (1) is incorrect. After the imposition of the effective quota, the supply curve will be kinked and become\n    vertical at Q1. At Q1, quantity supplied equals quantity demanded and the market is at equilibrium.",
