      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    The imposition of a per-unit sales tax will cause the supply to decrease and the price of good X will\n    increase. The decrease in the price of the substitute for good X will cause the demand for good X to\n    decrease and the price of good X will decrease. The effect of the imposition of a per-unit sales tax on the\n    price is offset by the effect of the decrease in demand on the price.\n    (2) is correct. As both the supply of and demand for good X decrease, the quantity transacted will\n    decrease.\n    (1) is incorrect. Since the quantity transacted of good X decreases, i.e. to fewer than 40 units, the tax\n    revenue must be smaller than $160.\n    (3) is incorrect. At the new equilibrium, marginal benefit is higher than marginal cost. There is a\n    deadweight loss.",
