      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/37/q-p1-18.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/37/a-p1-18.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The market of air transport in Hong Kong can be classified as an oligopoly. Which of the following statements\n      about the market of air transport in Hong Kong are CORRECT?\n\n           (1)   The airlines engage in non-price competition.\n           (2)   Different airlines provide homogeneous services.\n           (3)   A few airlines have significantly larger market shares than the others.\n           (4)   The airlines are interdependent in their pricing strategies.\n\n           A.    (1) and (3) only\n           B.    (2) and (4) only\n           C.    (1), (3) and (4) only\n           D.    (2), (3) and (4) only\n\n1 9 . Refer to the following supply-demand diagram for good X.\n\n                            Unit price\n                                                              S\n\n                              P1\n\n                              P2\n\n                                                               D\n\n                               0                                         Quantity\n\n      If the government lowers the price ceiling from P1 to P2, the __________ will decrease.\n\n           (1)   producer surplus\n           (2)   total social surplus\n           (3)   deadweight loss\n           (4)   total sales revenue\n\n           A.    (1) and (2) only\n           B.    (3) and (4) only\n           C.    (1), (2) and (4) only\n           D.    (1), (3) and (4) only",
