      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/37/a-p1-22.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following will raise the Gini coefficient based on post-tax post-social transfer monthly household\n      income in Hong Kong?\n\n            (1)   cancelling the rates concession\n            (2)   increasing the rent for public rental housing units\n            (3)   decreasing the marginal tax rates for the salaries tax\n\n            A.    (1) and (2) only\n            B.    (1) and (3) only\n            C.    (2) and (3) only\n            D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n     (2) is correct. People living in public rental housing units generally have low income. If the government\n     increases the rent of public rental housing units, their income after taxes and social transfers will\n     decrease while people with high income will not be affected. The income gap between the rich and the\n     poor will widen. The Gini coefficient based on post-tax post-social transfer monthly household income\n     will increase.\n     (3) is correct. Decreasing the marginal tax rates for the salaries tax will allow high-income earners to\n     pay less tax while low-income earners will not be affected. The income gap between the rich and the\n     poor will widen and the Gini coefficient based on post-tax post-social transfer monthly household\n     income will increase.\n     (1) is incorrect. The rates concession mainly benefits people with high income. If the government\n     cancels the rates concession, their income after taxes and social transfers will decrease, while people\n     with low income will not be affected. The income gap between the rich and the poor will be narrowed\n     and the Gini coefficient based on post-tax post-social transfer monthly household income will decrease.",
