      "questionTextEng": "The following diagram shows the Lorenz curves of Country A and Country B.\n\n                       100\n                                                                            Lorenz curve of Country A\n\n                                                                            Lorenz curve of Country B\n\n             Cumulative\n            percentage of\n           original income\n\n                         0                                      100\n                                    Cumulative percentage\n                                       of households\n\n      Based on the above information, which of the following statements about the two countries is CORRECT?\n\n           A.    The tax system of Country A is likely to be regressive while that of Country B is likely to be\n                 progressive.\n           B.    The gross domestic product of Country A is lower than that of Country B.\n           C.    Compared to Country B, the living standard of low-income households in Country A is lower.\n           D.    The Gini coefficient of Country A is higher than that of Country B.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    Compared with Country B, Country A’s Lorenz curve is further away from the line of perfect income\n    equality. The area between the line of perfect income equality and the Lorenz curve is larger, so the Gini\n    coefficient of Country A is higher.\n    Option A is incorrect. We cannot infer the tax systems of the two countries from the Lorenz curves\n    based on pre-tax income.\n    Options B and C are incorrect. The information does not reflect the level of GDP or the living standard\n    of people at different income levels.",
