      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/37/a-p1-25.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The following table shows some data for an economy in a certain year.\n\n                                                                    Year 1          Year 2\n                             Change in the price level               2%              −3%\n                             Change in population size               0%              3%\n                             Change in nominal GDP                   1%              1%\n\n       Which of the following statements about the economy is CORRECT?\n\n             A.    Real GDP decreased in year 1 and increased in year 2.\n             B.    Per capita nominal GDP decreased in year 1 and increased in year 2.\n             C.    Per capita real GDP decreased in year 2.\n             D.    The inflation rate increased in year 1 and decreased in year 2.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    Implicit price deflator of GDP = (Nominal GDP / Real GDP) × 100\n    In year 1, the percentage change in nominal GDP is 1%, while the percentage change in the price level\n    is 2%. Since the percentage increase in nominal GDP is smaller than the percentage increase in the price\n    level, real GDP decreased in year 1.\n    In year 2, the percentage change in nominal GDP is 1%, while the percentage change in the price level\n    is –3%. Since nominal GDP increased and the price level decreased, real GDP increased in year 2.\n    Option B is incorrect.\n    In year 1, since the percentage increase in nominal GDP (1%) is greater than the percentage increase in\n    the population (0%), per capita nominal GDP increased.\n    In year 2, since the percentage increase in nominal GDP (1%) is smaller than the percentage increase in\n    the population (3%), per capita nominal GDP decreased.\n    Option C is incorrect.\n    1 + Growth rate of real GDP = (1 + Growth rate of nominal GDP) / (1 + Growth rate of price level)\n    In year 2:\n    1 + Growth rate of real GDP = (1 + 1%) / [(1 + (–3%)]\n    Growth rate of real GDP = 4%\n    As the percentage increase in real GDP (4%) is larger than the percentage increase in population size\n    (3%), per capita real GDP increased in year 2.\n    Option D is incorrect. There is insufficient information to determine whether the inflation rate in year 1\n    increased or decreased compared to the previous year.",
