      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    The professor worked in Hong Kong for less than a year, so he/she is not a resident of Hong Kong.\n    Therefore, the salary he/she earned would be regarded as factor income earned by a non-resident within\n    the economic territory and should be deducted from the GDP of Hong Kong to calculate its GNI.\n    Options B and C are incorrect. They would be regarded as factor income earned by residents outside the\n    economic territory and should be added to the GDP of Hong Kong to calculate its GNI.\n    Option D is incorrect. The fee reflects the value of production of a resident producing unit and would be\n    included in the GDP and GNI of Hong Kong.",
