      "questionTextEng": "An economy initially has an inflationary (output) gap. Which of the following would widen the inflationary\n    (output) gap?\n\n           A.    The central bank prints more money.\n           B.    The government raises the business registration fee.\n           C.    The transport cost of raw materials increases.\n           D.    A major trading partner of the economy experiences an economic recession.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    When the central bank prints more money, the money supply will increase and the interest rate will\n     decrease. Consumption and investment will increase. Aggregate demand will increase and the\n     inflationary (output) gap will widen.\n     Option B is incorrect. When the government raises the business registration fee, investment\n     expenditures will decrease. Aggregate demand will decrease and the inflationary (output) gap will be\n     narrowed.\n     Option C is incorrect. The increase in the transport cost of raw materials will cause the short run\n     aggregate supply to decrease, and the inflationary (output) gap will be narrowed.\n     Option D is incorrect. When the major trading partner of the economy experiences an economic\n     recession, net exports will decrease. Aggregate demand will decrease and the inflationary (output) gap\n     will be narrowed.",
