      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/37/a-p1-31.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following transactions will lead to an increase in Hong Kong’s money supply M2?\n\n           A.    Miss Li withdraws HK$10,000 from her time deposit account in a licensed bank and holds it in cash.\n           B.    Miss Wong deposits HK$500,000 in cash into a time deposit account in a restricted licence bank.\n           C.    Mr. Cheung transfers HK$10,000 from his savings account in a licensed bank to his current account in\n                 the same bank.\n           D.    Mr. Chan withdraws HK$10,000 from a time deposit account in a restricted licence bank and uses the\n                 amount to purchase a negotiable certificate of deposit issued by a licensed bank.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n     M2 = M1 + Customers’ savings and time deposits with licensed banks + Negotiable certificates of\n     deposit (NCDs) issued by licensed banks held outside the banking sector\n     When Mr. Chan withdraws HK$10,000 from a time deposit account in a restricted licence bank and uses\n     the amount to purchase an NCD issued by a licensed bank, this will increase M2 by HK$10,000.\n     Option A is incorrect. When Miss Li withdraws HK$10,000 from her time deposit account in a licensed\n     bank and holds it in cash, M2 will not change.\n     Option B is incorrect. When Miss Wong deposits HK$500,000 in cash into a time deposit account in a\n     restricted licence bank, M2 will decrease.\n     Option C is incorrect. When Mr. Cheung transfers HK$10,000 from his savings account in a licensed\n     bank to his current account in the same bank, M2 will not change.",
