      "questionTextEng": "Refer to the following balance sheet of a banking system. The required reserve ratio of the banking system is 25%\n    and the public always hold $50 in cash.\n\n                                    Assets ($)                         Liabilities ($)\n                       Reserves                      500    Deposits                     1 ,2 0 0\n                       Loans                         700\n\n    Suppose some banks lend out their excess reserves. After deposit creation, the amount of deposits in the banking\n    system is $1,500. Which of the following statements about the banking system is CORRECT?\n\n           A.    The money supply of the economy becomes $1,500.\n           B.    The excess reserves of the banking system become $125.\n           C.    The reserves of the banking system become $800.\n           D.    The monetary base of the economy becomes $425.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    After deposit creation, the amount of deposits in the banking system is $1,500.\n    New excess reserves = ($500 – $1,500 × 25%) = $125\n    Option A is incorrect.\n    Money supply = Cash in public circulation + Bank deposits = $50 + $1,500 = $1,550\n    Option C is incorrect. The reserves of the banking system remain unchanged at $500.\n    Option D is incorrect.\n    Monetary base = Cash in public circulation + Bank reserves = $50 + $500 = $550",
