      "questionTextEng": "Study the following information.\n\n                          Monetary base                                 $150 million\n                          Cash in public circulation                    $70 million\n                          Required reserve ratio                           20%\n                          Actual banking multiplier                          4\n\n    Which of the following statements is CORRECT?\n\n           A.    The amount of excess reserves is $80 million.\n           B.    The amount of loans is $240 million.\n           C.    The amount of deposits is $400 million.\n           D.    The amount of money supply is $470 million.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    Reserves = Monetary base – Cash in public circulation = $150 million – $70 million = $80 million\n    Deposits = Reserves × Actual banking multiplier = $80 million × 4 = $320 million\n    Required reserves = Deposits × Required reserve ratio = $320 million × 20% = $64 million\n    Excess reserves = Actual reserves – Required reserves = $80 million – $64 million = $16 million\n    Loans = Deposits – Reserves = $320 million – $80 million = $240 million\n    Money supply = Cash in public circulation + Bank deposits = $70 million + $320 million\n    = $390 million",
