      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    Real rate of return on holding money = Nominal rate of return on holding money ‒ Actual inflation rate\n    = 0% ‒ (‒1%) = 1%\n    Therefore, the real rate of return on holding money is greater than the nominal rate of return on holding\n    money.\n    Option A is incorrect. Nominal rate of return of holding money = 0%\n    Option B is incorrect.\n    Actual real interest rate = Nominal interest rate – Actual inflation rate = 5% – (‒1%) = 6%\n    Option C is incorrect. Expected real interest rate = Nominal interest rate – Expected inflation rate\n    The question does not provide information on the expected inflation rate.",
