      "questionTextEng": "Suppose the central bank continues to sell government bonds to the public. According to the classical quantity\n    theory of money,\n\n           A.    the velocity of circulation of money will decrease.\n           B.    the economy will experience deflation.\n           C.    the real output will increase.\n           D.    the nominal output will remain unchanged.\n\n3 6 . The following table shows some data for an economy.\n\n                                                              Number of persons (’000)\n                          Aged 15 or above                            9,050\n                          Employed persons                            7,500\n                          Underemployed persons                        120\n                          Unemployed persons                           400\n\n    Based on the above data,\n\n           A.    the labour force is 8,020,000.\n           B.    the employment rate is 96.46%.\n           C.    the unemployment rate is 5.06%.\n           D.    the underemployment rate is 1.33%.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    Quantity theory of money: MV = PY, where M = money supply, V = velocity of circulation of money, P\n    = price level and Y = real output.\n    Assume V and Y are both constant.\n    When the central bank continues to sell government bonds to the public, the money supply (M) will\n    decrease continuously, causing the price level (P) to decrease continuously, i.e. there will be deflation.",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/37/ae-p1-35.jpg",
      "originalQuestionImageEng": "originals/37/qe-p1-35.jpg",
      "stemPatterns": [
        "（中央銀行公開市場操作）根據古典貨幣數量論，下列哪項正確？"
      ]
