      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/37/q-p1-38.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/37/a-p1-38.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "There have been incidents of cyberattacks targeting electronic payment tools in Country A, causing many citizens\n    to stop using these tools due to concerns over data leakage. Which of the following can offset the effects of the\n    incident on the economy’s output level and interest rate at the same time in the short run?\n\n            A.    More enterprises change from monthly payments to weekly payments.\n            B.    The government increases the allowance for the salaries tax.\n            C.    The government issues more government bonds to the public.\n            D.    The risk of investing in the stock market increases.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    When the citizens stop using the electronic payment tools, the transaction demand for money will\n    increase, causing the interest rate to increase. Consumption and investment will decrease. Aggregate\n    demand will decrease and the output level will decrease.\n    Option A is correct. When more enterprises change from monthly payments to weekly payments, the\n    transaction demand for money will decrease and the interest rate will decrease. Consumption and\n    investment will increase, aggregate demand will increase and the output level will increase.\n    Option B is incorrect. Increasing the allowance for the salaries tax rate will raise people’s disposable\n    income, so private consumption expenditure will increase and aggregate demand will increase. The\n    output level will increase. However, when people’s disposable income increases, the transaction demand\n    for money will increase and the interest rate will further increase.\n    Option C is incorrect. When the government issues more government bonds to the public, the money\n    supply will decrease and the interest rate will increase. Consumption and investment will decrease.\n    Aggregate demand will decrease and the output level will further decrease.\n    Option D is incorrect. When the risk of investing in the stock market increases, the asset demand for\n    money will increase, causing the interest rate to further increase. Consumption and investment will\n    decrease. Aggregate demand will decrease and the output level will further decrease.",
