      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/37/a-p1-40.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following measures may increase the aggregate output and the balance of payments surplus at the\n    same time?\n\n            A.    canceling the tax incentives for foreign investors\n            B.    increasing the amount of transfer payments\n            C.    holding more international competitions to attract tourists\n            D.    importing more raw materials from foreign countries to replace local production",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    Holding more international competitions to attract tourists will increase exports of services. Aggregate\n    demand will increase and aggregate output will increase.\n    When exports of services increase, the balance of invisible trade will improve and the balance of\n    payments surplus will increase.\n    Option A is incorrect. Cancelling the tax incentives for foreign investors may lead to a reduction in their\n    investments. Aggregate demand will decrease and aggregate output will decrease.\n    When foreign investors reduce their investment, capital inflow will decrease. The balance of payments\n    surplus will decrease.\n\n    Option B is incorrect. When the government increases the amount of transfer payments, people’s\n    disposable income will increase. Private consumption expenditure will increase and aggregate demand\n    will increase. Aggregate output will increase.\n    When people’s disposable income increases, their demand for imports will increase. The balance of\n    visible trade will worsen and the balance of payments surplus will decrease.\n    Option D is incorrect. Importing more raw materials from foreign countries will lead to an increase in\n    imports of goods. Aggregate demand will decrease and aggregate output will decrease.\n    When imports of goods increase, the balance of visible trade will worsen. The balance of payments\n    surplus will decrease.",
