      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/37/a-p1-41.jpg",
      "inlineDiagrams": "diagrams/MT37-P1-41.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The diagram below shows the money demand and money supply curves of an economy. The original equilibrium\n    point is at E.\n\n                             Nominal\n                           interest rate       Ms1 Ms0 Ms2\n\n                                                 A\n\n                                                           B\n                                                       E\n                                                 D\n                                                           C\n                                                                          Md2\n\n                                                           Md1      Md0\n                                                                                Quantity of money\n                                0\n\n    Suppose the government increases the discount rate and the liquidity of other interest-bearing assets increases. The\n    new equilibrium point will be at __________.\n\n           A.    A\n           B.    B\n           C.    C\n           D.    D",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    Increasing the discount rate will cause the money supply to decrease, and the money supply curve will\n    shift to the left to Ms1.\n    When the liquidity of other interest-bearing assets increases, the asset demand for money will decrease.\n    The money demand curve will shift to the left to Md1.",
