      "questionTextEng": "The following table shows the change in the exchange rate between the Hong Kong dollar (HKD) and the Japanese\n    yen (JPY).\n\n                               2024                            Exchange rate\n                            3 January                        HKD 1 = JPY 18.18\n                              3 June                         HKD 1 = JPY 20.12\n\n    Under the linked exchange rate system, the above change in the exchange rate will lead to\n\n           A.    a decrease in the number of Hong Kong tourists to Japan.\n           B.    a decrease in the total value of Japanese goods exported to Hong Kong (in terms of HKD).\n           C.    an increase in the competitiveness of Hong Kong goods exported to Japan.\n           D.    a decrease in the total value of Hong Kong goods exported to Japan (in terms of HKD).\n\n                                                EN D O F PAP E R",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    The Hong Kong dollar appreciates against the Japanese yen. Given the price of Hong Kong goods\n    remains unchanged, Hong Kong’s exports will become more expensive. Japanese importers will buy\n    fewer Hong Kong goods. Demand for Hong Kong’s exports will decrease and the quantity transacted\n    will decrease. The total value of Hong Kong’s exports to Japan (in terms of HKD) will decrease.\n    Option A is incorrect. As the Hong Kong dollar appreciates against the Japanese yen, the price of\n    Japanese goods and services (in terms of HKD) will decrease. The cost of travelling to Japan (in terms\n    of HKD) will decrease and so more Hong Kong tourists will visit Japan.\n    Option B is incorrect. The price of goods exported from Japan to Hong Kong will decrease (in terms of\n    HKD), resulting in an increase in the quantity of Japanese goods exported to Hong Kong. The total\n    value of Japanese goods exported to Hong Kong (in terms of HKD) may increase or decrease,\n    depending on the price elasticity of demand.\n    Option C is incorrect. The price of Hong Kong’s exports to Japan will increase (in terms of JPY), so the\n    competitiveness of Hong Kong goods exported to Japan will decrease.",
