      "questionTextEng": "The table below shows Country A’s implicit price deflator of GDP in 2022 and 2023.\n                                                                                       Year                  Implicit price deflator of GDP\n                                                                                       2022                              101.3\n                                                                                       2023                              105.6\n\n                                                           (a)   Calculate the inflation rate of Country A in 2023.                                            (1 mark)\n\n                                                           (b)   The following table shows the money supply in Country A.\n\n                                                                                       Year                    Money supply ($ million)\n                                                                                       2022                            8,290,000\n                                                                                       2023                            8,260,000\n\n                                                                 According to the quantity theory of money, explain under what condition the above change in the\n                                                                 money supply would result in an increase in the general price level in the short run.      (3 marks)\n\n                                                           (c)   Mr. Chan is a resident of Country A. In 2022, Mr. Chan deposited an amount into his time deposit\n                                                                 account and earned a fixed interest rate. Supposing he did not expect any change in the price level\n                                                                 from 2022 to 2023, would he gain or lose during the above period? Explain.                    (2 marks)",
