      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/37/a-p2-06.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Since the year of assessment 2024-25, a two-tiered standard rates regime is implemented for salaries tax and\n                                                           tax under personal assessment.\n\n                                                                                                                                 New two-tiered standard\n                                                                          Net income                   Existing system\n                                                                                                                                      rates regime\n                                                                     On the first $5 million                                              15%\n                                                                                                        15%\n                                                                           Remainder                                                      16%\n                                                                (Source: Inland Revenue Department, HKSAR Government)\n\n                                                          (a)   Explain whether the salaries tax and tax under personal assessment are a direct tax or an indirect tax in\n                                                                Hong Kong.                                                                                     (2 marks)\n\n                                                          (b) Evaluate the above change in the tax system in terms of ONE principle of taxation put forward by\n                                                              Adam Smith.                                                                             (2 marks)\n\n                                                          (c)   Explain ONE possible undesirable effect of the above change in the tax system on the Hong Kong\n                                                                economy as a whole.                                                                    (2 marks)",
