      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/37/a-p2-07.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The table below shows the amount of goods that can be produced with 1 unit of resources in Country A and\n                                                          Country B respectively.\n\n                                                                                              Coffee (units)                     Clothing (units)\n                                                                        Country A                   40               OR                 50\n                                                                        Country B                   10               OR                 20\n\n                                                          (a)   Which good would Country A export according to its comparative advantage? Explain.           (3 marks)\n\n                                                          (b) Suppose the terms of trade is 1 unit of coffee = 1.5 units of clothing and Country A needs to pay 0.1\n                                                              units of imports as transportation cost per unit of exports. Calculate Country A’s gain from exporting 10\n                                                              units of the good. Show your workings.                                                          (3 marks)\n\n                                                                                                  END OF SECTION A\n\n                                                     Section B (60 marks)",
