      "questionTextEng": "The Chinese University of Hong Kong announced an increase in its University Admission Scholarships\n                                                           starting from the 2024-2025 academic year to a total amount of $35.9 million. The University Admission\n                                                           Scholarships are awarded based on students’ HKDSE results. Students with better results will receive\n                                                           scholarships of higher award values.\n\n                                                          (a)   To which type of production does a university belong?                                          (1 mark)\n\n                                                          (b) Explain whether the amount of the University Admission Scholarships provided to students would be\n                                                              included in the calculation of Hong Kong’s gross domestic product (GDP).                 (2 marks)\n\n                                                          (c)   Suppose there is a deflationary (output) gap in the Hong Kong economy. With the aid of an AS-AD\n                                                                diagram, explain how the above scholarship scheme will affect the deflationary (output) gap in the short\n                                                                run.                                                                                          (7 marks)\n\n                                                          (d) Jace was a candidate for the 2024 HKDSE Examination. She was considering her study plans. She had\n                                                              several options and her order of preference was as follows:\n\n                                                                First option:       to enroll in an arts programme abroad\n                                                                Second option:      to enroll in a law programme at the University of Hong Kong\n                                                                Third option:       to enroll in an accounting programme at the Chinese University of Hong Kong\n\n                                                                Suppose Jace was eligible to receive a University Admission Scholarship from the Chinese University\n                                                                of Hong Kong. Explain whether Jace’s opportunity cost of choosing to enroll in an arts programme\n                                                                abroad would necessarily remain unchanged when the amount of the University Admission\n                                                                Scholarships increased.                                                                   (3 marks)",
      "originalQuestionImageEng": "originals/37/qe-p2-08.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/37/ae-p2-08.jpg",
