      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/37/a-p2-09.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Greece has announced that starting from 2025, it will charge different cruise passenger fees for popular\n                                                           islands during peak, shoulder and low seasons. For example, cruise passengers who get off in Mykonos and\n                                                           Santorini during peak season will be charged 20 euros (approximately HK$170) per person.\n\n                                                          (a)   Many residents of Santorini think that the city has become overcrowded due to too many tourists.\n\n                                                                (i)   Explain, in terms of externalities, how too many tourists visiting Santorini may result in\n                                                                      inefficiency.                                                                   (3 marks)\n\n                                                                (ii) Explain how charging cruise passenger fees may improve economic efficiency.\n                                                                                                                                                             (2 marks)\n\n                                                          (b) ‘As every visitor has to pay the same fee regardless of their place of departure, the proportion of\n                                                              European visitors to Santorini is expected to decrease while the proportion of Asian visitors is expected\n                                                              to increase.’ Explain this argument using the law of demand.                                    (4 marks)\n\n                                                          (c)   Someone has pointed out that even if the cruise passenger fees are introduced, the number of tourists\n                                                                visiting Santorini during peak season may not be significantly reduced.\n\n                                                                Based on this viewpoint, what can we conclude about the price elasticity of demand and/or supply of\n                                                                trips to Santorini during peak season? Explain.                                           (3 marks)\n\n                                                          (d) Travel agencies generally pay tour guides a basic salary plus commission. From the viewpoint of the\n                                                              travel agencies, explain why a basic salary plus commission is preferable to a time rate. (2 marks)",
