      "questionTextEng": "The seafood market in Country A is perfectly competitive.\n\n                                                                                              Figure 1\n\n                                                                              Unit price\n                                                                                                                                MC: Marginal cost\n                                                                                                                    MC\n                                                                                                                                D: Demand\n\n                                                                                                                D\n                                                                                                                          Quantity\n                                                                                0\n\n                                                           (a)   Indicate the profit-maximising output and price as Qc and Pc respectively in Figure 1.        (2 marks)\n\n                                                           Later, one of the seafood producers, firm X, acquires all the other seafood producers in the market, thus\n                                                           becoming a monopolist. Suppose firm X adopts simple monopoly pricing and the marginal cost of\n                                                           production remains the same as in the perfectly competitive market.\n\n                                                           (b)   Indicate the new profit-maximising output and price as QM and PM respectively in Figure 1. (3 marks)\n\n                                                           (c)   With the aid of Figure 1, explain the effect of the change in the market structure on economic\n                                                                 efficiency.                                                                                   (4 marks)\n\n                                                           (d)   Firm X offers a 10% discount to customers aged 70 or above.\n\n                                                                 (i)   Define price discrimination and explain why this price arrangement constitutes price\n                                                                       discrimination.                                                                         (3 marks)\n\n                                                                 (ii) Suggest ONE condition for practising this type of price discrimination.                   (1 mark)\n\n                                                           (e)   Firm X requires customers to purchase the store’s delivery service when buying seafood. Name the\n                                                                 anti-competitive behaviour firm X may be engaged in. State TWO ways in which the behaviour may\n                                                                 harm consumers.                                                                           (3 marks)",
