      "inlineDiagrams": "diagrams/MT37-P2-12.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Refer to Figure 2. PPFA is the production possibility frontier of Country A.\n\n                                                                                                       Figure 2\n\n                                                                                Food (units)\n\n                                                                                 100\n\n                                                                                   80\n                                                                                                    PA\n                                                                                   60\n\n                                                                                   40\n\n                                                                                   20                                  PPFA\n\n                                                                                                                                    Computers (units)\n                                                                                    0       20    40      60      80   100\n\n                                                           Both Country A and its trading partner, Country B, produce food and computers only. Both countries have\n                                                           100 units of resources. Country B requires 1 unit of resources to produce 1 unit of food and 2.5 units of\n                                                           resources to produce 1 unit of computers.\n\n                                                           (a)   Draw the production possibility frontier of Country B (PPF B) in Figure 2.                      (1 mark)\n\n                                                           (b)   Explain which country has an absolute advantage in producing computers.                        (2 marks)\n\n                                                           (c)   PA is the production point of Country A before trade. The slope of the dotted line is the world price of\n                                                                 computers. Suppose both countries engage in trade and practise complete specialisation according to\n                                                                 their comparative advantages.\n\n                                                                 (i)   Indicate the production points of Country A and Country B after trade as PTA and PTB\n                                                                       respectively in Figure 2.                                                                 (2 marks)\n\n                                                                 (ii) Indicate Country A’s consumption possibility frontier after trade (CPFA) in Figure 2.     (2 marks)\n\n                                                                 (iii) Suppose Country A consumes the same amount of food before and after trade. Indicate the\n                                                                       consumption point (CTA), export volume and import volume of Country A after trade in Figure 2.\n                                                                                                                                                           (3 marks)\n\n                                                           (d)   Suppose Country A develops a new production technology that increases the output of food and\n                                                                 computers by the same proportion. Explain whether the direction of trade between the two countries\n                                                                 will be affected.                                                                         (2 marks)\n\n                                                           (e)   An economist of Country A states that although economic growth of Country A will improve after\n                                                                 engaging in trade, its economic development may worsen. Justify the view of the economist.\n                                                                                                                                                           (4 marks)",
