      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/38/q-p1-02.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/38/a-p1-02.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Zoe is thinking about her career plan. She has several options and her order of preference is shown below:\n\n     First option: to work as an intern at a restaurant in Japan\n     Second option: to work at a local bank\n     Third option: to work in Australia for one year through the Working Holiday Scheme\n\n     Which of the following factors would affect Zoe’s cost-benefit analysis for her choice?\n\n           (1)   The restaurant provides free meals to Zoe.\n           (2)   The bank increases the wage level of new employees.\n           (3)   Finding a job in Australia is more difficult than expected.\n\n           A.    (1) and (2) only\n           B.    (1) and (3) only\n           C.    (2) and (3) only\n           D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n     Zoe would choose the first option as the benefit of choosing the first option (the value of the first option)\n     is higher than the cost (the value of the second option).\n     (1) is correct. This would increase the value of the first option, thus affecting Zoe’s benefit of choosing\n     the first option.\n     (2) is correct. This would increase the value of the second option, thus raising Zoe’s cost of choosing the\n     first option.\n     (3) is incorrect. This would reduce the value of the third option, without affecting Zoe’s benefit or cost\n     of choosing the first option.",
