      "calculationType": "產量計算",
      "source": "模擬試卷三十八 卷一",
      "reviewedByAI": "Y",
      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/38/q-p1-13.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/38/a-p1-13.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The following table shows the relationship among input, output and cost for a firm.\n\n          Machinery (units)             Labour (units)           Total product (units)      Total production cost ($)\n                 5                           1                             5                          200\n                 5                           2                            15                          300\n                 5                           3                            24                          400\n                 5                           4                            32                          500\n                 5                           5                            39                          600\n\n      Which of the following statements about the firm is CORRECT?\n\n            A.    The law of diminishing marginal returns applies to the firm.\n            B.    The firm enjoys economies of scale.\n            C.    The optimal scale of production is 24 units.\n            D.    When the quantity of labour is 2 units, the average output of labour is the highest.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n        Machinery           Labour         Total product         Total          Marginal          Average\n           (units)           (units)          (units)      production cost       product           product\n                                                                ($)              (units)           (units)\n              5                1                 5               200                5                 5\n              5                2                15               300                10               7.5\n              5                3                24               400                9                 8\n              5                4                32               500                8                 8\n              5                5                39               600                7                7.8\n     When the quantity of machinery remains unchanged and the quantity of labour increases from 2 units to\n     3 units, the marginal product of labour decreases from 10 units to 9 units. Therefore, the law of\n     diminishing marginal returns applies to the firm.\n     Options B and C are incorrect. Since there is a fixed factor (machinery), the data shows the short run\n     situation; however, the situations described in the options will only occur in a long run situation.\n     Option D is incorrect. The average product of labour is the highest when the quantity of labour is 3 or 4\n     units.",
