      "questionTextEng": "Mr. Lee runs a travel agency that specialises in organising local tours. Which of the following will raise its profit-\n      maximising output?\n\n            A.    The rental for the premises of the travel agency decreases.\n            B.    The basic hourly wage of tour guides increases.\n            C.    More tourists prefer to travel by themselves instead of joining local tours.\n            D.    Some travel agencies that used to organise local tours close their businesses.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    When some travel agencies that used to organise local tours close their businesses, the supply of local\n     tours services will decrease, and the market price will increase. Marginal revenue will increase and the\n     profit-maximising output will increase.\n\n     Option A is incorrect. When the rental for the premises of the travel agency decreases, the fixed cost of\n     production will decrease and the profit-maximising output will not be affected.\n     Option B is incorrect. When the basic hourly wage of tour guides increases, the marginal cost of\n     production will increase and the profit-maximising output will decrease.\n     Option C is incorrect. When more tourists prefer to travel by themselves instead of joining local tours,\n     the demand for local tours will decrease and the market price will decrease. Marginal revenue will\n    decrease and the profit-maximising output will decrease.",
