      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/38/a-p1-17.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Country A is an importing country of electronic products. As the price of oil drops, the transportation cost for\n      electronic products decreases. Which of the following is/are effect(s) of the above event?\n\n            (1)   The sales volume of electronic products will increase.\n            (2)   The average quality of electronic products sold in the market will decrease.\n            (3)   The proportion of high-end electronic products sold in the market will increase.\n\n            A.    (2) only\n            B.    (3) only\n            C.    (1) and (2) only\n            D.    (1) and (3) only",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n     (1) is correct. When the transportation cost decreases, the price of electronic products will decrease and\n     the sales volume will increase.\n     (2) is correct. The money price of high-end electronic products is generally higher than that of ordinary\n     electronic products. When the transportation cost decreases, the relative price of high-end electronic\n    products (in terms of ordinary electronic products) will increase. According to the law of demand,\n    relative to ordinary electronic products, people will buy fewer high-end electronic products. The\n    proportion of high-end electronic products sold in the market will decrease. Therefore, the average\n    quality of electronic products sold in the market will decrease.",
