      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/38/a-p1-20.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "An increase in the price of ______________ will lead to an increase in the price of ______________.\n\n            (1)   fitness centre membership ... home fitness equipment\n            (2)   beef … leather\n            (3)   milk … ice cream\n\n            A.    (1) and (2) only\n            B.    (1) and (3) only\n            C.    (2) and (3) only\n            D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n     (1) is correct. Fitness centre membership and home fitness equipment are substitutes in general. When\n     the price of fitness centre membership increases, the demand for home fitness equipment will increase.\n     The price for home fitness equipment will increase.\n     (3) is correct. Milk is an input for ice cream. When the price of milk increases, the cost of producing ice\n     cream will increase and the supply of ice cream will decrease. The price of ice cream will increase.\n     (2) is incorrect. Beef and leather are in joint supply. When the price of beef increases, the supply of\n     leather will increase. The price of leather will decrease.",
