      "inlineDiagrams": "diagrams/MT38-P1-26.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Refer to the following diagram.\n\n                            Unit price\n\n                                                                  S\n                                                                  0\n\n                                                 M\n                              P0\n\n                                                                      D\n                                                                            Quantity\n                                0                 Q0\n\n      Point M is the mid-point of the demand curve. When the government imposes an effective price floor on the good,\n      the total revenue of producers will __________ and consumer surplus will __________.\n\n           A.    increase ... increase\n           B.    increase ... decrease\n           C.    decrease ... decrease\n           D.    decrease ... increase",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    Imposing an effective price floor will cause the quantity transacted to decrease and the price to increase.\n    Consumer surplus will decrease. As shown in the diagram, since the arc between the effective price\n    floor and the equilibrium price is above the mid-point of the demand curve, demand is elastic within this\n    price range. The percentage decrease in quantity transacted will be greater than the percentage increase\n    in price, and total revenue will therefore decrease.",
