      "inlineDiagrams": "diagrams/MT38-P1-27.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The diagram below shows the demand-supply diagram for good X. Initially, the market for good X is in\n      equilibrium.\n                       Unit price\n\n                                                           S\n\n                        P0\n\n                                                               D\n                                                                           Quantity\n                         0                Q0\n\n      Suppose the demand for good X increases. Which of the following statements are CORRECT?\n      (Assume the demand curve for good X shifts parallel.)\n\n            (1)   The consumer surplus in the market of good X will increase.\n            (2)   The producer surplus in the market of good X will increase.\n            (3)   The marginal cost of producing the last unit of good X will increase.\n\n            A.    (1) and (2) only\n            B.    (1) and (3) only\n            C.    (2) and (3) only\n            D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n                            Unit price\n\n                                                             S\n                                         a\n                                    b\n\n                              P1     c         e\n                              P0\n                                    d\n\n                                                                 D0   D1\n                               0              Q0 Q1                          Quantity\n\n    (1) is correct. The original consumer surplus is area (b + c) and the new consumer surplus is area (a + b).\n    Consumer surplus increases.\n    (2) is correct. The original producer surplus is area d and the new producer surplus is area (c + d + e).\n    Producer surplus increases by area (c + e).\n    (3) is correct. When the demand for good X increases, the price will increase. Since marginal cost\n    equals the price, the marginal cost of producing the last unit of good X will increase.",
