      "questionTextEng": "Read the following news excerpt.\n\n                                                           To help meet the housing needs of young people and support their development, the government has\n                                                           launched a subsidy scheme to subsidise non-governmental organisations in renting hotels and\n                                                           guesthouses and converting rooms into youth hostels for eligible young people.\n\n                                                           Individuals applying to live in these youth hostels must meet certain criteria, including being\n                                                           employed, being a Hong Kong permanent resident aged 18 to 30, and not owning any residential\n                                                           property in Hong Kong. The government and the non-governmental organisations managing the youth\n                                                           hostels will provide various support and training activities for the young people staying there, such as\n                                                           entrepreneurial training and mental wellness development.\n\n                                                           (a)   Give ONE reason to explain why young people who rent rooms in youth hostels do not have a full set\n                                                                 of private property rights over the rooms they rent.                                   (2 marks)\n\n                                                           (b)   Explain which TWO basic economic problems are related to the above information.              (4 marks)\n\n                                                           (c)   Explain how the above scheme will affect the occupational mobility of young people living in youth\n                                                                 hostels.                                                                                   (3 marks)\n\n                                                     .",
