      "questionTextEng": "Original Factory is a food production factory that produces various desserts and supplies them to different\n                                                           restaurants. The firm is a legal entity and the ownership of the firm cannot be freely transferred.\n\n                                                          (a)   Explain which type of production Original Factory engages in.                                  (2 marks)\n\n                                                          (b) Which type of business ownership does Original Factory belong to? Apart from the features of legal\n                                                              status and transfer of ownership, list ONE other feature of this type of business ownership. (2 marks)\n\n                                                          (c)   After doubling the scale of production, Original Factory’s average cost of production decreased. Suggest\n                                                                TWO reasons for the above change in average cost.                                              (2 marks)\n\n                                                          (d) Suppose the owner of Original Factory hopes to ensure a stable market outlet for its products through\n                                                              internal expansion. Which type of expansion should it engage in? Give ONE example to explain how\n                                                              this type of expansion can help achieve the above objective.                                (3 marks)\n\n                                                          (e)   The chefs of Original Factory are paid by time rate. From the viewpoint of the employer, state ONE\n\n                                                                advantage and ONE disadvantage of this wage payment method over piece rate.                (2 marks)",
