      "questionTextEng": "The tourism industry is one of the traditional pillar industries of Hong Kong, with hotels and guesthouses\n                                                           serving many tourists who visit the city each year.\n\n                                                          Source A: News report on re-imposing Hotel Accommodation Tax (HAT)\n\n                                                           The Hong Kong SAR Government has kept the HAT tax rate at 0% since 1 July 2008. In the\n                                                           2024-25 Budget, the government proposed to reintroduce the HAT. Starting from 1 January 2025,\n                                                           the HAT tax rate will be set at 3% of the room rate.\n\n                                                           Taking high tariff A hotels as an example, the average room rate per night is around $2,350, and\n                                                           HAT payable for accommodation per night is around $70; while for medium tariff hotels, the\n                                                           average room rate per night is around $730, and HAT payable for accommodation per night is\n                                                           around $22.\n\n                                                          (Source: Inland Revenue Department, HKSAR Government; Hong Kong Tourism Board, HKSAR\n                                                          Government)\n\n                                                          Source B: Data on Hong Kong hotels in September 2024\n                                                                 Number of hotel rooms           Hotel room occupancy rate\n                                                                        91,961                             81%\n                                                           (Source: Hong Kong Tourism Board, HKSAR Government)\n\n                                                          Source C: Some views on the tourism industry\n                                                                                                    The imposition of HAT may not necessarily result in an\n                                                                                                    increase in the total expenditure on hotel accommodations\n                                                                                                    by overseas tourists during their stay in Hong Kong.\n\n                                                                      A commentator\n                                                                                                    Hotel room rates in Hong Kong are much higher than those\n                                                                                                    in neighbouring areas (such as Shenzhen). Unless this gap\n                                                                                                    significantly narrows, I would choose to stay in a hotel in a\n                                                                                                    neighbouring area overnight after visiting Hong Kong.\n\n                                                                          A tourist\n                                                                                                    Hotels need to hire many workers for various positions, such\n                                                                                                    as front desk receptionists, housekeeping staff, laundry\n                                                                                                    service workers, etc. At current wage levels, some hotels\n                                                                                                    find it difficult to hire enough staff to provide hotel services.\n                                                                                                    If there is a severe shortage of staff, they cannot offer\n                                                                                                    services to guests, even if there are vacant rooms available.\n                                                              A member of the hotel industry\n\n                                                        (a) Refer to Source A. Give ONE reason to explain why the market structure of the hotel industry in Hong\n                                                            Kong is NOT perfectly competitive.                                                         (2 marks)\n\n                                                        (b) Illustrate the phenomenon in the hotel market shown in Source B in a demand-supply diagram. (3 marks)\n\n                                                        (c) Refer to Sources A and B. Justify the view of the commentator in Source C with reference to the concept\n                                                            of price elasticity of demand/supply.                                                         (3 marks)\n\n                                                        (d) Refer to the view of the member of the hotel industry in Source C. Which economic principle is illustrated\n                                                            by the hotels’ work arrangements? State TWO reasons why such arrangements can increase labour\n                                                            productivity.                                                                                  (3 marks)\n\n                                                        For part (e), candidates are required to present their answer in essay form. Criteria for marking will include use\n                                                        of sources and economic theories, relevant content, logical presentation and clarity of expression.\n\n                                                        (e) Suppose there are two proposals to support the hotel industry.\n\n                                                               Proposal I          Distributing HK$100 accommodation vouchers to overseas tourists\n                                                                                   that can only be used in Hong Kong hotels\n                                                               Proposal II         Relaxing the restrictions on the importation of low-skilled foreign\n                                                                                   workers by the Hong Kong hotel industry\n\n                                                             With reference to the above sources and your own knowledge in Economics, discuss the effects of the\n                                                             above two proposals on Hong Kong, including:\n\n                                                             - profits of local hotels\n                                                             - income distribution\n                                                                                                                                                                (9 marks)",
