      "reviewedByAI": "Y",
      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/39/q-p1-11.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/39/a-p1-11.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following is INCONSISTENT with the law of demand?\n\n           A.    When the government abolishes the airport departure tax charged to each passenger, the average flight\n                 distance for departing travellers decreases.\n           B.    When the government imposes an ad valorem sales tax on each bottle of wine, the quantity of high-\n                 quality wine sold decreases.\n           C.    When the transportation cost per kilogram of goods increases by 10% due to an increase in fuel price,\n                 the average quality of imported white rice people purchased decreases.\n           D.    The price and quantity transacted of air conditioners increase during the summer.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n     When the transportation cost per kilogram of goods increases by 10%, the transportation cost per\n     kilogram for all types of white rice will increase by the same amount. The relative price of high-quality\n     white rice (in terms of average-quality white rice) will decrease. According to the law of demand,\n     relative to average-quality white rice, people will buy more high-quality white rice. The average quality\n     of imported white rice people purchase will increase.\n     Option A is incorrect. When the government abolishes the airport departure tax charged to each\n     passenger, the relative price of long-distance flights (in terms of short-distance flights) will increase.\n     According to the law of demand, relative to short-distance flights, people will take fewer long-distance\n     flights. The average flight distance will decrease. This is consistent with the law of demand.\n     Option B is incorrect. When the government imposes an ad valorem sales tax on each bottle of wine, the\n     money price of all types of wine will increase and the quantity of wine sold (including high-quality wine)\n     will decrease. This is consistent with the law of demand.\n     Option D is incorrect. This may be caused by an increase in the demand for air conditioners, which does\n    not violate the law of demand.",
