      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/39/a-p1-13.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following would most likely cause an increase in total expenditure on air services?\n\n           A.    The government reduces the basic allowance for the salaries tax and air services are normal goods.\n           B.    The fare for cross-border trains increases.\n           C.    More airlines enter the market.\n           D.    The price of fuel increases.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n     Cross-border train services and air services are substitutes. An increase in the fare for cross-border trains\n     will increase the demand for air services. The price and quantity transacted of air services will increase\n     and total expenditure will increase.\n\n    Option A is incorrect. When the government reduces the basic allowance for the salaries tax, people’s\n    tax payment will increase and their post-tax income will decrease. Since air services are normal goods,\n    demand for air services will decrease. The price and quantity transacted will decrease and total\n    expenditure will decrease.\n    Option C is incorrect. As more airlines enter the market, the supply of air services will increase. The\n    price will decrease and quantity transacted will increase. Total expenditure may increase, decrease or\n    remain unchanged, depending on the price elasticity of demand.\n    Option D is incorrect. When the price of fuel increases, the cost of providing air services will increase.\n    The supply of air services will decrease. The price will increase and quantity transacted will decrease.\n    Total expenditure may increase, decrease or remain unchanged, depending on the price elasticity of\n    demand.",
