      "inlineDiagrams": "diagrams/MT39-P1-14-1.jpg,diagrams/MT39-P1-14-2.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "In which of the following situations will the government imposing a per-unit tax on the producers of a good not\n    affect the producers’ total revenue net of tax?\n\n         A.                                                    B.\n              Unit price                                             Unit price\n\n                               S\n                               0\n\n                                                                                                S\n                                                                                                0\n\n                                            D                                                       D\n                 0                              Quantity                0                               Quantity\n\n         C.                                                    D.\n              Unit price                                             Unit price\n\n                               D                                                                    S\n                                        S\n\n                                                                                                D\n\n                 0                              Quantity                0                               Quantity\n\n1 5 . Refer to the following demand-supply diagram for good X.\n\n                             Unit price\n\n                                                                  S\n\n                                                                   D\n                                0                                            Quantity\n\n     Which of the following statements about good X are CORRRCT?\n\n           (1)   If the government has imposed an effective price ceiling on good X, an increase in the price of its\n                 complements may cause the price ceiling to become ineffective.\n           (2)   If the government has imposed an effective price ceiling on good X, an increase in the price of its\n                 factor of production must reduce the total revenue of producers.\n           (3)   If the government has imposed an effective price floor on good X, an increase in people’s preference\n                 for good X must increase the marginal benefit of the last unit of good X.\n\n           A.    (1) and (2) only\n           B.    (1) and (3) only\n           C.    (2) and (3) only\n           D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    Producers’ total revenue net of tax = Price actually received by producers × Quantity transacted after tax\n    = (Price after tax – Per-unit tax) × Quantity transacted after tax\n    Option C is correct. If the demand is perfectly inelastic, after a per-unit tax is imposed, the equilibrium\n    price will rise by the amount of the per-unit tax, the price actually received by producers will remain\n    unchanged and the quantity transacted will also remain unchanged. The total revenue net of tax will\n    remain unchanged.\n\n                   Unit price\n                                    D\n                                               S1          S0 = Supply without per-unit tax\n                                                S0         S1 = Supply with per-unit tax\n\n                     P1\n                                        T\n            P0 = P1 – T\n\n                     0             Q                 Quantity\n\n    Option A is incorrect. If the supply is perfectly inelastic, after a per-unit tax is imposed, the equilibrium\n    price will remain unchanged. The price actually received by producers will decrease, while the quantity\n    transacted will remain unchanged. Total revenue net of tax will decrease.\n    Option B is incorrect. If the supply is perfectly elastic, after a per-unit tax is imposed, the equilibrium\n    price will rise by the amount of the tax. The price actually received by producers will remain unchanged,\n    while the quantity transacted will decrease. Total revenue net of tax will decrease.\n    Option D is incorrect. If the demand is perfectly elastic, after a per-unit tax is imposed, the equilibrium\n    price will remain unchanged. The price actually received by producers will decrease, and the quantity\n    transacted will decrease. Total revenue net of tax will decrease.",
