      "questionTextEng": "Refer to the following table that shows the marginal benefit schedule of a consumer for coffee.\n\n                                       Quantity (units)         Marginal benefit ($)\n                                              1                         10\n                                              2                          8\n                                              3                          6\n                                              4                          4\n                                              5                          2\n\n      When the consumer’s marginal benefit per unit increases by $2 and the market price of coffee decreases from $6\n      to $4 due to a good harvest, the consumer surplus will\n\n           A.    decrease by $14.\n           B.    decrease by $20.\n           C.    increase by $14.\n           D.    increase by $20.\n\n1 8 . Refer to the following demand-supply diagram for good X.\n\n                     Unit price\n                                       SQuota\n                                                          S\n\n                                                          D\n                        0                                        Quantity\n\n     If the government lowers the quota limit on good X, which of the following will decrease?\n\n           (1)   consumer surplus\n           (2)   total variable cost\n           (3)   deadweight loss\n\n           A.    (1) and (2) only\n           B.    (1) and (3) only\n           C.    (2) and (3) only\n           D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n              Quantity (units)        Original marginal benefit ($)    New marginal benefit ($)\n                      1                           10                               12\n                      2                            8                               10\n                      3                            6                                8\n                      4                            4                                6\n                      5                            2                                4\n    The original market price is $6 and the consumer will buy 3 units. The consumer surplus is equal to $6\n    [= ($10 + $8 + $6) – $6 × 3].\n    The new market price is $4. Under the new marginal benefit schedule, the consumer will buy 5 units.\n    The consumer surplus is equal to $20 [= ($12 + $10 + $8 + $6 + $4) – $4 × 5].\n    Consumer surplus will increase by $14.",
