      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/39/q-p1-20.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/39/a-p1-20.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Refer to the following news excerpt.\n\n                A factory in Country A has been found discharging sewage into a river, causing the death\n                of a large number of fish in the downstream area. This is not only destroying the local\n                ecological environment but also seriously affecting the livelihood of fishermen.\n\n      Based on the above information, which of the following statements are CORRECT?\n\n           (1)     If the government imposes fines on the factory that discharges sewage, the divergence between\n                   private cost and social cost may decrease.\n           (2)     If the government prohibits the factory from discharging any sewage into the river, the total social\n                   surplus will increase.\n           (3)     If the factory provides compensation to the fishermen in the downstream area, deadweight loss may\n                   decrease.\n\n           A.      (1) and (2) only\n           B.      (1) and (3) only\n           C.      (2) and (3) only\n           D.      (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    (1) is correct. If the government imposes fines on the factory that discharges sewage, the marginal\n    private cost of the factory discharging sewage will increase and the divergence between private cost and\n    social cost will decrease.\n\n    (3) is correct. If the factory provides compensation to the affected fishermen, the external cost of\n    pollution can be internalised. The amount of sewage discharged will be reduced to a level closer to the\n    efficient level. Deadweight loss will decrease.\n    (2) is incorrect. If the deadweight loss due to excessive discharge of sewage is smaller than the\n    maximum total social surplus, prohibiting the factory from discharging any sewage into the river will\n    reduce the total social surplus from some positive number (the maximum total social surplus minus the\n    deadweight loss due to excessive discharge of sewage) to zero. The total social surplus will decrease.",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/39/ae-p1-20.jpg",
      "originalQuestionImageEng": "originals/39/qe-p1-20.jpg",
      "stemPatterns": [
        "（界外影響新聞）下列哪些陳述是正確的？"
      ]
