      "questionTextEng": "In November 2024, the Macao SAR Government announced that it would implement the Wealth Partaking\n      Scheme again the next year and distribute MOP 10,000 to each Macao permanent resident. Which of the\n      following statements about the above scheme is CORRECT?\n\n                  A.          Since all Macao permanent residents receive the same amount of money, it will not help reduce\n                              income inequality.\n                  B.          It will not help equalise opportunity.\n                  C.          It will increase Macao residents’ demand for all goods.\n                  D.          The amount distributed will be included in the calculation of government consumption expenditure of\n                              Macao.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    Compared to the rich, the poor do not get more resources to improve their productivity or increase their\n    future income, so distributing the same amount of cash to all permanent residents will not help equalise\n    opportunities.\n    Option A is incorrect. The same amount of money will increase the income of low-income people by a\n    larger percentage, which can reduce income inequality.\n    Option C is incorrect. When people’s income increases, demand for inferior goods will decrease.\n    Option D is incorrect. The amount distributed is a transfer payment and will not be included in the\n    calculation of Macau’s government consumption expenditure.",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/39/ae-p1-23.jpg",
      "originalQuestionImageEng": "originals/39/qe-p1-23.jpg",
      "stemPatterns": [
        "（現金分享計劃）下列哪項關於計劃的陳述是正確的？"
      ]
