      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    When the long run aggregate supply increases while the aggregate demand remains unchanged, the new\n     long run equilibrium point may be at A.\n     When the technology for production improves, the productive capacity of Country A will increase. Long\n     run aggregate supply will increase while aggregate demand will not change.\n     Option B is incorrect. More people choosing to retire early will lead to a decline in the labour force,\n     Country A’s productive capacity will decrease and long run aggregate supply will decrease.\n     Option C is incorrect. A decrease in the price of raw materials will reduce the cost of production of firms.\n     Short run aggregate supply will increase while long run aggregate supply will not be affected. The long\n     run equilibrium point will remain at E.\n\n    Option D is incorrect. When the government increases transfer payments, people’s disposable income\n    will increase and private consumption expenditure will increase. Aggregate demand will increase while\n    long run aggregate supply will not be affected.",
