      "questionTextEng": "Refer to the following conversation.\n\n             John:      I deposited HK$500,000 into institution A for two months. In addition, I also deposited\n                        HK$300,000 into institution B for three months.\n\n             Cindy: Institution A refused to accept my deposit of HK$80,000, so I deposited the money into\n                    institution B.\n\n      Based on the above information, institution A may be a ___________, while institution B may be a ____________.\n\n             A.      restricted licence bank … licensed bank\n             B.      restricted licence bank … deposit-taking company\n             C.      deposit-taking company … licensed bank\n             D.      deposit-taking company … restricted licence bank\n\n3 0 . Suppose the money supply data of Hong Kong is as follows:\n\n                                         Components                                              $ billion\n          Total issue of legal tender                                                               10\n          Legal tender held by all authorised institutions                                           3\n          Demand deposits                                                                           12\n          All types of deposits with licensed banks                                                 32\n          Negotiable certificates of deposit issued by licensed banks (other than\n                                                                                                    5\n          those held by authorised institutions)\n          Deposits with restricted licence banks and deposit-taking companies                       40\n          Negotiable certificates of deposit issued by restricted licence banks and\n          deposit-taking companies (other than those held by authorised                             30\n          institutions)\n\n      The money supply M2 is $ _____________ billion.\n\n             A.      39\n             B.      44\n             C.      56\n             D.      114",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    Licensed banks can accept deposits of any amount and maturity.\n    Restricted licence banks can accept deposits of any maturity of HK$500,000 or above.\n    Deposit-taking companies can accept deposits of HK$100,000 or above with an original maturity of at\n    least three months.\n    Only licensed banks can accept Cindy’s deposit of HK$80,000, so institution B is a licensed bank.\n    Since the maturity of John’s deposit is less than three months, institution A is not a deposit-taking\n    company. Institution A may be a licensed bank or a restricted licence bank.",
