      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    Monetary base = $10 billion, reserves = $3 billion, cash in public circulation = $(10 – 3) billion = $7\n    billion\n    Money supply M2 = Cash in public circulation + All types of deposits with licensed banks + NCDs\n    issued by licensed banks held outside the banking sector = $(7 + 32 + 5) billion = $44 billion\n    Option C is incorrect. Demand deposits ($12 billion) are already included in all types of deposits with\n    licensed banks ($32 billion), and thus should not be counted twice.",
