      "questionTextEng": "Refer to the following table.\n\n                  Policy I                                Policy II                             Policy III\n      ⚫ Tighten the requirements for          ⚫ Change civil servants’ salary        ⚫ Introduce a dividend tax\n        consumers opening a stored              payment from monthly to              ⚫ Sell government bonds in the\n        value facility account                  weekly                                 open market\n      ⚫ Raise the discount rate               ⚫ Raise the required reserve ratio\n\n    Which of the policies in the above table will cause the nominal interest rate to rise?\n\n            A.    Policy I only\n            B.    Policy II only\n            C.    Policy III only\n            D.    Policy I and Policy III only",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    Policy I: Tightening the requirements for consumers opening a stored value facility account will lead to\n     an increase in transaction demand for money, so money demand will increase. Raising the discount rate\n     will reduce the money supply. To conclude, the nominal interest rate will rise.\n     Policy II: Changing civil servants’ salary payment from monthly to weekly will reduce the transaction\n     demand for money, so money demand will decrease. The nominal interest rate will decrease. Raising the\n     required reserve ratio will cause the money supply to fall and the nominal interest rate will increase. To\n     conclude, the change in the nominal interest rate will be uncertain.\n     Policy III: After introducing the dividend tax, people will tend to reduce the proportion of shares in their\n     asset portfolios, so asset demand for money will increase and money demand will increase. Selling\n     government bonds in the open market will reduce the money supply. To conclude, the nominal interest\n    rate will rise.",
