      "questionTextEng": "The diagram below shows the consumer price index for Country A.\n          140\n\n          120\n\n          100\n\n           80\n\n           60\n\n           40\n\n           20\n\n            0\n            Jan-23           Apr-23            Jul-23            Oct-23            Jan-24\n\n      Suppose people did not expect any change in the price level in 2023. When the price level changed as above,\n      which of the following people would lose?\n\n            A.    holders of fixed rate bonds\n            B.    tenants who rent residential units at a fixed rent\n            C.    banks that provide loans to businesses at floating interest rates\n            D.    people holding cash",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    There was unexpected deflation in Country A in 2023.\n    The real value (purchasing power) of the fixed rental paid by the tenants would increase, so they would\n    lose.\n    Option A is incorrect. The real value (purchasing power) of the interest received by holders of fixed rate\n    bonds would increase. They would gain.\n    Option C is incorrect. The interest rate would be adjusted in accordance with the inflation rate, so the\n    purchasing power of the repayment received by the banks would not be affected.\n    Option D is incorrect. When there was unexpected deflation, the purchasing power of cash would\n    increase, so people holding cash would gain.",
