      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following will reduce the effectiveness of an expansionary monetary policy on real output?\n\n           (1)        The public’s willingness to deposit cash obtained from loans into the banking system decreases.\n           (2)        Companies tend to issue bonds rather than borrow from banks to raise capital.\n           (3)        Commercial banks are more willing and able to lend out their excess reserves.\n\n           A.         (1) and (2) only\n           B.         (1) and (3) only\n           C.         (2) and (3) only\n           D.         (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    The effect of an expansionary monetary policy on real output is affected by the deposit creation ability\n    of the banking system. When the deposit creation ability of the banking system decreases, the\n    effectiveness of an expansionary monetary policy on real output will decrease.\n    (1) is correct. If more loans lent out by commercial banks are not redeposited into the banking system,\n    but are held in cash by the public, the deposit creation ability of the banking system will decrease and\n    the effectiveness of an expansionary monetary policy on real output will be reduced.\n    (2) is correct. If companies are less willing to obtain loans from banks, demand for loans may be\n    insufficient. The deposit creation ability of the banking system will decrease and the effectiveness of an\n    expansionary monetary policy on real output will be reduced.\n    (3) is incorrect. If commercial banks are more willing and able to lend out their excess reserves, the\n    deposit creation ability of the banking system will increase.",
