      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/39/q-p1-42.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/39/a-p1-42.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The table below shows the data about Country A.\n\n                                                                        Good X                             Good Y\n                                                                        (units)                            (units)\n          Total output with no international trade                        10                 AND             40\n          Total output with specialisation and international trade        30                 AND             0\n          Total consumption with international trade                      20                 AND             25\n\n    Which of the following statements about Country A is CORRECT?\n\n           A.    Country A has an absolute advantage in producing good X.\n           B.    The opportunity cost of producing 1 unit of good X is 4 units of good Y.\n           C.    The terms of trade is 1 unit of good X = 1.25 units of good Y.\n           D.    Country A’s total gain from exports is 5 units of good Y.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    Option A is incorrect. The question does not provide production information for Country A’s trading\n    partners, so we cannot determine whether Country A has an absolute advantage in producing good X.\n\n    Option B is incorrect. Comparing the total output with no international trade with the total output with\n    specialisation and international trade, Country A produces an additional 20 (= 30 – 10) units of good X\n    and gives up 40 units of good Y.\n    Country A’s opportunity cost of producing 1 unit of good X = 2 (= 40 / 20) units of good Y\n    Option C is incorrect. Comparing the total consumption with international trade with the total output\n    with specialisation and international trade, Country A exports 10 units of good X in exchange for 25\n    units of good Y. The terms of trade is 1 unit of good X = 2.5 units of good Y or 1 unit of good Y = 0.4\n    units of good X.\n    Option D is correct. Country A’s gain from trade of exporting 1 unit of good X = 2.5 units of good Y – 2\n    units of good Y = 0.5 units of good Y\n    Country A’s gain from trade of exporting 10 units of good X = 0.5 units of good Y × 10 = 5 units of\n    good Y",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/39/ae-p1-42.jpg",
      "originalQuestionImageEng": "originals/39/qe-p1-42.jpg",
      "stemPatterns": [
        "（貿易表格）下列哪項關於甲國的陳述是正確的？"
      ]
