      "inlineDiagrams": "diagrams/MT39-P1-43.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The diagram below shows the market of wheat in a small open economy.\n\n                           Unit price\n\n                                                                           S\n\n                            P1\n                            PW\n\n                                                                          D\n\n                             0                                                    Quantity\n                                             Q1             Q2\n\n    Pw is the international price of wheat and the import quota imposed by the government is (Q 2 – Q1) units. If the\n    demand for wheat increases,\n\n           A.    the domestic price of wheat will remain unchanged.\n           B.    the total revenue of domestic producers of wheat will increase.\n           C.    the international price of wheat will increase.\n           D.    the import volume will increase.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    When the demand for wheat increases, the domestic price of wheat will increase. Domestic production\n    will increase, and the total revenue of domestic producers will increase.\n    Option A is incorrect. The domestic price will increase.\n    Option C is incorrect. A change in demand in a small open economy will not affect the international\n    price. It will remain at PW.\n    Option D is incorrect. The import volume will remain unchanged at the quota limit.",
