      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/39/q-p1-44.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/39/a-p1-44.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The diagram below shows the percentage changes in the total value of exported goods and the total value of\n    imported goods in an economy. The economy recorded a trade surplus in 2021.\n\n                      6\n\n                      5\n\n                      4\n                (%)\n\n                      3\n\n                      2\n\n                      1\n\n                      0\n                       2021                      2022                      2023                      2024\n                                                              Year\n\n                                   Year-on-year percentage change in total value of exported goods\n                                   Year-on-year percentage change in total value of imported goods\n\n    According to the above diagram, from 2021 to 2024, the economy’s\n\n           A.     invisible trade balance increased.\n           B.     total value of goods exported decreased.\n           C.     current account balance increased.\n           D.     trade surplus increased.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    The economy recorded a trade surplus in 2021, meaning that the total value of exported goods was\n    greater than the total value of imported goods. From 2021 to 2024, the year-on-year percentage change\n    in the total value of exported goods was greater than the year-on-year percentage change in the total\n    value of imported goods, indicating that the increase in the total value of exported goods was greater\n    than the increase in the total value of imported goods, so the trade surplus was increasing.\n    Option A is incorrect. The question does not provide information about exports of services and imports\n    of services, so we cannot determine the change in the invisible trade balance.\n    Option B is incorrect. From 2021 to 2024, the year-on-year percentage change in the total value of\n    exported goods was positive, indicating that the total value of exported goods was increasing.\n    Option C is incorrect. The question does not provide information about services, external factor income\n    flows and current transfers, so we cannot determine the change in the current account balance.",
