      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/39/a-p1-45.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The following table shows the change in the exchange rate between the Canadian dollar (CAD) and Hong Kong\n    dollar (HKD).\n\n                                   Date                                Exchange rate\n                              31 October 2023                        CAD 1 = HKD 5.66\n                              31 October 2024                        CAD 1 = HKD 5.58\n\n    On 31 October 2023, Mr. Cheung exchanged HKD 100,000 for Canadian dollars. Later, he exchanged the amount\n    back to Hong Kong dollars on 31 October 2024. Suppose Mr. Cheung needs to pay 1% of the transaction amount as\n    a handling fee for each transaction. From the above transactions, Mr. Cheung ______________.\n\n           A.     lost about HKD 585\n           B.     lost about HKD 1,413\n           C.     lost about HKD 3,375\n           D.     gained about HKD 1,434\n\n                                                        EN D O F PAP E R",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    After deducting the handling fee, Mr. Cheung could exchange HKD 100,000 for approximately\n    CAD 17,491 (= 100,000 × (1 – 1%) / 5.66) on 31 October 2023.\n    On 31 October 2024, Mr. Cheung exchanged the amount back to Hong Kong dollars. After deducting\n    the handling fee, he could get approximately HKD 96,624 [= 17,491 × (1 – 1%) × 5.58]. Mr. Cheung\n    lost approximately HKD 3,375.",
