      "questionTextEng": "Country A and Country B each have 30 units of resources. The table below shows the amount of resources\n                                                          required to produce garments and rice in the two countries respectively.\n\n                                                                                                     1 unit of garments         1 unit of rice\n                                                                                 Country A                    1                       2\n                                                                                 Country B                    2                       3\n\n                                                          (a)   Which good would Country A export according to its comparative advantage? Explain.            (3 marks)\n\n                                                          (b) If the two countries completely specialise their production and trade with each other, find the total\n                                                              output of garments and rice of both countries.                                             (2 marks)\n\n                                                          (c)   Suppose the transportation cost for each unit of rice traded is 0.15 units of garments and the cost is\n                                                                borne by the exporting country. Find the range of terms of trade (in terms of 1 unit of rice) over which\n                                                                exchange between the two countries is mutually beneficial.                                     (2 marks)\n\n                                                                                                   END OF SECTION A\n\n                                                     Section B (60 marks)",
