      "questionTextEng": "Figure 1 shows the AS-AD diagram for an economy. Point E is the initial short run equilibrium point of the\n                                                           economy.\n                                                                                               Figure 1\n\n                                                                              Price level\n                                                                                        LRAS0                 SRAS0\n\n                                                                                                  E\n\n                                                                                                                 AD0\n                                                                                  0                                    Aggregate output\n\n                                                          (a)   Suggest ONE reason to explain why the short run aggregate supply curve is upward sloping. (3 marks)\n\n                                                          (b) Explain whether the economy has an inflationary (output) gap or a deflationary (output) gap. (2 marks)\n\n                                                          (c)   Suppose the government considers raising the standard tax rate of the salaries tax to restore the\n                                                                aggregate output to the full-employment output level. With the aid of Figure 1, explain how the measure\n                                                                can achieve the objective.                                                                    (6 marks)\n\n                                                          (d) An economist suggests that the government adjust the sales tax rate to restore the aggregate output to\n                                                              the full-employment output level. In terms of equity, evaluate this suggestion and the measure in part (c)\n                                                              respectively.                                                                                  (3 marks)\n\n                                                          (e)   Suggest ONE monetary policy that can also restore the aggregate output to the full-employment output\n                                                                level. Explain how the monetary policy would affect the nominal interest rate in the economy.\n                                                                                                                                                              (2 marks)",
