      "questionTextEng": "Between October and November 2024, several typhoons hit the Philippines. They caused a lot of damage,\n                                                           and many people were injured or died.\n\n                                                           (a)   A lot of crops were damaged by the typhoons, forcing the farmers to destroy them. Explain whether the\n                                                                 value of the destroyed crops would be included in the calculation of the Philippines’ gross domestic\n                                                                 product of 2024.                                                                           (2 marks)\n\n                                                           (b) Suppose the prices of most domestic food in the Philippines increased sharply after the typhoon.\n\n                                                                  (i)   Explain whether the above change in price can be regarded as inflation.                 (2 marks)\n\n                                                                  (ii) Explain ONE function of price illustrated in this case.                                  (2 marks)\n\n                                                           (c)   Suppose some Hong Kong citizens purchased locally produced goods and donated them to victims of\n                                                                 the disaster in the Philippines. Explain how this would affect Hong Kong’s balance of payments.\n\n                                                                                                                                                              (2 marks)\n\n                                                           Ms. Chan is a retiree who plans to go to the Philippines to volunteer and help those affected by the disaster. A\n                                                           friend has offered to cover all her monetary expenses during her volunteer work in the Philippines.\n\n                                                           (d) ‘Since Ms. Chan is retired and has no income and does not need to pay for any monetary expenses, her\n                                                               volunteer work does not involve any opportunity cost.’ Do you agree with this statement? Explain.\n                                                                                                                                                            (2 marks)",
