      "questionTextEng": "Refer to Figure 3. PPFA is the production possibility frontier of Country A and PA is the production point of\n                                                           the country when there is no trade.\n\n                                                                                                      Figure 3\n                                                                       Good Y (units)\n\n                                                                          100\n\n                                                                          80\n                                                                                         PA\n                                                                          60\n\n                                                                          40    A\n\n                                                                           20\n\n                                                                                                             B         PPFA\n                                                                            0                                                          Good X (units)\n                                                                                        20       40        60        80        100\n\n                                                           (a)   Explain why the production possibility frontier of Country A is concave to the origin.         (1 mark)\n\n                                                           (b)   The slope of the dotted line AB is the world price of good X. With the aid of Figure 3, explain whether\n                                                                 Country A has a comparative advantage in producing good X. (Hint: you may add a straight line at\n                                                                 PA.)                                                                                          (4 marks)\n\n                                                           (c)   Suppose Country A engages in international trade.\n\n                                                                 (i)   Indicate the production point (PT) and the consumption possibility frontier (CPFA) of Country A\n                                                                       after trade in Figure 3.                                                               (3 marks)\n\n                                                                 (ii) Suppose Country A consumes 30 units of good X after trade. Indicate the import volume of\n                                                                      Country A in Figure 3.                                                               (1 mark)\n\n                                                           (d)   After Country A engages in international trade, its Gross National Income per capita rank increases,\n                                                                 but its Human Development Index (HDI) rank decreases.\n\n                                                                 (i)   Suggest TWO possible reasons for the decrease in the HDI rank of Country A.             (4 marks)\n\n                                                                 (ii) State ONE developmental dimension that is not measured in the HDI.                        (1 mark)\n\n                                                           (e)   Suggest ONE policy that would improve Country A’s HDI ranking. Explain your answer.           (2 marks)",
