      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/40/q-p1-03.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/40/a-p1-03.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Mr. Wong plans to purchase an exercise bike from a second-hand trading website. Which of the following\n     situations would increase his cost of purchasing the exercise bike?\n\n           A.     Mr. Wong needs to pay an additional transportation fee to have the exercise bike delivered to his\n                  home.\n           B.     Mr. Wong finds that the usage experience of the exercise bike is not as good as expected after\n                  purchasing it.\n           C.     Mr. Wong gets injured while using the exercise bike.\n           D.     Mr. Wong finds that the exercise bike is damaged after purchasing it and needs to pay extra repair fees\n                  before he can use it.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n     Mr. Wong paying an additional transportation fee to have the exercise bike delivered to his home will\n     increase the monetary cost of purchasing it.\n     Option B is incorrect. Mr. Wong finding that the usage experience of the exercise bike is not as good as\n     expected after purchasing it will only affect the value of purchasing the exercise bike, not the cost of\n     purchasing it.\n     Option C is incorrect. Mr. Wong getting injured while using the exercise bike will increase the cost of\n     using the exercise bike, but this will not affect the cost of purchasing it.\n     Option D is incorrect. Mr. Wong finding that the exercise bike is damaged after purchasing it and\n     needing to pay extra repair fees before he can use it will only affect the cost of using the exercise bike,\n     not the cost of purchasing it.",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/40/ae-p1-03.jpg",
