      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following is/are considered as ‘land’ in economics?\n\n           (1)   water in a natural lake\n           (2)   rainwater collected in a reservoir\n           (3)   water used for cooling machinery in a factory\n\n           A.    (1) only\n           B.    (1) and (2) only\n           C.    (2) and (3) only\n           D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n     (1) is correct. It is a natural resource which has not gone through any man-made processes, so it is\n     considered as ‘land’.\n     (2) and (3) are incorrect. They have gone through man-made processes, so they should be considered as\n     ‘capital’.",
