      "questionTextEng": "Refer to the following conversation between a music studio owner and a music teacher.\n\n                 Music studio owner: I purchased this place and opened this music studio. You can\n                                     pay the rent to use this studio.\n\n                 Music teacher:          I will rent your music studio to launch music courses, and I\n                                         will recruit students and teach violin by myself.\n\n      The income earned by the studio owner consists of ______________ while the income earned by the music\n      teacher consists of ______________.\n\n           A.    rent ... wage\n           B.    interest and profit ... wage and profit\n           C.    profit ... interest and profit\n           D.    wage ... profit",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    The physical effort the music teacher used in the production is considered labour, so her income\n    includes wages. At the same time, since the music teacher needs to bear risks in the production process,\n    her income includes profits.\n    The music room belongs to capital, so the income of the music room owner includes the return on\n    capital, that is, interest. At the same time, since the music room owner needs to bear risks in the\n    production process, his income includes profits.",
