      "questionTextEng": "The table below shows the input-output relationship of a firm. Labour is the only input of the firm. The cost per\n      unit of labour is $10.\n\n                                       Labour (units)           Total product (units)\n                                            1                             5\n                                            2                            12\n                                            3                            24\n                                            4                            31\n                                            5                            35\n\n      The table above shows a __________ situation, where __________.\n\n            A.    short run ... the law of diminishing marginal returns applies\n            B.    short run ... the law of diminishing marginal returns does not apply.\n            C.    long run ... diseconomies of scale exists when output increases from 24 units to 31 units\n            D.    long run ... economies of scale exists when the output increases from 31 units to 35 units",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    The firm operates in the long run as there are only variable factors.\n          Labour (units)          Total product (units)            Total cost ($)              Average cost ($)\n                 1                            5                            10                               2\n                 2                            12                           20                           1.67\n                 3                            24                           30                           1.25\n                 4                            31                           40                           1.29\n                 5                            35                           50                           1.43\n    When output increases from 24 units to 31 units, average cost increases, indicating that diseconomies of\n    scale exists.",
