      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/40/q-p1-19.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/40/a-p1-19.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The following table shows the cost-output relationship of a profit-maximising firm. Suppose the market price is\n      $8.\n\n       Output (units)            2                3                4                    5              6\n       Total cost ($)            6                12               20                   30             42\n\n      Suppose the firm’s average cost per unit of output increases by $2. The profit-maximising output of the firm will\n      __________ and the profit will be _________.\n\n            A.    decrease by 1 unit ... $6\n            B.    decrease by 1 unit ... $12\n            C.    remain unchanged ... $6\n            D.    remain unchanged ... $12",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    Before the average cost changes:\n      Output (units)                2              3              4                 5               6\n      Total cost ($)                6              12            20                 30             42\n      Average cost ($)              3              4              5                 6               7\n      Marginal cost ($)             -              6              8                 10             12\n    The profit-maximising output is 4 units. At this output level, marginal revenue (price) = marginal cost =\n    $8.\n    After the average cost per unit of output increases by $2:\n      Output (units)                2              3              4                 5               6\n      Average cost ($)              5              6              7                 8               9\n      Total cost ($)                10             18            28                 40             54\n      Marginal cost ($)             -              8             10                 12             14\n    The profit-maximising output will be 3 units. At this output level, marginal revenue (price) = marginal\n    cost = $8.\n    Profit = Total revenue ‒ Total cost = $8 × 3 units ‒ $18 = $6",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/40/ae-p1-19.jpg",
      "originalQuestionImageEng": "originals/40/qe-p1-19.jpg",
      "stemPatterns": [
        "（成本表）利潤極大化產出會 __________，利潤會是 __________"
      ]
