      "questionTextEng": "Karmen operates a baking studio. Under which of the following situations would Karmen reduce production to\n      maximise profit?\n\n            A.    The business registration fee increases.\n            B.    The monthly rent of the baking studio decreases.\n            C.    The price of flour rises significantly.\n            D.    A television drama related to baking has inspired more people to take an interest in baking.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    Flour is a variable cost and an increase in its price will lead to an increase in marginal cost. At a given\n     price, the output level that the firm is willing and able to supply will decrease. The profit-maximising\n     output level will decrease.\n     Options A and B are incorrect. They are fixed costs, and changes in fixed costs will not affect the\n     determination of the profit-maximising output level.\n     Option D is incorrect. This will increase the market demand for baking courses. The market price will\n     increase, leading to an increase in the marginal revenue of baking courses. Given the marginal cost per\n    unit of output, the profit-maximising output level will increase.",
