      "questionTextEng": "To celebrate the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region Establishment Day on 1 July, many restaurants\n      launched discount promotions. As a result, the number of customers visiting these restaurants on 1 July increased\n      significantly. Some customers, even though willing to pay the price set by the restaurants, were unable to reserve\n      a table.\n\n      Based on the above information, which of the following statements about the situation on 1 July is/are\n      CORRECT?\n\n            (1)   The demand for restaurant services provided by the restaurants increased due to the discount\n                  promotions.\n            (2)   There was a shortage in the market of restaurant services.\n            (3)   The restaurants offering discounts did not maximise their profits.\n\n            A.    (1) only\n            B.    (2) only\n            C.    (1) and (2) only\n            D.    (2) and (3) only",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n     (2) is correct. Some customers are unable to reserve a table even though they are willing to pay the price\n     set by the restaurants, indicating that the quantity supplied of restaurant services is smaller than the\n     quantity demanded. There is a shortage in the market.\n     (1) is incorrect. When the price of restaurant services decreases, the quantity demanded of restaurant\n    services will increase, while the demand for restaurant services remains unchanged.\n    (3) is incorrect. The restaurants offering discounts may have a promotional effect, which does not mean\n    that they are not striving for maximum profits.",
