      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following will increase the price elasticity of demand for bus services?\n\n            A.    More minibus routes stop their services.\n            B.    The wage rate of bus drivers increases.\n            C.    More railway branch lines are completed.\n            D.    The breakdown rate of buses decreases.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    The completion of more railway branch lines will increase alternative modes of transportation (e.g.,\n    consumers will be more likely to switch to rail when bus fares increase), increasing the price elasticity\n    of demand for bus services.\n    Option A is incorrect. When more minibus routes stop their services, the number of alternatives to bus\n    services will decrease. The price elasticity of demand for bus services will decrease.\n    Option B is incorrect. An increase in the wage rate of bus drivers will increase the costs of providing\n    bus services and affect the supply of buses, but this is not a factor that affects the price elasticity of\n    demand.\n    Option D is incorrect. A decrease in the breakdown rate of buses will increase consumers’ demand for\n    bus services, but this will not increase the price elasticity of demand.",
