      "questionTextEng": "With technological advancements, Country A’s drug production technology has significantly improved. As a result,\n      the price of locally produced drugs has changed by 40% and the quantity transacted has changed by 20%. Which\n      of the following statements are CORRECT?\n\n           (1)   The total revenue of locally produced drugs will decrease.\n           (2)   Both the demand for and supply of locally produced drugs will increase.\n           (3)   The price and quantity transacted of imported drugs will decrease.\n           (4)   The total expenditure on imported drugs may increase.\n\n           A.    (1) and (3) only\n           B.    (1) and (4) only\n           C.    (2) and (3) only\n           D.    (2) and (4) only\n\n                                                EN D O F PAP E R",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    Advancements in technology will lead to an increase in the supply of locally produced drugs, causing\n    the price of locally produced drugs to decrease and the quantity transacted to increase.\n    (1) is correct. Since the percentage decrease in the price of locally produced drugs (40%) is greater than\n    the percentage increase in the quantity transacted (20%), the total revenue of locally produced drugs will\n    decrease.\n    (3) is correct. Locally produced drugs and imported drugs are substitutes. A decrease in the price of\n    locally produced drugs will reduce the demand for imported drugs, leading to a decrease in both the\n    price and quantity transacted of imported drugs.\n    (2) is incorrect. The supply of locally produced drugs will increase, and the price will decrease, resulting\n    in an increase in the quantity demanded of locally produced drugs. The demand for locally produced\n    drugs does not change.\n    (4) is incorrect. The price and quantity transacted of imported drugs will decrease, leading to a decrease\n    in total expenditure.",
