      "questionTextEng": "Kai Tak Sports Park officially opened in March 2025. It is Hong Kong’s largest integrated sports and\n                                                           entertainment landmark, providing sports venues, recreational spaces, retail and dining outlets and other\n                                                           facilities.\n\n                                                          Source A: News report on the first concert held at Kai Tak Sports Park\n\n                                                            The British band Coldplay held a concert at Kai Tak Stadium in Hong Kong in April 2025. This\n                                                            was the first large-scale concert after the opening of the Sports Park. The four concerts attracted a\n                                                            total of about 200,000 fans. Most tickets sold out quickly during the presale and public sale. Many\n                                                            fans reported that, with so many people waiting online to buy tickets, it was difficult to access the\n                                                            ticketing website, so they were unable to buy any tickets.\n\n                                                          Source B: Special traffic and transport arrangements at Kai Tak Sports Park during the dispersal period on the\n                                                          concert dates\n\n                                                            ⚫ Railway services: the service headway of the MTR Tuen Ma Line and East Rail Line will be\n                                                                enhanced, and spare trains will be arranged to meet the additional demand\n                                                            ⚫ Special bus route services:\n                                                                 - bus companies will arrange two additional special bus routes to Lok Ma Chau and the Hong\n                                                                 Kong-Zhuhai-Macao Bridge Hong Kong Port/Airport\n                                                                - a total of 11 special bus routes will be provided, covering major districts across the territory\n                                                            ⚫ Cross-boundary coach services: KTSP Limited (體育園公司) will arrange cross-boundary coach\n                                                                services to facilitate travellers’ return to the Mainland\n\n                                                          Source C: Some opinions on holding concerts at Kai Tak Sports Park\n                                                                                                         Organising a concert involves a huge amount of\n                                                                                                         manpower, including venue managers, stage technicians,\n                                                                                                         lighting engineers, and audiovisual equipment operators.\n\n                                                             A staff member of Kai Tak Sports Park\n                                                                                                         The concert attracted many people to the Kai Tak area,\n                                                                                                         and my restaurant was full during the days of the\n                                                                                                         concerts!\n\n                                                               A merchant in Kai Tak Sports Park\n                                                                                                         Many people buy tickets and resell them at high prices\n                                                                                                         for profit. I think this practice should be curbed!\n\n                                                               A fan who has watched the concert\n\n                                                        (a) Refer to Source A. Illustrate the market situation for the concert tickets mentioned in a demand-supply\n                                                            diagram.                                                                                      (3 marks)\n\n                                                        (b) Which TWO basic economic problems are being tackled by the special traffic and transport arrangements\n                                                            in Source B? Use ONE example for each to explain.                                           (4 marks)\n\n                                                        (c) Refer to the view of the staff member of Kai Tak Sports Park in Source C. Which economic principle is\n                                                            illustrated by the arrangements for concerts? State THREE reasons why such an arrangement can increase\n                                                            labour productivity.                                                                        (4 marks)\n\n                                                        For part (d), candidates are required to present their answer in essay form. Criteria for marking will include use\n                                                        of sources and economic theories, relevant content, logical presentation and clarity of expression.\n\n                                                        (d) Suppose there are two suggestions to help make better use of Kai Tak Sports Park.\n\n                                                                                Suggestion                                        Objective",
