      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following statements about interest is CORRECT?\n\n           A.    Interest only exists in a monetary economy.\n           B.    Interest only exists in a market economy.\n           C.    When the interest rate decreases, people will reduce current consumption.\n           D.    Without scarcity, interest will not exist.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n     Interest is the cost or price of earlier availability of resources. Without scarcity, people do not need to\n     make choices about current or future consumption, so interest does not exist.\n     Option A is incorrect. Interest can be in the form of goods or services. Interest can exist even without\n     money.\n     Option B is incorrect. Interest exists in any economy as long as there is borrowing and lending.\n     Option C is incorrect. A decrease in the interest rate reduces the cost of current consumption, thus\n     increasing current consumption.",
