      "questionTextEng": "A public limited company decides to issue bonds to raise capital for the expansion of its business. From the\n     viewpoint of the existing shareholders, which of the following is an advantage of issuing bonds over shares?\n\n           A.    The interest paid to the bondholders is lower than the dividends paid to the shareholders.\n           B.    The company does not need to disclose its accounting information to the public.\n           C.    The risk of the company being taken over by others will not be increased.\n           D.    The company can raise more capital.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n     Bondholders are creditors of the company, not owners, so issuing bonds does not increase the risk of the\n     company being taken over.\n     Option A is incorrect. The company needs to pay interest at a fixed rate to bondholders, while the\n     dividend is determined by the board of directors based on the company’s profits. Therefore, the amount\n     of dividend may be lower than the interest.\n     Option B is incorrect. A public limited company needs to disclose its accounting information to the\n     public, and issuing more bonds or shares does not affect this requirement.\n     Option D is incorrect. Issuing bonds does not necessarily raise more capital than issuing shares.",
