      "questionTextEng": "The following table shows the production information of a firm. The firm employs two inputs only, namely\n     machines and labour.\n\n          Machines (units)            Labour (units)         Average product (units) Total production cost ($)\n                2                          3                           20                      150\n                2                          4                           22                      200\n                2                          5                           25                      250\n                2                          6                           24                      300\n                2                          7                           23                      350\n\n     Which of the following statements about the above firm is CORRECT?\n\n           A.    The firm enjoys economies of scale.\n           B.    The law of diminishing marginal returns applies to the firm.\n           C.    The total product is at the highest when the quantity of labour is 6 units.\n           D.    The firm is at its optimal scale of production when the quantity of labour is 5 units.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n           Machines               Labour          Average product        Total product       Marginal product\n            (units)               (units)             (units)               (units)              (units)\n               2                     3                   20                      60                  -\n               2                     4                   22                      88                  28\n               2                     5                   25                   125                    37\n               2                     6                   24                   144                    19\n               2                     7                   23                   161                    17\n\n     When labour increases from 5 units to 6 units, the marginal product of labour decreases from 37 units to\n     19 units, so the law of diminishing marginal returns applies to the firm.\n     Options A and D are incorrect. There is a fixed factor of production (machines), showing that the firm is\n     operating in the short run. Economies of scale and optimal scale of production are thus not applicable to\n     the firm.\n     Option C is incorrect. The total product is at the highest when the quantity of labour is 7 units.",
