      "questionTextEng": "After opening more branches, a restaurant finds that its average production cost has increased. Which of the\n     following can be a possible reason?\n\n           (1)   The restaurant is suffering from external diseconomies of scale due to increased labour costs.\n           (2)   The restaurant is enjoying internal economies of scale due to decreased borrowing costs.\n           (3)   The restaurant is suffering from internal diseconomies of scale due to increased marketing expenses.\n\n           A.    (1) only\n           B.    (2) only\n           C.    (3) only\n           D.    (1) and (3) only",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n     (3) is correct. When the restaurant opens more branches, marketing expenses will increase. If the\n     increase in sales fails to cover the additional marketing expenses, the average production cost will\n     increase and the restaurant will suffer internal diseconomies of scale.",
