      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/41/a-p1-08.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "A singer sold some clothes he had previously worn, and they were all sold out within a short period of time. Many\n     people expressed that they were unable to buy them even though they were willing to pay the listed price.\n\n     From the information above, we can infer that at the prevailing price, the quantity transacted of the clothes is\n     _____________.\n\n           A.    equal to the quantity demanded and smaller than the quantity supplied\n           B.    equal to the quantity demanded and greater than the quantity supplied\n           C.    equal to the quantity supplied and smaller than the quantity demanded\n           D.    equal to the quantity supplied and greater than the quantity demanded",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n     The situation indicates that the price of the clothes is below the equilibrium price. At this price, the\n     quantity demanded exceeds the quantity supplied. Therefore, the quantity transacted equals the quantity\n     supplied, which is smaller than the quantity demanded.",
