      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/41/a-p1-10.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Good X and good Y are in joint supply. If consumers expect the price of good X to increase in the future,\n\n            (1)    the marginal benefit of the last unit of good Y will increase.\n            (2)    total revenue of good Y will increase.\n            (3)    consumer surplus in the market for good Y will increase.\n            (4)    the quantity transacted of good Y will increase.\n\n            A.     (1) and (2) only\n            B.     (1) and (4) only\n            C.     (2) and (3) only\n            D.     (3) and (4) only",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    If consumers expect the price of good X to increase in the future, the demand for good X will increase\n    and the price will increase. Since good X and good Y are in joint supply, an increase in the price of good\n     X will increase the supply of good Y. The price of good Y will decrease and the quantity transacted will\n     increase.\n     (3) is correct. Since consumers can buy more good Y at a lower price, consumer surplus in the market\n     for good Y will increase.\n     (1) is incorrect. Consumers consume until the price equals the marginal benefit, so the price reflects the\n     marginal benefit of the last unit of good Y. As the price of good Y decreases, the marginal benefit of the\n     last unit of good Y decreases.\n     (2) is incorrect. As the price of good Y decreases and the quantity transacted increases, total revenue\n     may increase, decrease or remain unchanged, depending on the price elasticity of demand for good Y.",
