      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/41/a-p1-13.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Refer to the following supply-demand diagram of good X.\n\n                     Unit price\n                                                       S\n\n                                                       D\n                                                                  Quantity\n                         0          Q1          Q2\n\n      Suppose the government adjusts the quota of good X from Q1 to Q2. Which of the following statements is\n      CORRECT?\n\n           A.    The consumer surplus will decrease.\n           B.    Deadweight loss will be eliminated.\n           C.    The total expenditure on good X will decrease.\n           D.    The quota will change from ineffective to effective.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    Q2 is an ineffective quota because it is greater than the equilibrium quantity of good X. When the quota\n    changes from effective to ineffective, the quantity transacted will increase to the efficient level and the\n    deadweight loss will be eliminated.\n    Option A is incorrect. As the price decreases and the quantity transacted increases, consumer surplus\n    will increase.\n    Option C is incorrect. As the increase in total expenditure due to the increase in quantity transacted is\n    greater than the decrease in total expenditure due to the decrease in price, the total expenditure on good\n    X will increase.",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/41/ae-p1-13.jpg",
