      "questionTextEng": "The following table shows the marginal benefit schedule of a consumer for coconut water.\n\n        Quantity (units)               1                2           3                4             5\n        Marginal benefit ($)          25                24         23                22            21\n\n      If the price of coconut water increases from $22 to $23, consumer surplus will _____________.\n\n           A.    increase by $1\n           B.    increase by $3\n           C.    decrease by $1\n           D.    decrease by $3",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    When the price is $22, quantity demanded is 4 units. Consumer surplus = ($25 − $22) + ($24 − $22) +\n    ($23 – $22) + ($22 − $22) = $6\n    When the price is $23, quantity demanded is 3 units. Consumer surplus = ($25 − $23) + ($24 − $23) +\n    ($23 − $23) = $3\n\n    Therefore, if the price of coconut water increases from $22 to $23, consumer surplus will decrease by\n    $3.",
