      "inlineDiagrams": "diagrams/MT41-P1-18.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Refer to the following supply-demand diagram for rice. P0 is the price ceiling set by the government.\n                     Price\n\n                                                                   S\n\n                    P0\n\n                                                               D\n                      0                                                Quantity\n\n      Suppose rice is a normal good and the economy is experiencing an economic recovery. Which of the following\n      statements are CORRECT?\n\n            (1)   The excess demand for rice will increase.\n            (2)   Deadweight loss will increase.\n            (3)   The marginal cost of the last unit of rice will decrease.\n\n            A.    (1) and (2) only\n            B.    (1) and (3) only\n            C.    (2) and (3) only\n            D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    (1) is correct. If the economy experiences an economic recovery and rice is a normal good, demand for\n    rice will increase. Since the quantity supplied remains at Q0, excess demand for rice will increase.\n    (2) is correct. At the quantity transacted (Q0), an increase in the demand for rice will widen the gap\n    between marginal benefit and marginal cost, and deadweight loss will increase.\n    (3) is incorrect. The marginal cost of the last unit of rice will remain unchanged (MC1).\n\n               Price\n                                                                           Original deadweight loss\n            MB2\n                                                        S\n                                                                            New deadweight loss\n            MB1\n\n                                           New excess demand\n      P0 = MC1\n                             Original excess demand         D1\n\n                                                    D\n                0                                           Quantity\n                                Q0     Q1",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/41/ae-p1-18.jpg",
