      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/41/q-p1-19.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/41/a-p1-19.jpg",
      "inlineDiagrams": "diagrams/MT41-P1-19.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The following diagram shows the Lorenz curves of Country A and Country B.\n\n                       100\n\n                         80\n\n                         60\n          Cumulative\n          percentage\n          of income      40\n\n                                           Country B\n                         20\n                                                          Country A\n\n                          0          20       40       60        80       100\n                                Cumulative percentage of households\n\n      Suppose the total incomes in the two counties are equal. Based on the above information, which of the following\n      statements are CORRECT?\n\n           (1)   The total income of the bottom 20% of households in Country A is lower than the total income of the\n                 bottom 20% of households in Country B.\n           (2)   The top 10% of households in Country A earn a smaller proportion of the country’s total income than\n                 that in Country B.\n           (3)   Country A has more high-income people.\n\n           A.    (1) and (2) only\n           B.    (1) and (3) only\n           C.    (2) and (3) only\n           D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    (1) is correct. When the cumulative percentage of households is 20%, Country A’s Lorenz curve is\n    below Country B’s Lorenz curve, indicating that the total income of the lowest 20% of households in\n    Country A is lower than that in Country B.\n\n    (2) is correct. When the cumulative percentage of households is 90%, Country A’s Lorenz curve is\n    above Country B’s Lorenz curve, meaning that the proportion of income earned by the lowest 90% of\n    households in Country A is higher than that of Country B. In other words, the proportion of income\n    earned by the highest 10% of households in Country A is lower than that of Country B.\n    (3) is incorrect. The Lorenz curve shows the cumulative percentage of households. Since we do not have\n    data on the number of households in both countries, we cannot determine which country has more\n    high-income people.",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/41/ae-p1-19.jpg",
      "originalQuestionImageEng": "originals/41/qe-p1-19.jpg",
