      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/41/a-p1-21.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The following diagram shows the production chain for umbrellas in an economy.\n\n                                                                                      $2,000\n       Imported raw                                                                   ($100 tax\n         materials       $300                                                         inclusive)\n                                    Local umbrella      $1,200\n                                                                      Retailers                       Local\n                                    manufacturers\n         Local raw       $250                                                                       consumers\n         materials                                          $X\n\n                                                                      Foreign\n                                                                     consumers\n\n      The contribution of the above production chain to the economy’s GDP at factor cost is $3,000. The value of X is\n      ________.\n\n           A.    $1,150\n           B.    $1,200\n           C.    $1,400\n           D.    $1,700",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    Value added of local raw materials = $250\n    Value added of local umbrella manufacturers = ($1,200 + $X) – ($300 + $250) = $650 + $X\n    Value added of retailers = $2,000 – $1,200 = $800\n    Contribution of the production chain to the economy’s GDP at market prices = $250 + $650 + X + $800\n    = $1,700 + X\n    Contribution of the production chain to the economy’s GDP at factor cost ($3,000) = $1,700 + X – $100\n    X = $1,400",
