      "questionTextEng": "The following table shows the Gross Domestic Product (GDP) data of an economy in a certain year.\n\n                                  Components                     $ million\n                     Private consumption expenditure               500\n                     Net domestic fixed capital formation          300\n                     Government consumption expenditure            350\n                     Changes in inventories                         20\n                     Net export of goods                           600\n                     Re-exports                                     80\n                     Imports of services                           300\n                     Exports of services                           350\n                     Capital consumption allowance                  25\n                     Direct taxes                                   20\n                     Indirect taxes                                  5\n\n      The GDP at market prices is $_____________ million.\n\n           A.    1,820\n           B.    1,805\n           C.    1,845\n           D.    1,925",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    GDP = Private consumption expenditure + Gross investment + Government consumption expenditure +\n    Net exports\n    GDP at market prices = $500 million + $(300 + 25 + 20) million + $350 million + $(600 + 350 − 300)\n    million\n    GDP at market prices = $(500 + 345 + 350 + 650) million = $1,845 million",
