      "questionTextEng": "The following table shows the data of an economy in a certain year.\n\n                        Indirect taxes                                      $20 million\n                        Direct taxes                                        $10 million\n                        Subsidies                                           $15 million\n                        Net factor income from abroad                       ‒$50 million\n                        Net exports                                         ‒$50 million\n                        GDP deflator                                            98\n\n      Which of the following statements about the economy is CORRECT?\n\n           A.    Nominal GDP is greater than real GDP.\n           B.    Gross national income is smaller than gross domestic product.\n           C.    GDP at factor cost is greater than GDP at market prices.\n           D.    Total exports are greater than total imports.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    GNI = GDP + Net factor income from abroad\n    Since net factor income from abroad is negative, GNI is smaller than GDP.\n    Option A is incorrect. GDP deflator = (Nominal GDP/Real GDP) × 100\n    The GDP deflator is smaller than 100, which means nominal GDP is smaller than real GDP.\n    Option C is incorrect. GDP at factor cost = GDP at market prices − Indirect taxes + Subsidies\n    GDP at factor cost = GDP at market prices − $20 million + $15 million\n    GDP at factor cost is smaller than GDP at market prices.\n    Option D is incorrect. Net exports = Total exports − Total imports\n    Since net exports are negative, total exports are smaller than total imports.",
