      "questionTextEng": "Country A’s implicit price deflator of GDP rose by 8% in 2024, while its nominal GDP rose by 6% and its\n      population fell by 1% during the same period.\n\n      Based on the above information, we can conclude that Country A’s per capita nominal GDP in 2024 has\n      _____________, while its per capita real GDP has _____________.\n\n           A.    increased ... increased\n           B.    increased ... decreased\n           C.    decreased ... increased\n           D.    decreased ... decreased",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    An increase in nominal GDP (6%) and a decrease in population (–1%) reflect an increase in per capita\n    nominal GDP.\n    Real GDP = (Nominal GDP / Implicit price deflator of GDP) × 100\n    In 2024, the growth rate of nominal GDP (6%) is lower than the growth rate of implicit price deflator of\n    GDP (8%), which means that real GDP has decreased by about 1.85% [= 1 − (1 + 6%) / (1 + 8%)].\n    Since the percentage decrease in real GDP (1.85%) is higher than the percentage decrease in population\n    (1%), it reflects a decrease in per capita real GDP.",
