      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/41/q-p1-30.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/41/a-p1-30.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The government of an economy has the following policy proposals:\n\n          I. to introduce more capital to support production\n          II. to tighten the visa requirements for foreign visitors\n          III. to raise the salaries tax rate\n          IV. to provide transportation subsidies to housewives who re-enter the workplace\n\n      Which of the following combinations is most likely to increase the economy’s aggregate output in the short run?\n\n            A.    policies I and II\n            B.    policies I and IV\n            C.    policies II and III\n            D.    policies III and IV",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    Policy I: When the government introduces more capital to support production, firms’ productivity will\n    increase and short run aggregate supply will increase. In the short run, aggregate output will increase.\n    Policy II: When the government tightens the visa requirements for foreign visitors, the number of\n    travelers to the economy will decrease. Net exports will decrease and aggregate demand will decrease.\n    In the short run, aggregate output will decrease.\n    Policy III: When the government raises the salaries tax rate, people’s disposable income will decrease.\n    Private consumption expenditure will decrease and aggregate demand will decrease. In the short run,\n\n    aggregate output will decrease.\n    Policy IV: When the government provides transportation subsidies to housewives who re-enter the\n    workplace, it encourages more housewives to work. Short run aggregate supply will increase. In\n    addition, the transportation subsidies will increase people’s disposable income, private consumption\n    expenditure will increase and aggregate demand will increase. To conclude, in the short run, aggregate\n    output will increase.\n    Option B is correct. In the short run, aggregate output will increase.\n    Options A and D are incorrect. In the short run, aggregate output may increase, decrease or remain\n    unchanged.\n    Option C is incorrect. In the short run, aggregate output will decrease.",
