      "questionTextEng": "Study the following information about an economy.\n\n             Monetary base                             $1,400 million\n             Money supply                              $5,000 million\n             Cash in public circulation                 $200 million\n\n      Suppose the banks do not hold excess reserves. If the public deposit $100 million in cash into the banking system,\n\n           A.    the maximum possible amount of money supply will be $5,400 million.\n           B.    the maximum possible amount of loans will be $3,900 million.\n           C.    the maximum possible amount of deposits will be $4,900 million.\n           D.    the monetary base of the economy will decrease by $100 million.",
