      "questionTextEng": "Figure 2 shows the aggregate demand (AD) curve, short run aggregate supply (SRAS) curve and long run\n                                                          aggregate supply (LRAS) curve for an oil-importing country.\n\n                                                                                              Figure 2\n                                                                         Price level\n                                                                                       LRAS\n\n                                                                                                              SRAS\n\n                                                                                                              AD\n\n                                                                                                                        Aggregate output\n                                                                            0            Yf\n\n                                                          (a)   Explain whether the economy has a deflationary (output) gap or an inflationary (output) gap. (2 marks)\n\n                                                          (b) Suppose the price of oil drops significantly. With the aid of Figure 2, explain how the gap will be\n                                                              affected.                                                                                 (6 marks)\n\n                                                          (c)   WITHOUT using a diagram, explain how market forces can restore the output level to the long run\n                                                                equilibrium in the long run.                                                          (4 marks)",
