      "questionTextEng": "The following table shows the balance sheet of a banking system. The banks hold an excess reserve of\n                                                           $500 million and the public hold $200 million cash.\n\n                                                                                      Assets ($ million)               Liabilities ($ million)\n                                                                              Reserves                     3,000   Deposits                10,000\n                                                                              Loans                        7,000\n\n                                                          (a)   Calculate the required reserve ratio for the above banking system.                                (1 mark)\n\n                                                          Suppose the central bank reduces the required reserve ratio by 5 percentage points.\n\n                                                          (b) Suppose the banks no longer hold excess reserves and the amount of cash held in public remains\n                                                              unchanged. Complete the following balance sheet after the deposit creation process is completed.\n\n                                                                                      Assets ($ million)               Liabilities ($ million)\n                                                                              Reserves                _______      Deposits              _______\n                                                                              Loans                   _______\n                                                                                                                                                                 (3 marks)\n\n                                                          (c)   Explain the short run effects of a reduction in the required reserve ratio on the output and price levels of\n\n                                                                the economy.                                                                                      (5 marks)",
      "originalQuestionImageEng": "originals/41/qe-p2-08.jpg",
