      "questionTextEng": "Macy is a university student who is planning how to spend her summer holiday. She has several options and her\n     order of preference is shown below:\n\n                             First option: to travel to Europe\n                             Second option: to work as a private Economics tutor\n                             Third option: to work part-time in a fast-food shop\n\n     Which of the following factors would LEAST likely affect Macy’s cost-benefit analysis for her choice?\n\n           A.    A tourist attraction in Europe that Macy longs to visit is temporarily closed for maintenance.\n           B.    Benefits for part-time workers at the fast-food shop are reduced.\n           C.    The working hours for working part-time at the fast-food shop become more flexible.\n           D.    The tutoring student gets along very well with Macy.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n     Macy would choose the first option as the benefit of choosing the first option (the value of the first\n     option) is higher than the cost (the value of the second option).\n     Option B is correct. This would reduce the value of the third option without affecting Macy’s cost or\n     benefit of choosing the first option.\n     Option A is incorrect. This would reduce the value of the first option, thus decreasing Macy’s benefit of\n     choosing the first option.\n     Option C is incorrect. This may increase the value of the third option to a level higher than that of the\n     second option, so the cost of choosing the first option may change from the value of the second option\n     to that of the third option.\n     Option D is incorrect. This would increase the value of the second option, thus increasing Macy’s cost\n     of choosing the first option.",
