      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following cases are related to the problem of ‘how to produce’?\n\n           (1)   A technology company locates its data centre in a country with lower electricity costs.\n           (2)   A hospital hires more non-local doctors to provide medical services.\n           (3)   An education center offers English phonics classes for children.\n\n           A.    (1) and (2) only\n           B.    (1) and (3) only\n           C.    (2) and (3) only\n           D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n     (1) is correct. Deciding which country to locate the data center involves a decision regarding the\n     production method and is related to the ‘how to produce’ problem.\n     (2) is correct. Hiring non-local doctors concerns what type of factors of production to use and is related\n     to the ‘how to produce’ problem.\n     (3) is incorrect. Deciding what courses to offer concerns the kinds of services to produce and is related\n     to the ‘what to produce’ problem.",
