      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/42/a-p1-06.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "In a newspaper company, different reporters specialise in covering different types of news. For example, some\n     reporters cover sports news, while others cover financial news.\n\n     Compared to an arrangement in which each reporter covering all types of news, which of the following are the\n     benefits of the above arrangement?\n\n           (1)   The time required for reporters to write each article will be reduced since practice makes perfect.\n           (2)   The time required to train junior reporters to master relevant knowledge will be reduced.\n           (3)   The tools required for writing articles will be reduced, such as requiring fewer personal computers.\n\n           A.    (1) and (2) only\n           B.    (1) and (3) only\n           C.    (2) and (3) only\n           D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n     (1) is correct. Having each reporter specialise in covering a specific type of news helps workers\n     accumulate experience, increasing average labour productivity.\n     (2) is correct. Each reporter only needs to have a deep understanding of a specific area of knowledge,\n     rather than learning all types of news writing, so training time is reduced.\n     (3) is incorrect. Having each reporter specialise in covering a specific type of news would not reduce the\n     number of personal computers (capital goods) required.",
