      "questionTextEng": "Mr. Cheung runs a restaurant in Mong Kok serving ‘Rice with two sides’ (「兩餸飯」). He is considering whether\n     to expand the kitchen of the existing restaurant to increase the number of meal boxes produced each day, or to\n     open a new branch in another district.\n\n     Based on the above information, which of the following is a possible reason for Mr. Cheung to choose to expand\n     the kitchen scale of the existing restaurant instead of opening a new branch?\n\n           A.    A greater degree of division of labour can be practised in the same kitchen to reduce the average cost\n                 of production.\n           B.    Mr. Cheung will receive discounts for purchasing more ingredients.\n           C.    The restaurant can spread the transportation costs over a larger quantity of output and enjoy external\n                 economies of scale.\n           D.    Business risks can be diversified.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n     When the kitchen is expanded, internal economies of scale can be enjoyed through a higher degree of\n     division of labour, which reduces the average cost of production.\n     Option B is incorrect. Regardless of whether the kitchen is expanded or a new branch is opened,\n     discounts may be obtained by purchasing larger quantities of ingredients.\n     Option C is incorrect. Reducing average cost by expanding the existing production scale reflects internal\n     economies of scale.\n     Option D is incorrect. Since both expanding the kitchen and opening a new branch are business\n    expansions that produce the same product, neither can diversify business risks.",
