      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/42/q-p1-10.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/42/a-p1-10.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The table below shows the cost-output relationship of a price-taking firm.\n\n            Output (units)                    2           3              4             5             6\n            Average cost ($)                  4           5              6             7             8\n\n     After the increase in the marginal cost per unit of output, the profit-maximising output level decreases from 5\n     units to 3 units. The marginal cost per unit of output has increased by __________ and the profit will\n     __________.\n\n           A.    $2 ... increase by $2\n           B.    $4 ... increase by $14\n           C.    $2 ... decrease by $2\n           D.    $4 ... decrease by $14",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n      Output (units)                   2             3            4            5            6\n      Original average cost ($)        4             5            6            7            8\n      Original total cost ($)          8            15           24            35           48\n      Original marginal cost ($)     MC2             7            9            11           13\n\n    At the profit-maximising output level, marginal revenue equals marginal cost. The original\n    profit-maximising output level is 5 units, reflecting a market price of $11. At the new profit-maximising\n    output level (3 units), marginal revenue ($11) equals the new marginal cost (= the original marginal cost\n    of the 3rd unit + the change in marginal cost), reflecting an increase of $4 in marginal cost per unit of\n    output.\n    Since both the marginal cost of the 1st unit and the marginal cost of the 2nd unit have increased by $4,\n    the total cost of the 2 units will increase by $8 (= $4 × 2).\n      Output (units)                   2              3             4          5            6\n      New marginal cost ($)        MC2 + 4           11             13        15           17\n      New total cost ($)             16              27             40        55           72\n                               = ($8 + $4 × 2)\n    Original profit = Total revenue – Total cost = ($11 × 5) – $35 = $20\n    New profit = ($11 × 3) – $27 = $6\n    The profit will decrease by $14.",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/42/ae-p1-10.jpg",
      "originalQuestionImageEng": "originals/42/qe-p1-10.jpg",
      "stemPatterns": [
        "（成本表）邊際成本改變後，利潤極大化產量及利潤會 __________"
      ]
