      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/42/q-p1-12.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/42/a-p1-12.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The underground railway in a city is often full during peak hours and passengers have to wait for multiple trains\n    before they can board. Which of the following events would shorten the waiting time for passengers?\n\n            (1)   The government increases bus fare concessions for the elderly.\n            (2)   The underground railway company increases the train frequency.\n            (3)   The underground railway company provides fare concessions during non-peak hours.\n\n            A.    (1) only\n            B.    (2) only\n            C.    (1) and (2) only\n            D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    There is excess demand for underground railway services during peak hours. Reducing the excess\n    demand can shorten the waiting time for passengers.\n    (1) is correct. Bus services and underground railway services are substitutes. Increasing bus fare\n    concessions for the elderly reduces their demand for underground railway services, and excess demand\n    will decrease.\n    (2) is correct. When the train frequency increases, the supply of underground railway services will\n    increase, and excess demand will decrease.\n    (3) is correct. Non-peak and peak-hour underground railway services are substitutes. If the underground\n    railway company provides fare concessions during non-peak hours, the demand for underground\n    railway services during peak hours will decrease, and excess demand will decrease.",
