      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/42/a-p1-15.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Suppose the demand for good Y is inelastic. In which of the following cases will an increase in the price of good X\n    lead to an increase in the total revenue of good Y?\n\n            (1)   Good X and good Y are in joint demand.\n            (2)   Good X and good Y are in competitive supply.\n            (3)   Good X and good Y are in joint supply.\n\n            A.    (1) only\n            B.    (2) only\n            C.    (3) only\n            D.    (1) and (3) only",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    (2) is correct. When the price of good X increases, the supply of good Y will decrease. As the demand\n    for good Y is inelastic, the percentage increase in price will be greater than the percentage decrease in\n    quantity demanded, and total revenue of good Y will increase.\n    (1) is incorrect. When the price of good X increases, the demand for good Y will decrease, and total\n    revenue of good Y will decrease.\n    (3) is incorrect. When the price of good X increases, the supply of good Y will increase. As the demand\n    for good Y is inelastic, the percentage decrease in price will be greater than the percentage increase in\n    quantity demanded, and total revenue of good Y will decrease.",
