      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    Producers’ total revenue (including the subsidy) = ($16 + $2) × 24 = $432\n    Option A is incorrect. The supply of good X is perfectly inelastic. If the government imposes a per-unit\n    tax of $2 on good X, the quantity transacted will remain at 24 units.\n    Option B is incorrect. The equilibrium price is $16. The price floor set at $14 is ineffective and the\n    market for good X is in equilibrium.\n    Option C is incorrect. The equilibrium price is $16. The price ceiling set at $14 is effective and\n    consumers’ total expenditure on good X will be $336 (= $14 × 24).",
