      "inlineDiagrams": "diagrams/MT42-P1-20.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Refer to the following demand-supply diagram for good X. Initially, the quota is set at Q1.\n\n                                 Unit price\n                                         SQ1    SQ2                 S\n                                   a\n\n                                    b\n                                                     d\n                                    P1    c\n\n                                                e\n\n                                          f\n\n                                     g\n                                                               D1       D2\n                                     0                                         Quantity\n                                          Q1        Q2\n\n      When the demand for good X increases from D1 to D2 and the quota changes from Q1 to Q2, the price remains at\n      P1. Which of the following statements about the above situation is CORRECT?\n\n            A.    There is no deadweight loss in the market for good X.\n            B.    Consumer surplus increases by area bcP1.\n            C.    Producer surplus increases by area cdef.\n            D.    There is an excess supply of (Q2 – Q1) in the market for good X.",
