      "questionTextEng": "To calculate Hong Kong’s gross national income (GNI), which of the following should be added to Hong Kong’s\n      gross domestic product (GDP)?\n\n           A.    the dividends received by a Japanese resident from a listed company in Hong Kong\n           B.    the salary earned by an American working in a bank in Hong Kong for six months\n           C.    the rent received by a Hong Kong resident from a property in the United Kingdom\n           D.    the salary earned by a Hong Kong engineer working in a Korean company for three years",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    GNI = GDP + Factor income earned by residents outside the economic territory − Factor income earned\n    by non-residents within the economic territory\n    Options A and B are incorrect. They are factor income earned by non-residents within the economic\n    territory.\n    Option D is incorrect. Since the engineer has worked in Korea for more than one year, he is no longer a\n    resident of Hong Kong and the income he earns does not belong to factor income earned by residents\n    outside the economic territory.",
