      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/42/q-p1-26.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/42/a-p1-26.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The following table shows some data of an economy in a certain year.\n\n                                                                   $ million\n                     Subsidies                                        20\n                     Direct taxes                                     15\n                     Indirect taxes                                   8\n                     Net exports of services                          40\n                     Total exports of goods                          105\n                     Total imports of goods                          180\n                     Re-exports of goods                              45\n                     Net factor income from abroad                   –25\n\n      Which of the following statements about the economy are CORRECT?\n\n           (1)   GDP at market prices is smaller than GDP at factor cost.\n           (2)   Net exports is positive.\n           (3)   GNI is smaller than GDP.\n\n           A.    (1) and (2) only\n           B.    (1) and (3) only\n           C.    (2) and (3) only\n           D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    (1) is correct. GDP at market prices = GDP at factor cost + Indirect taxes – Subsidies\n    Since indirect taxes are smaller than subsidies, GDP at market prices is smaller than GDP at factor cost.\n    (3) is correct. GNI = GDP + Net factor income from abroad\n    As net factor income from abroad is negative, GNI is smaller than GDP.\n    (2) is incorrect. Net exports of goods = Total exports of goods – Total imports of goods\n    Net exports of goods = $105 million – $180 million = –75 million\n    Net exports = Net exports of goods + Net exports of services = –75 million + $40 million = –35 million\n    Net exports is negative.",
