      "graphType": "-",
      "tableType": "-",
      "multipleSelectionType": "-",
      "calculationType": "-",
      "source": "模擬試卷四十二 卷一",
      "reviewedByAI": "Y",
      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/42/q-p1-27.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/42/a-p1-27.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following would MOST likely help an economy narrow the inflationary (output) gap?\n\n            A.    The government provides production subsidies to firms, and the trading partner of the economy\n                  experiences an economic recovery.\n            B.    Labour cost increases, and the government reduces its spending on national defense.\n            C.    The technological level of production increases, and people have an increased preference for imported\n                  consumer goods.\n            D.    Firms suspend their production due to a typhoon, and firms buy more inventories.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    An increase in labour cost will increase the cost of production for firms and short run aggregate supply\n    will decrease. A reduction in government spending on national defense will reduce government\n    expenditure and aggregate demand will decrease. To conclude, the output level will decrease and the\n    inflationary (output) gap will be narrowed.\n    Option A is incorrect. The government’s provision of production subsidies to firms will reduce the cost\n    of production for firms and short run aggregate supply will increase. As the trading partner of the\n    economy experiences an economic recovery, net exports will increase and aggregate demand will\n    increase. To conclude, the output level will increase and the inflationary (output) gap will be widened.\n    Option C is incorrect. When the technological level of production increases, short run aggregate supply\n    and long run aggregate supply will increase. When people have an increased preference for imported\n    consumer goods, net exports will decrease and aggregate demand will decrease. The change in the\n    output level in the short run will be uncertain, while the potential output level will increase and the\n    change in the inflationary (output) gap will be uncertain.\n    Option D is incorrect. When the typhoon caused firms to suspend production, short run aggregate\n    supply will decrease. When firms buy more inventories, investment expenditure will increase and\n    aggregate demand will increase. To conclude, the change in the output level will be uncertain.",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/42/ae-p1-27.jpg",
