      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    Reserves + Loans = Deposits\n    When reserves decrease by $100 million and deposits decrease by $400 million, this means that loans\n    decrease by $300 million.\n    Option A is incorrect. Monetary base = Cash in public circulation + Bank reserves\n    When the public withdraw money and remit it overseas, cash in public circulation will remain the same\n    and bank reserves will decrease by $100 million. Monetary base will decrease by $100 million.\n    Option B is incorrect. Money supply = Cash in public circulation + Bank deposits\n    Bank deposits decrease by $400 million, so the money supply decreases by $400 million.\n    Option C is incorrect. If banks hold excess reserves before the withdrawal, the required reserve ratio\n    may not be equal to 25%.",
