      "questionTextEng": "The diagram below shows the money supply curve (Ms) and money demand curve (Md) of an economy. Suppose\n    the initial equilibrium point is at E.\n\n                   Nominal interest rate (%)\n                                                 Ms\n\n                                                   E\n\n                                                                      Md\n                              0\n                                                                              Quantity of money\n\n    Suppose people are more concerned about bond defaults and the government increases the amount of government\n    bonds it buys from the public each month. In this case, the nominal interest rate ___________, and the quantity of\n    money ___________.\n\n           A.    will increase ... will increase\n           B.    will increase ... will decrease\n           C.    may increase or decrease ... will increase\n           D.    may increase or decrease ... will decrease",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    When people are more concerned about bond defaults, the asset demand for money will increase, and\n    the money demand will increase. The nominal interest rate will increase and the quantity of money will\n    remain unchanged.\n    The government increasing the amount of government bonds it buys from the public each month will\n    increase the money supply. The nominal interest rate will decrease, and the quantity of money will\n    increase.\n    To conclude, the nominal interest rate may increase or decrease, and the quantity of money will\n    increase.",
