      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following is/are contractionary monetary policy/policies?\n\n              (1)      The People’s Bank of China raises the required reserve ratio.\n              (2)      The Bank of China issues bonds denominated in Renminbi.\n              (3)      The Ministry of Finance of the People’s Republic of China provides cash subsidies to consumers to\n                       buy home appliances.\n\n              A.       (1) only\n              B.       (3) only\n              C.       (1) and (2) only\n              D.       (2) and (3) only",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    (1) is correct. Raising the required reserve ratio will reduce money supply, and the interest rate will\n    increase. Consumption and investment will decrease, and aggregate demand will decrease. Thus, it is a\n    contractionary monetary policy.\n    (2) is incorrect. The Bank of China is a commercial bank, not China’s central bank. The issuance of\n    bonds by a commercial bank does not constitute monetary policy.\n    (3) is incorrect. Providing cash subsidies to consumers is not a monetary policy, but a fiscal policy.",
