      "calculationType": "-",
      "source": "模擬試卷四十二 卷一",
      "reviewedByAI": "Y",
      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/42/q-p1-42.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/42/a-p1-42.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The following table shows the labour requirement for the production of good X and good Y in Country A and\n    Country B respectively.\n\n                                        1 unit of good X                1 unit of good Y\n                   Country A              2 man-hours                     3 man-hours\n                   Country B             0.4 man-hours                   1.2 man-hours\n\n    Suppose the transportation cost for 1 unit of good Y is 1 unit of good X and it is borne equally by both countries.\n    Which of the following is a mutually beneficial terms of trade between Country A and Country B?\n\n           (1)   1 unit of good X = 0.4 units of good Y\n           (2)   1 unit of good X = 0.45 units of good Y\n           (3)   1 unit of good X = 2.25 units of good Y\n\n           A.    (1) only\n           B.    (2) only\n           C.    (3) only\n           D.    (1) and (2) only",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    The opportunity cost of producing 1 unit of good Y in Country A = 1.5 (= 3 / 2) units of good X\n    The opportunity cost of producing 1 unit of good Y in Country B = 3 (= 1.2 / 0.4) units of good X\n    The range of terms of trade over which exchange between the two countries is mutually beneficial is\n    2X (= 1.5X + 0.5X) < 1Y < 2.5X (= 3X – 0.5X), that is, 0.4Y < 1X < 0.5Y.",
