      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/42/a-p1-43.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "A small open economy has imposed a per-unit tariff on imported good X. Suppose the international price of good X\n    decreases. Which of the following statements are CORRECT?\n\n           (1)   The domestic production of good X will decrease.\n           (2)   The government’s tariff revenue will increase.\n           (3)   The total value of imports of good X net of tax will increase.\n\n           A.    (1) and (2) only\n           B.    (1) and (3) only\n           C.    (2) and (3) only\n           D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    (1) is correct. When the international price decreases, domestic price will also decrease and domestic\n    production will decrease.\n    (2) is correct. When the international price decreases, the import volume will increase. Assuming the\n    per-unit tariff remains unchanged, the government’s tariff revenue will increase.\n    (3) is incorrect. The price net of tax will decrease and the import volume will increase. The total value\n    of imports net of tax may increase, decrease, or remain unchanged.",
