      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/42/a-p2-07.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The table below shows the production and consumption data of Country A. The country only produces and\n                                                          consumes food and computers.\n\n                                                                                                              Food (units)                Computers (units)\n                                                                Total production without trade                     60            AND              20\n                                                                Total production with specialisation               0             AND             100\n                                                                Total consumption with trade                       84            AND              30\n\n                                                          (a)   Calculate the opportunity cost of producing 1 unit of computers for Country A.                 (2 marks)\n\n                                                          (b) Find the terms of trade for 1 unit of computers.                                                 (2 marks)\n\n                                                          (c)   Suppose Country B is the only trading partner of Country A. Country B has to pay 0.1 units of food as\n                                                                transportation cost for each unit of computers traded and Country B’s total gain from trade is 17.5 units\n                                                                of food. Calculate the opportunity cost of producing 1 unit of computers in Country B.         (3 marks)\n\n                                                                                                   END OF SECTION A\n\n                                                     Section B (60 marks)",
