      "questionTextEng": "In 20X5, several egg farms in Country B experienced outbreaks of bird flu. To prevent the spread of the\n                                                           disease, Country B has culled over 50 million chickens.\n\n                                                          (a)   Explain whether the value of these culled chickens would be included in the calculation of the gross\n                                                                domestic product (GDP) of Country B.                                                      (2 marks)\n\n                                                          (b) With the outbreak of bird flu, the price of eggs has risen sharply. As a result, some people are planning\n                                                              to raise chickens in their backyards to produce eggs.\n\n                                                                 (i)   Explain ONE function of price illustrated in the above case.                          (2 marks)\n\n                                                                 (ii) Give TWO possible reasons to explain why the average cost of producing eggs in backyards is\n                                                                      often higher than that in firms specialising in egg production.                    (4 marks)\n\n                                                          (c)   Vaccinating chickens against bird flu can reduce their chances of contracting bird flu. Some people have\n\n                                                                suggested that the government provide subsidies to egg farms for vaccinating their chickens against bird\n                                                                flu. In terms of externalities, explain how this suggestion can improve economic efficiency. (4 marks)\n\n                                                          (d) Culling chickens has caused egg prices in Country B to rise. To lower the price of eggs, the government\n                                                              of Country B is importing more eggs from other countries. Explain how this will affect the current\n                                                              account balance of Country B.                                                                  (2 marks)",
