      "questionTextEng": "MusicNet is the only online streaming music platform in Country A. The cost of serving one additional\n                                                           listener is zero.\n                                                                                            Figure 2\n\n                                                                             Unit price\n\n                                                                                                                D0: Demand\n                                                                                                                MR0: Marginal revenue\n\n                                                                                               MR0        D0           Quantity\n                                                                               0\n\n                                                           (a)   Suppose MusicNet adopts simple monopoly pricing. Indicate the profit-maximising output and price\n                                                                 as QM and PM respectively in Figure 2.                                                  (2 marks)\n\n                                                           (b)   With the aid of Figure 2, explain why MusieNet adopting simple monopoly pricing will cause a\n                                                                 deadweight loss.                                                                        (2 marks)\n\n                                                           (c)    Suppose the demand for the services provided by MusicNet increases while MusicNet does not\n                                                                  change its output and price. With the aid of Figure 2, explain whether economic efficiency will be\n                                                                  affected.                                                                                   (5 marks)\n                                                                 (For simplicity, assume that the demand curve shifts in parallel.)\n\n                                                           (d)   MusicNet offers the following subscription plans.\n\n                                                                  Basic plan: 60 A-Dollar* per month, limited to 1 device\n                                                                  Standard plan: 90 A-Dollar per month, allowing 2 devices to stream simultaneously\n                                                                  Premium plan: 120 A-Dollar per month, allowing 4 devices to stream simultaneously\n\n                                                                  *the currency of Country A\n\n                                                                 Explain whether the pricing arrangement constitutes price discrimination.                   (3 marks)\n\n                                                           (e)   MusicNet has signed an agreement with another online music streaming platform in Country B that\n                                                                 prohibits that company from entering the market in Country A. In exchange, MusicNet will also not\n                                                                 enter the market in Country B.\n\n                                                                 (i)   Name the anti-competitive behaviour that the above agreement may engage in. State ONE\n                                                                       possible motive of MusicNet.                                                       (2 marks)\n\n                                                                 (ii) If the above case happened in Hong Kong, which conduct rule of the Competition Ordinance\n                                                                      would MusicNet have violated? Explain.                                            (2 marks)",
