      "inlineDiagrams": "diagrams/MT42-P2-12.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Refer to Figure 3. PPFA and PPFFB are the production possibility frontiers of Country A and Country B\n                                                           respectively.\n                                                                                                       Figure 3\n                                                                             Good Y\n\n                                                                                      PB\n\n                                                                                                                  PA\n\n                                                                                                                   PPFA\n                                                                                                          PPFB\n                                                                                0                                         Good X\n\n                                                           PA and PB are the production points under autarky of Country A and Country B respectively.\n\n                                                           (a)   Explain why the production possibility frontiers of Country A and Country B are concave to the\n                                                                 origin.                                                                                    (2 marks)\n\n                                                           (b)   Show the opportunity cost of producing good X in the two countries in Figure 3. Explain why\n                                                                 Country B has a comparative advantage in producing good X. (Hint: you may add two straight lines at\n                                                                 PA and PB respectively.)                                                                  (4 marks)\n\n                                                           (c)   Suppose Country A and Country B trade at an international price.\n\n                                                                 (i)   Indicate the production points of Country A and Country B after trade as PTA and PTB\n                                                                       respectively in Figure 3.                                                              (2 marks)\n\n                                                                 (ii) Indicate the consumption possibility frontiers of Country A and Country B after trade as CPFA\n                                                                      and CPFB respectively in Figure 3.                                                     (2 marks)\n\n                                                                 (iii) Suppose the quantity of good X consumed by Country A before and after trade is the same.\n                                                                       Indicate the consumption point (CTA), volume of exports and volume of imports of Country A\n                                                                       after trade in Figure 3.                                                             (3 marks)\n\n                                                           (d)   The following table shows some data for Country A before and after it opens up to trade.\n\n                                                                                                              Before trade           After trade\n                                                                   Human Development Index (HDI)                 0.75                   0.82\n                                                                   Expected years of schooling (years)           11.5                   10.8\n\n                                                                 (i)   State ONE possible reason to explain the change in the expected years of schooling after trade.\n                                                                                                                                                               (1 mark)\n\n                                                                 (ii) Although the HDI has increased, most citizens of Country A believe that their standard of living\n                                                                      has declined. State TWO possible reasons to explain their views.                       (2 marks)",
