      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n     (1) is correct. The rules concern who can obtain the tickets, so they are related to the problem of ‘for\n     whom to produce’.\n     (2) is correct. Real-name registration and the non-transferable nature of the tickets directly restrict the\n     holder’s right to resell or transfer the tickets to others. Therefore, the buyer’s right to transfer over the\n     tickets is weakened.\n     (3) is incorrect. Buyers still need to pay money (at least $280) to purchase the tickets, so price\n     competition still exists.",
