      "marks": 1,
      "section": "-",
      "questionNumber": "4",
      "questionTextChi": "參閱以下關於香港兩家廠商的資料。\n甲廠商\n乙廠商\n向公眾發行股票\n不可能\n可能\n東主的債務責任\n東主必須承擔企業的所有債務責任\n東主的債務責任只限於他們對該公司的投資額\n根據以上資料，下列哪項關於甲廠商和乙廠商的陳述是不正確的？\nA.\t甲廠商和乙廠商都可能有1,000名東主。\nB.\t乙廠商不能對其會計資料保密，甲廠商則能。\nC.\t乙廠商的延續性較甲廠商為佳。\nD.\t當兩間廠商有相同金額的利潤，乙廠商可能比甲廠商享有較低的利得稅稅率。",
      "plainText": "參閱以下關於香港兩家廠商的資料。\n甲廠商\n乙廠商\n向公眾發行股票\n不可能\n可能\n東主的債務責任\n東主必須承擔企業的所有債務責任\n東主的債務責任只限於他們對該公司的投資額\n根據以上資料，下列哪項關於甲廠商和乙廠商的陳述是不正確的？\nA.\t甲廠商和乙廠商都可能有1,000名東主。\nB.\t乙廠商不能對其會計資料保密，甲廠商則能。\nC.\t乙廠商的延續性較甲廠商為佳。\nD.\t當兩間廠商有相同金額的利潤，乙廠商可能比甲廠商享有較低的利得稅稅率。",
      "topic": "廠商的所有權形式",
      "question": "MT43-P1-04",
      "answerMC": "D",
      "answerChi": "答案：D\n甲廠商可能是獨資或合夥，乙廠商是公眾有限公司。\n選項D是不正確的陳述。適用於有限公司的利得稅稅率較適用於獨資或合夥的為高。\n選項A是正確的陳述。合夥和公眾有限公司的東主人數都沒有上限。若甲廠商是合夥，甲廠商和乙廠商都可能有1,000名東主。\n選項B是正確的陳述。甲廠商毋須向公眾公開其會計資料，而乙廠商則需要向公眾公開其會計資料。\n選項C是正確的陳述。獨資和合夥都缺乏延續性，若其中一名東主破產、退出或死亡，廠商便要解散。公眾有限公司是獨立法人，當其中一名東主破產、退出或死亡，乙廠商仍然繼續存在。",
      "curriculumClassification": [
        "B 廠商與生產"
      ],
      "AristochapterClassification": [
        "Ch03"
      ],
      "concepts": [
        "股票與債券"
      ],
      "patterns": [
        "選擇最佳答案"
      ],
      "graphType": "-",
      "tableType": "-",
      "multipleSelectionType": "-",
      "calculationType": "-",
      "source": "模擬試卷四十三 卷一",
      "reviewedByAI": "Y",
      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/43/q-p1-04.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/43/a-p1-04.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Refer to the following information about two firms in Hong Kong.\n\n                                                   Firm A                                      Firm B\n       Issuing shares to the public              Impossible                                   Possible\n          Liability of the owner       Owners bear all the liability of the    The liability of owners is confined to\n                                                     firm                        the amount of their investment\n\n     Based on the above information, which of the following statements about firm A and firm B is INCORRECT?\n\n           A.    Both firm A and firm B can possibly have 1,000 owners.\n           B.    Firm B cannot keep its accounting information confidential while firm A can.\n           C.    Firm B has better continuity than firm A.\n           D.    When both firms have the same amount of profit, firm B may enjoy a lower profits tax rate than firm\n                 A.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n     Firm A may be a sole proprietorship or a partnership, while firm B is a public limited company.\n     Option D is an incorrect statement. The profits tax rate for a limited company is higher than that for a\n     sole proprietorship or partnership.\n     Option A is a correct statement. There is no upper limit on the number of owners for both a partnership\n     and a public limited company. If firm A is a partnership, both firm A and firm B may have 1,000 owners.\n     Option B is a correct statement. Firm A is not required to disclose its accounting information to the\n     public, whereas firm B must disclose its accounting information to the public.\n     Option C is a correct statement. Both a sole proprietorship and a partnership lack continuity; if one of\n     the owners goes bankrupt, withdraws, or dies, the firm must be dissolved. A public limited company is a\n     legal entity, so even if one of the owners goes bankrupt, withdraws, or dies, firm B continues to exist.",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/43/ae-p1-04.jpg",
      "originalQuestionImageEng": "originals/43/qe-p1-04.jpg",
      "stemPatterns": [
        "甲乙廠商表格：分辦每間廠商屬哪種商業擁有權形式"
      ]
