      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/43/a-p1-06.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following are examples of public goods?\n\n           (1)    an ancient poem\n           (2)    public bus service\n           (3)    free television broadcasts\n           (4)    medicine provided by public hospitals\n\n           A.     (1) and (3) only\n           B.     (1) and (4) only\n           C.     (2) and (3) only\n           D.     (2) and (4) only",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n     (1) and (3) are correct. An ancient poem and free television broadcasts are non-rival and non-excludable\n     in consumption. Their consumption is concurrent in nature, so they are public goods.\n     (2) is incorrect. Public bus services are excludable in consumption. The bus company can exclude\n     people who have not paid from using the service.\n     (4) is incorrect. The medicine provided by public hospitals is rival in consumption. When someone\n     obtains some medicine, the quantity available for others decreases.",
