      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following statements about land and capital in economics is/are CORRECT?\n\n            (1)   The quantity of land cannot be increased by human effort, while the quantity of capital can.\n            (2)   The return on land is rent, while the return on capital is profit.\n            (3)   In the process of wind power generation, wind belongs to land while generators belong to capital.\n\n            A.    (1) only\n            B.    (2) only\n            C.    (1) and (3) only\n            D.    (2) and (3) only",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n     (1) is correct. Land is a natural resource, and its quantity cannot be increased by human effort.\n     (3) is correct. Natural wind is a natural resource, while a generator is a man-made resource used in the\n     process of generating electricity.\n    (2) is incorrect. The return on land is rent, while the return on capital is interest.",
