      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/43/a-p1-14.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The following table shows the cost-output relationship of a profit-maximising firm.\n\n                                       Output (units)         Average variable cost ($)\n                                            3                            4\n                                            4                            4\n                                            5                            5\n                                            6                            6\n                                            7                            7\n\n      Given the fixed cost is $5. If the profit-maximising output is 6 units, the market price will be ____________ and\n      the profit will be ____________.\n\n            A.    $6 ... $25\n            B.    $6 ... $30\n            C.    $11 ... $25\n            D.    $11 ... $30",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n           Output (units)        Average variable           Total cost            Marginal cost\n                                     cost ($)                  ($)                    ($)\n                 3                       4                      17                       -\n                 4                       4                      21                       4\n                 5                       5                      30                       9\n                 6                       6                      41                      11\n                 7                       7                      54                      13\n    When output is 6 units (the profit-maximising output), marginal revenue equals marginal cost, which\n    reflects that the market price is $11. Profit = 6 × $11 – $41 = $25",
