      "questionTextEng": "A profit-maximising firm will increase its output if ____________.\n\n            A.    fixed cost decreases by $20\n            B.    average cost for each unit of output decreases by $10\n            C.    demand for the good produced by the firm decreases\n            D.    the marginal cost of production for the firm increases",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    A decrease of $10 in the average cost for each unit of output means that the marginal cost for each unit\n    of output has decreased by $10. A decrease in marginal cost will lead to an increase in the\n    profit-maximising output level.\n    Option A is incorrect. A change in fixed cost will not affect the determination of the profit-maximising\n    output level.\n    Option C is incorrect. When demand decreases, the market price will fall and marginal revenue will fall.\n    With marginal cost for each unit of output unchanged, the profit-maximising output level will decrease.\n    Option D is incorrect. When marginal cost increases, with marginal revenue for each unit of output\n    unchanged, the profit-maximising output level will decrease.",
