      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/43/a-p1-17.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "A large chain convenience store posts a job advertisement to hire shop assistants at $50 per hour. Even though the\n      advertisement has been posted for a long time, the convenience store still cannot hire enough shop assistants.\n\n      From the information above, it can be inferred that the quantity transacted in the labour market is __________ the\n      quantity demanded and __________ the quantity supplied.\n\n            A.    smaller than ... larger than\n            B.    smaller than ... equal to\n            C.    equal to ... larger than\n            D.    equal to ... smaller than",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    This situation implies that the prevailing wage rate is below the equilibrium wage rate, resulting in\n    excess demand (shortage) in the labour market. Therefore, the quantity transacted will equal the quantity\n    supplied and will be smaller than the quantity demanded.",
