      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/43/a-p1-20.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The demand curve for smartphone repair services is D.\n\n                        Unit price\n\n                                          E1\n\n                                                    E2\n\n                                                               D\n                           0                                             Quantity\n\n      Which of the following reasons best explains the change in the equilibrium point for smartphone repair services\n      from E1 to E2?\n\n            A.    The price of brand-new smartphones decreases.\n            B.    The price of replacement parts for smartphones decreases.\n            C.    The equilibrium wage of repair technicians for other electronic products increases.\n            D.    Smartphones break down more frequently.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    When the price of replacement parts for smartphones decreases, the cost of providing smartphone repair\n    services will decrease and its supply will increase. The equilibrium point will shift from E1 to E2.\n    Option A is incorrect. When the price of brand-new smartphones decreases, if a smartphone breaks\n    down, people will be more likely to buy a new smartphone rather than repair the old one. Therefore, the\n    demand for smartphone repair services will decrease.\n    Option C is incorrect. When the equilibrium wage of repair technicians of other electronic products\n    increases, the supply of smartphone repair technicians will decrease and the supply of smartphone repair\n    services will decrease.\n    Option D is incorrect. When smartphones break down more frequently, the demand for smartphone\n    repair services will increase.",
