      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/43/a-p1-21.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The table below shows the demand schedule for good Y before and after a decrease in the supply of good X.\n\n      Price (units)                             10             11            12                13            14\n      Original quantity demanded (units)        20             18            16                14            12\n      New quantity demanded (units)             22             20            18                16            14\n\n      Based on the table above, good X and good Y are most likely __________.\n\n            A.    substitutes\n            B.    complements\n            C.    in joint supply\n            D.    in competitive supply",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    When the supply of good X decreases, the equilibrium price of good X will increase. If good X and\n    good Y are substitutes, the increase in the equilibrium price of good X will lead to an increase in the\n    demand for good Y. The quantity demanded of good Y will increase at all given prices.",
