      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/43/a-p1-24.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Refer to the following supply and demand schedules for good X.\n\n              Price ($)                           3               4                5                6              7\n              Quantity demanded (units)          12              11               10                9              8\n              Quantity supplied (units)          10              10               10                10            10\n\n      Which of the following statements about the market of good X is CORRECT?\n\n            A.    If the government imposes a price ceiling of $3 on good X, the quantity transacted of good X will be\n                  12 units.\n            B.    If the government imposes a price floor of $7 on good X, the quantity transacted of good X will\n                  remain unchanged.\n            C.    If the government provides a per-unit subsidy of $2 to the producers of good X, the equilibrium price\n                  of good X will fall.\n            D.    If the government imposes a per-unit sales tax of $2 on good X, the producers’ total revenue net of tax\n                  will be $30.",
