      "questionTextEng": "The following is the demand-supply diagram for good X. E0 is the initial equilibrium point.\n\n                               Unit price\n\n                                                                  S\n\n                                               c    E0\n                                     b                                     D\n\n                                 P1\n                                                d\n\n                                     a\n                                     0                                         Quantity\n\n      If the government sets a price ceiling of P1 for good X,\n\n            (1)   consumer surplus will increase by area P1bcd.\n            (2)   producer surplus will decrease by area P1bE0d.\n            (3)   total social surplus may increase, decrease or remain unchanged.\n\n            A.    (1) and (2) only\n            B.    (1) and (3) only\n            C.    (2) and (3) only\n            D.    (1), (2) and (3)",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    The price ceiling of P1 is below the equilibrium price and is an effective price ceiling.\n    (1) is correct. Before setting the price ceiling at P1, consumer surplus is zero. After setting the price\n    ceiling at P1, consumer surplus is area P1bcd.\n    (2) is correct. Before setting the price ceiling at P1, producer surplus is area abE0. After setting the price\n    ceiling at P1, producer surplus is area aP1d. Producer surplus decreases by area P1bE0d.\n    (3) is incorrect. The area by which producer surplus decreases is greater than the area by which\n    consumer surplus increases. Total social surplus will decrease, and the deadweight loss is area dcE0.",
