      "questionTextEng": "According to observations, some shops in shopping malls in Hong Kong have been unable to find tenants,\n                                                           and some premises have remained vacant for a long period.\n\n                                                          Source A: News report on shops in Hong Kong shopping malls\n\n                                                            Recently, many people on social media have been discussing the rising shop vacancy rates in\n                                                            shopping malls, with some units remaining vacant for a long time without being rented out.\n\n                                                            A resident said that the vacancy problem in the small shopping mall near his home is serious,\n                                                            causing him inconvenience. He needs to travel to large shopping malls in other districts to buy daily\n                                                            necessities. He also pointed out that the vacancy problem in large shopping malls is less serious.\n\n                                                            A politician stated that population ageing is one of the reasons for the rising shop vacancy rate,\n                                                            because the elderly generally consume less.\n\n                                                          Source B: A suggestion from a shopping mall tenant\n\n                                                                                                    When more shops in a shopping mall close down, fewer\n                                                                                                    visitors come to the mall and the business of the remaining\n                                                                                                    shops also worsens as a result.\n\n                                                                                                    If there are measures that can reduce the vacancy rate of\n                                                                                                    shop premises and attract visitors, all shops can benefit.\n\n                                                                   A tenant of a shopping mall\n\n                                                          Source C: Views of some stakeholders\n                                                                                                          Having other shops in the shopping mall helps attract\n                                                                                                          more visitors, which indirectly reduces the average\n                                                                                                          operating costs of my business.\n\n                                                                A tenant of a large shopping mall\n                                                                                                          If my shop premises remain vacant for a long time, I will\n                                                                                                          use them to operate my own business.\n\n                                                                 An owner of shop premises in a\n                                                                        shopping mall\n\n                                                        (a) Refer to Source A. With the aid of a demand-supply diagram, explain the situation of the rising vacancy\n                                                            rate mentioned by the politician in Source A.                                                 (6 marks)\n\n                                                        (b) Refer to Source A. Explain how residents travelling to more distant areas for shopping would affect the\n                                                            average number of items they purchase on each shopping trip.                                (3 marks)\n\n                                                        (c) In terms of the opportunity cost of using the shop premises to operate her own business, explain the plan of\n                                                            the owner of shopping mall shop premises in Source C.                                             (2 marks)\n\n                                                        For part (d), candidates are required to present their answer in essay form. Criteria for marking will include use\n                                                        of sources and economic theories, relevant content, logical presentation and clarity of expression.\n\n                                                        (d) Suppose the following suggestion is given to boost the retail market:\n\n                                                                 To provide residents a subsidy calculated at a fixed percentage of their\n                                                                 consumption amount when they shop in local shopping malls\n\n                                                             With reference to the above sources and your own knowledge in economics, discuss the effects of the\n                                                             suggestion on Hong Kong, including:\n\n                                                             -      economic efficiency\n                                                             -      the Gini coefficient based on post-tax post-social transfer household income\n\n                                                             -      the vacancy rate of shop premises in shopping malls\n                                                                                                                                                                  (10 marks)",
