      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n     Mr. Lam will choose the first option as the benefit of choosing the first option (the value of the first\n     option) is greater than the cost (the value of the second option).\n     Option A is correct. This would reduce the value of the third option without affecting Mr. Lam’s cost or\n     benefit of choosing the first option.\n     Option B is incorrect. This would reduce the value of the first option, thus decreasing Mr. Lam’s benefit\n     of choosing the first option.\n     Option C is incorrect. This would increase the value of the first option, thus increasing Mr. Lam’s\n     benefit of choosing the first option.\n     Option D is incorrect. This may decrease the value of the second option to a level lower than that of the\n     third option, so the cost of choosing the first option may change from the value of the second option to\n     that of the third option.",
