      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/44/q-p1-08.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/44/a-p1-08.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Suppose the government of Country A decides to increase the quota of its foreign talent admission scheme.\n\n     This will cause Country A’s ___________ and ___________ to increase.\n\n           A.    labour supply ... average labour productivity\n           B.    labour supply ... geographical mobility of labour\n           C.    geographical mobility of labour ... average labour productivity\n           D.    occupational mobility of labour ... average labour productivity",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n     When the government increases the quota of the foreign talent admission scheme, more foreign talent\n     will enter Country A’s labour market. The labour supply will increase. These workers possess good\n     education and experience, so Country A’s average labour productivity will increase.\n     The scheme has no significant effect on the ability or willingness of Country A’s labour to change from\n     one occupation to another. Thus it has no effect on the occupational mobility of labour.\n     The scheme will increase the geographical mobility of overseas talents, but it has no significant effect\n     on the ability and willingness of Country A’s workers to move from one place to another, so it has no\n     effect on the geographical mobility of Country A’s labour.",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/44/ae-p1-08.jpg",
      "originalQuestionImageEng": "originals/44/qe-p1-08.jpg",
