      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/44/q-p1-09.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/44/a-p1-09.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The following table shows the production plan of a firm. The firm employs two factors only, namely labour and\n     machinery.\n\n                  Labour (units)                   Machinery (units)                Average product (units)\n                       5                                  2                                    9\n                       5                                  3                                   10\n                       5                                  4                                   12\n                       5                                  5                                   13\n                       5                                  6                                   X\n\n      If the above data illustrates the law of diminishing marginal returns, the value of X _________.\n\n            A.    must be smaller than 13\n            B.    must be larger than 13\n            C.    can be 12\n            D.    can be 14",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n            Labour      Machinery        Average product        Total product (units)     Marginal product\n            (units)      (units)             (units)                                          (units)\n               5             2                   9                        18                       -\n               5             3                  10                        30                      12\n               5             4                  12                        48                      18\n               5             5                  13                        65                      17\n               5             6          X must be smaller       6X must be smaller       must be smaller than\n                                           than 13.67               than 82                       17\n                                             (= 82 / 6)              (= 65 + 17)\n     As the marginal product of machinery starts to decline when the 5th unit of machinery is put to work,\n     the marginal product of the 6th unit of machinery must be smaller than 17 units. Therefore, the total\n     product must be smaller than 82 units and the average product (X) must be smaller than 13.67 units.",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/44/ae-p1-09.jpg",
