      "marks": 1,
      "section": "-",
      "questionNumber": "11",
      "questionTextChi": "下表顯示某受價廠商的成本與產出的關係。該廠商的固定成本是$5。\n產出 (單位)\n2\n3\n4\n5\n6\n平均成本 ($)\n4\n5\n6\n7\n8\n根據上表，當市場價格由$9上升至$11，\nA.\t利潤極大化產量會由4單位上升至6單位。\nB.\t該廠商的利潤會上升$8。\nC.\t該廠商的總成本會上升$35。\nD.\t該廠商受損於規模負經濟。",
      "plainText": "下表顯示某受價廠商的成本與產出的關係。該廠商的固定成本是$5。\n產出 (單位)\n2\n3\n4\n5\n6\n平均成本 ($)\n4\n5\n6\n7\n8\n根據上表，當市場價格由$9上升至$11，\nA.\t利潤極大化產量會由4單位上升至6單位。\nB.\t該廠商的利潤會上升$8。\nC.\t該廠商的總成本會上升$35。\nD.\t該廠商受損於規模負經濟。",
      "topic": "生產及成本",
      "question": "MT44-P1-11",
      "answerMC": "B",
      "answerChi": "答案：B\n該廠商的總成本表與邊際成本表如下：\n產出 (單位)\n2\n3\n4\n5\n6\n平均成本 ($)\n4\n5\n6\n7\n8\n總成本 ($)\n8\n15\n24\n35\n48\n邊際成本 ($)\n-\n7\n9\n11\n13\n選項B是正確的。當市場價格為$9，利潤 = $9 × 4 – $24 = $12。當市場價格為$11，利潤 = $11 × 5 – $35 = $20。利潤上升了$8。\n選項A是不正確的。根據利潤極大化的一般條件，當市場價格由$9上升至$11，利潤極大化產量會由4單位上升至5單位。\n選項C是不正確的。總成本會由$24上升至$35，上升了$11。\n選項D是不正確的。規模負經濟的概念只適用於長期。該廠商存在固定成本，代表該廠商有固定生產要素，該廠商正處於短期生產。",
      "curriculumClassification": [
        "B 廠商與生產"
      ],
      "AristochapterClassification": [
        "Ch06"
      ],
      "concepts": [
        "成本",
        "利潤極大化"
      ],
      "patterns": [
        "表格判讀"
      ],
      "graphType": "-",
      "tableType": "成本產出表",
      "multipleSelectionType": "-",
      "calculationType": "-",
      "source": "模擬試卷四十四 卷一",
      "reviewedByAI": "Y",
      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/44/q-p1-11.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/44/a-p1-11.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The table below shows the cost-output relationship of a price-taking firm. The fixed cost of the firm is $5.\n\n             Output (units)                  2             3              4             5             6\n             Average cost ($)                4             5              6             7             8\n\n     According to the table above, when the market price increases from $9 to $11,\n\n            A.    the profit-maximising output will increase from 4 units to 6 units.\n            B.    the profit of the firm will increase by $8.\n            C.    the total cost of the firm will increase by $35.\n            D.    the firm will suffer from diseconomies of scale.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    The firm’s total cost schedule and marginal cost schedule are as follows:\n            Output (units)               2            3            4             5              6\n            Average cost ($)             4            5            6             7              8\n            Total cost ($)               8           15            24           35            48\n            Marginal cost ($)            -            7            9            11            13\n    Option B is correct. When the market price is $9, profit = $9 × 4 – $24 = $12. When the market price is\n    $11, profit = $11 × 5 – $35 = $20. Profit will increase by $8.\n    Option A is incorrect. According to the general condition for profit maximisation, when the market price\n    rises from $9 to $11, the profit-maximising output will increase from 4 units to 5 units.\n    Option C is incorrect. Total cost will increase from $24 to $35, an increase of $11.\n    Option D is incorrect. The concept of diseconomies of scale only applies in the long run. The firm has a\n    fixed cost, which indicates that it has fixed factors of production and is therefore operating in the short\n    run.",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/44/ae-p1-11.jpg",
      "originalQuestionImageEng": "originals/44/qe-p1-11.jpg",
      "stemPatterns": [
        "（成本表）市場價格改變，對利潤極大化產量及利潤的影響"
      ]
