      "questionTextEng": "Country A mainly imports fruit from Country B. Suppose the government of Country B requires stronger\n    packaging for each box of exported fruit. Which of the following statements is CORRECT?\n\n            A.    Country A’s demand for fruit from Country B will decrease.\n            B.    The proportion of high-quality fruit sold in Country A will increase.\n            C.    Country A’s total expenditure on fruit will decrease.\n            D.    The change in the import volume of fruit depends on the price elasticity of demand.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    The monetary price of high-quality fruit is generally higher than that of ordinary fruit. When the\n    packaging cost per box of fruit increases, the relative price of high-quality fruit (in terms of ordinary\n    fruit) will decrease. According to the law of demand, people will purchase more high-quality fruit\n    relative to ordinary fruit, and the proportion of high-quality fruit sold in Country A will increase.\n    Option A is incorrect. When the packaging cost per box of fruit increases, the supply of fruit will\n    decrease. The price of fruit will increase and the quantity demanded will decrease. This is not a change\n    in demand.\n    Option C is incorrect. When the price of fruit increases, the quantity demanded will decrease. The\n    change in total expenditure is uncertain, depending on the price elasticity of demand.\n    Option D is incorrect. When the packaging cost per box of fruit increases, the supply of fruit will\n    decrease. The quantity demanded will decrease and the import volume of fruit will decrease.",
