      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    It is given that the supply curve of good X is upward sloping, while its demand curve is vertical. When\n    the supply of good X increases, the equilibrium price will decrease, but the equilibrium quantity will\n    remain unchanged. When the demand for good X decreases, both the equilibrium price and equilibrium\n    quantity will decrease. Thus, both the equilibrium price and equilibrium quantity of good X will\n    decrease.",
