      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/44/q-p1-17.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/44/a-p1-17.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "With the rapid development of artificial intelligence, technology companies need more electricity to operate their\n    data centres. As a result, the price of electricity rises by 10% and the quantity transacted changes by 20%. Which\n    of the following best explains the above change in price and quantity transacted of electricity?\n\n           A.    Electricity is difficult to replace with other goods.\n           B.    Electricity companies have spare production capacity.\n           C.    The equipment required to produce electricity is not easy to install.\n           D.    Electricity is a necessity for consumers.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    As technology companies need more electricity to operate their data centres, the demand for electricity\n    increases, causing both its price and quantity transacted to increase. Since the percentage change in\n    quantity transacted (20%) is greater than the percentage change in price (10%), the supply of electricity\n    is elastic.\n    If the electricity companies have spare production capacity, the supply of electricity tends to be elastic.\n    Option A is incorrect. This is a factor affecting the price elasticity of demand for electricity and cannot\n    explain the above change.\n    Option C is incorrect. If the equipment required to produce electricity is not easy to install, the supply of\n    electricity tends to be inelastic.\n    Option D is incorrect. This is a factor affecting the price elasticity of demand for electricity and cannot\n    explain the above change.",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/44/ae-p1-17.jpg",
      "originalQuestionImageEng": "originals/44/qe-p1-17.jpg",
