      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/44/q-p1-18.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/44/a-p1-18.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Refer to the following market demand and supply schedules for good X.\n\n                    Unit price ($)            Quantity demanded (units)          Quantity supplied (units)\n                         10                              30                                 22\n                         12                              28                                 24\n                         14                              26                                 26\n                         16                              24                                 28\n                         18                              22                                 30\n                         20                              20                                 32\n\n     Suppose the government sets a price ceiling on good X at $12. Which of the following statements about good X is\n     CORRECT?\n\n           A.    If the government removes the price ceiling, the total revenue from good X will decrease.\n           B.    If the government lowers the price ceiling, the deadweight loss will decrease.\n           C.    If the government replaces the price ceiling with a quota of 24 units, the two measures will have\n                 equivalent effect on the price.\n           D.    If the government replaces the price ceiling with a per-unit tax of $4, the two measures will have\n                 equivalent effect on the quantity transacted.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    The original equilibrium price is $14 and the quantity transacted is 26 units.\n    When the government sets a price ceiling of $12 on good X, the price becomes $12 and the quantity\n    transacted is 24 units.\n    Option D is correct. If the government replaces the price ceiling with a per-unit tax of $4, the supply and\n    demand schedules after tax are as follows:\n               Unit price ($)     Quantity demanded       Quantity supplied       Quantity supplied\n                                        (units)               (units)              after tax (units)\n                    10                     30                     22                       -\n                    12                     28                     24                       -\n                    14                     26                     26                      22\n                    16                     24                     28                      24\n                    18                     22                     30                      26\n                    20                     20                     32                      28\n    The new equilibrium price is $16 and the quantity transacted is 24 units. Therefore, the imposition of a\n    per-unit tax of $4 has the same effect on the quantity transacted as the price ceiling.\n\n    Option A is incorrect. Under the price ceiling of $12, total revenue is $288 (= $12 × 24). If the\n    government removes the price ceiling, the market will return to the equilibrium, where the price will be\n    $14 and the quantity transacted will be 26 units. Total revenue will be $364 (= $14 × 26). Therefore,\n    removing the price ceiling will cause the total revenue to increase.\n    Option B is incorrect. If the government lowers the price ceiling, the difference between marginal\n    benefit and marginal cost will widen, and the deadweight loss will increase.\n    Option C is incorrect. If the government replaces the price ceiling with a quota of 24 units, the price will\n    be $16, which is different from the price under the price ceiling.",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/44/ae-p1-18.jpg",
      "originalQuestionImageEng": "originals/44/qe-p1-18.jpg",
      "stemPatterns": [
        "（供需表）價格上限下，下列哪項陳述正確？"
      ]
