      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/44/a-p1-22.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The table below shows Country A’s Gini coefficient based on post-tax post-social transfer household income.\n\n                                           Year                  Gini coefficient\n                                           2015                       0.411\n                                           2020                       0.390\n                                           2025                       0.372\n\n      Which of the following may explain the change in Country A’s Gini coefficient over the above period?\n\n           A.    The incomes of high-income households increased by a greater extent than those of low-income\n                 households.\n           B.    The tax system changed from regressive to progressive.\n           C.    The proportion of total income earned by the top of 20% households increased.\n           D.    The government of Country A introduced a general sales tax.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    From 2015 to 2025, the Gini coefficient continuously declined, indicating that income distribution\n    became more equal. When the tax system changes from regressive to progressive, the proportion of\n    income paid as tax by high-income groups will increase, which can lead to a more even income\n    distribution.\n    Option A is incorrect. If the income of high-income households increases by a greater extent than that of\n    low-income households, income distribution will become more uneven, which is inconsistent with the\n    data in the question.\n    Option C is incorrect. When the proportion of total income earned by the top 20% of households\n    increases, income distribution will become more uneven, which is inconsistent with the data in the\n    question.\n    Option D is incorrect. A general sales tax is a regressive tax. Imposing a regressive tax will lead to a\n    more uneven income distribution, which is inconsistent with the data in the question.",
      "originalAnswerImageEng": "originals/44/ae-p1-22.jpg",
