      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following may explain why income inequality among restaurant waiters tends to be smaller than that\n      among real estate agents?\n\n           A.    The market demand for real estate agents is smaller.\n           B.    The services provided by real estate agents are more heterogeneous.\n           C.    Gender discrimination among restaurant waiters is more serious.\n           D.    Restaurant waiters have a lower level of education.\n\n2 4 . The following diagram shows a production chain of garments in Country A.\n\n                                                          Foreign\n                                             $480         retailers\n           Local               Local\n          materials         manufacturers\n                       $100                                             $900 ($80 sales tax\n                                                           Local            inclusive)               Local\n                                             $400         retailers                                consumers\n\n                                                               $50\n\n                                                          Foreign\n                                                         exporters\n\n      The contribution of the above production chain to Country A’s GDP at factor cost is ________.\n\n           A.    $1,150\n           B.    $1,250\n           C.    $1,350\n           D.    $1,410",
      "answerEng": "Answer: B\n    Income inequality among real estate agents mainly arises from differences in their human capital (such\n    as service quality and sales skills) and the areas they serve. High-income real estate agents may earn\n    higher commissions by working in luxury housing districts and attracting high-end clients, while\n    average-income agents may earn lower commissions because they work in areas with mid-to-low-priced\n    properties. In contrast, the income of restaurant waiters is mainly determined by fixed hourly wages,\n    with smaller differences in human capital, resulting in a smaller income gap.",
