      "questionTextEng": "To calculate Hong Kong’s gross national income (GNI), which of the following should be deducted from Hong\n      Kong’s gross domestic product (GDP)?\n\n           A.    the rental income earned by a Hong Kong resident from an overseas property he owns\n           B.    the interest received by a Hong Kong resident from holding bonds of a foreign company\n           C.    the salary earned by a Mainland professor working at a university in Hong Kong for six months\n           D.    the salary received by a Korean working in a company in Hong Kong for two years",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    GNI = GDP + Factor income earned by residents outside the economic territory − Factor income earned\n    by non-residents within the economic territory\n    Option C is correct. It is factor income earned by a non-resident within the economic territory.\n    Options A and B are incorrect. They are factor income earned by residents outside the economic\n    territory.\n    Option D is incorrect. Since the Korean has worked in Hong Kong for more than one year, he is\n    regarded as a resident of Hong Kong. His income will be included in both Hong Kong’s GDP and GNI.",
