      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/44/a-p1-27.jpg",
      "inlineDiagrams": "diagrams/MT44-P1-27.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The diagram below shows the money supply curve (Ms) and money demand curve (Md) of an economy. Suppose\n    the initial equilibrium point is at E.\n\n                    Nominal interest rate (%)\n                                                Ms\n\n                                                   E\n\n                                                                    Md\n                              0\n                                                                           Quantity of money\n\n      Suppose more overseas companies remit money to the economy’s banking system and the volatility of the stock\n      market increases. In this case, the nominal interest rate ___________, and the quantity of money ___________.\n\n            A.    will increase ... will increase\n            B.    will increase ... will decrease\n            C.    may increase, decrease or remain unchanged ... will increase\n            D.    may increase, decrease or remain unchanged ... will decrease",
      "answerEng": "Answer: C\n    When more overseas companies remit money to the economy’s banking system, the money supply will\n    increase and the money supply curve will shift to the right. The nominal interest rate will decrease and\n    the quantity of money will increase. When the volatility of the stock market increases, people will hold\n    fewer stocks and hold more money as an asset. Asset demand for money will increase and the money\n    demand curve will shift to the right. The nominal interest rate will increase and the quantity of money\n    will remain unchanged. To conclude, the change in the nominal interest rate will be uncertain, while the\n    quantity of money will increase.",
