      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/44/q-p1-28.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/44/a-p1-28.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Which of the following would be most likely to cause the price level of an economy to fall in the short run?\n\n            A.    The price of raw materials decreases, and a major trading partner of the economy experiences an\n                  economic recession.\n            B.    Labour productivity increases, and the government carries out an open market purchase of\n                  government bonds.\n            C.    People’s desire to save decreases, and the economy’s currency appreciates.\n            D.    The required reserve ratio decreases, and a major natural disaster occurs that disrupts production.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    A fall in the price level can be caused by a decrease in aggregate demand and/or an increase in short run\n    aggregate supply.\n    When the price of raw materials decreases, short run aggregate supply will increase. At the same time,\n    when a major trading partner of the economy experiences an economic recession, the economy’s net\n    exports will decrease and aggregate demand will decrease. To conclude, the price level will decrease.\n    Option B is incorrect. When labour productivity increases, short run aggregate supply will increase and\n    the price level will decrease. In addition, when the government carries out an open market purchase of\n    government bonds, the money supply will increase and the interest rate will decrease.\n    Consumption/investment will increase, aggregate demand will increase and the price level will increase.\n    To conclude, the change in the price level will be uncertain.\n    Option C is incorrect. When people’s desire to save decreases, private consumption expenditure will\n    increase. Aggregate demand will increase and the price level will increase. In addition, when the\n    economy’s currency appreciates, net exports will decrease. Aggregate demand will decrease and the\n    price level will decrease. To conclude, the change in the price level will be uncertain.\n    Option D is incorrect. A reduction in the required reserve ratio will increase the money supply, and the\n    interest rate will decrease. Consumption/investment will increase and aggregate demand will increase.\n    The price level will increase. In addition, a major natural disaster that disrupts production will cause the\n    short run aggregate supply to decrease. The price level will increase. To conclude, the price level will\n    increase.",
