      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/44/a-p1-32.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Miss Tai withdraws HK$200,000 cash from a deposit-taking company. She then uses $50,000 cash to purchase a\n    negotiable certificate of deposit issued by a licensed bank and remits the remaining amount overseas.\n\n    What will be the immediate effect of the above actions on the money supply of Hong Kong?\n\n           A.    Money supply M1 will remain unchanged.\n           B.    Money supply M1 and M2 will both remain unchanged.\n           C.    Money supply M3 will decrease by HK$200,000.\n           D.    Money supply M2 and M3 will both decrease by HK$150,000.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    Withdrawing HK$200,000 cash from a deposit-taking company will cause M1 and M2 to increase by\n    HK$200,000, while M3 will remain unchanged.\n    Using HK$50,000 cash to purchase a negotiable certificate of deposit issued by a licensed bank will\n    cause M1 to decrease by HK$50,000, while M2 and M3 will remain unchanged.\n    Remitting the remaining amount ($150,000) overseas will cause M1, M2 and M3 to decrease by\n    HK$150,000, as this amount is no longer included in the money supply of Hong Kong.\n    The overall effects of the above actions on M1, M2 and M3:\n    M1 will remain unchanged.\n    M2 will increase by HK$50,000.\n    M3 will decrease by HK$150,000.",
