      "questionTextEng": "The following diagram shows the relationship between taxable income and tax payment in a tax system.\n\n                           Tax payment\n\n                                                                        Taxable income\n                              0\n\n    Which of the following statements about the above tax system is/are CORRECT?\n\n            (1)   The tax system is in line with the equity principle of taxation put forward by Adam Smith.\n            (2)   The tax leads to a more uneven income distribution.\n            (3)   The tax allowance of the tax system is zero.\n\n            A.    (2) only\n            B.    (3) only\n            C.    (1) and (2) only\n            D.    (2) and (3) only",
      "answerEng": "Answer: A\n    The diagram shows a regressive tax.\n    (2) is correct. A regressive tax will make income distribution more uneven because the tax payment\n    accounts for a higher proportion of the income of low-income people than of high-income people.\n    (1) is incorrect. As income rises, the proportion of income paid as tax decreases. Therefore, this tax\n    system violates the equity principle of taxation put forward by Adam Smith.\n    (3) is incorrect. The x-axis of the diagram shows taxable income, which is the amount used to calculate\n    tax after deducting allowances and tax deductions. Therefore, we cannot determine whether this tax has\n    an allowance.",
