      "questionTextEng": "Suppose the government lowers the required reserve ratio of the banking system. Which of the following would\n    weaken the effect of the above policy on the price level in the short run?\n\n            A.    lowering the standard tax rate of the salaries tax\n            B.    lowering the profits tax rate\n            C.    removing tariff exemptions for imported goods\n            D.    tightening the criteria for receiving unemployment benefits",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    A lower required reserve ratio will cause the money supply to increase. The interest rate will decrease\n     and consumption/investment will increase. Aggregate demand will increase and the price level will\n     increase.\n     Tightening the criteria for receiving unemployment benefits will reduce people’s disposable income,\n     causing private consumption expenditure and aggregate demand to decrease. The price level will\n     decrease.\n     Option A is incorrect. Lowering the standard tax rate of the salaries tax will increase people’s disposable\n     income, causing private consumption expenditure and aggregate demand to increase. The price level\n     will increase.\n     Option B is incorrect. Lowering the profits tax rate will stimulate investment, increase aggregate\n     demand and cause the price level to increase.\n     Option C is incorrect. Removing the tariff exemptions on imported goods will cause the price of\n     imported goods to increase. Import volume will decrease. Net exports and aggregate demand will\n     increase and the price level will increase.",
