      "questionTextEng": "Suppose the risk of holding bonds in Country A increases. Which of the following can offset the effects of the\n    above event on Country A’s output level and nominal interest rate in the short run?\n\n            A.    The government increases the allowance for the salaries tax.\n            B.    The government raises the required reserve ratio.\n            C.    More enterprises extend the income payment interval.\n            D.    Electronic payment methods become more popular in the market.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    When the risk of holding bonds increases, asset demand for money will increase. The nominal interest\n     rate will increase, and consumption and investment will decrease. Aggregate demand will decrease and\n     the output level will decrease.\n     Option D is correct. When citizens use electronic payment methods more, transaction demand for\n     money will decrease. The nominal interest rate will decrease. Consumption and investment will increase.\n     Aggregate demand will increase and the output level will increase.\n     Option A is incorrect. When the government increases the allowance for the salaries tax, people’s\n     disposable income will increase. Private consumption expenditure will increase and aggregate demand\n     will increase. The output level will increase. However, when the output level increases, transaction\n     demand for money will increase and the nominal interest rate will increase further.\n     Option B is incorrect. Raising the required reserve ratio will cause the money supply to decrease. The\n     nominal interest rate will increase further. Consumption and investment will decrease. Aggregate\n     demand will decrease and the output level will decrease further.\n     Option C is incorrect. When more enterprises extend the income payment interval, transaction demand\n     for money will increase and the nominal interest rate will increase further. Consumption and investment\n     will decrease. Aggregate demand will decrease and the output level will decrease further.",
