      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/44/a-p1-43.jpg",
      "inlineDiagrams": "diagrams/MT44-P1-43.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "Below is the supply-demand diagram for good X in a small open economy. S0 is the domestic supply curve of good\n    X and S1 is the supply curve after an import quota is imposed.\n\n                             Unit price\n\n                                                                        S0\n\n                                                                        S1\n\n                              P1\n                             P0                                         International price\n\n                                                                         D\n                                                                             Quantity\n                               0            Q1 Q2           Q3    Q4\n\n    Suppose the international price of good X decreases. Which of the following is CORRECT?\n\n           A.    The domestic price of good X will decrease.\n           B.    The increase in import volume will be (Q4 – Q3).\n           C.    The domestic production of good X will decrease.\n           D.    Consumers’ total expenditure on good X will remain unchanged.",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    After the international price decreases (e.g., to P2), the domestic price will remain at P1 and the quantity\n    transacted will be Q3, which is the same as before the international price decreases. Consumers’ total\n    expenditure on good X will remain unchanged.\n    Option A is incorrect. The domestic price will remain at P1.\n    Option B is incorrect. The quota has not changed, so the import volume remains at (Q3 – Q2).\n    Option C is incorrect. The domestic production of good X will not change (i.e., will remain at Q2).\n\n                    Unit price\n\n                                                           S0\n\n                                                           S1\n\n                      P1\n                      P0                                   International price\n                      P2                                    D\n                                                                   Quantity\n                       0            Q1 Q2       Q3   Q4",
