      "questionTextEng": "Under the linked exchange rate system in Hong Kong, which of the following statements is CORRECT?\n\n           A.             The market exchange rate of the Hong Kong dollar against the US dollar is fixed.\n           B.             The money supply of Hong Kong is fully backed by the US dollar.\n           C.             The Hong Kong Monetary Authority can exchange Hong Kong dollars for US dollars with the public\n                          at the linked exchange rate.\n           D.             There will be inflationary pressure in Hong Kong when the US dollar continuously depreciates\n                          against the renminbi.\n\n                                                       EN D O F PAP E R",
      "answerEng": "Answer: D\n    When the US dollar depreciates against the renminbi, the Hong Kong dollar also depreciates against the\n    renminbi. Goods imported from the Mainland will become more expensive (in terms of Hong Kong\n    dollars), putting upward pressure on the general price level. When the general price level continues to\n    rise, it will result in inflation.\n    Option A is incorrect. The market exchange rate of the Hong Kong dollar against other currencies is\n    determined by the supply and demand in the foreign exchange market.\n    Option B is incorrect. Only Hong Kong’s monetary base (i.e. cash in public circulation + bank reserves)\n    is fully backed by the US dollar.\n    Option C is incorrect. Only the note-issuing banks can exchange Hong Kong dollars for US dollars with\n    the Hong Kong Monetary Authority at the linked exchange rate.",
