      "reviewedByAI": "Y",
      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-24",
      "originalQuestionImage": "originals/44/q-p2-06.jpg",
      "originalAnswerImage": "originals/44/a-p2-06.jpg",
      "questionTextEng": "The amount of resources in Country A is double that in Country B. Suppose both countries allocate half of\n                                                           their resources to producing garments and half to producing food. Their total output is shown below:\n\n                                                                                                 Garments (units)               Food (units)\n                                                                             Country A                    15                         20\n                                                                             Country B                    8                          18\n\n                                                          (a)   Explain whether Country B has\n\n                                                                 (i)   an absolute advantage\n\n                                                                 (ii) a comparative advantage\n\n                                                                 in producing food.                                                                           (5 marks)\n\n                                                          (b) Suppose the terms of trade is 2 units of food for 1 unit of garments. Calculate the gain from trade for the\n                                                              food-importing country if it imports 5 units of food. Show your workings.                        (3 marks)",
