      "questionTextEng": "Happy Food House is a shop selling baked goods. Miss Lee is the sole owner of the shop. She enjoys limited\n                                                           liability. The shop is not required to disclose its financial information to the public. Miss Lee employs Mr.\n                                                           Wong to be responsible for all the operations of the shop.\n\n                                                          (a)   What is ‘limited liability’?                                                                   (2 marks)\n\n                                                          (b) Name the type of business ownership of Happy Food House. Apart from liability, give ONE economic\n                                                              reason why Miss Lee operates her shop in this form of business ownership rather than as a partnership.\n                                                                                                                                                          (2 marks)\n\n                                                          (c)   Which type of factor of production do Miss Lee and Mr. Wong respectively belong to? Explain.\n                                                                                                                                                           (4 marks)\n\n                                                          (d) Miss Lee raised Mr. Wong’s monthly salary from $25,000 to $30,000, while the quantity of daily output\n\n                                                              of the shop remains unchanged.\n\n                                                                Explain Miss Lee’s output decision with reference to the profit-maximising condition under perfect\n                                                                competition.                                                                            (3 marks)",
