      "questionTextEng": "Read the following news report.\n\n                                                                 In November 2025, the 15th National Games of the People’s Republic of China were held in\n                                                                 Guangdong, Hong Kong and Macao. This was the first time Hong Kong participated in hosting\n                                                                 this national sporting event. During the National Games, many events were broadcast live on\n                                                                 local free television channels. Tickets for some popular events were sold out shortly after they\n                                                                 went on sale.\n\n                                                                 In the first week of the National Games, a total of about 990,000 visitor arrivals were recorded in\n                                                                 Hong Kong, of which about 720,000 were from the Mainland, representing a weekly increase of\n                                                                 about 100,000. Some hotels were fully booked during the National Games period.\n\n                                                           (a)    With reference to the above information, which component of Hong Kong’s balance of payments would\n                                                                  be affected by hosting the National Games? Give ONE example to illustrate.              (2 marks)\n\n                                                           (b) Explain whether the live broadcasts of the events by local free television channels are public goods.\n                                                                                                                                                               (3 marks)\n\n                                                           (c)    Some people who were unable to purchase event tickets through official channels chose to buy tickets\n                                                                  from touts (黃 牛 黨 ) at prices higher than the official ticket price. Which function of price does the\n                                                                  above situation illustrate? Explain your answer.                                            (2 marks)\n\n                                                           (d) Some foreign short video creators came to Hong Kong to watch the National Games. They filmed\n                                                               videos introducing Hong Kong and posted them on social media, attracting many viewers who learned\n                                                               useful information. However, these viewers did not pay the short video creators. Explain why\n                                                               externality is NOT necessarily involved in the above situation.                         (3 marks)",
