      "questionTextEng": "Suppose the government imposes a per-unit tax on the seller of every bottle of milk sold in the market.\n\n                                                           (a)   With the aid of a diagram, explain under what condition the consumers’ tax burden would be greater\n                                                                 than the producers’ tax burden.                                                         (7 marks)\n\n                                                           (b) A survey found that after the per-unit tax was imposed on milk, people in the country consumed\n                                                               relatively more large bottles of milk. Explain this phenomenon using the law of demand. (4 marks)\n\n                                                           (c)   The following is a recruitment advertisement by a milk producer.\n\n                                                                                  Position: Milk salesperson\n                                                                                  Working hours: 10:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m., 3 days per week\n                                                                                  Salary: $8,000 per month, plus commission\n\n                                                                 From the viewpoint of the milk producer, explain ONE advantage and ONE disadvantage of using the\n\n                                                                 above wage payment method over time rate.                                             (2 marks)",
