      "questionTextEng": "Lok Travel is the only company in Country A that provides tour bus services.\n\n                                                                                           Figure 3\n\n                                                                          Unit price\n\n                                                                                                                D: Demand\n                                                                                                                MC: Marginal cost\n\n                                                                                                                    MC\n\n                                                                                                          D\n                                                                            0                                           Quantity\n\n                                                           (a)   Suppose Lok Travel adopts simple monopoly pricing. Indicate the profit-maximising output and price\n                                                                 as QM and PM respectively in Figure 3.                                                  (2 marks)\n\n                                                           (b)   With the aid of Figure 3, explain why Lok Travel adopting simple monopoly pricing will cause a\n                                                                 deadweight loss.                                                                         (2 marks)\n\n                                                           (c)   Suppose the oil price increases and the efficient output level of Lok Travel falls to QM in (a). With the\n                                                                 aid of Figure 3, explain whether Lok Travel’s production is efficient after the above change.\n                                                                                                                                                                (5 marks)\n\n                                                           (d)   Lok Travel offers the following charging scheme:\n\n                                                                  Monday to Thursday: $300 per hour\n                                                                  Friday to Sunday: $350 per hour\n\n                                                                 Explain whether the pricing arrangement constitutes price discrimination.                      (3 marks)\n\n                                                           (e)   Lok Travel requires customers to purchase guided tour services offered by its subsidiaries together\n                                                                 with its tour bus services.\n\n                                                                 (i)   Name the anti-competitive behaviour that Lok Travel may engage in. State ONE possible harm\n                                                                       this behaviour may cause to consumers.                                            (2 marks)\n\n                                                                 (ii) If the above case happened in Hong Kong, which conduct rule of the Competition Ordinance\n                                                                      might Lok Travel violate? Explain.                                                (2 marks)",
