      "questionTextEng": "Refer to Figure 4. PPFA is the production possibility frontier of Country A. PA is the production point of\n                                                           Country A under autarky. TT’ is the international price line.\n\n                                                                                                     Figure 4\n                                                                                Good Y\n\n                                                                                       T\n\n                                                                                                                    PA\n\n                                                                                                                       PPFA\n                                                                                   0                                          Good X\n                                                                                                                     T’\n\n                                                           (a)   Explain why the production possibility frontier of Country A is concave to the origin.        (2 marks)\n\n                                                           (b)   Country A engages in international trade.\n\n                                                                 (i)   Explain which good Country A has a comparative advantage in producing.                   (2 marks)\n\n                                                                 (ii) Indicate the production point of Country A after trade as PTA in Figure 4.                (1 mark)\n\n                                                           (c)   Suppose Country A consumes the same quantity of good X before and after trade. In Figure 4,\n\n                                                                 (i)   indicate the consumption possibility frontier of Country A after trade as CPFA.           (1 mark)\n\n                                                                 (ii) indicate the consumption point (CTA), volume of exports and volume of imports of Country A\n                                                                      after trade.                                                                        (3 marks)\n\n                                                           (d)   Suppose after Country A adopts artificial intelligence technology, its productivity for both goods\n                                                                 increases by 50%, and its Human Development Index also rises.\n\n                                                                 (i)   How will Country A’s production possibility frontier change?                              (1 mark)\n\n                                                                 (ii) Explain whether your answer in (b)(i) will be affected by the above change in productivity.\n                                                                                                                                                             (2 marks)\n\n                                                                 (iii) Give TWO reasons to explain why adopting artificial intelligence technology may cause\n                                                                       Country A’s Human Development Index to rise.                                        (4 marks)",
