      "questionTextEng": "Since the 2010s, the government of Saudi Arabia has been actively promoting football development.\n(a)\tSuppose a football club in Saudi Arabia constructs a large football stadium there. With the aid of a diagram, explain how Saudi Arabia's aggregate output in the short run will be affected during the construction period of the stadium.\t(5 marks)\nSome football clubs in Saudi Arabia have established their own football academies to train young players.\n(b)\tSuppose some unemployed youngsters stopped seeking jobs and enrolled in the full-time training programmes of these football academies. Explain how the unemployment rate in Saudi Arabia would be affected.\t(4 marks)\n(c)\tAhmed, an unemployed youngster in Saudi Arabia, is considering whether he should stop seeking jobs and enrol in a full-time training programme of a football academy. His order of preference is as follows:\nFirst option:\tto enrol in a training programme of Football Academy A\nSecond option:\tto enrol in a training programme of Football Academy B\nThird option:\tto continue seeking jobs\nSuppose Football Academy B offers a scholarship to Ahmed. Explain whether the opportunity cost for Ahmed to continue seeking jobs would necessarily remain unchanged.\t(3 marks)\n(d)\tNeymar is a famous Brazilian footballer. He has been recruited by a football club in Saudi Arabia recently. Suppose he is required to pay an income tax of 20% on his taxable income to the Government of Saudi Arabia. Explain whether the income tax paid by Neymar is\n(i)\ta direct tax or an indirect tax.\t(2 marks)\n(ii)\tprogressive, proportional or regressive.\t(2 marks)",
      "markersReportChi": "12(a)        尚可。只有約四分之一考生能提供全面的分析。一些考生未能意會到題目要求解釋興建計劃在場館興建期間的短期影響，而討論了長期的影響。部分考生未能正確指出題目個案中受影響的總需求的組成部分。\n12(b)        尚可。只有少於四分之一考生能提供完整的解釋。許多考生未能指出當那些失業青年停止求職並參加全日制訓練課程時，失業人口和勞動人口會有相同數量的下跌。\n12(c)        尚可。約三分之一考生能寫出艾德繼續求職的機會成本改變的條件。\n12(d)(i)        令人滿意。\n12(d)(ii)        尚可。",
