      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-30",
      "marks": 5,
      "questionTextEng": "The table below shows the input-output relationship of a firm.\nMachine (units)        Labour (units)        Average output of labour (units)\n3        1        20\n3        2        22\n3        3        23\n3        4        23\n3        5        18\nState the law of diminishing marginal returns and explain whether the above data illustrate the law.        (5 marks)",
      "answerEng": "The law states that (holding technology constant), when more units of a variable factor are added successively to a given quantity of fixed factors, the marginal product of this factor will eventually decrease. (2)\nYes, because given a constant number of machines, a fixed factor, when labour increases from 3 units to 4 units, the marginal product of labour drops from 25 units to 23 units. (3)",
