      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-30",
      "marks": 8,
      "questionTextEng": "In Hong Kong, there are many yoga studios providing yoga classes.\n(a)\tGive TWO reasons to explain why the market of yoga classes in Hong Kong is NOT perfectly competitive\t(4 marks)\n(b)\tMiss Chan and her friends jointly operate a yoga studio in the form of a private limited company in Hong Kong\n(i)\tDefine ‘limited liability’.\t(2 marks)\n(ii)\tGive TWO possible reasons why they chose to set up a private limited company instead of a public limited company.\t(2 marks)",
      "answerEng": "(a) Reasons:\nYoga studios provide heterogeneous services, e.g. different types of classes / different styles of teaching.\n- Market information is imperfect, e.g. information about the prices and quality is not readily available to consumers.\n- Sellers engage in non-price competition, e.g. advertising.\n- any other relevant point\n[Mark the FIRST TWO points only.]\n(b) (i) Limited liability means that when a firm is liquidated, the liability of an owner of the firm is confined to the amount of his/her investment in the firm. (2)\n2@ max: 4\n(ii) Advantages of a private limited company over a public limited company:\n- lower risk of being taken over as the transfer of ownership requires consent of other owners\n- no need to disclose financial accounts to the public\n[Mark the FIRST TWO points only.]\n1@ max: 2",
      "imageChi": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/19-4ugIOBQV3HVr_KEttpYBLAOxYn-VIo/view?usp=drivesdk,https://drive.google.com/file/d/1SzUD-Gx9TNnRa-2rm_MnXKvMWu8RWzEF/view?usp=drivesdk,https://drive.google.com/file/d/1gqQ194qLcLH6rMKAcxtgVJL7X4TqYpMg/view?usp=drivesdk",
