      "questionTextEng": "In a small village, all villagers accept rice in settling payments for exchanges.\n(a)\tGive TWO reasons to explain why rice is NOT a good form of money compared to ban1motes even if rice is generally acceptable.\t(4 marks)\n(b)\tBelow is a conversation between two villagers in the above village.\nVillager A: I would like to borrow your fishing rod for a month.\nVillager B: Please return the fishing rod together with one bag of rice after one month.\nExplain why the bag of rice can be regarded as interest to Villager B in the above situation.\t(2 marks)",
      "answerEng": "(a) Reasons:\n- Not durable, as rice may decay within years and cannot be stored for a long time.\n- Not homogeneous, as rice does not have uniform physical characteristics.\n- Not portable, as people need to carry a large quantity of rice for high-value\ntransactions.\n- Any other relevant point\n[Mark the FIRST TWO points only.]\n2@ max: 4\n\n(b) As a lender, Villager B receives the bag of rice as compensation for deferred consumption. (2)",
