      "lastReviewDate": "2026-09-30",
      "marks": 6,
      "questionTextEng": "The following table shows the balance sheet of a banking system. Initially, all banks do not hold excess reserves and the public holds $500 million cash.\nAssets ($ million)\tLiabilities ($ million)\nReserves\t1 000\tDeposits\t5 000\nLoans\t4 000\t\t\n(a)\tFind the required reserve ratio.\t(1 mark)\nSuppose the central bank sells $200 million worth of government bonds to the public and the public continues to hold $500 million cash.\n(b)\tCalculate the new monetary base. Show your workings.\t(2 marks)\n(c)\tCalculate the change in money supply after the process of credit creation / contraction has been completed. Show your workings.\t(3 marks)",
      "answerEng": "(a) Required reserve ratio = 1 000 / 5 000=0.2 (1)\n(b) New monetary base = 1 000 +500-200 = $1 300 million (2)\n(c) Initial money supply = 5 000 +500 = $5 500 million (1)\nNew money supply = (1 000 – 200) x 1/0.2 + 500 = $4 500 million (1)\nChange in money supply = 4 500-5500 =-$1 000 million (1)",
