      "questionTextEng": "A small open economy imports agricultural products from other countries although agricultural products are also produced by domestic farmers in the economy. To protect the domestic farmers, the government of the economy imposes a per-unit tariff on imported agricultural products. The economy remains to be an importer of agricultural products after the imposition of the tariff.\n\nFigure 1: Market of agricultural products in the small open economy\nPrice ($)\nS\nS: domestic supply of agricultural products\nD: domestic demand for agricultural products\nPw: world price of agricultural products\nD\nP_{w}\n0\nQuantity (units)\n\n(a)\tIn Figure 1, indicate the following after the imposition of the tariff:\n(i)\tthe quantity of domestic production as Q1,\n(ii)\tthe import volume as QM, and\n(iii)\tand the tariff revenue.\n\t\t(4 marks)\n\n(b)\tExplain the effect of the imposition of the tariff on the economy's trade balance.\n\t(Hint: the tariff revenue is not included in the calculation of trade balance.)\t(3 marks)",
