      "questionTextEng": "In the 2024-25 Budget, the Financial Secretary proposed to adjust the rate of the hotel accommodation tax (HAT) from 0% to 3% with effect from 1 January 2025. Hotels and guesthouses would be required to pay the HAT at the rate of3% on accommodation charges.\n(a)\tExplain whether the proposed HAT is a progressive tax, a proportional tax or a regressive tax.\t(3 marks)\n(b)\tAn economist comments, ‘Both the indirect tax revenue and the direct tax revenue of the Government may be affected by the above proposed HAT.’ Justify the economist's comment.\t(4 marks)\n\nThere are receptionists, bell boys, room attendants and managers working in hotels.\n(c)\tWhat economic principle is illustrated by the above phenomenon? List THREE reasons why the application of this principle can increase labour productivity.\t(4 marks)\n(d)\tThe following is a job advertisement for room attendants in a hotel.\nRoom attendants\nMajor duty: tidying up hotel rooms\nWorking hours: 10am-2pm\nSalary: $85 per hour\nFrom the viewpoint of the hotel owners, give ONE advantage and ONE disadvantage of the above wage payment method over piece rate.\t(2 marks)\n(e)\tMany hotels in Hong Kong charge a higher room rate during public holidays than on other days. Explain whether the opportunity cost of staying in those hotels in Hong Kong is necessarily higher during public holidays than on other days.\t(3 marks)",
