      "questionTextEng": "Airline A is the only airline which operates flights to and from City X.\nSuppose Airline A adopts uniform pricing.\n\n(a)\tIndicate in Figure 2\n(i)\tthe price and output level of the airline as P0 and Q0 respectively.\t(2 marks)\n(ii)\tthe efficient output level as Q1.\t(1 mark)\n(iii)\tthe deadweight loss.\t(1 mark)\n\n(b)\tDue to an increase in oil price, the efficient output level of Airline A drops to Qo as in (a)(i).\n\t‘Airline A will produce at the efficient output level after the change.’ Do you agree? Explain your answer with the aid of Figure 2.\t(5 marks)\n \n \nThe table below shows some information for flights from City X to City Y operated by Airline A.\nFlight details\tTicket Price\n4:15pm-7:20pm (3 hours 5 minutes)\t$924\n7:35am-10:25am (2 hours 50 minutes)\t$1 015\n1:25pm-4:20pm (2 hours 55 minutes)\t$1 007\n\n(c)\tBased on the above information, explain whether the above pricing arrangement constitutes price discrimination.\t(3 marks)\n\n(d)\tIn City Y, most airlines raise the prices of air tickets during peak seasons.\nA politician: The airlines engage in anti-competitive behaviour in the above situation.\nAn economist: No, this is merely a response of the airlines to changing market conditions.\n(i)\tExplain under what situation the politician's comment is correct.\t(2 marks)\n(ii)\tGive ONE reason to support the economist's comment.\t(2 marks)",
