      "questionTextEng": "Refer to Figure 3. PPFA and PPFB are the production possibility frontiers of Country A and Country B respectively. A0 is the consumption point of Country A without trade.\n\n \n\n(a)\tState the change in the marginal cost of producing Good X in Country A when its output of Good X increases. Explain the reason behind.\t(2 marks)\n\nSuppose the opportunity cost of producing 1 unit of Good X in Country A is 0.5 units of Good Y at A0.\n(b)\tDoes Country A enjoy a comparative advantage in producing Good X over Country B? Explain your answer.\t(2 marks)\n \nThe two countries open to international trade and the slope of the dotted line is the world price of Good X.\n(c)\tIndicate in Figure 3\n(i)\tthe production point and the consumption possibility frontier of Country A as PA and CPFA respectively.\t(2 marks)\n(ii)\tthe consumption possibility frontier of Country B as CPFB.\t(1 mark)\n\n(d)\tSuppose 10 units of Good X are traded by Country B. Indicate in Figure 3\n(i)\tthe consumption point of Country В аѕ СB.\t(1 mark)\n(ii)\tthe import volume and export volume of Country B.\t(2 marks)\n\n(e) The government of Country B has changed its policies on human capital. As a result, the productivity of Country B in producing Good Y has increased.\n(i)\tExplain whether Country B's direction of trade will be affected.\t(2 marks)\n(ii)\tExplain ONE policy change that may raise the productivity of producing Good Y in Country B.\t(2 marks)\n(iii)\t‘The increase in productivity in Country B does NOT necessarily imply an increase in the Human Development Index in Country B.’ Support this statement with ONE reason. Explain your answer.\t(2 marks)",
