      "questionTextEng": "Pop Mart International Group Limited (Pop Mart) is a Chinese company that manufactures and sells toys through its official stores. Labubu is one of the most successful collectible toy series of 2024, and many photos of this toy series have been shared on social media platforms.\n\n(a) Which types of production is Pop Mart engaged in? Explain. (4 marks)\n\n(b) Explain whether the Labubu photos on social media platforms are public goods. (3 marks)\n\n(c) In 2024, many people were unable to purchase Labubu toys through official stores. They chose to buy Labubu toys in the secondary resale market at prices significantly higher than the official prices. Which function of price is illustrated in this phenomenon? Explain. (2 marks)\n\n(d) In the first half of 2025, Pop Mart has expanded rapidly, opening more physical stores to sell its toys. Explain what type of expansion Pop Mart was engaged in. (2 marks)\n\nRefer to the following sources.\n\nSource A: A news extract about Pop Mart\n\nIn the first half of 2025, the revenue from the sales of the Labubu series accounted for approximately 35% of the company’s total revenue. However, the price of Labubu toys fell in the secondary resale market in October 2025 due to a cooling of speculative demand for the toys and increased production by the manufacturer.\n\nSource B: Stock price of Pop Mart International Group Limited (stock code: 9992) on the Hong Kong Stock Exchange from June 2025 to November 2025\n\nStock price (HKD)\n350\n300\n250\n200\n150\n100\n50\n0\nJune July August September October November\n\n(e) To what type of business ownership does Pop Mart International Group Limited belong? (1 mark)\n\n(f) Based on the information in Source A, explain the change in Pop Mart International Group Limited’s stock price in October 2025 shown in Source B WITHOUT using a diagram. (4 marks)",
