      "questionTextChi": "China is the world's leading producer and consumer of new energy vehicles (NEVs).\n\n(a) It is observed that some identical NEVs are sold at different prices in different retail shops. Give TWO possible reasons to explain why there is such a price difference. (4 marks)\n\nThe Chinese government provided subsidies to local NEV producers from 2016 to 2020. Some environmentalists point out that the use of NEVs to replace traditional vehicles can reduce carbon emissions. For simplicity, the subsidy is assumed to be a per unit one.\n\n(b) In terms of externalities, explain how the subsidy can improve economic efficiency. (5 marks)\n\n(c) With the aid of a supply-demand diagram, explain how the subsidy would affect NEV producers' total revenue (including the subsidy). (6 marks)\n\n(d) WITHOUT using a diagram, state the condition under which the subsidy benefit enjoyed by NEV producers is larger than the subsidy benefit enjoyed by their consumers. (2 marks)",
