      "questionTextChi": "There are two food delivery service platforms in City A.\n\n(a) It is reported that Platform Y agrees to let Platform X be the sole food delivery service provider in some housing estates. In return, Platform X agrees not to compete with Platform Y in other housing estates.\n\n(i) Which conduct rule of the Competition Ordinance have these food delivery service platforms violated in the above case? Explain. (1 mark)\n(ii) Based on the above case, list TWO possible motives for the platforms to make such an agreement. (2 marks)\n(iii) List TWO undesirable economic effects of the above behaviours on consumers. (2 marks)\n\nAssume Platform X is the only food delivery service platform in certain housing estates and adopts simple monopoly pricing.\n\n(b) With the aid of Figure 4, explain why simple monopoly pricing may lead to economic inefficiency. (4 marks)\n\nFigure 4\n(A graph is shown with P on the y-axis and Q on the x-axis. It features a downward-sloping demand curve labeled D₁ and an upward-sloping marginal cost curve labeled MC₁, with the text \"MC = marginal cost\" next to it.)\n\n(c) Suppose food delivery services are becoming increasingly popular in those housing estates.\n\n(i) Indicate in Figure 4 the new price and new quantity transacted of services provided by Platform X as P₂ and Q₂ respectively. (3 marks)\n(ii) Indicate in Figure 4 the new deadweight loss. (1 mark)\n\nBelow is a promotional message displayed on Platform X's app.\n\nNew User Promotion\nDelivery service charge for new users:\n50% off\nRegister your account using your phone number!\n\n(d) Explain whether the pricing arrangement described in the above promotional message constitutes price discrimination. (3 marks)",
